<strong>BACOLOD CITY PROJECT -  </strong>Mesavirre Garden Residences

<a href="http://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/mesavirre.jpg"><img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1957" src="http://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/mesavirre.jpg" alt="" width="679" height="960" /></a>

&nbsp;

The team also had fun exploring the tourist destinations of Singapore. During the City Tour the team was introduced to the history and culture of Singapore allowing them to understand further the success and discipline of the Singaporeans.

Per one of the Brokers who’s in Singapore for the first time, the ways and discipline of Singapore in their transportation and traffic rules is a strong indication of good governance. The developments and construction of public transportation like MTR lines are fast and evident that even if the GST (tax) of Singapore is high, the people experience convenience and efficiency in their transport system.

Traffic Enforcers are not visible but there’s a lot of CCTV everywhere. The strict implementation and obedience of the law is quite amazing that it gives them very low crime rates. It is in this reason why there are a lot of tourists and investors coming in to Singapore.

In the Philippines, the current government have plans of replicating Singapore\'s success in development and its transport system. The Mindanao Rail plan and the current growing development of real estate in the Philippines is something to look forward for. Join the real estate boom and the increasing investment opportunities in the Philippines, contact the nearest Filipino Homes Office and members in your area for your investment options..','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => NULL,'views' => '42','category_id' => '14','published_at' => '2017-05-28 09:57:30','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:52'),
  array('id' => '182','title' => 'Philippines companies win big at Asia Pacific Property Awards','slug' => 'philippines-companies-win-big-asia-pacific-property-awards','content' => '<p style="text-align: center;"><strong>The Asia Pacific Property Awards is the most prestigious industry event in the region, and in the just-announced 2017-2018 Awards, companies from the Philippians have won a glittering array of honours.</strong></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Presented at The Marriott Marquis Queen’s Park Bangkok on 25-26 May, a total of 14 Philippines companies received awards for categories ranging across property development, real estate, interior design and architecture categories. Chosen from over 900 entries across the Asia Pacific region, these companies have proved themselves to be the very best in their sector.</p>
&nbsp;

Winners include:

<strong>Company: </strong>Ayala Land Premier

<strong>Award: Five-Star Award</strong>

<strong>Project: </strong>Park Central Towers

<strong>Category: </strong>Residential Development

<strong> </strong>

<strong>Company: </strong>Empire Designs

<strong>Award: Five-Star Award </strong>

<strong>Project: </strong>The Gentry Residences Showroom

<strong>Category: </strong>Interior Design
<p style="text-align: center;"><img class="alignnone wp-image-1940 " src="http://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/IMG_8216-1024x683.jpg" alt="" width="689" height="460" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><img class="alignnone wp-image-1941 " src="http://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/IMG_8253-1024x683.jpg" alt="" width="682" height="455" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">The Asia Pacific Awards are part of the International Property Awards that include the regions of Africa, Arabia, Europe, The Americas and the UK. The awards celebrate the very best projects and professionals in the industry.</p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Five Philippines company winners at country level have also been nominated to compete against other companies in the Asia Pacific region to become Best in Asia Pacific, and perhaps ultimately Best in the World. Results at these levels will be announced on 4 December at the Savoy Hotel in London, United Kingdom.</p>
<p style="text-align: center;">The awards presentations also played host to the IPAX Asia Pacific property industry exhibition on 25<sup>th</sup> and 26<sup>th</sup> May, which saw record attendance levels this year. Top industry suppliers were on hand to showcase their products and services, whilst delegates networked with the very best industry CEOs, Managing Directors and decision makers within the Asia Pacific area.</p>
<strong>For more information about the Asia Pacific Property Awards 2017 </strong>

