<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Misamis University </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>H.T. Feliciano St, Ozamiz City </h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://scontent.fcgy1-1.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/49249060_10156895702374085_6494435364134977536_o.jpg?_nc_cat=109&amp;_nc_oc=AQlHgSO_sMcHCQiDOCUQalYJfNnSsqn7eRQXn1wJ4a0tN8dtVMs5W8sxHSWO-LzJrVg&amp;_nc_ht=scontent.fcgy1-1.fna&amp;oh=d5c1cf4d4755f835e6c4c220a4d7dac2&amp;oe=5D675696" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Misamis University is a privately owned, non-sectarian, non-profit educational institution founded by the Feliciano family in 1929.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>&nbsp;The only autonomous university granted by the&nbsp;Commission on Higher Education&nbsp;(CHED) in Northwestern Mindanao, an&nbsp;ISO 9001:2015&nbsp;Management System Certified granted by Det Norske Veritas-Germanischer Lloyd Business Assurance, granted COD (Center of Development) by CHED for Criminology, Information Technology and Teacher Education and awarded by PACUCOA (The Philippine Association of Colleges and Universities Commission on Accreditation) as the Most Number of Accredited Programs in Region X.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Misamis University caters to more than 8,000 students every year in its 7.5 hectare campus in Ozamiz City and Oroquieta City, Misamis Occidental Philippines.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
