<p><!--EndFragment--></p>','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/05/filipino-homes-realtor-blogger-xyza-yape-4.png','views' => '63','category_id' => '11','published_at' => '2019-05-28 23:00:06','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '321','title' => 'Why OFWs should take advantage of attending Philippine Property Roadshows?','slug' => 'why-ofws-should-take-advantage-of-attending-philippine-property-roadshows','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes often hosts Philippine Property Roadshows outside the country. It is one way of letting our overseas Filipino Workers know about the latest developments and projects on going and coming in the Philippines. It is also one way of letting them know how good the economy of the Philippines today. Filipino homes, provide them the necessary information to help them decide to give back and invest back in the Philippines. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4190} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/61259566_10216341240622130_7120610727961821184_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4190"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Philippines currently receives 28 to 32 Billion dollars of remittance every year [<a href="http://www.bsp.gov.ph/statistics/keystat/ofw.htm">Read BSP Report Here]</a>. That greatly helps the rising economy of the Philippines. The OFW contribution in our current economy is undeniable. However, they only receive news from the media more about politics and what\'s bad happening rather than what is good happening in the country. Other countries look at what\'s good in the Philippines thus they are actively investing in the country today. Our country men however are not open to investing back in our country because of limited information. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes advocate providing enough knowledge and information prioritizing Filipinos for the investment opportunities currently available in the Philippines today. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Investment Opportunities available for Overseas Filipino Workers</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Overseas Filipino Workers may be too focused in their overseas jobs. Information like what\'s new and what\'s happening in the Philippine economy are not readily available. Information in social media are sometimes exaggerated, fabricated and not true. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Free real estate advise for your properties. </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>During the property roadshow, real estate brokers and agents from Filipino Homes will be there to assist you in whatever real estate concerns you may have. Get an advise from the Top real estate broker in the Philippines. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Investment Tips from the Top real estate broker in the Philippines. </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you are not sure yet what to invest in, how to be successful in real estate investing and how to do smart investing with real estate, this is the best venue. This information are not usually given free, but during Property roadshows these are given to you free of charge. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Registrations for Property roadshows are FREE with Filipino Homes.  All you have to do is arrive at the venue and listen to the talks. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes will be in Tokyo, Japan this June 15-16, 2019 for the Philippine Property Roadshow. Please see invitation below. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4191} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/53915117_261903834746117_7172625427616235520_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4191"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you are interested to join, contact your Filipino Homes Agent today! And see you there. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/03/filipinohomes-real-estate-ph-xyzayape-5.png','views' => '69','category_id' => '11','published_at' => '2019-06-03 05:00:43','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '322','title' => 'Emerald Estates Making Your Dream Home Come True in Iloilo','slug' => 'emerald-estates-making-your-dream-home-come-true-in-iloilo','content' => '<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://filipinohomes.com/projectimg/500/500-1496110903.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Emerald Estates is a new development project of South Prime Developers, Inc. The South Prime Developers, Inc. or "South Prime", is a new development company rising up from a well-experienced and established real estate company in Metro Manila.  South Prime expanded its market in Iloilo, after  a successful launch of a Davao house and lot subdivision development last February 2016, South Prime expanded its market in Iloilo. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://filipinohomes.com/projectimg/500/500-1496110856.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>South Prime establishes itself as an innovative developer, embracing a distinctive philosophy of "Koi", going against the current to build and provide unique spaces and homes. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Source:  <a href="https://www.emeraldestatesiloilo.com/">Emerald Estates Iloilo</a>]</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://filipinohomes.com/projectimg/500/500-1496110932.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Last February 2019, together with Filipino Homes CEO and <a href="http://www.leuteriorealty.com">Leuterio Realty &amp; Brokerage</a> lead broker Anthony Gerard O. Leuterio, we visited the on-going construction and development of Emerald Estates. As part of our responsibility at property endorsers of Emerald Estates, the team came for inspection and close look on the ongoing site development. Emerald Estates is a top selling project highly recommended by Filipino Homes. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://filipinohomes.com/projectimg/500/500-1496110875.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Beyond your ordinary house and lot subdivision, the <a href="https://filipinohomes.com/developers/southprime/maOg">Emerald Estates</a> is designed with you in mind:<br></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>Where the old traditions meet with new innovations,<br>Where the roots of culture gravitate towards the future,<br>Where the place of dreams comes into your reality.</p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><br>For more details, contact a Filipino Homes Agent near you. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>HLURB License to Sell : 031976</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Projects similar to Emerald Estates of Davao and Iloilo will soon to rise in another soon to be Mega City in Mindanao. Just keep posted and follow our Filipino Homes pages. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/06/filipino-homes-xyza-yape-real-estate-agent-.png','views' => '43','category_id' => '15','published_at' => '2019-06-11 11:10:51','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '323','title' => 'Filipino Homes OJT John Alex Magno Oliver is 2nd placer in the Real Estate Broker Licensure Exam','slug' => 'ojt-john-alex-magno-oliver-2nd-placer-in-the-real-estate-broker-licensure-exam','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Filipino Homes family welcomes <strong>six (6) new licensed brokers</strong> who passed the <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="Real Estate Brokers Licensure Examination (opens in a new tab)" href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Fnor-GyEHDvhAARmDZu0B6KGUq5Fj-Bq/view" target="_blank">Real Estate Brokers Licensure Examination</a> given by the Professional Regulation Commission (PRC) Board of Real Estate Service on June 16, 2019.  Our on-the-job trainee from the Cagayan de Oro City office, <strong>Mr. John Alex Magno Oliver</strong> of Xavier University, garnered the second highest score nationwide of 87.75%. Joining him as the new Filipino Homes brokers are <strong>Divi Mesha Romero, Jamz Exequiel Fulguernas, Rikkia Eve Baguio, Mary Joy Montenegro Bolaso,</strong> and <strong>Tricia Santos.</strong> </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4216} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/64397169_10214660857457842_6237471508084555776_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4216"/><figcaption>The new Real Estate Brokers with Filipino Homes founder, Mr.  Anthony Leuterio  </figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> The REB Exam 2nd placer, Mr. Oliver, shares his story: "<em>I’m originally from Davao City po. Prior to my REM course, I graduated from Ateneo de Davao University with a degree in BS in Marketing. I decided to take REM because my family is in the real estate business, specifically into subdivision development. Our company is Island Hills Land Corporation, and we are based in the Island Garden City of Samal." </em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>An on-the-job training in a realty company was part of the BS Real Estate Management curriculum in Xavier University - Ateneo de Cagayan. The topnotcher says he decided to join Filipino Homes because he "<em>find(s) Filipino Homes to be the best realty company not just in Cagayan de Oro City but also in the whole Philippines. Its vast network of brokers and developers nationwide coupled with the company’s modern technological innovations, allow the Filipino Homes real estate salespersons and brokers to provide their clients with the best services possible." </em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4215} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/64574158_2279452232372855_5881365040744890368_n-1024x632.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4215"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>He adds, "<em>I am proud to be a part of Filipino Homes and I look forward to serving my future clients with best services available only at Filipino Homes. </em>"</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Kudos to our newest real estate brokers! Your Filipino Homes family is extremely proud of you. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Real Estate Service Act (RESA) requires aspiring real estate professionals seeking to be registered and licensed as a real estate service practitioner, except a&nbsp;<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/how-to-be-a-prc-accredited-real-estate-salesperson/" target="_blank">real estate salesperson</a>), to pass the Real Estate Broker Licensure Exam. If you are considering a career in real estate, check out these list of schools/universities that offer the BS Real Estate Management course in <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="Luzon (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/schools-universities-offering-bs-real-estate-management-in-luzon/" target="_blank">Luzon</a>, <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="Visayas (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/schools-universities-offering-bs-real-estate-management-in-visayas/" target="_blank">Visayas</a>, and <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="Mindanao (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/schools-universities-offering-bs-real-estate-management-in-mindanao/" target="_blank">Mindanao</a>. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/06/64574158_2279452232372855_5881365040744890368_n.jpg','views' => '41','category_id' => '16','published_at' => '2019-06-20 14:43:33','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '324','title' => '3 Ways To Help Your Child Buy A Home While On A Budget','slug' => '3-ways-to-help-your-child-buy-a-home-while-on-a-budget','content' => '<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><em>Offering assistance when gifting a down payment might not be possible</em></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":2590} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2018/04/d851d8843796367ec7b73d64cd513f2a.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-2590"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>I have been receiving emails and messages in our Facebook pages about parents mostly mothers who wish their child can already buy a home for their own family. Some would request for assistance on how their child can actually afford a property they find appropriate for them. That is indeed a sweet gesture for parents to still think about their child and their future even if they are already adults. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Sometimes, Millennial like me (ahemm) would tend to live the YOLO (You only live once) lifestyle and think about the future later. Well not all millennial though, because some may have already been investing and managing their financial resources well on other things. Millennial most specially for singles would tend to invest secretly, buy life insurances, health insurances and the likes first, and prefer to not inform parents and relatives about it. That is why sometimes people get them wrong thinking they\'re not planning for their future. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Married millenials however, have different struggles (oh well) slightly different from the single ones. Married millenials they have twice or thrice responsibility and allocations financially depending on how big their family is. Sometimes because of that, renting a house is a good option for them and buying a house is a second option. But parents definitely think differently. Mothers knows best, they say. They\'d prefer them buying their own so they don\'t have to rent out. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you are a parent and would like to help your child get his/her first home, but paying for a down payment is not possible. Here are the things that you can do for them;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>1. Help Them Find Resources</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":2583} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2018/04/978d8d4eb030552a2e7db2bcf78c4630.jpeg.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-2583"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Increasing their capacity to pay is one big help in making their dream of buying their own home a reality. It takes a little sacrifice for you and for them but it will surely pay off the moment they get to live in their own home. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can start a business that doesn\'t need big capital. Join a real estate company and sell properties perhaps to earn commissions? Choose to sell insurances and earn commission based without having to leave your current job. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Remember</strong>: <em>Their own home may not be their dream home yet. If the time comes they can already afford their dream home, at least they can have their own home get rented and earn from it as well. That\'s another source of income. </em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>2. Save For A Downpayment Together</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":2342} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/pool-money-with-family-and-friends-real-estate-investment-filipinohomes.jpg" alt="pool money with family and friends real estate investment filipinohomes" class="wp-image-2342"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can offer to match the amount of what he/she can set aside to save for a down payment. For example, You can both commit to save 5,000 per month to help them reach the desired down payment amount faster. Make sure that this money are really saved for the sole purpose of saving for down payment and not use it for anything else, even for emergencies. <br><br>You should both have a separate savings for emergencies. And it takes real discipline really. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>3. Consider Co-Ownership</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4226} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/istockphoto-860175838-612x612.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4226"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If  you are a parent and you are still working ; which means you still receive salary and not yet in retirable age, you can co-own and loan the property with your child.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When you will be paying for the property in cash,  both of you, will have to produce the money and sign the documents of the purchase. If he\'s/she\'s married that will take 4 signatures; since the property will be owned by 2 couples. If your child is still single, then there will be 3 owners, your child will be the principal owner if his/her salary is a bit bigger than your combined salary with your spouse. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you will loan the property in the bank or PAG-IBIG housing loan, both of you will have to provide documents necessary for the approval of the loan. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We all know parents wants the best for their child, and their child owning a home is one of their pride. Sometimes they just couldn\'t afford it alone and help is what they need. If you are an able parent but couldn\'t afford to pay off the down payment yourself yet, offer your help whether offering them an opportunity to earn more, help them save up or co-own the property for them. Make sure they will make the decision on which house or property and not push it too hard that it may offend them. As a millennial, we know you are doing it out of love. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Hope this helps. Do you need help from your parents? Share this to your friends or momma\'s :)</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"customFontSize":10} -->
<p style="font-size:10px"><em>Reference: https://homeownershipmatters.realtor/issues/3-ways-to-help-your-child-buy-a-home-while-on-a-budget/</em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/06/filipino-homes-xyza-yape-real-estate-agent-1.png','views' => '52','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2019-07-10 21:00:25','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '325','title' => 'Cebu Landmasters brings Casa Mira to CDO','slug' => 'cebu-landmasters-brings-casa-mira-to-cdo','content' => '<p><!--StartFragment--></p>

<!-- wp:image {"id":4376} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/46749928_271981630128602_1755034400057196544_n-1.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4376"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Cebu Landmasters Inc. (CLI) is bringing its best-selling economic housing development, Casa Mira, to more Filipino families as it expands to Cagayan de Oro City (CDO).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>CLI\'s sixth Casa Mira development in the country, Casa Mira Towers CDO will soon rise in Barangay Kauswagan. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>"We want to give more to Filipino families through Casa Mira --- more space, more amenities and more value for their investment," said CLI chief executive officer and founder Jose Soberano III. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4334} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/img_4407-1024x576.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4334"/><figcaption>Casa Mira Towers CDO Scale model</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With a total land area of 6,315 square meters, Casa Mira towers CDO will consist of two residential towers, Amenities include a fitness gym, clubhouse, viewing deck, prayer room, adult and kiddie pool, and play area. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>"The security and peace of mind of residents are guaranteed as there is 24/7 CCT system and 100% back-up power among Casa Mira Towers CDO\'s many amenities", said Soberano. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Casa Mira Towers CDO is in the vicinity of big establishments, hospitals, churches, and schools.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>"Casa Mira Towers CDO will have its own retail spaces on the ground floor for the residents\' convenience. They won\'t need to go far to get what they need," said Soberano. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4374} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/46831037_346661232779458_500327272956297216_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4374"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There are a total of 986 units available in Casa Mira Towers CDO for both towers; 444 units in Tower `1 and 542 units in Tower 2. Studio and one-bedroom units which feature a modern design has a floor area ranging from 20 to 36 square meters. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Other Casa Mira\'s include Casa Mira South, Casa mira Linao, Casa Mira towers Labanagon, and Casa Mira towers Guadalupe in Cebu and Casa Mira Coast in Dumaguete. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>"Casa Mira demonstrates our commitment to providing better homes throughout Visayas and Mindanao. We aim to serve many Filipino families through the quality of our delivery and giving more than what is expected."</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<p><!--EndFragment--></p>','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/09/46749928_271981630128602_1755034400057196544_n-1.jpg','views' => '40','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2019-07-17 17:56:25','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '326','title' => 'Cebu Landmasters launches prime subdivision development in Cagayan de Oro','slug' => 'cebu-landmasters-launches-prime-subdivision-development-in-cagayan-de-oro','content' => '<p><!--StartFragment--></p>
<p>Vismin\'s leading developer Cebu Landmasters Inc. (CLI) is bringing its upper mid market residential subdivision line to CDO as it contnious its expansion in Visayas and Mindanao.&nbsp;</p>
<p><!--StartFragment--></p>
<p>CLI will be launching Velmiro Uptown CDO on July 17 following the overwhelming success of its Velmiro Heights development in Minglanilla, Cebu.&nbsp;</p>

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4339,4340,4343]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/IMG_9160-1024x576.jpg" alt="" data-id="4339" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4339" class="wp-image-4339"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/IMG_9156-1024x576.jpg" alt="" data-id="4340" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4340" class="wp-image-4340"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/IMG_9159-1024x576.jpg" alt="" data-id="4343" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4343" class="wp-image-4343"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Velmiro Uptown is a modern residential community composed of spacious well-designed homes with scenic views and premier amenities in the midst of an expansive natural environment. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With house and lots efficiently designed to maximize space, optimize breathtaking views, and use natural light and good air circulation, Velmiro Uptown CDO will be composed of 396 units in a 14.3 hectare area. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4342} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/IMG_9158-1024x576.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4342"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>"Velmiro Uptown give you the amenities of the city and the benefits of an expansive natural environment, making residents feel more relaxed. They can enjoyo serenity while remaining in the comforts of city life," said CLI Chief executive officier and founder Jose Soberano III. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4341} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/IMG_9157-1024x576.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4341"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Nestled at a prime location in Upper Canitoan, Cagayan de Oro City, there is easy access to major establishments which are just a few blocks away. Velmiro Uptown CDO is in the vicinity of SM City CDO, Xavier University and iNternational School of CDO, German Doctors Hospital , Our lady of Guadalupe Churhch, among others. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This secured and gated community also features a generous open sace comprising of 70 percent of the entire subdivision. This area promotes leisure and relaxation with amenities such as swimming pool, basketball court, clubhouse, outdoor meditation area, parks and a lot more. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>"There are various house and lot types including townhouse units, single-attached, and single detached houses that one can choose from whether you are starting a family, expanding your family or just looking for a comfortable living space," said Soberano. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<p><!--EndFragment--></p>
<p><!--EndFragment--></p>','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/09/filipino-homes-xyza-yape-real-estate-agent-1.png','views' => '44','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2019-07-18 09:34:04','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '327','title' => 'Cebu Landmasters expands presence in Northern Mindanao with two new residential projects','slug' => 'cebu-landmasters-expands-presence-in-northern-mindanao-with-two-new-residential-projects','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leading VisMin property developer Cebu Landmasters Inc. boosts its presence in under-served Northern Mindanao with the recent launch of two residential projects valued at Php 1.26 billion that innovatively meet the needs of mid and economic-income housing clients. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4334} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/img_4407.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4334"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Casa Mira Towers CDO is a Php 824 million, two-tower condominium development offering 986 units ranging from 20sqm studios at 36sqm one-bedroom units in a strategic Barangay Kauswagan location and generous amenities. projected completion date will be in the fourth quarter of 2022.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4327} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/img_4401.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4327"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Php 437 million Velmiro Uptown CDO offers 396 house-and-lots in 14-hectare gated subdivision in the rapidly developing Upper Canitoan area of Uptown Cagayan de Oro is the second largest economic driver of Mindanao and Cebu Landmasters is rapidly expanding to serve the evolving real estate market needs in the area."</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4332} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/img_4399.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4332"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>CLI\'s popular housing brand Casa Mira, for example, has sold close to 6,000 units in four Cebu province locations and another location in Dumaguete City by "offering more to the Filipino family," according to Soberano. The economic housing project gives clients amenities such as pool, gym, clubhouse and play area, all of which are more closely associated with higher-end residential products.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4331} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/img_4443.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4331"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Velmiro likewise exceeds client expectations with its strategic and rapidly developing location in CDO near schools, hospitals and malls and upscale amenities. It offers units designed to maximize space, optimize views, and use natural lighting and ventilation. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4335} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/img_4402.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4335"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Cebu Landmasters has mastery of its VisMin markets and was recently named best developer in the country by Property Guru Philippines Property Awards. It now has 58 projects in different stages of development covering residential, office, retail, hotels and a 22-hectare township in Davao City. "We expect to roll out 29 more before the year ends," declared Soberano who remain bullish about prospects of the VisMin markets. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/09/Cebu-Landmasters-CLI-logo-pse.jpg','views' => '36','category_id' => '14','published_at' => '2019-07-18 18:25:30','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '328','title' => 'Filipino Homes Opens its 42nd Office','slug' => 'filipino-homes-opens-its-42nd-office','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes opens its 42nd office at Mastersons Avenue Cagayan de Oro City last August 8, 2019. This office is operated and managed by REB Aldin Tagolimot of Leuterio Realty CDO. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4263} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/img_4639.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4263"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Opening of the new office was lead by Filipino Homes CEO and Leuterio Realty &amp; Brokerage lead broker Anthony Gerard O. Leuterio with his lovely wife May Leuterio, who traveled all the way from Cebu City to grace the event. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Other Leuterio Realty brokers and property investment endorsers were also present during the blessing and opening of the 42nd office of Filipino Homes. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here are some photos taken during the opening. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4264} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/img_4629.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4264"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<p><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/img_4638.jpg" class="size-full wp-image-4268" width="1200" height="802"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/img_4637.jpg" class="size-full wp-image-4266" width="1200" height="802"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/img_4636.jpg" class="size-full wp-image-4267" width="1200" height="802"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/img_4635.jpg" class="size-full wp-image-4265" width="1200" height="802"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/img_4634.jpg" class="size-full wp-image-4269" width="1200" height="802"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/img_4633.jpg" class="size-full wp-image-4272" width="1200" height="802"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/img_4632.jpg" class="size-full wp-image-4270" width="1200" height="802"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/img_4631.jpg" class="size-full wp-image-4271" width="1200" height="802"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/img_4630.jpg" class="size-full wp-image-4273" width="1200" height="802"></p>
<p>Congratulations! </p>','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => NULL,'views' => '44','category_id' => '9','published_at' => '2019-08-08 13:32:34','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '329','title' => 'Top 4 Infrastructure Projects To Boost Real Estate In Cebu','slug' => 'top-4-infrastructure-projects-to-boost-real-estate-in-cebu','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Solid infrastructure has always been a benchmark of economic growth.&nbsp;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When reliable infrastructure is in place, more jobs are created, better services are provided to the public and investors will be attracted to put in money for even more development. This gives our growing economy a more competitive edge over others.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The government seems keen to seize this opportunity, since lots of projects are already in the pipeline as part of the current administration’s Build, Build, Build campaign.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We’re looking at multi-billion projects aimed to usher in the “Golden Age of Infrastructure” in many emerging provinces outside the capital, like Cebu. This opens a huge window of opportunity for many sectors, including real estate.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here are some of the top infrastructure projects we can look forward to in the coming years:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>Mactan-Cebu International Airport Terminal Two</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4279} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/Night-Mactan-Cebu-International-Airport-2018-Update.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4279"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Airports are the windows to any city, so they have to make a good first impression, especially to first-time visitors. That’s why Mactan-Cebu International Airport (MCIA) has developed its bigger, better and resort-inspired terminal two.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>MCIA\'s terminal two is a stunning three-storey structure made with wooden arches, concrete flooring and mother-of-pearl interior accents. It adopts Cebu\'s laid-back, tropical island vibe with its use of natural light and graceful architecture, so much so that its developers proudly state that it could be considered "one of the most beautiful terminal buildings in the world".</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4280} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/Perspective-Mactan-Cebu-International-Airport-2018-Update.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4280"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This terminal is set to increase passenger arrivals by as much as 12% . This means that more people (roughly 1 million more, based on the&nbsp;<a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.google.com/url?q%3Dhttp://www.sunstar.com.ph/cebu/business/2018/01/25/mactan-airport-terminal-2-open-july-585640%26amp;sa%3DD%26amp;ust%3D1566138485033000&amp;sa=D&amp;ust=1566138485047000&amp;usg=AFQjCNF8PdHDqnwPeP-AHMTH-wyfqrKrfA">current statistics</a>) can visit Cebu and enjoy its sights and sounds. This is good news for many sectors, including tourism and real estate.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Tourism-driven real estate investments have been on a steady rise since last year. The improvement of the airport can translate into an increased demand in accommodations like rental units and condotels. Many tourists are preferring these types of accommodations due to ease of access and affordability.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4281} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/Mactan-Cebu-International-Airport-2018-Update.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4281"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Better airport services and an increase in direct international flights could also mean that OFWs can come to the island more frequently. OFWs are keen on investing in real estate, whether for end-use or rental properties. Let\'s hope that this terminal can really live up to they hype when it opens on June or July 2018.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>3rd Mactan-Cebu Bridge (And More!)</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4282} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/maxresdefault-3-1024x576.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4282"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Connectivity and logistics between the islands has always been a big challenge for an archipelago like the Philippines. This is why the government is slated to invest as much as P458 billion on its Philippine Inter-Island Linkage Project, which aims to connect the islands through multiple bridges.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For Cebu, this means the building of the Cebu-Cordova Link Expressway (CCLEX), also known as the "3rd bridge". Worth around P23 billion, the bridge spans 8 kilometers long and will connect the two islands of Mactan and Cebu through the municipality of Cordova and the city of Talisay. This project will not only ease traffic congestion in two of Cebu\'s existing bridges, it will also boost the growing real estate climates in both Cordova and Talisay.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Cordova and Talisay city are fast becoming prime areas for a variety of residential properties. With the third bridge still on the way, one can expect more and more real estate investments pouring into these locations. Think about it: once the bridge is completed, these areas will become more accessible. Travel will be faster and more convenient. Commerce will flourish and property values will sky-rocket. If you\'re interested in investing real estate, these two locations are the places to be, and the perfect timing is now, when the price tags are still relatively low.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And the Build, Build, Build project doesn\'t stop there. The government is also looking at the possibility of linking Cordova to the neighboring province of Bohol as well as a&nbsp;<a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.google.com/url?q%3Dhttp://cebudailynews.inquirer.net/144816/billions-pesos-infrastructure-projects-seen-fuel-growth-cebu%26amp;sa%3DD%26amp;ust%3D1566138485036000&amp;sa=D&amp;ust=1566138485047000&amp;usg=AFQjCNEj-zmEnOw0800JDiK6Qvgu8j3Rfw">possible 4th bridge</a>, which will connect Mactan and Cebu through Consolacion and Pusok. &nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Metro Cebu Expressway</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4283} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/cebuexpressway-1024x683.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4283"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Traveling from the northern parts of Cebu to the southern areas and vice versa is nothing short of stressful, especially during rush hour. This can all change once the Metro Cebu Expressway is constructed.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The 50-billion peso project, which stretches for 74 kilometers, will have four to six lanes and promises to cut the 3-hour travel time from Naga to Danao to just one hour. This should hopefully decongest problematic areas like Minglanilla in the south and Consolacion in the north as well.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As far as real estate is concerned, this move could mean more interest in the developments constructed in these areas. Like Cordova and Talisay, Naga and Danao are burgeoning real estate hotspots. Once the expressway is completed, expect more developments to flourish and property values to increase.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Bus Rapid Transit (BRT)</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4284} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/Cebu-BRT-Station-Example.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4284"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Last but not the least is the Bus Rapid Transit or (BRT).&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Increased vehicular traffic is a common problem among growing cities like Cebu. Sadly, this is not only causing people to lose precious time and &nbsp;energy, it\'s also costing businesses money. According to a&nbsp;<a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.google.com/url?q%3Dhttp://cebudailynews.inquirer.net/86098/cost-of-traffic%26amp;sa%3DD%26amp;ust%3D1566138485039000&amp;sa=D&amp;ust=1566138485048000&amp;usg=AFQjCNG9eko-RX4jR2N7kyBFA5I7sjADHQ">study</a>, millions of pesos in man-hours are lost when people get stuck in traffic. As a solution, the Cebu City government has come up with the Bus Rapid Transit (BRT). As one of the earliest proposed mass transit systems, the BRT aims to upgrade Cebu City from the usual jeepneys and alleviate traffic conditions along major thoroughfares.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Once completed, the BRT is projected to use more than 170 buses and 33 stations across Metro Cebu. Feasibility studies show that the BRT can save Cebuanos millions of hours--- and pesos--- in the long run.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Having an efficient mass transit system is important for a growing city like Cebu. This will ensure that the city will have a sustainable way to ferry people to and from their destinations. Less traffic also translates in cut losses from businesses. A system like the BRT would ensure that investors would keep pouring in, and developments will continue to flourish to accommodate the demands of the public.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Final Thoughts</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There are more developments in the pipeline as of this writing...not only in Cebu but also in other provinces across the country. With the government keen on decentralizing funds and projects, one can expect many improvements on the country’s infrastructure in the coming years. This means that many real estate projects are also projected to soar in the near future. If you’re interested in the next real estate hotspot, keep an eye on the government’s Build, Build, Build campaign and you’ll know.<br class="Apple-interchange-newline"></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/08/filipino-homes-xyza-yape-real-estate-agent-2.png','views' => '64','category_id' => '9','published_at' => '2019-08-18 13:33:40','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '330','title' => 'PH tourism industry poised to attract more real estate investments','slug' => 'ph-tourism-industry-real-estate-investments','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="JLL (opens in a new tab)" href="https://www.jll.com.ph" target="_blank">JLL</a>, the Philippines\' leading real estate consultancy firm, recently released its Q2 2019 property market report. Based on the comprehensive study, the state of the Philippine real estate industry remains dynamic - and poised to attract more investments in the ensuing months.&nbsp; </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A recent study by Santos Knight Frank, an integrated real-estate service provider, corroborates the claim that Philippine tourism continues to generate interest among investors [<a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="src (opens in a new tab)" href="https://businessmirror.com.ph/2019/06/19/tourism-industry-attracting-major-hospitality-players/" target="_blank">src</a>]. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/reserve/8T8J12VQxyqCiQFGa2ct_bahamas-atlantis.jpg?ixlib=rb-1.2.1&amp;ixid=eyJhcHBfaWQiOjEyMDd9&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;w=1050&amp;q=80" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="Department of Tourism (DOT) (opens in a new tab)" href="http://www.tourism.gov.ph/news_features/ForeignTouristApril2019.aspx" target="_blank">Department of Tourism (DOT)</a> reported that foreign visitor count for January to April 2019 totaled 2,867,551, registering an 8.59% growth from 2,642,241 of the same period in 2018. International tourist arrivals in April 2019 reached 662,987, up 12.15% compared with 591,137 visitors last year.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://www.tourism.gov.ph/images/news/JanApril2019a3.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The top five markets with their respective volumes and growth rates are: China with 139,177 (+26.77%), Korea with 130,707 (+13.68%), USA with 87,710 (+2.5%), Japan with 57,724 (+17.75%) and Australia with 28,683 (+13.41%).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The DOT also reported that Filipinos are a strong market for the hospitality industry with 60 million domestic trips made by locals every year. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Demand and Supply</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>These figures indicate a bullish tourism sector as the Philippines continuously catches up with its neighbors. With this growth, the demand for condominiums and other short-term lease accommodations exceeds the supply of hotels that can accommodate the tourists and travelers in key cities in the country. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://s3-ap-southeast-1.amazonaws.com/filipinohomes/members/6736/listings/12194/719431891.received_585908205170235.jpeg" alt=""/><figcaption> 32 Sanson by Rockwell, Cebu City </figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Property developers continue to invest in condominium developments to accommodate this growing demand. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>What does this mean for you?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you are looking for opportunities to increase your passive income in the near future, invest in a condominium and make it a self-liquidating asset.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Related Articles</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Learn more about this real estate investment opportunity. Read more:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="Basic Tips When Buying A Condo In The Philippines (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/5-tips-buying-condo-philippines/" target="_blank">Basic Tips When Buying a Condo in the Philippines</a></li><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="What You Need to Know about the Condominium Act (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/condominium-act/" target="_blank">What You Need to Know About the Condominium Act</a></li><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="Tips for Millennials Who Want to Invest in Real Estate (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/tips-for-millennials-who-want-to-invest-in-real-estate/" target="_blank">Tips for Millennials Who Want to Invest in Real Estate</a></li><li> <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/best-cities-to-invest-in-rental-housing-for-millennials/" target="_blank">Best Cities to Invest in Rental Housing for Millennials</a> </li><li> <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/how-much-charge-condo-for-rent/" target="_blank">How much rent should I charge for my condo?</a> </li></ul>
