<!-- /wp:separator -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/07/filipino-homes-xyza-yape-real-estate-agent-5.png','views' => '76','category_id' => '15','published_at' => '2019-08-28 23:59:52','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '334','title' => '43rd Filipino Homes Office Opens in Lapu-Lapu City','slug' => '43rd-filipino-homes-office-opens-in-lapu-lapu-city','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>43rd Filipino Homes Office opened in Pusok Lapu-Lapu City last September 1, 2019. The 43rd office is owned and managed by REB Lucy Yu of Team Realty Masters of Leuterio Realty. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4348} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/69471281_10215119090513382_7010276875008212992_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4348"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>On the same day, they also had their mid-year awarding of top-performing real estate agents and brokers of Team Realty Masters .</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4349} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/Filipinohomes-001.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4349"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Mr. Anthony Leuterio, CEO and Founder of Filipino Homes graced the event as he leads the ribbon-cutting for the said new office. As promised by the visionary broker, more Filipino Homes office will open soon all over the country. To provide service and help Filipinos own their dream homes. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4350} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/Filipinohomes-002.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4350"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Learn more about Filipino Homes <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="here (opens in a new tab)" href="http://www.filipinohomes.com" target="_blank">here</a>. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/09/Filipinohomes-09.2019-1.png','views' => '47','category_id' => '14','published_at' => '2019-09-01 18:58:05','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '335','title' => 'Davao City Residential Property Market Report [1H 2019] and What This Means For You','slug' => 'davao-city-residential-property-market-report-1h-2019-and-what-this-means-for-you','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> JLL ( Jones Lang LaSalle IP, Inc.), the Philippines’ leading real estate and investment management firm, recently published the&nbsp;<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.jll.com.ph/en/trends-and-insights/research/1h19-philippine-property-market-overview" target="_blank">Philippine Property Market Report</a>&nbsp;for the first six months of 2019. This comprehensive report highlights updates and key movements in the real estate market of the country,  specifically the office, residential, retail and hospitality sectors of <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="Metro Manila (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/metro-manila-residential-property-market-report-1h-2019" target="_blank">Metro Manila</a>, <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="Metro Cebu (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/cebu-residential-property-market-report-%5B1h-2019%5D-and-what-this-means-for-you" target="_blank">Metro Cebu</a>, and Davao.  This blog post focuses on the state of the residential property market in Davao, covering the districts of Agdao, Buhangin, Talomo, and Poblacion.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4252} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/davao-city-districts-property-market-report.png" alt="" class="wp-image-4252"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>Residential&nbsp;Property Market</strong> - Davao</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4244} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/residential-property-market-cebu.png" alt="" class="wp-image-4244"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong><em>Supply</em></strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Only about 480 units were completed in the half of 2019, with most developments located in Talomo, bringing the total supply to 24,515 units. A total of 3,280 units are anticipated for completion for the rest of the year, assuming no construction delays for SMDC\'s massive Lane Residences development&nbsp;project.<br></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>At present, more than half of the existing residential condominiums are located in Talomo (57%).  In the next three years, almost half of the total future supply will still come from the district.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4254} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/market-share-residential-property-market-davao.png" alt="" class="wp-image-4254"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4><strong><em>Demand</em></strong></h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The most number of units taken up is also observed in Talomo district, in terms of ready-for-occupancy (RFO) developments at nearly full capacity. This is followed by Buhangin with 90% sales take-up and Poblacion with an 88% sales rate.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The reverse is true for future residential supply in Talomo with a sales take-up of 63%. A relatively stronger performance is recorded in Agdao (92%) and Buhangin (87%).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":5} -->
<h5>Demand Drivers</h5>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Demand for upper mid to luxury residential units in Davao City is driven by strong leasing activities from local and foreign students, mostly enrolled in universities.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The sale market in Davao is heavily dominated by OFW investors, taking advantage of the relatively cheaper value of the peso to acquire more properties for investment purposes. They either lease out their properties or <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="flip their properties (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/flip-houses-for-profit/" target="_blank">resell the units</a>. There is also an observed growing number of units taken up by people from outside Davao City, but within the Mindanao Island.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":5} -->
<h5>Rent and Selling Prices</h5>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The average rental price of residential units in Davao City ranges from Php610 to Php1,130 per sqm per month. The leasing activity is strongest in Poblacion, commanding the highest monthly rental of Php640 to Php1,130 per sqm. The cheapest rents can be found in Talomo, ranging from Php610 to Php640 per sqm per month. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For existing developments, average selling prices range from Php78,400 to Php216,000 per square meter.&nbsp;  For future supply, the average selling prices range from Php78,600 to Php215,200 per square meter.  Ready-for-occupancy units are most expensive in Poblacion, commanding a price range from Php103,600 to Php216,000 per sqm. On the other hand, pre-selling units are most expensive in Buhangin (Php80,600 to Php215,200 per sqm).  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>What This Means For You</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The comprehensive research of the property market in Davao City for the first half of 2019 indicates that the Philippine real estate industry continues to be strong.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The observed growth in business in Davao makes property investments in the city more lucrative. &nbsp;If you are actively looking for opportunities to increase your passive income in the near future, it is a good time to invest in a condominium. Talk to a&nbsp;<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/what-are-the-different-real-estate-professionals/" target="_blank">professional real estate service provider</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Related Articles</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Learn more about property investing. Read more:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="Best Cities to Invest in Rental Housing for Millennials (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/best-cities-to-invest-in-rental-housing-for-millennials/" target="_blank">Best Cities to Invest in Rental Housing for Millennials</a></li><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="Tips for first-time investor (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/tips-first-time-investor-critical/" target="_blank">Tips for first-time investors</a></li><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/why-invest-in-real-estate-property/" target="_blank">Why Invest In Real Estate Property</a></li><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="How to Make Money in Philippine Real Estate (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/money-real-estate/" target="_blank">How to Make Money in Philippine Real Estate</a></li><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="How to Effectively Flip Houses for Profit (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/flip-houses-for-profit/" target="_blank">How to Effectively Flip Houses for Profit</a></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Full report:&nbsp;<a href="https://www.jll.com.ph/en/trends-and-insights/research/1h19-philippine-property-market-overview">https://www.jll.com.ph/en/trends-and-insights/research/1h19-philippine-property-market-overview</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

