<p><!--EndFragment--></p>','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/09/filipino-homes-xyza-yape-real-estate-agent-.png','views' => '45','category_id' => '15','published_at' => '2019-09-01 23:00:44','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '336','title' => '45th Office of Filipino Homes Opens in Banawa, Cebu City','slug' => '45th-office-of-filipino-homes-opens-in-banawa-cebu-city','content' => '<!-- wp:image {"id":4359} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/70034919_353129468903205_7635204387626811392_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4359"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Buying a home helps build a nation and FilipinoHomes helps you buy a home. The Cebu real estate market is too big and we can hardly accommodate all the buyers. With this, Filipino Homes now has its 45th office in Banawa, Cebu City.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4354} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/Filipinohomes-00145.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4354"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> Today "office" means an environment to which people dedicate most of their business hours. That is why Mr. Anthony Leuterio, CEO and Founder of Filipino Homes urges his brokers and leaders to open one for their team. There are 7 reasons why Broker teams need to open an Office;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} -->
<ol><li>Attracting New Aspiring Agents to build your team.</li><li>It Promotes team building</li><li>A venue for the team members to socialize and create a relationship with each other. (<em>thus promotes team building</em>)</li><li>Helps practice punctuality, most especially for team meetings</li><li>Practices accountability</li><li>Visibility and positive impression to clients and investors.</li><li> Facilitate and effectively market more professional-development opportunities to your team.</li></ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4358,4357]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-2 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/Filipinohomes-00545.jpg" alt="" data-id="4358" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4358" class="wp-image-4358"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/Filipinohomes-00445.jpg" alt="" data-id="4357" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4357" class="wp-image-4357"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Choosing to open an office as a Broker is not a light decision. It will represent one of your major expenses and it typically requires a lifetime commitment, that can be scary when you don\'t know where your business or team is leading you. But you can always consult resources to help you determine whether or not you are ready to open your own branch office. They\'ll surely enlighten you on what to prepare and what you need to prepare yourself in opening your own branch office of Filipino Homes. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4357} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/Filipinohomes-00445.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4357"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Congratulations again to Brokers Angela and Paul Abarquez for your new Filipino Homes Office in Banawa, Cebu City! </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/09/Filipinohomes-09.2019.png','views' => '43','category_id' => '14','published_at' => '2019-09-09 11:05:58','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '337','title' => 'Cebuano Broker, Stepped up his Digital Business Strategy with MIT Sloan School of Management','slug' => '4362-2','content' => '<!-- wp:image {"id":4363} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/70166914_10215198988870791_2368599361945862144_o-1024x791.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4363"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT) Sloan School of Management awarded Mr. Anthony Gerard O. Leuterio, a Cebuano, CEO, and founder of Filipino Homes and a lead broker of Leuterio Realty and Brokerage, as he completes their Executive Program "Digital Business Strategy: Harnessing Our Digital Future" this month of September 2019. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4364} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/69720365_353129415569877_1288841783412785152_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4364"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Despite busy schedules and frequent out of town and out of the country trips to manage his team and business, Mr. Leuterio never stops learning to stay ahead and on top of the game. He is also the first Filipino to complete this course offered by MIT. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4365,"align":"right","width":311,"height":311} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="alignright is-resized"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/12472790_10206159008036920_4967849496496967928_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4365" width="311" height="311"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>&nbsp;"This certificate means so much not to me, but to my business partners who trust in my valuable inputs as their source of knowledge in the complex world of real estate! All that I have learned I will generously give to those who believe in our vision and mission to change the real estate service landscape! It has been a difficult few months navigating business, training commitments, NATCON preparation, business expansion, personal life, all at the same time." - says Anthony Leuterio</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Digital Credential&nbsp;<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://l.facebook.com/l.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.credential.net%2Fwndq4tvn%3Ffbclid%3DIwAR17TLBTcP-ccmM2fyxs5h5dk1Lws4WExyLq0wRaPWwwHXE1abJXc4e0Bis&amp;h=AT0_TmdY6XQR6e_y5C61Gq7nlVWxk-A87V_BGv2vu08x6pWBFdJFTpr_8YvSuzA0-Vmp2Ku7mtzp6p-IEuwRZsvJumFWUGRSBSAJ1ZpS72KqASbAQGPOjRKT8iq6VeKmSmtwmkejDb0XAsNRcMfn8QjoV88aODAjDuTJyOrZYGsaVX8raKjJ2NoVlLR-QFRcddylarrE_ecQYqm0ipbH5d2TeHrFdTce4cyK_SIpowaNuwxnksba7hrt45tKy4aTXpAwMOgIDdXQoAmbs_cVtcHFBHFFH--AlgzNbyigacSCXv4AREQwmP8rp-_cKy9jb9dFmvaqsb5Q7oZkAF5-oON50EuyQ-svCvNwXPzcje3rJ-qk3Sy4dQNqm-fnX1Tmxjxa8JxYJQAweQprr2QUbxt3Mq79K638dUAnSnL09ngmYknRDu_SryIM3dZlLqhVFq8mqYrapuJPz68T34xyN6yCoWeggDo5jihBL-CsDgNfPU1zpGYSO5jCzybTjCJCdlKH-jyg8BBEDbigMhleQp4pD-YKIrlKtlxels9J" target="_blank">https://www.credential.net/wndq4tvn</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Mr. Leuterio also completed "Disruptive Strategy Programme" of Oxford Digital Marketing last May 13, 2019, developed by SAID Business School University of Oxford. [See credentials here:  <a href="https://www.credential.net/l82a4cdg">https://www.credential.net/l82a4cdg</a> ]</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/09/Cebuano-Broker-Stepped-up-his-Digital-Business-Strategy-with-MIT-Sloan-School-of-Management-1.png','views' => '47','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2019-09-13 16:50:46','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '338','title' => '3 Major Updates In Metro Manila We Should Look Forward To','slug' => '3-major-metro-manila-updates-to-look-forward-to','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Metropolitan Manila commonly known as Metro Manila or simply Manila is  a number of interlocking cities in close proximity to each other. Metro Manila has 12.8 million in population in the 2015 census and is predicted to have a population of 20 million by 2020. Besides the growing population of this highly urbanized area, here are the newest updates and what we can look forward to in Metro Manila!<br></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>Implementation of Rail and Road Expansion Projects﻿</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4393} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/CLLEX-2-BBB.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4393"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The implementation of rail and road expansion projects in the south allows the growth and development of the southern regions. These infrastructure projects includes Muntinlupa – Cavite Expressway (MCX), Light Rail Transit (LRT) 1 Cavite Extension, and Cavite – Laguna Expressway (CALAx). his will allow easier and faster transport from Metro Manila to Cavite and other neighbouring provinces. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>Construction of Metro Manila Subway begins﻿</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4394} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/MMS_VMapawall-1024x578.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4394"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> After 45 years since a Metro Manila subway was first proposed in 1973, the construction of the Philippines\' first intercity underground railway officially started Wednesday, February 27, 2019. The Metro Manila Subway is a 35-kilometer line that will operate from Mindanao Avenue in Quezon City to the Ninoy Aquino International Airport in Pasay City. It is estimated to accommodate around 370,000 passengers daily and fully operational by 2025. The project would be funded by the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) through an overseas development assistance loan with a projected cost of P356.96 billion. <br></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>Manila Bay Rehabilitation﻿</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4395} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/before-after-1024x576-1024x576.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4395"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Government initiated the rehabilitation of Manila Bay came after Boracay island underwent a 6-month rehabilitation, with President Rodrigo Duterte warning establishments along the body of water to comply with environment regulations or face closure.&nbsp; The Manila Bay rehabilitation, which experts said would take years to fully rehabilitate. Environment Secretary Roy Cimatu appealed to over a hundred city and town mayors of cities and towns surrounding the bay to clean up "esteros" or waterways in their respective areas connected to the Manila Bay. The environment chief also reminded local government units of the Ecological Solid Waste Management Act of 2000 that requires local officials to be responsible for waste segregation and disposal in their respective localities. Aside from the cleanup, relocation of informal settlers is also part of the Manila Bay rehabilitation. While cleanup efforts of Manila Bay\'s shore free of garbage is underway, its waters continue to be hazardous for swimming as its level of fecal coliform remains high. But it is a promising development on the clean-up drive of the once-pride of Manila, the Manila Bay.<br></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Being the busiest place of the country with several business centres, main government offices, and residential areas sprouting around, infrastructures like these will be a big help to those living in the metropolitan.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/05/Your-Condo-View-–-Enjoy-it-While-You-Can-2.png','views' => '49','category_id' => '16','published_at' => '2019-09-15 00:00:45','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '339','title' => 'Your Condo View – Enjoy it While You Can','slug' => 'your-condo-view-enjoy-it-while-you-can','content' => '<!-- wp:image {"id":4382} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/1-bedroom-condo-for-sale-in-maribago-cebu-1024x538.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4382"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Downtown condo living, complete with easy access to transit, shopping, a short walk to work, no maintenance yard and best of all, the view. It was the birds-eye view of the city, the mountains, and the breathtaking sunset that sold you on the place – no one mentioned it was only temporary.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>What happens when the view that came along with your 33 story condominium disappears because a neighboring building is built only 18 feet away? That is what happened to a condo owner when he purchased a unit in the downtown Cebu building in 2008.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4383} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/condo-2671021_1280-1024x698.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4383"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>He realized that other condos were scheduled for nearby developments, but at the time, the height restrictions limited the number of floors of an adjacent building. The rules were changed and a 34 story condo was constructed right next door. Which eliminating he\'s view, sunlight, and privacy. Whose responsibility was it to inform the new tenants that the city regulations had changed? According to city requirements, the developer and the adjacent property owners should be notified; however, future tenants are on their own to discover these new developments.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4387} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/2-2.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4387"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>New construction does not automatically assume the condo owner will lose their view. Different areas of the city have different separation requirements based on density. Some areas require no separation whereas others mandate a minimum of 60 to 200 feet.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Potential buyers cannot depend solely on their realtor or developer for zoning information. A bit of research before purchasing their property may save some nasty surprises down the road. Here are some areas to consider: </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} -->
<ol><li>Get as much information as possible from the developers regarding nearby proposals for developments, zoning restrictions and whether they have invested in air rights for the surrounding real estate to protect views.</li><li>Visit the city planning office and look up the zoning laws for the nearby sites.</li><li>Look up the addresses for any project applications and add your name and email address to the notification list for changes or new developments.</li><li>Speak to the city planners about possible changes to the existing zoning laws.</li><li> Let your comments be heard at design review hearings about future projects. </li><li>Spend the extra money to hire a land-use lawyer to complete this due diligence on your behalf.</li></ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>I know the suggestions are quite a handful for someone who simply wanted to start their own investment. If you are that critical about the view and all, you may consider checking on these things though for your peace of mind. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/09/Your-Condo-View-–-Enjoy-it-While-You-Can.png','views' => '50','category_id' => '27','published_at' => '2019-09-27 10:25:47','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '340','title' => '4 Steps To Real Estate Investing Success!','slug' => '4-steps-to-real-estate-investing-success','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Real estate investing is always good and sometimes it\'s red hot. When it\'s hot dozens of real estate seminars begin rolling across the country and thousands of people spend thousands of dollars for investing education. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It\'s startling to learn that of all those thousands of eager folks who attend these seminars only about 5% buy even one investment house. Why? The real estate gurus sell the "sizzle" and make profiting from real estate sound easy. The truth is that it\'s simple, but not easy. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here\'s a quick plan that will enable anyone to begin building financial independence. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4401} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/dilapidated-house-1024x576.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4401"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There are basically four steps to investing in single family homes: </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>1. Buy homes below full market value. </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Yes, people really do sell homes for less than the home\'s full value. The key is to understand that most home owners will only consider a purchase offer that is all cash and within 5% to 10% of their asking price. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The successful investor learns to find financially distressed home owners who have no choice but to sell for less than market value. They have lost their job or been suddenly transferred; they been living beyond their income; the family has been overwhelmed with medical bills and, the likes. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Those are examples of motivated sellers. They have to sell and they will accept something other than a conventional, all cash offer. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>2. How do you find motivated sellers? You work at it! Like any business it is important to develop a little marketing plan.</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> One that is simple, yet very effective, is the one that was proven 75 years ago by the Fuller Brush company; door to door sales. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You are selling your skill as a home buyer to people who must sell. Your are there when they need you and you have the skill to help them solve at least part of their problem. With door to door prospecting you will learn more and buy more homes quicker than any other method. However, most people just won\'t walk door to door for three or four hours per week. OK, there are other ways. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can watch public notices for the announcement of foreclosure sales. Meeting with a home owner right after they\'ve received a notice that they are about to lose their home allows you to deal with a very motivated seller. Other public notices that provide buying opportunities include probate, divorce and bankruptcy. You can follow the Homes For Sale listings in your local newspaper or Internet site. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can call the names found in these notices or, and this is the least time consuming, send a postcard expressing your interest in buying their property. It will produce buying opportunities, just not as many as personal contact. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>3. After you\'ve found a motivated seller you must understand how to frame offers that provide benefits for both you and for the home owner. </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A good real estate investor quickly learns that this is not a business of stealing property, but of solving problems in a way that benefits the seller. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The home owner is in a tight spot of some kind and you can save them from public embarrassment and, in most cases, give them at least a little cash to get a new start. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>No investor can afford to leave cash in every deal. No one but Bill Gates has that much available money. You must use creative techniques like, leases, option and taking over mortgage payments. Little or no cash is needed for those deals. You can find plenty of reasonable priced educational material on those subjects in book stores or on EBay. The same education that seminars sell for thousands of dollars. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>4. You make your profit when you buy! Never make a purchase until you\'ve carefully determined exactly how you will get to your profit. </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you hold it as a long term investment will the monthly rental income more than cover the monthly mortgage payment? Will you sell the deal to another investor for fast cash? Will you do some fix-up and sell the property for full value? Will you quickly trade it for a more desirable property? Have a plan before you buy. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There you have four steps that even a part-time investor can execute in three to four hours per week. What\'s the missing ingredient? Your determination and perseverance. If you will unfailingly follow the plan for a few months you will be well on your way to financial independence.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If these steps is too much for you, contact a Filipino Homes agent in you area and let them deal with things listed above for you. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Real estate investing is always good and sometimes it\'s red hot. When it\'s hot dozens of real estate seminars begin rolling across the country and thousands of people spend thousands of dollars for investing education.','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/09/Your-Condo-View-–-Enjoy-it-While-You-Can-3.png','views' => '40','category_id' => '9','published_at' => '2019-09-27 22:00:43','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '341','title' => '3 Tips to Staging the Outside of Your Home Like a Pro','slug' => '3-tips-to-staging-the-outside-of-your-home-like-a-pro','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Are you considering putting your house up for sale, but not sure where to start? Afraid it will take too long to sell, or that you won’t get the price you want? Think about “staging” your home, or in other words, setting the scene for immediate buyer interest in your property. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>To be really effective, you need to look at both the outside and the inside of your home. <strong>Here are 3 tips to get you started with the outside of your home:</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4407,4408]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-2 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/camella-homes-fatima-model-for-sale-cavite-1024x614.jpg" alt="" data-id="4407" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4407" class="wp-image-4407"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/92bb50f1ec1b9dc7e1bd872a37d3e9fc.jpg" alt="" data-id="4408" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4408" class="wp-image-4408"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} -->
<ol><li>Go stand on the street to see what clients see when driving up to the house. Be aware that any negative impressions they get outside the house (landscaping not maintained or non-existent, peeling paint, etc.) is just going to make them think that the house itself has not been well taken care of. So even if you have spent the time and money to fix up the interior, it would all be wasted if the clients get a bad first impression as they drive up to the house.<br></li><li>Next, step outside your front door and close the door; then stand on the stoop and look around for 5 minutes. While the realtor fumbles for keys and tries to figure out how to open the door, the clients are standing behind and looking around. So what are they seeing? Dead plants, old Halloween decorations in the middle of January, cobwebs?  Again, not a good first impression! <br><br>It’s definitely worth it to take some time and clean it up. Want to go a step further? Try a new coat of paint or some new furniture or accessories.<br></li><li>Don’t forget the backyard. While that might not be part of the potential buyers’ first impression experience, you still should make sure it’s in the best condition possible. Pull up weeds, water plants, do some sweeping (if that’s applicable in your case) and maybe even purchase new furniture or accessories (plant pots, bird houses, etc.)</li></ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And the biggest tip of all? Imagine yourself as a potential buyer looking at your property for the very first time. What impressions are you getting? Would YOU buy your house? What would you like to see changed before you put an offer on your house?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4409,4410]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-2 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/uptown_cagayan_de_oro_house_and_lot_xavier_estates_119537.jpg" alt="" data-id="4409" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4409" class="wp-image-4409"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/Ventura_residences_II_plain-1024x742-1024x742.jpg" alt="" data-id="4410" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4410" class="wp-image-4410"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And don’t worry about spending several thousand pesos to get your house ready to sell – you’ll get it all back when your house sells. Proper staging helps you sell your house in a shorter time and at the price you want.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Are you considering putting your house up for sale, but not sure where to start? Afraid it will take too long to sell, or that you won’t get the price you want?  Here are three tips to help ensure that won\'t happen to you.','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/09/Your-Condo-View-–-Enjoy-it-While-You-Can-4.png','views' => '43','category_id' => '15','published_at' => '2019-09-29 00:09:07','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '342','title' => 'Selling A Lot With Mother Title','slug' => 'selling-a-lot-with-mother-title','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href="http://localhost:3001/mother-title-mean/">Mother Title </a>is the original title of ownership of a land or property. It’s the first registered title of the property and the document that traces the origin of the property. Most of the time, it is called the ancestral lot. <br><br>As the property changes hands from one owner to another through various transactions like gift deed, inheritance, etc., these needs to follow through the transfer document.&nbsp;However, some property owners fail to file and process the transfer of property hence leaving the property bearing the Mother Title.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>How to sell a property or a portion of it with a Mother Title?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Do not consider selling a piece of property and the person when you are not the rightful owner of if. Even if you are the legal heir to the owners of the land, if the title is not under your name - you are not the owner of the property. &nbsp;If the the person listed on the title is deceased, the first thing you need to do is check with every last heir to the title.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Now if the owner of the property is your maternal grandmother and she has two children including your mother. It means that in instance that your mother is deceased, you and your siblings is next in line to her share. But a portion of it is also a share of your mother\'s sibling. If both your aunt and mom are deceased but you have cousins from your aunt. It means that they also have the right to the property.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can contact every heir and ask for their interest in the property. If they are willing to sell or not. An extrajudicial settlement of estate can be done by compiling signatures that they allow and sign off their rights to the property in question. They can file an adverse claim on the property and have that annotated on the title so that before the property or any portion of it is sold, they need to sign off a Deed of Absolute Sale, and receive their percentage of the proceeds. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It can be a tedious task to go over all your relatives, especially if they leave far away from you or even abroad but it is the only way for you to sell the property or your share/portion of it.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/05/Your-Condo-View-–-Enjoy-it-While-You-Can-1.png','views' => '64','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2019-09-29 22:03:57','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '343','title' => '3 Tips to Staging the Inside of Your Home Like a Pro','slug' => '3-tips-to-staging-the-inside-of-your-home-like-a-pro','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Are you considering putting your house up for sale, but not sure where to start? Afraid it will take too long to sell, or that you won’t get the price you want? Think about “staging” your home, or in other words, setting the scene for immediate buyer interest in your property. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>To be really effective, you need to look at both the outside and the inside of your home. Here are 3 tips to get you started with the inside of your home:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>1. De-clutter</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4414,4415]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-2 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/1140-declutter-room-after.imgcache.reva43832160e154c93a8ba68ae0f74f52d-1024x588.jpg" alt="" data-id="4414" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4414" class="wp-image-4414"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/white-family-room1.jpg" alt="" data-id="4415" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4415" class="wp-image-4415"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is one of the most important things you can do. It might be easier to think of de-cluttering like this – you’re moving anyway, so why not start packing now?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Pack up everything you don’t need and store the boxes out of sight in the garage (or consider temporarily renting a small storage locker). </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>2. Organize your closets </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4416,4417]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-2 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/custom-closets-reviews-closet-doors-near-me-and-cabinets-simply-organized-bathrooms-extraordinary-las-vegas-systems-inc-nv-magnificent.jpg" alt="" data-id="4416" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4416" class="wp-image-4416"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/download.jpg" alt="" data-id="4417" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4417" class="wp-image-4417"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Put similar colors together, pants together, skirts together, shirts together etc. Why? Because it will make the closets look bigger. (Really.) An organized closet appears bigger, and you want your closets to look as spacious as possible.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>3. Make your home look like a model. </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4418,4419]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-2 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/1539198575376.jpeg" alt="" data-id="4418" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4418" class="wp-image-4418"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/elsie-kitchen-a-beautiful-mess.jpg" alt="" data-id="4419" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4419" class="wp-image-4419"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You want to de-personalize as much as possible so potential buyers can imagine themselves and their own belongings occupying the space in your house. That means minimizing – putting away everything you don’t need or use. Clear off kitchen counters as much as possible – stash all those appliances you don’t use, and put miscellaneous small clutter in a few attractive baskets or boxes</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And the biggest tip of all? Imagine yourself as a potential buyer looking at your property for the very first time. What impressions are you getting? Would <strong>YOU </strong>buy your house? What would you like to see changed before you put an offer on your house?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And don’t worry about spending several thousand pesos to get your house ready to sell – you’ll get it all back when your house sells. Proper staging helps you sell your house in a shorter time and at the price you want.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Are you considering putting your house up for sale, but not sure where to start? Afraid it will take too long to sell, or that you won’t get the price you want?  Here are three tips to help ensure that won\'t happen to you.','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/09/Your-Condo-View-–-Enjoy-it-While-You-Can-5.png','views' => '48','category_id' => '15','published_at' => '2019-09-30 23:00:40','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '344','title' => 'Winning The Commercial Real Estate Game','slug' => 'winning-the-commercial-real-estate-game','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The game of commercial real estate can be won in many ways.  It’s more of an essay test than true or false.  There’s definitely more than one correct answer.  A large percentage of the world’s millionaires earned their wealth through real estate investment.  While nothing is a sure thing, real estate offers many opportunities for the savvy investor.  Whether you want to build wealth or simply maintain it, there are several strategies that you can implement to get where you want to be.  Where should you begin?  You don’t want to put your hard earned money into a dead market.  You want to protect what you’ve worked so hard for.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Let’s look at a few of the more popular methods for investing in commercial real estate. </h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Buy and Hold Strategy</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4430} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/833b0d79d1aace.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4430"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>One of the more classic approaches to commercial real estate investment is <strong>the buy and hold strategy</strong>.  In this maneuver, you buy property that is valued at a fair price.  It may be a few miles away from town or outside of a development area.  You then simply hold the land for a number of years.  While you do this, the city comes to you.  Developments are going up all around you.  Yours is the last piece of raw land around and every developer in the state wants a piece of it.  You, the genius entrepreneur, then sell the land for millions more than you pay for it.  It couldn’t get much better than this.  While this is obviously the ideal scenario, it can work like this.  As you know, land is the only commodity that they don’t produce any more of.  Therefore the price of your land will eventually go up.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>While there is a great deal of money to be made in this sort of venture, it can take a long time to mature.  This is great for someone who has a big chunk of money that they want to sit on for a few years.  There is no set time limit as to how long it will take you to win.  You basically have to go with your gut on this one.  Should you sell it five years from now for twice what you paid for it?  What if in year six, SM or AYALA wants to move in and pay you 10 times what you paid?  There is really no way to know.  You have to get out when you feel the time is right. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> Look for the signs around you.  If the trends of development in your area are coming towards you, wait for a while.  If you’ve had the land for ten years and the city that you just knew would be the next boom-town turned into a ghost town, you might want to get out.  This strategy can produce a great return and it’s a pretty passive source.  You don’t really have to do anything except buy the land and wait.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>The Rehab Market</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Another great way to invest in commercial property is through <strong>the rehab market. </strong> This is where you <em>buy a run-down property that needs a lot of work done.  You fix it up with a little elbow grease</em>.  Then after it’s up to par, you put it back on the market and make a tidy profit.  This is a growing segment in the real estate industry.  There is a definite need for this as property is always getting old.  The most important thing to remember in this type of venture is you make your money when you buy the property, not when you sell it.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You must find properties that are undervalued.  If you overpay, no matter what you do to the property, you’ll still come out behind.  You need to find properties that need a lot of work.  This has the highest potential for a great return.  Don’t get involved with a property that just needs a new coat of paint and the yard mowed.  This will not make you any money.  In fact, you’ll most likely lose money.  Stick with the properties that need the most TLC and you’ll come out on top.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Quick Turning a Property [Flipping]</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":246} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/foreclosure.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-246"/><figcaption><a href="http://localhost:3001/5-simple-guidelines-purchasing-foreclosed-house/">http://localhost:3001/5-simple-guidelines-purchasing-foreclosed-house/</a></figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Another popular strategy is that of <strong>quick turning a property</strong>.  This involves finding distressed properties.  You search for a great deal that is extremely undervalued.  This could be a property that is facing foreclosure or a bankruptcy.  Someone may take a significant cut in the price in order to get out fast.  This can benefit you, the investor, greatly.  You then take the distressed property and put it back on the market quickly.  Since you don’t have to sell quickly, the property will get fair market value and you can make thousands of dollars in profit.  As with rehabbing property, the key is finding cheap properties that you know are worth more.  This is where all of the money comes from in this type of transaction.  If you know the market, you can do very well with this type of deal.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Invest in an already Profitable Property</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For investors that already have a good sum of money saved up, there is another form of investment that is very appealing.  Professionals who want another steady income can <strong>invest in expensive real estate that is already a great performing asset.</strong>  This could be a luxury apartment complex or condos or any number of properties.  The investor then takes over the cash flow that is generated by the subject property.  They will most likely leave the existing property management in place and just take the steady cash flow.  This is a great form of investment for those that are looking for a <em>passive source of income from their investment</em>.  People who would benefit from this are usually very busy and already successful in some other walk of life.  They understand that the only way to create wealth is through multiple sources of income.  Diversification is the key.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Whichever method of commercial real estate investment you decide on, make sure it’s the right one for you.  Consider all the factors carefully before making your decision.  Just remember that you too can succeed in real estate investment.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'There’s definitely more than one correct answer.  A large percentage of the world’s millionaires earned their wealth through real estate investment.  While nothing is a sure thing, real estate offers many opportunities for the savvy investor.  Whether you want to build wealth or simply maintain it, there are several strategies that you can implement to get where you want to be.  Where should you begin?','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/10/Filipinohomes-.png','views' => '38','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2019-10-01 23:15:28','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '345','title' => '3 Pitfalls to Avoid When Playing in the Real Estate Game','slug' => '3-pitfalls-to-avoid-when-playing-in-the-real-estate-game','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So you’ve seen your umpteenth infomercial with the guy in his neatly pressed button-upped white T-Shirt grinning ear to ear waving his rock-solid no-money-down rags-to-riches real estate investment course for 3 easy payments of a gazillion pesos (but only if you call now) and now you are thinking, "wow this looks like a great deal, I better get it fast before the special offer expires." You notice how there’s always a special offer? Anyway, I am not saying this guy isn’t telling the truth, however regardless of which course or school of thought you buy into there are several key areas that one must avoid when engaging in any real estate related transaction.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Pitfall Number 1: Don’t Overpay!</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The whole point in investing is to find properties that are undervalued. How does one find out what is undervalued versus overvalued? Without getting into technical details, the bottom line is you need experience. Yes much like shopping for anything else, real estate is essentially one of the highest ticket items in the shopping center of life. It’s advisable to stick with one market, perhaps the one closest to you in proximity as a starting off point. Through your experience and asking the right questions, you will eventually have a feel for the pulse of the market you are looking after, and of course identify what is considered a good buy.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Pitfall Number 2: Know the Market</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Yes, you are actually going to have to do more work! This part is really common sense though, but executing it where the beauty and the payoff comes in. How do you make money in real estate? The most basic way is to <em>buy low and sell high</em>. So from the first step, you have identified general trends in the value of homes, and are pretty good at spotting undervalued homes. Assuming you acquire that home, you may want to profit from it by selling it off to someone else for a higher price. How can you do this? Well there are many ways. For one, most markets appreciate in value over time so if you want a longer term approach that will work. Making upgrades to the property will automatically raise the price of the home as well. Think in terms of what the market wants, not what you personally want. You aren’t the one buying it; you are trying to sell it to someone else for a higher price than you bought it.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Pitfall Number 3: Know Your Budget</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It may be a fine philosophy to go through life on a whim, but real estate is serious business, and thus diligent financial planning and budgeting is critical to your success. Don’t worry you don’t need to be a finance geek, however you need to be disciplined and know your budget from the onset, or you may be finding you are learning that you need to make certain renovations or upgrades, and didn’t anticipate it going over to a certain cost. Think ahead as to what is needed before actually going forth with investing in real estate.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Don\'t rush blindly towards real estate investing. Here are 3 big pitfalls to avoid.','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/09/Filipinohomes-1.png','views' => '36','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2019-10-02 23:00:51','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '346','title' => 'A Beginner\'s Guide to Real Estate Investing Strategies','slug' => 'a-beginners-guide-to-real-estate-investing-strategies','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you\'re thinking about investing in real estate to make money, you need to first determine your financial goals. Do you need to make money quickly, invest for your children\'s college fund, or build wealth for your retirement? Once you determine your financial goals, you need to decide which type of investing strategy works for you.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>Make Money in Real Estate - Fast Cash Strategy</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://cashloan.com.ph/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/Cash-Loan-Teachers-Philippines.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you\'re low on cash, get started by finding a bargain house and selling the contract to another real estate investor. Join a real estate investing club to find investors willing to pay you for finding good deals. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>Make Money in Real Estate - Income Property Strategy</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4448} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Rental-Income.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4448"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you want to increase your monthly income, look for income property that returns a positive net income from month to month. Start with single family house. Look for a bargain below market value. Fix up the house to generate top rental income. Find houses that will rent for more than your mortgage payment. You may need to go out from your home area to a location that supports this type of return on your money. You can\'t pay Php 560,000 for a home with a mortgage of Php 4,500 that only rents for Php 3,500. You might start with a home for around Php 560,000 that rents for Php 6,000. You will need good credit to get a loan with good interest rates. In a few years, your rental income should go up. Many real estate investors enjoy thousands of pesos each month generated by income property.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>However, some investors don\'t like dealing with tenants and prefer to make money in other real estate ventures.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>Make Money in Real Estate - Investment Property Strategy</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://thumbor.forbes.com/thumbor/960x0/https%3A%2F%2Fspecials-images.forbesimg.com%2Fdam%2Fimageserve%2F1077636488%2F960x0.jpg%3Ffit%3Dscale" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you want to make money focusing on profits, investment property offers a different strategy. Instead of worrying about rental income, look for property that you can transform and sell or property that will appreciate significantly over time. Besides fixing a house up, you can transform a property by changing it. For instance, some investors buy apartment buildings and turn them into condominiums. Many investors speculate in land and make money by holding the land until new development in the area increases the value.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Examine your financial situation along with your long term goals. You can get started by flipping properties, move onto income properties, and then make larger profits with investment properties. You might end up using a combination of all three strategies to make money investing in real estate.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'What\'s the difference between income and investment property? If you\'re thinking about investing in real estate to make money, you need to first determine your financial goals. Do you need to make money quickly, invest for your children\'s college fund, or build wealth for your retirement?','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/10/Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape.png','views' => '49','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2019-10-03 23:00:50','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '347','title' => '6 Key Factors Successful Vacation Rental Owners Always Use','slug' => '6-key-factors-successful-vacation-rental-owners-always-use','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you are going to spend money advertising your vacation rental property on vacation rental websites, you want to make sure it is a success. Here are 6 things you can practice which will help ensure you receive the most "bang for the buck".</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>1. SET RENTAL RATES APPROPRIATELY </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4453} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Rental-rates-increase.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4453"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you want your vacation property to rent, you must be realistic, optimistic, but not greedy! Set realistic rental rates for your property and ensure that the rates are correct on the site(s) your listing and regularly reviewed as the market changes. Search for comparable properties ("comps") in the same location as yours. Only charge a premium if your property has some distinct features. And, be willing to discount your property on occassion as needed. In this business, if you lose money for a week long rental, you can\'t make that up!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>2. CHECK E-MAIL REGULARLY </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4454,"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/656716-how-to-disable-image-loading-in-email.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4454"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> When using an internet vacation rental property website such as <a href="http://www.rent.ph">Rent.ph</a>, airbnb, booking.com or agoda, remember your users. They are typically Internet "savvy" and probably check their e-mails frequently. Especially if they have requested some info. Also, be sure your phone number is listed on sites that allow you to as sometimes people choose to just call you directly, so be sure to check phone messages.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>3. RESPOND IMMEDIATELY </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4455} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/email-1024x546.jpeg" alt="" class="wp-image-4455"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Vacation goers usually see a few properties that are of interest to them and then contact those owners. The faster you respond, the better chance (most of the time) you have of winning them over. There have been times I have rented properties in the past and because it took an owner 24 hours to respond, I had already chosen another property. A timely and efficient response gives the renter confidence that the rental experience will follow suit.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>4. YOUR LISTING SHOULD BE ACCURATE AND COMPLETE </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4456,"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/home-for-sale.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4456"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Be sure that your listing details are kept up to date and are complete. Review your online listing frequently to be sure that your contact information are up-to-date. Also, be sure that it is accurate on the description of your property and its amenities. This will help you with repeat customers, but will also keep you out of trouble with rental contracts or laws in regards to such things.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>5. GREAT PHOTOS </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4457,"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/product-photography-lead-image_800x.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4457"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> It is true what they say, "a picture speaks a thousand words". Remember, renters are considering staying at your rental based (most of the time) solely on your pictures and your word. The more pictures to help them be comfortable with the decision, the better. Here is how I look at it. If you were going to buy a used car, would you do so over the Internet without a good look at the outside/inside of the vehicle, the engine, etc. Not exactly the same, but you get the picture. The more pictures and the prettier, the better. Be sure to have pictures of your rental amenities such as a pool, the beach, a mountain view, the lake or a golf course - these are top vacation rental sellers!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>6. BOOST YOUR EXPOSURE </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4458} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/post-312_SGkxqRn-1024x682.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4458"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There are many "hot spots" for vacationers throughout the world. Before we owned property, my family used to head to Camiguin every year, usually twice. There are thousands of vacation rental properties in the Camiguin, Misamis Oriental Beach area. In areas like this, boost your exposure by getting to the top of your sites search engine. If it costs you 2000, 5000, even 10000 to do so but that gets you one extra rental a year, that makes it more than worth it.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Share this article if you find it useful. For more rental properties in the Philippines visit <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="http://rent.ph (opens in a new tab)" href="http://rent.ph" target="_blank">http://rent.ph</a>. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'If you are going to spend money advertising your vacation rental property on vacation rental websites, you want to make sure it is a success. Here are 6 things you can practice which will help ensure you receive the most "bang for the buck".

1. SET RENTAL RATES APPROPRIATELY - If you want your vacation property to rent, you must be realistic, optomistic, but not greedy! Set realistic rental rates for your property and ensure that the rates are correct on the site(s) your l...','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/10/Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape-1.png','views' => '52','category_id' => '15','published_at' => '2019-10-08 00:00:28','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '348','title' => 'Another Filipino Homes Office Opens in Escario Cebu City','slug' => 'another-filipino-homes-office-opens-in-escario-cebu-city','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes Office in Escario Cebu City officially opens today, October 8, 2019. The 46th office opened at  Unit 101 G/F Atelier Residences, Juana Osmeña St. Ext.,  Camputhaw, Cebu City.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4476,4477]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-2 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/71854678_10215374826786629_7733479011795337216_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4476" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4476" class="wp-image-4476"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/71891826_10215374826226615_5527245274952499200_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4477" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4477" class="wp-image-4477"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The new office will be the home office of Team X-Factor in Cebu City. Lead by Real Estate Broker Mark Anthony Villarubia together with his wife Melissa Villarubia.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4478,4479,4480]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/71824358_10215374831746753_7205557810912821248_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4478" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4478" class="wp-image-4478"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/71792145_10215374830506722_6295895338326687744_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4479" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4479" class="wp-image-4479"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/72646679_10215374829626700_8023048069123670016_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4480" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4480" class="wp-image-4480"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The event was graced by guests and team members of Team X-Factor and also with the CEO and Founder of Filipino Homes Anthony Gerard O. Leuterio and his lovely wife Ms. May Leuterio. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4481]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-1 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/72124913_10215374827866656_6931360871033602048_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4481" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4481" class="wp-image-4481"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Congratulations again Team X-Factor for your new office and Good Luck in your team expansions. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4482,4483]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-2 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/71660076_10215374828586674_4800651862053224448_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4482" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4482" class="wp-image-4482"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/72651726_10215374828386669_4733487008859553792_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4483" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4483" class="wp-image-4483"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The new office will be the new training home for all new real estate agents and brokers under REB Villarubia. REB Villarubia also manages team in  Pangasinan, Metro Manila, Ormoc, Bohol, Dumaguete, Cagayan de oro City, Davao, Gensan, Iloilo, Bacolod, San Carlos, Cebu City. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '46th Filipino Homes Office in Escario Cebu City officially opens today, October 8, 2019. ','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/10/71891826_10215374826226615_5527245274952499200_n.jpg','views' => '47','category_id' => '14','published_at' => '2019-10-08 12:52:46','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '349','title' => 'Words That Will Save You Big Time In Repairs or Renovation Jobs','slug' => 'words-that-will-save-you-big-time-in-repairs-or-renovation-jobs','content' => '<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[3689,3669,2586]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2018/08/loans_home_improvement_hero_16_9.large_.medium_quality-1024x576.jpg" alt="" data-id="3689" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/how-to-increase-your-propertys-value/loans_home_improvement_hero_16_9-large-medium_quality/" class="wp-image-3689"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/01/pexels-photo-1409215-1024x681.jpeg" alt="" data-id="3669" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/moving-into-your-new-home-stress-free-hacks/pexels-photo-1409215/" class="wp-image-3669"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2018/04/Cutting-Plywood-Subfloor-With-Circular-Saw-185001220-56a4a04b5f9b58b7d0d7e37f.jpg" alt="" data-id="2586" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/10-worst-first-time-homebuyer-mistakes/cutting-plywood-subfloor-with-circular-saw-185001220-56a4a04b5f9b58b7d0d7e37f/" class="wp-image-2586"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Power Tip!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Have you ever wanted just one phrase that you could say at the right time, and it save you hundreds, or thousands of pesos?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When it comes to getting the best price from contractors, plumbers, electricians, HVAC techs, you name it, there is a simple phrase that often works like magic in reducing your costs.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>These specialties are always competing for work. However, if you ask any of them they will likely tell you that they are extremely busy!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>They might be. They might not.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There\'s a game going on here. They need to appear very busy so their services are in demand and support the prices they will ask for. At the same time, you need to appear to be willing and able to get prices from many sources. (Don\'t just make it appear that way, get multiple bids whenever it\'s practical!) It\'s a balance that must be struck.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The good part is that now you know the game…so play both sides since you know what the other side\'s play.<br>
How to turn the tables</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Have an idea of what the job will cost. Just a ball park idea will do.</li><li>If you are told something that you think it high, ask why so high. There might be more to it than you know. The reason for the high price might be reasonable. Discuss alternatives.<br>(For example, if you electrician points out that the breakers you need are especially expensive, ask if he\'s got any used breakers that are still in good shape.)</li><li>Then use the magic phrase...</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here it is…</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote {"className":"is-style-large"} -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-style-large"><p><strong>"Is that your final and best price?"</strong></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Very often the person you are talking to will squirm a bit at this point. They are having to think…</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>"Is my price fair?"<br><br>"Am I over pricing something here?"<br><br>"Can I save this customer some money?"<br><br>"Does the customer know something I don\'t?"</p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>While your contractor/laborer thinks about this, don\'t say a word.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>I\'ve experienced many reactions from<strong><em> "That\'s the best I can do"</em></strong> to<em><strong> "If you give me the job, I\'ll knock it down to…" </strong></em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Often I\'ve gotten a range of options that could save me money. More often than not, it saves my money!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It works like magic if:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>They understand that they aren\'t your sole source of the service they provide </li><li>They know you are willing to wait for the best price </li><li>They know you aren\'t a push over </li><li>They know you might be a source of future income</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>But, it will work like magic when properly applied. In my own experience, I can point to many thousands of pesos of savings using this simple question.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"backgroundColor":"pale-pink"} -->
<p class="has-background has-pale-pink-background-color">We like to save money by keeping prices for services reasonable, true enough. At the same time, I advocate and approach of "don\'t let anyone get hurt." If you award a job to someone and it winds up costing them more than expected, I help that person out. I don\'t want someone to lose money on a job and leave with a bad taste in their mouth and never want to do work for me again. Be aware of when someone gets hurt. That said, watch out for those that claim to get hurt with each job.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Try out that phrase today. It works in many situations…not just repairs or renovation of a property, but in just about any competitive environment.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'A power tip from Bruce W. Ford!  Use these magic words and reap more profits from your repairs or renovation of real estate investments!','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/10/Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape-2.png','views' => '42','category_id' => '28','published_at' => '2019-10-08 23:00:37','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '350','title' => '3 Ways Renters Lose Money','slug' => '3-ways-renters-lose-money','content' => '<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Are you still renting a home or apartment for yourself or your family? </h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If so, you\'re losing money. Think about these three ways you lose money by renting:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>1. You\'re paying for someone else\'s mortgage payment. </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You\'re missing out on the appreciation that the property gives to the landlord. Appreciation is a term used in accounting relating to the increase in value of an asset, which means in real estate terms, added value to the property. Over the past five years, houses appreciated significantly, making many new real estate investor multimillionaires.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>2. Renters don\'t get to freeze their monthly housing expenses like home buyers can. </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Of course, many home buyers get mortgage payments with adjustable interest rates and their payments go up over time. However, these payments will not go up over the long term like rising rents. Just think about how much an apartment costs today compared to ten years ago. A two bedroom apartment in Cebu City (for example) leases for 15,000 pesos today. The exact same apartment rented for 3,000 in 1996, when it was brand new. Home buyers who had low monthly payments in 1996, who did not refinance their mortgage, enjoy low payments and don\'t have to worry about rising rents.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>3. Renters don\'t benefit from tax advantages. </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Home owners get income tax deductions. Tax deductions for interest costs, for instance, save tax payers thousands of pesos. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"backgroundColor":"pale-cyan-blue"} -->
<p class="has-background has-pale-cyan-blue-background-color"><strong>Emotional Satisfaction of Home Ownership</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Besides losing out on making money with real estate, renters don\'t get the same satisfaction of home enjoyment that benefits home buyers. Many landlords won\'t allow you to paint your walls in colors that you desire. Also, you won\'t feel like fixing up the property with custom window coverings and you get little say in flooring materials. Because you can\'t make your personal statement, you won\'t feel like you\'re HOME as much as home owners who feel emotionally connected to their property.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"backgroundColor":"luminous-vivid-amber"} -->
<p class="has-background has-luminous-vivid-amber-background-color"><strong>How to Buy Your First Home</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong><em>The biggest barrier to home ownership is often accumulating funds for a down payment. </em></strong>People think they have to have thousands of pesos for a down payment.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>In the Philippines, <a href="http://localhost:3001/pre-selling-properties/">pre-selling properties</a> or projects have down payments that are payable by installment, stretched from 12 up to 60 months depending on project and developer. You do not really have to shell out a big amount of cash at once. </li><li>Developers also offer discounts for those who can pay for the down payment one time. With today\'s mortgage finance plans, you may be surprised to find out how much of a home you can afford with payments similar to what you currently pay in rent. </li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You may have to go out of the major metropolitan areas to buy a home. That\'s why so many people commute in neighboring Municipalities. Affordable housing costs much less in outlying areas. But so do the rents. If you\'re renting an apartment for P 15,000  in Cebu City, you could buy a 1.5 Million Pesos home in Lapu-Lapu City or Consolacion with a mortgage of as low as 8,000 pesos per month. I purchased a home in January of 2015 and my mortgage payment, for a 23 sqm new home (it\'s a socialized condo) in Cagayan de Oro, costs less than 3,500 pesos per month. With my tax savings, I pay even less than renting a small apartment or pad closer to downtown Cagayan de Oro. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If these amounts sound high to you, check your local area. Perhaps your monthly rent is only 10,000 pesos and houses cost less than 2M. <a href="http://www.filipinohomes.com">Talk to a  realtor</a> and see how much of a home you can afford.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"align":"center","backgroundColor":"light-green-cyan"} -->
<p style="text-align:center" class="has-background has-light-green-cyan-background-color">If you\'re renting, make one of your priorities to buy your own home.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Are you still renting a home or apartment for yourself or your family? If so, you\'re losing money. Besides losing out on making money with real estate, renters don\'t get the same satisfaction of home enjoyment that benefits home buyers. If you\'re renting, find out how to to buy your own home.
','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/10/Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape-3.png','views' => '44','category_id' => '16','published_at' => '2019-10-09 23:00:21','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '351','title' => 'Advice on Picking a Real Estate Agent','slug' => 'advice-on-picking-a-real-estate-agent','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph {"customBackgroundColor":"#fc8d8d"} -->
<p style="background-color:#fc8d8d" class="has-background">The ideal agent is not always the one with the most sales under his or her belt, or the most years on the job. The ideal agent is one who listens to you, is easy to get along with, and has the tools and skills to address your unique situation. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Every home buyer is different. Some have credit issues. Some are buying from out of state. Some need help selling their current home in addition to buying a new one. Just as buyers have different needs, real estate agents have different skills and specialties.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":3831} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/03/img_2115-1024x683.png" alt="" class="wp-image-3831"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here\'s how to find the agent who\'s right for you:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>1. Ask friends and family for agent referrals.</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> Nobody knows you as well as your friends and family do. So they\'re often in the best position to recommend an agent who is well-suited for your needs. You can also trust a referral from friends or family more than one that comes from a stranger.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>2. Talk to multiple agents.</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> I once saw a statistic that 84% of home buyers choose the first real estate agent they contact. This means one of two things. Either most people are choosing wisely the first time, or they\'re just rushing into things without shopping around. Probably a little of both.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4364,4357,4350,4266],"columns":4} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-4 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/69720365_353129415569877_1288841783412785152_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4364" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/4362-2/69720365_353129415569877_1288841783412785152_n/" class="wp-image-4364"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/Filipinohomes-00445.jpg" alt="" data-id="4357" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/45th-office-of-filipino-homes-opens-in-banawa-cebu-city/filipinohomes-00445/" class="wp-image-4357"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/Filipinohomes-002.jpg" alt="" data-id="4350" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/43rd-filipino-homes-office-opens-in-lapu-lapu-city/filipinohomes-002/" class="wp-image-4350"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/img_4637-1024x684.jpg" alt="" data-id="4266" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/filipino-homes-opens-its-42nd-office/img_4637-jpg/" class="wp-image-4266"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You don\'t have to exhaust yourself interviewing agent after agent, but at least talk with two or three to see who you\'re most comfortable with (which leads to the next point).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>1. Consider the vibe factor.</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> Professional expertise is an important criterion when choosing a real estate agent. But interpersonal skills are equally important. After all, you\'ll be working with this person anywhere from 2 to 12 months, so it helps to get along with them. We all have unique personalities, and that\'s the way it should be. But when working with someone professionally, if helps if their personality "meshes" well with your own.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>2. Ask how they hunt.</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> When deciding on a real estate agent, ask how they search for homes. Some agents have their own preferred listings that they favor. But you want what\'s best for you, not what\'s best for your agent. You\'re paying them, right? So make sure the agent is willing to search high and low to find the best home for you. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>3. Read paperwork carefully.</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This advice is heavily used for a reason. It\'s critical that you examine all documents during the home buying process, and that includes your agent agreement. At some point during the relationship, your agent will probably ask you to sign an agent agreement. Basically, it just means that if the agent shows you a particular property, your purchase of the property should be credited to that agent. In most cases it\'s a simple, just be sure to read it carefully and ask questions.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'The ideal agent is not always the one with the most sales under his or her belt, or the most years on the job. The ideal agent is one who listens to you, is easy to get along with, and has the tools and skills to address your unique situation.','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/10/Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape-4.png','views' => '59','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2019-10-10 23:00:21','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '352','title' => '"Successful real estate investor tips"','slug' => 'successful-real-estate-investor-tips','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Becoming a successful real estate investor requires being able to find good real estate investment deals and put them together. Your job is not to become a closing attorney, a management expert, or a repair person. Use professionals! </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You must learn how to appraise and find the true value of real estate this information will help you make better investment decisions. <a href="http://www.filipinohomes.com">Realtors</a>, appraisers, and banks determine what a property is worth by looking at comparable sales usually three to five sales of similar property that has recently sold in the same neighborhood. You must be able to do the same.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Getting a list of comparable prices of properties bought or sold (and when it sold) for the neighborhood you need information about, and asking active real estate investors in your area what the market is like will be helpful and making a better investment decision.                                                                                                                                                                      </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>What is the ideal market for investing? </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There is no such thing as an ideal real estate market for investing. It tends to be more difficult to find bargains in rising markets if the market keeps rising the probability of selling the property quickly for a large profit increases. In contrast but when property values are falling more bargains become available. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You need to be able to assess the true value of properties based on when you expect to sell. Your purchase must be made at a good enough discount to allow for a profitable sale at a later date.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Leverage </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leverage is very important for investors because the less cash you put down on each property the more properties you can buy. If the properties go up in value your rate of return goes up. However, if the properties go down in value and you have a lot of debt on the property this can result in negative cash flow. [<a href="https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/leverage">Leverage Meaning</a>]</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Since real estate is generally cyclical negative cash flow is only a short-term problem. It can be handled if you have other income or cash reserves. This makes "Nothing down" investing very helpful to protect against negative cash flow for high leverage investors. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you are a long term real estate investor leverage will work in your favor if the markets in which you invest appreciate in the long run and your income from the properties can pay for most of your monthly debt.                                                                                                            </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Strategies to limit the risk</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>To limit risk to become educated in your local real estate market first by understanding the large scale trends from global down to national regional and specific neighborhoods. Learn about target neighborhoods with the help of successful real estate investors in your area along the way. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href="http://localhost:3001/can-an-ofw-buy-a-property-while-outside-the-philippines/">Real estate investors</a> can help you interpret market indicators such as the average length of time houses have been on the market this month versus last month or last year. This information will help you make better investment decisions.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Exit strategies </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It is important not to guess the future of a local real estate market you need to have a clear plan in mind when purchasing a property. As a  real estate investor, you must know exactly how you will exit the property before you buy it. And have a backup plan or two in case the first course of action doesn\'t work. You must know your market and your plan before you begin to invest. [Source: <a href="http://www.TrumpUniversityCo.com">Trump University]</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Real estate investor tips','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/10/Copy-of-Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape.png','views' => '42','category_id' => '15','published_at' => '2019-10-15 13:15:04','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '353','title' => 'An Agents Guide To Personal Safety','slug' => 'an-agents-guide-to-personal-safety','content' => '<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>A major concern for real estate agents and brokers is personal safety.</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> Many times the agent/broker is working alone in showing a property, having an open house, or manning the model house in a new subdivision. Some personal safety issues should include:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"backgroundColor":"luminous-vivid-amber"} -->
<p class="has-background has-luminous-vivid-amber-background-color">At the first meeting of a client, have them meet you at the office. Get as much personal information as possible. A copy of the driver’s license is a good start not only for safety but also for the client database.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4511} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/69505151_3366126646730762_1441543989797847040_n.jpg" alt="An Agents Guide To Personal Safety" class="wp-image-4511"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"backgroundColor":"very-light-gray"} -->
<p class="has-background has-very-light-gray-background-color">If you have a strange feeling about the client, don’t show property by yourself. Ask a co-worker to go with you; at worst you might have to give him/her a share or incentive if the deal is closed. If you are manning an open house and you feel that you might be in danger, leave the property and call for help. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"backgroundColor":"pale-pink"} -->
<p class="has-background has-pale-pink-background-color">Always drive your own car to the property as this might be the only means of escape. On the way make notes on the type of car, color, and license plate number and call the office with this information. Once at the property make sure your car is not blocked and you have an easy escape (no backing-up).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"backgroundColor":"luminous-vivid-orange"} -->
<p class="has-background has-luminous-vivid-orange-background-color">As you are showing the property, always have the client lead you; this allows the property to present itself and keeps the client where you can see them.  Make sure they sign-in on the registry or logbook and if the office does not have the information on the client, give the information to them. Your office/broker/leader will know you are with a client at this time.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"backgroundColor":"light-green-cyan"} -->
<p class="has-background has-light-green-cyan-background-color">Keep your keys and cell phone close and easy to access. If need be, keys can be an effective weapon of surprise. If you have a handbag, keep it with you at all times or locked in the trunk of your car. Know the property, not only do you look more professional, but safer; your client does not know all of the exits as well as you should. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4508} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/4ae07fbddfd18e00d7e589d89aa957d3.jpg" alt="An Agents Guide To Personal Safety" class="wp-image-4508"/><figcaption>From: Pinterest</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"backgroundColor":"pale-cyan-blue"} -->
<p class="has-background has-pale-cyan-blue-background-color">Take a few self-defense classes, as a few minutes head starts out of the property means the difference in a safe escape and being trapped. Take the first chance to escape and don’t try to talk your way out; keep your advantage. The more time you spend in a dangerous situation means a diminished chance of a safe exit.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"backgroundColor":"very-light-gray"} -->
<p class="has-background has-very-light-gray-background-color">Let the client see that you have contacted your office and the office knows who you are with. It is also a good idea to have a secret code for trouble such as “<em><strong>Pick up dog food</strong></em>” when you don’t have a dog. It is also a good idea to set your phone to vibrate as your client will not know if you are calling or if you are receiving a phone call.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"customBackgroundColor":"#deafe7"} -->
<p style="background-color:#deafe7" class="has-background">If there is an emergency your office can play a vital role. Make sure they have the make of your car, its color, and license plate. If you are using a different car that day, make sure they have their description as well. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"customBackgroundColor":"#99cee5"} -->
<p style="background-color:#99cee5" class="has-background">Make sure your office has your schedule for the day and that you check in on each appointment. If that is not possible, at least contact your Broker or Manager. If you are hosting an open house, make sure you have a registry book for clients to sign in. See if you can also include the client’s car description. Tell the client it is just in case they get a parking ticket and you want to document the reason for parking there or some other reason.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4509} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/maxresdefault-1024x576.jpg" alt="An Agents Guide To Personal Safety" class="wp-image-4509"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"customBackgroundColor":"#f9b2e1"} -->
<p style="background-color:#f9b2e1" class="has-background">Make sure you have your Broker,  family members and reliable friends in your quick dial list. Remember to add "911" and your local police hotline too. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Many of these points may already in practice for the profession. Look at these procedures as also a safety concern. These safety tips should become second nature with little thought to be truly effective. Being an <a href="http://localhost:3001/advice-on-picking-a-real-estate-agent/">agent </a>means sometimes you will work alone. With today’s cell phones and e-mail capabilities and some careful thought, you will be safer and will be in contact with help quicker.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'A major concern for agents/brokers is personal safety. Many times the agent is working alone in showing a property, having an open house, or manning the model house in a new subdivision.
','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/10/Copy-of-Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape-1.png','views' => '50','category_id' => '10','published_at' => '2019-10-15 23:02:55','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '354','title' => '47th Filipino Homes Office Opens','slug' => '47th-filipino-homes-office-opens','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The 47th <a href="http://www.filipinohomes.com">Filipino Homes</a> Office officially opens today. The first office of Filipino Homes Cagayan de Oro City at Capistrano Cruz Taal is now managed by  Leo Ross Torralba, Rose Torralba, and  REB Elpie Maghanoy,  of Leuterio Realty CDO. It officially opened today October 18, 2019. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4528,4548]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-2 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/fb_img_15713878900506965800498099314658.jpg" alt="" data-id="4528" class="wp-image-4528"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/74224140_721375861674973_85553815801036800_n-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4548" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4548" class="wp-image-4548"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The mother and son tandem is currently leading the most productive Team of Leuterio Realty Cagayan de Oro for the year 2019.  This office plays an important role in growing and adding individuals to its team, the idea of organized workspace with dependable infrastructure and room to fit a budding workforce shouldn’t be so easily dismissed. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4529} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/img_20191018_111408251825015409901106.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4529"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Anthony Gerard Leuterio, CEO of Filipino Homes and his lovely wife May Leuterio graced the event. They also lead the blessing and opening of the new Filipino Homes team office.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4530,4544,4545,4546,4547]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/img_20191018_1111004562933142106759494.jpg" alt="" data-id="4530" class="wp-image-4530"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73045516_418914951990041_8991520652720603136_n-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4544" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4544" class="wp-image-4544"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73375534_405227703737789_4700087706783318016_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4545" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4545" class="wp-image-4545"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/72459344_2411024679144938_3851719472687611904_n-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4546" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4546" class="wp-image-4546"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73018612_425976118059352_3856772806654033920_n-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4547" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4547" class="wp-image-4547"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Torralba\'s joined the Leuterio Realty &amp; Brokerage team last 2012. A celebratory thanksgiving lunch followed after. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4550,4532,4549,4531],"align":"center"} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery aligncenter columns-3 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73250905_512730552895280_1950175186883969024_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4550" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4550" class="wp-image-4550"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/img_20191018_1113317218490473420686212-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4532" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4532" class="wp-image-4532"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/72946427_424858964835431_4982242301939023872_n-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4549" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4549" class="wp-image-4549"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/img_20191018_1113275934840985180396959-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4531" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4531" class="wp-image-4531"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->','excerpt' => 'The 47th Filipino Homes Office officially opens today. The first office of Filipino Homes Cagayan de Oro City at Capistrano Cruz Taal is now managed by  Leo Ross Torralba, Rose Torralba, and  REB Elpie Maghanoy,  of Leuterio Realty CDO. It officially opened today October 18, 2019. ','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/10/74224140_721375861674973_85553815801036800_n.jpg','views' => '48','category_id' => '14','published_at' => '2019-10-18 15:12:19','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '355','title' => 'New World-Class Office Opens in Cagayan de Oro','slug' => 'new-world-class-office-opens-in-cagayan-de-oro','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leuterio Realty and Filipino Homes Cagayan de Oro\'s main office officially moved to their new world-class office at 2nd flr Tomas Saco Scapes last October 18, 2019. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4541,4540]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-2 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/fb_img_1571384846508364584979434862178-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4541" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/fb_img_1571384846508364584979434862178-jpg/" class="wp-image-4541"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/fb_img_15713848497303768735831471835524-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4540" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/fb_img_15713848497303768735831471835524-jpg/" class="wp-image-4540"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>"The CDO real estate market has grown so much that our previous office can no longer cope up with the rising demand, so we decided to move to a bigger one. Presenting, Worldclass Filipino Homes’ new main branch office in CDO. Come and visit us now!" said Anthony Leuterio.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4539} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/fb_img_15713848542544182736448592512073-1024x768.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4539"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Real estate agents from Bukidnon, <a href="http://www.filipinohomes.com/charmaine-xy-za-yape">Iligan City</a>, and Cagayan de Oro gathered and joined the blessing and opening of the new branch office. Partners from Bria Homes and Cebu Landmasters Inc also visited during the blessing of the new office in Tomas Saco Scapes. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4543,4542]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-2 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/fb_img_15713848600962977082317904215738-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4543" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/fb_img_15713848600962977082317904215738-jpg/" class="wp-image-4543"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/fb_img_15713848382032642777830917322642-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4542" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/fb_img_15713848382032642777830917322642-jpg/" class="wp-image-4542"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The new office was staged and dressed up by <a href="https://www.philstar.com/the-freeman/cebu-business/2019/08/01/1939614/filipino-homes-launches-construction-mgmt-firm">Filipino Homes Plus</a>. Filipino Homes Plus is a construction company of Filipino Homes. Partnered with the top architects and engineers in the country. For your future interior design and construction needs, contact a <a href="http://localhost:3001/filipino-homes-launches-digital-buy-and-sell-app/">Filipino Homes</a> agent to assist you.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4553,4554,4555,4556,4557,4558]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/72625511_481869206006648_6992867143469498368_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4553" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4553" class="wp-image-4553"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/72718609_438754416999794_209212005926567936_n-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4554" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4554" class="wp-image-4554"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/72754856_396556131023484_5811835812349739008_n-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4555" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4555" class="wp-image-4555"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73417764_442159659741243_5951045748341604352_n-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4556" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4556" class="wp-image-4556"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73321479_1143415355849723_7630886004169113600_n-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4557" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4557" class="wp-image-4557"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/72463424_397585127585646_9004062953657335808_n-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4558" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4558" class="wp-image-4558"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/10/Copy-of-Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape-2.png','views' => '46','category_id' => '14','published_at' => '2019-10-19 09:34:08','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '356','title' => 'Filipino Homes National Convention Opening Salvo 2019','slug' => 'filipino-homes-national-convention-opening-salvo-2019','content' => '<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4582,4583,4584]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/opening-salvo-LR-natcon-2019-8.jpg" alt="" data-id="4582" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4582" class="wp-image-4582"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/opening-salvo-LR-natcon-2019-1.jpg" alt="" data-id="4583" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4583" class="wp-image-4583"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/opening-salvo-LR-natcon-2019-2.jpg" alt="" data-id="4584" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4584" class="wp-image-4584"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In anticipation of the 3-day Filipino homes National Convention 2019 which commences this weekend in Cebu City, dozens of Filipino homes\' vehicles converged at the SM Seaside, yesterday, for an Opening Salvo. The whole day fun activity started with a motorcade and was followed with a blessing, mass, and a program held at the Madani BayEvent Tent. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<figure><iframe width="560" height="315" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/S2i2HxBSDSM" allowfullscreen=""></iframe></figure>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The event was well participated by Brokers and Agents of Leuterio Realty from different parts of the country. The majority of the attendees were from Cebu City. This is part of the 3 day National Real Estate Convention which will happen this October 26 to 28, 2019 at Waterfront Hotel Lahug Cebu City. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4585,4586,4587]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/opening-salvo-LR-natcon-2019-3.jpg" alt="" data-id="4585" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4585" class="wp-image-4585"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/opening-salvo-LR-natcon-2019-5.jpg" alt="" data-id="4586" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4586" class="wp-image-4586"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/opening-salvo-LR-natcon-2019-6.jpg" alt="" data-id="4587" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4587" class="wp-image-4587"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Over a thousand accredited brokers and agents of Leuterio Realty &amp; Brokerage are expected to attend the event. Registration and confirmation of attendees were closed last September 19, 2019. This is a special event for the highly productive and hardworking agents of Filipino Homes. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4588,4589,4590]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/opening-salvo-LR-natcon-2019-9.jpg" alt="" data-id="4588" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4588" class="wp-image-4588"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/opening-salvo-LR-natcon-2019-4.jpg" alt="" data-id="4589" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4589" class="wp-image-4589"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/opening-salvo-LR-natcon-2019-7.jpg" alt="" data-id="4590" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4590" class="wp-image-4590"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->','excerpt' => 'Opening Salvo LR Natcon 2019 Leuterio Realty & Brokerage','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/10/Copy-of-Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape-9.png','views' => '50','category_id' => '14','published_at' => '2019-10-21 13:27:38','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '357','title' => 'Earnest Money - What You Need To Know','slug' => 'earnest-money-what-you-need-to-know','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You include earnest money with an offer on a house to show the seller that you are serious about purchasing the house. It becomes part of the down payment if the offer is accepted, is returned if the offer is rejected, or is forfeited if you pull out of the deal for reasons other than those stipulated in the offer. A financing contingency is an example of the latter - if your offer was contingent on getting a loan, and you can\'t, you can cancel the contract and get your earnest money deposit back.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>How Much Earnest Money?</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The size of the earnest money deposit is up to you.You can write the offer with a thousand pesos deposit if you wish, and the agent still has to present the offer. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As an agent, to protect the owner of the property, I would usually require 50,000 to 100,000 pesos earnest money. The earnest money can be part of a downpayment of the buyer if he then pursues the purchase of the property. The buyer will have to give an offer to the seller or an intent to buy with the earnest money. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can also do a two-part deposit. You can make an offer with just 50,000  in earnest money, for example, but specify in the offer that this will be increased to 100,000 or more once the offer is accepted, or once when an inspection, appraisal or other contingency is met. This keeps your money from being tied up until you know that the seller is serious about selling to you. This will usually still be seen as a serious offer if the deposit is to be seriously increased at some point.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4522} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/triijqojsgqysgjaiubs.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4522"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>Who Gets The Earnest Money Deposit?</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Never give your earnest money check to the seller. The last thing you want is a seller trying to keep your money after you pull out of a deal because of financing problems, termite infestations or other valid contingencies in your offer. If the real estate office handling the sale has an escrow account, it should be safe to make the check out to the broker. Always give your deposit to a third party to hold.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Ask how they handle it too. I once had an offer rejected and then had to wait a week to get my money back. They told me that they had to wait for my check to clear before they could issue a check back to me. I prefer it when it is handled like it was on our recent home purchase. They just hold the check until the offer is accepted, and return or destroy it if the offer is rejected.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>How To Protect Yourself</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Things can happen, right? If you pull out of the deal for some unforeseen reason - one not included in the contract - you\'ll lose your deposit. However, the seller could also sue you for additional damages or even force you to buy the home. To protect yourself, have a clause in the offer that specifies the earnest money as "liquidated damages" if you are in default. The real estate agent can help with the language, but this basically means that if you need to default on the contract, the seller can\'t ask for more than what you have already included as earnest money.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you are a real estate agent dealing with a brokerage sale. It is a good practice to help protect the seller and the buyer through earnest money. It is like a reservation fee (if that would make it easier to comprehend) for brokerage listings where a buyer wants the property reserved to them for a period of time, with the intent to buy.  This will help the seller be confident to deal with the buyer and a strong indication for buyers that they are serious with their intent. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If they decide to continue the purchase of the property, it will be part of the full payment of the said property. However, if they choose to withdraw, depending on the clause and duration stated in the contract, you may not be able to get the earnest money anymore. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'An earnest money deposit is the norm when making an offer on a house, but how much should it be for, and who should hold the money? Here is what you need to know.','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/10/Copy-of-Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape-4.png','views' => '52','category_id' => '15','published_at' => '2019-10-21 23:00:58','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '358','title' => 'Condo Hotels in the Philippines: The Hottest Niche in the Philippine Investment Property market','slug' => 'condo-hotels-in-the-philippines-the-hottest-niche-in-the-philippine-investment-property-market','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Condo ownership in the Philippines is viewed to be the most unstable real estate unit. A lot of people have this understanding that owning a condominium is simply owning a piece of paper without having the physical lot in it. Contrary to what people believe, Condominium ownership in the Philippines is free-hold. This means it can be passed on to heirs and the ownership of the property is absolute. [Read: <a href="http://localhost:3001/condominium-act/">Condo ownership here</a>]</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4564,4565]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-2 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/b01d4401-6201-4760-9ee2-7c9d2485d116-725-438.jpg" alt="" data-id="4564" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4564" class="wp-image-4564"/><figcaption>Grand Tower Cebu City</figcaption></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/tambuli1.jpg" alt="" data-id="4565" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4565" class="wp-image-4565"/><figcaption>Tambuli Seaside Living Cebu</figcaption></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Anthony Leuterio of Filipino Homes and <a href="http://www.leuteriorealty.com">Leuterio Realty</a> said When the unit owners are not using the condo-hotel suite, the unit is put in the managed pool and rented out for them. The buyers have what is considered "hassle-free" ownership. The condo-hotel unit owners also benefit from having a professional onsite management company to handle marketing, booking of their room and general expertise that they bring to the table. If a problem should arise with their condo hotel unit, the management company will take care of it instead of the owner having to worry about it. This makes the traditional landlord-tenant issues a thing of the past.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The condo-hotel buyer sees the benefit of owning a vacation property that also has the potential to produce income for them. The typical condo hotel produces higher levels of income than the traditional vacation home (and fewer headaches), making it all the more appealing to buyers.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4566],"align":"center"} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery aligncenter columns-1 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/97524_14011815040018100049-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4566" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4566" class="wp-image-4566"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Developments such as the Lancaster Suites Manila Tower I was sold out in less than 18 months and the building was completed in the Summer of 2007. We also have the Tambuli Seaside Living Phase 1 in Mactan Cebu that is already operational, and we have more in Cebu that is currently preselling. Condo hotels are different from traditional condos because they are sold "turn-key". Clients initially purchase the standard condo unit and then when the time comes for interior ‘fit-out’ they can avail of the in-house Condotel package of furniture and furnishings for the unit. This means buyers do not have to worry about hiring a designer or contractor to come in to finish out the unit. Everything is included from linens, dishes, pillows, and etc</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4567,4568,4569]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/97524_14090513420021891045-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4567" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4567" class="wp-image-4567"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/de940befb153f4f5c87052b62e638ffb-1024x588.jpg" alt="" data-id="4568" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4568" class="wp-image-4568"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/97524_14090513460021891239-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4569" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4569" class="wp-image-4569"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leading the way in the Metro Manila condo hotel market is Pacific Concord Properties Lancaster Brand of condotel investments. Pricing for condo hotels can range anywhere from Php 5,000,000 up to Php 85,000,000 for Penthouse suites. Of course, the pricing depends on location, views, and types of finishes. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4570,4571]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-2 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Citadines_Cebu_City_Studio_Bed_750x490.jpg" alt="" data-id="4570" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4570" class="wp-image-4570"/><figcaption>Citadines Baseline Cebu</figcaption></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Citadines_Cebu_City_1BR_Living_Dining_750x490.jpg" alt="" data-id="4571" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4571" class="wp-image-4571"/><figcaption>Citadines Baseline Cebu</figcaption></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Citadines at Baseline development is currently enjoying the great success of its clientele with property appreciation for its initial buyers. <a href="https://filipinohomes.com/p/thesuitesatgorordo/naSb=">The Suites at Gorordo</a> in Cebu,<a href="https://filipinohomes.com/devpartners/condominium/tambuli-seaside-living/eg==/dXU="> Tambuli Seaside Living</a> Phase 2, <a href="http://localhost:3001/10-highly-recommended-projects-to-invest-in-at-mactan-cebu/">Aruga </a>in Cebu, <a href="https://filipinohomes.com/devpartners/condominium/astra-centre/dg==/fHM=">One Astra Place </a>by Cebu Landmasters and One Paragon Place in Davao City is currently on preconstruction selling and looks set to sell out within the next few months. These projects offer clients the choice of Studio, One, Two and Three Bedroom suites that all have kitchen facilities as regular residential condo units. This type of project is very appealing to <a href="http://localhost:3001/can-an-ofw-buy-a-property-while-outside-the-philippines/">overseas Filipino workers</a>, simply because it\'s hassle-free.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If this interests you, contact your Filipino Homes agent today for your option. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Condo hotels have quietly become one of the hottest areas of the real estate market in the Philippines. The condotel concept provides buyers the benefit by owning a property in a hotel environment that they can use for themselves, and take advantage of the amenities not normally found in typical residential condominium developments','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/10/Copy-of-Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape-5.png','views' => '40','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2019-10-22 23:30:22','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '359','title' => '“Renting Back” After Your Home Is Sold','slug' => 'renting-back-after-your-home-is-sold','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Sometimes it’s helpful to sell your home before you really want to move. This often happens when you are having a new home built, but aren’t sure of the completion date. Is there any way you can sell your home so you’re sure of the funds available for the new purchase, but continue to live in your old home until construction of the new one is complete. Yes, there is the renting back strategy.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Enter the Lease-Back or <a href="http://www.rent.ph">Rent</a>-Back Agreement</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4576} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Copy-of-Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape-7.png" alt="" class="wp-image-4576"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The particulars of this strategy vary from location, but in the strong seller’s market we’re experiencing, buyers will often agree to let the seller stay in the home for a period of time as long as rent is paid. In a competitive situation, the buyer willing to do this will often have the winning bid even though there is another offer as high as his.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4575,"align":"left","width":307,"height":204} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="alignleft is-resized"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/shutterstock_50097079-2ec9cc-630x420.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4575" width="307" height="204"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The agreement covering the situation states the length of time the seller will remain.  It can be done with a specific date named or wording that allows the seller to remain up to a specific date with the possibility of her moving sooner. The amount can be a fixed figure paid out of the proceeds of a settlement or a monthly amount or a daily amount. It is usually, but not always, tied to the amount of the mortgage payment under the buyer’s new loan. Sometimes there is a deposit against damage, sometimes not.  There is usually a clause saying the seller will hold the buyer harmless for any damage to himself or his property which occurs after the sale is completed and before the seller moves. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The attorney who draws up your contract offer can create such an agreement. If you’re using online forms, you should be able to find one for this situation. If you’re working with a real estate broker, he or she can handle it for you too.   </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4577,"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Copy-of-Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape-8.png" alt="" class="wp-image-4577"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>An Example</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>I’ve recently seen a very pleasant example of this idea in action.  I had a listing that was sold a year ago with this kind of situation. The owners of the unit were out of the country. The house was up for rent by the owner. 6 months after a couple got interested in the listing and decided to buy the property earlier than expected. The problem of the owner is that the house was being leased for a year. And they haven\'t consumed their 1-year contract yet. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The couple made an offer that is quite below her asking price. The owner countered with a proposal that she “rent back” for a period of “up to” a certain date (a date beyond the contract date of the lessor) in exchange for a modest flat sum to be paid to the buyer at settlement. The total rent-back period was less than 10 months. The rental payment of the lessor will be paid directly to the new owner (the couple), but they cannot do <a href="http://localhost:3001/words-that-will-save-you-big-time-in-repairs-or-renovation-jobs/">renovations </a>or any other movement within the property until the lessor finishes its lease contract. The couple really wanted the home, so they accepted the counteroffer. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Another win, win situation was created. The seller/owner was able to comply with the lease contract and the couple got the property. If you find yourself in a situation similar to either the widow or the young couple, perhaps you can work out a similar solution.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Sometimes it’s helpful to sell your home before you really want to move. This often happens when you are having a new home built, but aren’t sure of the completion date. Is there any way you can sell your home so you’re sure of the funds available for the new purchase, but continue to live in your old home until construction of the new one is complete. Yes, there is with the renting back strategy.','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/09/Copy-of-Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape-6.png','views' => '41','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2019-10-23 23:00:40','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '360','title' => 'Leuterio Realty NATCON 2019 Opens','slug' => 'leuterio-realty-natcon-2019-opens','content' => '<!-- wp:image {"id":4597} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Filipinohomes-LRNATCON2019.jpg" alt="Leuterio Realty Natcon 2019" class="wp-image-4597"/><figcaption>#LRNatcon2019 #Filipinohomes</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leuterio Realty &amp; Brokerage officially open the National Real Estate Convention today October 26, 2019, at Waterfront Hotels &amp; Casino Lahug, Cebu City.  One thousand active and highly productive real estate agents and brokers of Leuterio Realty gathered today from the different regions of the Philippines. Day one is a series of talk and overflowing raffles prizes. It is a day of learning and honoring. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4598} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73285480_2476838849228880_7127414046352998400_n.jpg" alt="Leuterio Realty Natcon 2019 Eduardo G. Ong" class="wp-image-4598"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The father of Philippine Real Estate, <a href="http://localhost:3001/father-of-philippine-real-estate/">Dr. Eduardo G. Ong</a> shared the current status of the Real Estate Industry in the Philippines and it\'s future predictions. "The journey of highly professionalized real estate services begins with Filipino Homes", said Dr. E.G. Ong. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4599,4600,4601]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73074811_2476802252565873_2162899015769784320_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4599" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4599" class="wp-image-4599" /></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73200797_2476800482566050_7962732937147842560_o-1024x683.jpg" alt="" data-id="4600" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4600" class="wp-image-4600" /></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/72906283_10159689117153018_7150351400801665024_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4601" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4601" class="wp-image-4601" /></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Dr. Ong also shared the Philippines ranked among Asia\'s 10 fastest growing economies. Consumer power, remittances from overseas workers and an influx of call centers had given it that status, raising hopes for easing rampant poverty. To attract more capital, the government is building $171 billion worth of infrastructure by 2022, one of Pres. Duteret\'s priorities in office. By the same year, the government aims to cut poverty from 22 percent to 14 percent of the population. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4603} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73018193_2476669022579196_1028466181436080128_n.jpg" alt="Leuterio Realty Natcon 2019" class="wp-image-4603"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And for the real estate agents and brokers to succeed in this industry we must "Learn. Re-Learn and Earn", said Dr. E.G. Ong. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4602} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73268914_2476874725891959_4606700291541172224_n.jpg" alt="Leuterio Realty Natcon 2019 Any Manalac" class="wp-image-4602"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href="http://iamrealestate.ph">Mr. Alejandro "Andy" Mañalac,</a> Co-Founder of the Havitas Development Corporation, "Mr. Shark" himself shared statistics and studies of the international real estate industries. He also expressed how noble it is being a real estate agent. Their studies in Havitas Development Corp showed that there is a growing real estate market due to the growing tourist influx in the country and the growth of the buying market.  The international buyers in the country are also making a mark in the real estate industry. Chinese buyers are the highest spenders and China has shown to be growing faster as a tourist market - which is partly due to the rising market for Philippine Offshore Gaming Operators ("POGO") business in Metro Manila. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4604} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/75247485_2476929739219791_2050079648062111744_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4604"/><figcaption>FILIPINO HOMES delegates to the National Association of Realtors Convention in San Francisco USA.</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The high influx of tourist markets also increases the estimated housing backlog in the Philippines. The government and private sectors are trying their best to meet these housing requirements in the country. This means there is a great opportunity for real estate developers and agents and brokers to help decrease the said real estate backlog. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4605,4606,4607]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/75322631_2476797769232988_4941112290658222080_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4605" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4605" class="wp-image-4605" /></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/72982473_2476797739232991_4748882070023962624_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4606" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4606" class="wp-image-4606" /></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/74456376_2476802579232507_9172824927525404672_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4607" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4607" class="wp-image-4607" /></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In the rising modernization and adaption to technologies, Mr. Mañalac shared that the role and the relationship built by an agent and client cannot be replaced. Empathy, compassion, and care are things that modernization doesn\'t have. Thus, "being an agent is (a noble and )a respectable career" , Andy Mañalac. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4609,4610,4611,4614,4613,4612,4608]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/75439371_2476837135895718_3965369298091769856_n.jpg" alt="Leuterio Realty Natcon 2019" data-id="4609" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4609" class="wp-image-4609" /></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/72603911_2476838025895629_1907235199075221504_n.jpg" alt="Leuterio Realty Natcon 2019" data-id="4610" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4610" class="wp-image-4610" /></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73375675_2476839559228809_7370378404962500608_n.jpg" alt="Leuterio Realty Natcon 2019" data-id="4611" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4611" class="wp-image-4611" /></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/74610069_2476839379228827_3863023594682449920_n.jpg" alt="Leuterio Realty Natcon 2019" data-id="4614" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4614" class="wp-image-4614" /></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73515635_2476839525895479_1315756303347351552_n.jpg" alt="Leuterio Realty Natcon 2019" data-id="4613" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4613" class="wp-image-4613" /></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73214056_2476837925895639_4390110760160722944_n.jpg" alt="Leuterio Realty Natcon 2019" data-id="4612" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4612" class="wp-image-4612" /></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/75223813_2476837125895719_5478032349968990208_n.jpg" alt="Leuterio Realty Natcon 2019" data-id="4608" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4608" class="wp-image-4608" /></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Mr. Anthony Gerard O. Leuterio, the founder of Filipino Homes and lead broker of<a href="http://www.leuteriorealty.com"> Leuterio Realty &amp; Brokerage</a> also gave a power training and forecast of the future of real estate in the Philippines. His recently completed course at <a href="http://localhost:3001/4362-2/">MIT Sloan University </a>helped him equip himself in the latest and future trends of the real estate industry. He strongly emphasized the Value creation of each agent to its customers, to the organization and to the society. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4616,4617,4618,4619,4620]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/72726314_2477027202543378_7717236471979048960_n.jpg" alt="Leuterio Realty Natcon" data-id="4616" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4616" class="wp-image-4616" /></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73296316_2477027095876722_9122785199862579200_n.jpg" alt="Leuterio Realty Natcon" data-id="4617" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4617" class="wp-image-4617" /></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/74662467_2477011305878301_6946892413373775872_n.jpg" alt="Leuterio Realty Natcon" data-id="4618" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4618" class="wp-image-4618" /></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/74911471_2476875022558596_8783906378923114496_n-1.jpg" alt="Leuterio Realty Natcon 2019" data-id="4619" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4619" class="wp-image-4619" /></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73056408_2476838082562290_1913594173034856448_n.jpg" alt="Leuterio Realty Natcon" data-id="4620" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4620" class="wp-image-4620" /></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It was a very powerful, meaningful and emotional night to remember. Overflowing cash prizes and high-end mobile phones were also raffled off. A night of dancing and celebration capped the night of Day 1. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Follow <strong>#LRNatcon2019 </strong>and <strong>#FilipinoHomes</strong> for real-time updates. LR Natcon 2019 will happen from October 26 to 28, 2019. For more photos <a href="https://www.facebook.com/filipinohomes/">click here. </a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Leuterio Realty & Brokerage officially open the National Real Estate Convention today October 26, 2019, at Waterfront Hotels & Casino Lahug, Cebu City','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/10/Filipinohomes-LRNATCON2019.jpg','views' => '46','category_id' => '14','published_at' => '2019-10-26 16:10:04','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '361','title' => 'Filipino Homes Delegates Safely Arrived USA','slug' => 'filipino-homes-safely-arrived-usa','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes delegates safely arrived in the USA last November 6, 2019. 60 to 70 members of the top-performing agents and brokers of Leuterio Realty &amp; Brokerage will be attending the<a href="https://www.conference.realtor/"> National Association of Realtors Convention </a>starting November 8 to 11, 2019 at the Moscone Convention Center in San Francisco California.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4625} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/fb_img_15730994745678307112002986936179.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4625"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Over 70 agents and brokers of Filipino Homes flew in from the Philippines to attend the annual event. 66 countries all over the world participated in this annual event. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4626} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/fb_img_15730994368505378389280400449685.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4626"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4627} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/fb_img_15730994710949041317295628576722.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4627"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For real-time social media, updates follow #Nar2019  #Filipinohomes</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/11/Copy-of-Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape-10.png','views' => '42','category_id' => '10','published_at' => '2019-11-06 15:43:25','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '362','title' => 'Filipino Homes Recognized by NAR','slug' => 'filipino-homes-recognized-by-nar','content' => '<!-- wp:image {"id":4635} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/73415919_10215614918468771_7146092528410820608_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4635"/><figcaption>Filipino Homes Delegates </figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes, a 100% Filipino owned company was recognized by the National Association of Realtors during the Global Alliance Advisory Board Meeting at Park Central, Metropolitan III, Level 2 San Francisco, California USA. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4644,4643,4642]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/img_6033-1024x768.jpg" alt="filipino homes ruby hamilton jenny acebes xyza yape" data-id="4644" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4644" class="wp-image-4644"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/img_6032-1024x768.jpg" alt="filipino homes ruby hamilton jenny acebes xyza yape" data-id="4643" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4643" class="wp-image-4643"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/img_6035-1024x768.jpg" alt="filipino homes ruby hamilton jenny acebes xyza yape" data-id="4642" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4642" class="wp-image-4642"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In attendance are the Global Ambassadors, Global Coordinators, and domestic and international guests come together for global presentations and the NAR global volunteer program and year-end updates. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4638} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/74304261_10214432533878926_1797544075092557824_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4638"/><figcaption>From Left to Right: Ms. Vicky Silvano,  Global Real Estate Liaison; Filipino Homes team Ruby Hamilton, Charmaine Xy-Za Yape, REB Jennifer Acebes and Filipino Homes founder Mr. Anthony Gerard O. Leuterio.</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The purpose of the gathering is to provide guidance in the operation of NAR\'s Global Networks program. Lead by Chairperson Yin Bihr, GRI, CIPS, CRS.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4647,4646,4645]} -->
<ul class="wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/img_6036-1024x768.jpg" alt="filipino homes ruby hamilton jennifer acebes xyza yape" data-id="4647" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4647" class="wp-image-4647"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/img_6037-1024x768.jpg" alt="filipino homes ruby hamilton jennifer acebes xyza yape" data-id="4646" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4646" class="wp-image-4646"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/img_6038-1024x766.jpg" alt="filipino homes ruby hamilton jennifer acebes xyza yape" data-id="4645" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4645" class="wp-image-4645"/></figure></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>During the Global Coordinator Reports, Filipino Homes lead by Mr. Anthony Gerard O. Leuterio was recognized for having the most numbered registered delegates for the NAR 2019 Convention, with a total of 70 participating registered brokers and agents.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4640} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/75418270_10214432533518917_8986464874917789696_n-1-1.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4640"/><figcaption>Filipino Homes Team with <strong>Evangeline Alzona Yi</strong><em><strong>a</strong></em>, CIPS, CREBA-NAR Chairperson and other International Realtors</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Tomorrow, November 8, 2019, is the official opening of the National Association of Realtors Convention and Expo. The learning sessions will also start from November 8 until November 11, 2019. [<a href="https://www.conference.realtor/event-type/education-sessions/">View NAR Schedule here</a>].</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/11/Copy-of-Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape-11.png','views' => '42','category_id' => '10','published_at' => '2019-11-08 09:14:15','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '363','title' => 'Continuing Professional Development for Real Estate Held in Davao City','slug' => 'continuing-professional-development-for-real-estate-held-in-davao-city','content' => '<!-- wp:image {"id":4821,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/78058579_10215730114068589_3995787751130660864_o-1.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4821"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes has always partnered with the Professional Regulation Commission (PRC) Accredited Speakers like Dr. Ed Ong, Ph.D., REC, REA, REB, and Engr. Eleanor Liganor, REB, to ensure that Leuterio Realty &amp; Brokerage agents comply with the<strong> </strong><a href="https://www.prc.gov.ph/cpd-irr-page"><strong>CPD or Continuing Professional Development</strong>&nbsp;(<strong>CPD</strong>) </a> requirements set by the <a href="https://www.prc.gov.ph/">PRC [Professional Regulation Commission]</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4822,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/77259128_10215730115228618_1405376349371105280_n-1.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4822"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As the real estate brokerage with the biggest number of licensed brokers and registered salespersons in the country, Leuterio Realty agents are continuously trained to set the example and showcase professionalism, ethics, and honesty in their practice. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4820,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/76652818_10215730113868584_7595620830860541952_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4820"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes commits to organize  <a href="https://www.prc.gov.ph/cpd-irr-page"><strong>Continuing Professional Development</strong>&nbsp;</a> Programs for their Licensed Brokers and Agents. Follow us in our page for CPD Schedule Announcements for the year 2020. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you are new to the real estate service, click <a href="http://localhost:3001/how-to-be-a-prc-accredited-real-estate-salesperson/">here</a> to know the basic requirements to have yourself registered through PRC. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Filipino Homes has always partnered with the Professional Regulation Commission (PRC) Accredited Speakers like Dr. Ed Ong, Ph.D., REC, REA, REB, and Engr. Eleanor Liganor, REB, to ensure that Leuterio Realty & Brokerage agents comply with the CPD or Continuing Professional Development (CPD)  requirements set by the PRC [Professional Regulation Commission].','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/01/filipino-homes-xyza-yape-real-estate-agent-.png','views' => '39','category_id' => '9','published_at' => '2019-11-14 05:17:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '364','title' => 'Leuterio Realty Hold its First International Awarding','slug' => 'leuterio-realty-hold-its-first-international-awarding','content' => '<!-- wp:image {"id":4730,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/77100915_10215663704048380_8759129696140001280_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4730"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leuterio Realty &amp; Filipino Homes honors its high performing brokers and agents and holds its first International Awarding in Las Vegas, Nevada USA. Last November 13, 2019, Filipino Homes gathered their best performing realtors and presented an award in celebration of their success. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4731,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/76986933_10215716494848117_5656376404464369664_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4731"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The event was held at The Plaza at Whitney Ranch Las Vegas Nevada USA. The event was participated by the 70 top-performing realtors of Filipino Homes. Dr. Eduardo G. Ong, PhD, DPA, DBA the first Chairman of the Professional Regulatory Board of Real Estate Service (PRB-RES) and his lovely wife Jessa, Mr. Tom Blanchard, the President-elect of the 15,400 members strong Las Vegas Association of Realtors and his wife also graced the event and recognized the awardees of Filipino Homes 2019 Internation Real Estate awards. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>" &nbsp;It was my honor to speak to such a great group of caring individuals. You are all top-notch agents doing great work that you all should be extremely proud of! " <a href="https://www.facebook.com/LasVegasBroker">Thomas Blanchard</a>&nbsp; </p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4732,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/75380313_10215663807730972_8979311044245585920_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4732"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> Outstanding Filipino American and Rotary Club of Lancaster, California President&nbsp;<a href="https://www.facebook.com/edward.abad.12?__tn__=K-R&amp;eid=ARDGbhA1j3qnFppYSOexCYuyjZpF8MVgGx_LS5mbpEAhv2wGGU6wEPASf0FEScL8MmpVwGjTPKVvAe6g&amp;fref=mentions&amp;__xts__%5B0%5D=68.ARA0u4rqp75DSlKBP3axvOBEQ4llVWBDmyZewEa0cfJpS5K3gcjKWLU4eLveBPtjBqB59rIVyROjYlTaYscik3upQanGgIMoBFdUhl6zdRNgH9vEYCNc682ncOKkJ9WoG7TsWCv47ziVbLRKECAQiPfvLy62NWBCIkTQB2Ul7ih--nF0BAn5vTEd3Ux3Xn1ajiGzyJ9uGTKfmF5m6lajdj_YM0lTC3UkR-Ayd25hig3jcvN1e8zM_RhDJwl8qtokjHpIkuYeMOXwEt2ZuwVJ9rMmUH4">Edward Duterte Abad</a>&nbsp;who will be assisting the company in managing the venues for the Filipino Homes’ roadshows and expansion events in the USA was also there to grace the event. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4735,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/73513706_3010014632347507_2924578673640079360_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4735"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>One of the special guests during the International Real Estate Awarding was the renowned composer of Filipino Homes Jingle and award-winning OPM songs, Mr. Jimmy Borja. Jimmy Benedicto T. Borja is a Boholano composer now based in USA; the songwriter/composer of Ariel Rivera\'s "Sana Ngayong Pasko" and Ella Mae Saison\'s "If The Feeling Is Gone".</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Download the <a href="https://filipinohomes.com/jingle/">Filipino Homes Jingle here.</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Leuterio Realty & Filipino Homes honors its high performing brokers and agents and holds its first International Awarding in Las Vegas, Nevada USA. Last November 13, 2019, Filipino Homes gathered their best performing realtors and presented an award in celebration of their success. ','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/12/76652048_10215657277607723_3490134435259482112_o.jpg','views' => '35','category_id' => '9','published_at' => '2019-11-18 07:22:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '365','title' => 'What You Need to Know about the Rent Control Act of 2009','slug' => 'what-you-need-to-know-about-the-rent-control-act-of-2009','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Whether you are a landlord or a tenant, it may be time to brush up on your knowledge of the Rent Control Act to better understand your rights and responsibilities.  This act covers housing rentals in the country, protecting renters from sudden increases in rental rates. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1450101499163-c8848c66ca85?ixlib=rb-1.2.1&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;w=1050&amp;q=80" alt=""/><figcaption> Photo by&nbsp;<a href="https://unsplash.com/@helloquence?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">Helloquence</a>&nbsp;on&nbsp;<a href="https://unsplash.com/s/photos/contract?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">Unsplash</a> </figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>What is Rent Control Act?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href="https://www.lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra2009/ra_9653_2009.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label=" (opens in a new tab)">Republic Act No 9653</a>&nbsp;or  <em>“An Act Establishing Reforms in the Regulation of Rent of Certain Residential Units, Providing the Mechanisms Therefore and For Other Purposes”</em>  also known as <em>“The Rent Control Act” </em>aims to protect housing tenants in the lower-income brackets and other beneficiaries from unreasonable rent increases.  It was approved in 2009; expired on December 31, 2013, but has been extended by the Housing and Urban Development Coordinating Council (HUDCC), the government agency tasked to oversee the law’s implementation, until December 31, 2020.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Coverage of this Act</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>RA 9653 covers the following residential units nationwide, whose monthly rent is&nbsp;up to P10,000&nbsp; &nbsp;and below: </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} -->
<ol><li> Apartments;</li><li>Houses and/or land on which another’s dwelling is located and used for residential purposes; and</li><li>Buildings or parts thereof, which are being used solely as dwelling units, boarding houses, dormitories, rooms and bed spaces. </li></ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Rent-to-own units, commercial spaces, motels, and hotels are not covered.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Advances and Deposits</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>According to the Rent Control Act, it is illegal for landlords to demand more than one (1) month advance rent or more than two (2) months deposit. The law also requires lessors to deposit the amount of the 2-month deposit in a bank account under the landlord’s name, with all accrued and accumulated interest to be returned to the tenant, along with the deposit, at the expiration of the rental contract.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This amount will be forfeited, however, in the event that the tenant fails to settle rent or utility bills. The amount can also be used for repair of damages and replacement of any component of the rented unit.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Subleasing Guidelines</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://cdn.pixabay.com/photo/2017/06/08/20/11/airbnb-2384737_1280.jpg" alt=""/><figcaption>Image by <a href="https://pixabay.com/users/TeroVesalainen-809550/?utm_source=link-attribution&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=image&amp;utm_content=2384737">TeroVesalainen</a> from <a href="https://pixabay.com/?utm_source=link-attribution&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=image&amp;utm_content=2384737">Pixabay</a></figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The act addresses issues on subleasing. A tenant is not permitted to sub-lease the unit without prior written consent from the landlord. Doing such may be used as a reasonable ground to evict the tenant from the rented unit. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Maximum Rent Increase</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The increase in the monthly rental rate of any residential unit shall not be more than:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Four percent (4%) annually for residential units with a monthly rent of below P4,000; and</li><li>Seven percent (7%) for units with a monthly rent of P4,000.00 up to P10,000.00 for as long as the unit is&nbsp;occupied by the&nbsp;same lessee.</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Rental accommodations offered to students such as boarding houses, dormitories, rooms, and bed spaces are only allowed to increase rents once a year, even if a new renter occupies the unit within the same year. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Grounds for Evicting Tenants</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The landlord has the right to eject the tenant on the following grounds:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>The lessee assigns the lease or sub-leases the unit, without the written consent of the owner/lessor;</li><li>The renter has accumulated arrears in rental equivalent to three (3) months;</li><li>After the expiration of the lease period, the lessor/owner has a legitimate need to repossess the property for his/her own&nbsp;use or that of his/her family as a residential unit, provided that the renter was notified three months in advance;</li><li>The lessor/owner needs to make necessary repairs on the leased premises which is the subject of an existing order of&nbsp;condemnation by appropriate authorities concerned in order to make the premises safe and habitable; and</li><li>The lease contract has expired.</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The lessee cannot be ejected on the ground that the leased premises have been sold or mortgaged to a third&nbsp;person&nbsp;regardless of whether the lease or mortgage is registered or not.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Penalties for Violators of the Rent Control Act</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Violators of the act face a fine of not less P25,000 but not more than P50,000 or imprisonment of one (1) month and one (1) day&nbsp;up to(6) months, or both. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4><strong>References</strong></h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can read the full version/copy of the original signed Act below:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:file {"id":4495,"href":"http:\\/\\/localhost:3001\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2019\\/10\\/Republic-Act-No-9653.pdf"} -->
<div class="wp-block-file"><a href="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Republic-Act-No-9653.pdf">Republic-Act-No-9653</a><a href="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Republic-Act-No-9653.pdf" class="wp-block-file__button" download>Download</a></div>
<!-- /wp:file -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>FAQ on the Extension of Rent Control Act here:  <a href="http://www.hudcc.gov.ph/QandA" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label=" (opens in a new tab)">http://www.hudcc.gov.ph/QandA</a> </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Whether you are a landlord or a tenant, it may be time to brush up on your knowledge of the Rent Control Act to better understand your rights and responsibilities.  This act covers housing rentals in the country, protecting renters from sudden increases in rental rates. ','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/11/Copy-of-Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape-13.png','views' => '37','category_id' => '10','published_at' => '2019-11-29 00:25:23','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '366','title' => '5 Ways to Know if You\'re Ready to Live Alone for the First Time','slug' => '5-ways-to-know-if-youre-ready-to-live-alone-for-the-first-time','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Living with the family or roommates may be fun, easy, and comfortable, but the time comes when we need to embrace adulthood and move out in order to find our own path in life. Whether you\'re considering <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="renting or buying (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/buying-versus-renting-a-property/" target="_blank">renting or buying</a> a house (or condominium unit), here are 5 tell-tale signs to know that your time to live alone has come. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3> <br>1. You Have Your Finances in Order </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1554224155-6726b3ff858f?ixlib=rb-1.2.1&amp;ixid=eyJhcHBfaWQiOjEyMDd9&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;w=1172&amp;q=80" alt=""/><figcaption> Photo by&nbsp;<a href="https://unsplash.com/@kellysikkema?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">Kelly Sikkema</a>&nbsp;on&nbsp;<a href="https://unsplash.com/s/photos/finances?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">Unsplash</a> </figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Living alone means you shoulder all expenses associated with it. You pay your own rent or mortgage, utility bills, groceries, and even repair and maintenance. This means you have to make sure you are able to pay <span style="text-decoration: underline;">all your bills on time</span>. Otherwise, you might be coming home to a place with no electricity or water. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>I recently shared a financial planner I personally designed, which helped me have an honest-to-goodness assessment of my finances and set some actionable steps to get me to my goals. <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="Get your copy of the financial planner here (opens in a new tab)" href="https://lovettejam.com/free-printable-financial-planner/" target="_blank">You can go ahead and get your copy of the ultimate printable financial planner here</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><br>2. You\'re Comfortable With Being Alone</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4670,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/photo-1478707734876-10bbf5b7a44b-1024x683.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4670"/><figcaption> Photo by&nbsp;<a href="https://unsplash.com/@freestocks?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">freestocks.org</a>&nbsp;on&nbsp;<a href="https://unsplash.com/s/photos/home-alone?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">Unsplash</a> </figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Living alone could mean literal freedom. You can do whatever you like, cook anything you want, use the bathroom without the pressure of someone else needing to use it, and binge-watch via Netflix without headphones on. Living alone also means you enjoy your own company. Sure, you can invite friends over and maybe go out as often as you like, but most of the time, you\'re really on your own.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3> <br>3. You Can Take Care of Yourself </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4671,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/plumber-228010_1280-1024x680.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4671"/><figcaption>Image by <a href="https://pixabay.com/users/fran1-112250/?utm_source=link-attribution&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=image&amp;utm_content=228010">fran1</a> from <a href="https://pixabay.com/?utm_source=link-attribution&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=image&amp;utm_content=228010">Pixabay</a></figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Taking care of yourself means you\'re responsible enough to get yourself up in the morning, making sure you have enough supplies at all times, and keeping your home in tiptop shape. This also means you are able to change a lightbulb, unclog the toilet without getting squeamish, deal with spiders, or maybe just know who to call (and not panicking) when you have a leaking faucet. Living alone means you need to be independent and resourceful, able to figure out problems on your own.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><br>4. You are organized</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4672,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/photo-1547822281-5c9d3ab15297.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4672"/><figcaption> Photo by&nbsp;<a href="https://unsplash.com/@chuttersnap?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">chuttersnap</a>&nbsp;on&nbsp;<a href="https://unsplash.com/s/photos/closet?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">Unsplash</a> </figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When you\'re living alone, you have to be organized and responsible. You need to keep your home clean, wash your dishes, get food for yourself, and make sure you have clean clothes to wear. Well, technically, you don\'t necessarily have to keep your home picture-perfect at all times, but at a minimum, you have to wash your dishes and get food for yourself. You have to have a working system -- for cleaning, grocery shopping, laundry, etc -- to keep your home livable.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><br>5. You Want to Create a Home </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4673,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/photo-1519974719765-e6559eac2575.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4673"/><figcaption> Photo by&nbsp;<a href="https://unsplash.com/@hutomoabrianto?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">Hutomo Abrianto</a>&nbsp;on&nbsp;<a href="https://unsplash.com/s/photos/home?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">Unsplash</a> </figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You’ve probably daydreamed about decorating your own space. You may even have purchased some homely items, like special cushions, organizational items, and kitchen stuff. You may get too excited and giddy browsing through the home section of the department store. <br><br>Living alone is an opportunity to discover and embrace your own personal style. You get to decide where the couch goes, what artworks to go on the walls, and explore your personal design aesthetic.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><br></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Living with the family or roommates may be fun, easy, and comfortable, but a time comes when we need to embrace adulthood and move out in order to find our own path in life. Whether you\'re considering renting or buying a house (or condominium unit), here are 5 tell-tale signs to know that your time to live alone has come. ','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/11/filipinohomes-xyzaspeaks-xyza-yape.png','views' => '45','category_id' => '13','published_at' => '2019-11-29 21:11:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '367','title' => 'Do you work from home?  Buy your next home with your office in mind','slug' => 'do-you-work-from-home-buy-your-next-home-with-your-office-in-mind','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The flexibility afforded by a “zero-commute” combined with the skyrocketing price of gasoline has strengthened the case for a full time teleworking and telecommuting.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>“ Filipinos <strong>spend</strong>&nbsp;an&nbsp;<strong>average</strong>&nbsp;of 45.5 minutes before reaching their workplace. ” [<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Traffic_in_Metro_Manila">Source</a>]</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The artist community has been well acquainted with the use of work/living spaces for years, but improvements in technology have made the benefits of teleworking and occasional telecommuting more attractive to general consumers.  According to the key findings from the International Telework Association &amp; Council (ITAC) Telework America study:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>“Home-based teleworkers also have larger homes, on average, than non-teleworkers; the difference amounting to about 500 square feet (46sqm).  The most popular place for an office in these larger homes is a spare bedroom, with the living room a distant second.  The primary home telework activity is computer work (55% of total activities), followed by telephoning, reading, and—averaging 7% of the time—face to face meetings.” </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As you purchase your next home, there are certain factors to consider if you need to set up a new home office:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>Make sure that your high-tech needs can be met. </h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4713,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/internet-1024x538.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4713"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> Have a qualified electrician inspect the wiring of the house to see if the system can handle the extra power load that your home office requires.   Older homes may need significant upgrades to handle the extra power. While newer homes are built with more energy-efficient systems to handle the additional power along with heating/air conditioning requirements. If you use cable, DSL or satellite internet access, check with your local service provider to see if access is available in your new neighborhood. Shop around for your telephone provider—in some cases, business service bundles may be more cost-effective than regular residential service. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>Designate where your office space will be.  </h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4714,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/1.-Desks0110-r01-PJ_01_250k@2x-1024x637.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4714"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Determine the amount of space you will need to accommodate your work style and space.  In many cases, a spare bedroom or living room space can be used if a formal den option is not available.  If your work requires heavy telephone usage or just heads-down concentration, you may want to consider utilizing a room with a door.  Doors can be closed to reduce interruptions from other family and household noises.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>Plan your office blueprint to include all the required furniture, bookcases, computers, fax, and printers.  </h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Make sure to allow for filing and storage space for files and extra office supplies.  Lighting is critical for computer or assembly work, so make sure to allow for direct sunlight.  Select flooring options that will allow you to work comfortably—you may wish to go with hardwood or laminate flooring to allow for your chair to move smoothly across the floor. Install enough phone lines to cover your home, business and fax machines needs.   </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>Is the office easily accessible?  </h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you will expect regular package deliveries, make sure that your designated office is easily accessible to the front door of the home.  This is also necessary if you will need to meet clients or visitors in your office and would like to ensure a professional appearance for your business. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>Find out about local business requirements. </h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> Some cities have zoning restrictions and guidelines for work/living spaces along with tax implications.  Make sure to check with your local government to determine if special restrictions exist. It may not be that complicated in the Philippines setting, but it is always better to be completely legal most especially that there are no guidelines and concrete laws and restrictions yet.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'If you work from home, and it is time to move to your next home, there are some factors you should consider carefully before making your decision.
','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/11/filipinohomes-xyzaspeaks-xyza-yape-1.png','views' => '43','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2019-11-30 23:37:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '368','title' => 'The Opening and Appreciation Night of Tambuli Seaside Resort & Spa','slug' => 'the-opening-and-appreciation-night-of-tambuli-seaside-resort-spa','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Last November 30, 2019, Tambuli Seaside Resort &amp; Spa was officially opened for guests, shareholders, and tourists. Among the invited guests are the shareholders and homeowners of Tambuli Seaside Living Condominiums and real estate partners. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4765,4766,4767]} -->
