<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>365 days of endless vacations right here in Tambuli Seaside Living. If this interests you in availing Phase 2 of Tambuli Seaside Living, contact your Filipino Homes/Leuterio Realty Agent today!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => ' Tambuli Seaside Resort & Spa was officially opened for guests, shareholders, and tourists. Among the invited guests are the shareholders and homeowners of Tambuli Seaside Living Condominiums and real estate partners. ','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/12/Copy-of-Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape-17.png','views' => '43','category_id' => '14','published_at' => '2019-12-02 09:21:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '369','title' => '5 Ground Rules for Home Buying Success','slug' => '5-ground-rules-for-home-buying-success','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There are few purchases in life that carry the financial and psychological weight of buying a home.  Whether you are buying your first home, moving up to your dream home, or downsizing your home and your life after the kids have gone, it is important to understand the ground rules for success in the world of buying a home.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Making the wrong decision in buying a home can have devastating and long-lasting effects while making a wise decision in home buying can greatly enhance the overall value of the investment.  It is necessary to learn all you can about the world of home buying and mortgages before setting out to purchase the home of your dreams.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>While there are plenty of web sites designed to help first-time homeowners learn all they can, most financial experts say that there is no substitute for the good old one-on-one learning. Fortunately, most mortgage lenders, home inspectors, and real estate agents will be able to provide this kind of one-on-one learning.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When buying a home it is often best to use a systematic approach as this is often the best way to be sure that all decisions are based on information and reason, not on impulse or emotion.  Buying a home can be an emotional process, nevertheless, it is imperative to keep your emotions under control and not let them cloud your judgment.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There are five basic ground rules when it comes to buying a home and shopping smart, and they are:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>#1 – Get your financing before you get your home</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4522,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/triijqojsgqysgjaiubs.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4522"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There are few things in life as disappointing as losing out on the home of your dreams due to not being able to secure funding.  While the desire to get out there is a search for that great home is understandable, it is vital to line up the financing you will need before you start shopping for a home.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Getting the financing ahead of time has a number of important advantages, including knowing how much you can buy and gaining more respect from the listing agents.  By knowing how much home you can afford before you shop you will avoid wasting your time looking at unaffordable properties, and the listing agent will be more than willing to show you the homes in your price range.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It is also important to take a good look at the various types of mortgage on the market before getting started in the home buying process.  These days, mortgages come in far more choices than the typical 15 or 30 years. For that reason, potential home buyers need to understand how each type of mortgage works, and to gauge which mortgage is the best choice for their needs.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>#2 – Look at the community, not just the home</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn%3AANd9GcSld2qP54o4jHQPMs3Asv00gtrsSpwEGI4e37jTF4Wi10YOc1_E"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It is a good idea to look at the entire community, instead of focusing on a single home. This can be a particularly important thing to consider for those moving to a new metropolitan area, as these buyers will be unfamiliar with the local climate and lifestyle.  It is crucial to determine the areas of town that are most desirable and to consider things like distance from work and local shopping opportunities.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We have all heard that location is the key consideration when it comes to real estate, and that is certainly the case.  Buying a house in the wrong area can be a big mistake, and it is important to choose the location as well as the home.  Potential buyers can learn a great deal about the nature of the various neighborhoods simply by driving around town, as well as by talking to other residents if you are buying a resell, however for pre-selling properties or projects you can base it on its category and probably asking the realtors on who already bought properties in the area. So you can have at least an outlook on what probably the future neighborhood would look like. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>#3 – Be fair with your first offer</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn%3AANd9GcTd2vnH7ZO8tleZJ76WSb4R4BAGehnZgQ7bk8SJkokEj0S4fdAD" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Trying to lowball a seller on the first offer can backfire, as can paying too much. It is important to carefully evaluate the local market and to compare the asking price of the home with what similar houses in the neighborhood have sold for.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Comparing the sales of comparable homes, what are known as "comps" in the industry, is one of the best ways to determine what is fair, and to make sure that you neither overpay or underbid on the property.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>#4 – Always get a home inspection</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"width":580,"height":386,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large is-resized"><img src="https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn%3AANd9GcRFoWKxC_w77TPhe2endgpkFD67TdjrKF_50UMuTCIWhfeTREmj" alt="" width="580" height="386"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Always investigate the home for any possible defects before making an offer.  Compared to the cost of the average home, the price of a quality home inspection is virtually negligible. Hence, get a good home inspection done before you buy it.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>To find the best home inspector, it is a good idea to seek out word of mouth referrals as many of the best home inspectors rely on word of mouth advertising.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>#5 – Do not isolate the sellers of the home</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn%3AANd9GcR5ns1Ied_k6LD-TB3IJ7YiMBaSOjOqqysY537Yi5meCd_CI9zE" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Many real estate deals have fallen apart due to the personal animosity of the buyer and the seller.  It is important to avoid alienating the seller of the home during the process and to avoid nitpicking every little detail during the sale. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Keeping the goodwill of the seller will help the transaction go smoothly, and it will provide the best environment for sellers and buyers alike. If you are actively looking for a property to buy, contact a <a href="http://www.filipinohomes.com">Filipino Home</a>s real estate agent or broker today!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can also <a href="https://apkpure.com/filipino-homes/com.filipinohomesmobile">download Filipino Homes App</a> for you to be notified of new listings available near you. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'There are five basic ground rules that you must know when it comes to buying a home and shopping smart, and they are ....
','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/10/Copy-of-Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape-14.png','views' => '51','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2019-12-06 23:30:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '370','title' => 'Things You Can Do in Puerto Princesa in 24 Hours','slug' => 'things-you-can-do-in-puerto-princesa-in-24-hours','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Puerto Princesa is a coastal city in the island of Palawan in the Western Philippines. It is home to the world-known Puerto Princesa Underground River National Park. It brings in massive loads of tourists every year and is one of the top tourist destinations in the Philippines. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This city is best known for the various tourist destinations and activities that you can do. But if you do not have a few days to tour and explore Puerto Princesa, you  you can explore Puerto Princesa in 24 hours.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4661} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/Things-You-Can-Do-in-Puerto-Princesa-in-24-Hours-05.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4661"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>HONDA BAY TOUR</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Honda Bay Tour is one of the popular tourist activities in Puerto Princesa City. You will take a boat and hop from one island to another and enjoy  spending the whole day in white sand beaches consisting of  of 4-5 islands around Puerto Princesa. This activity alone will keep you the whole day frolicking in the seawater but it is something that you would not want to miss.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>PALAWAN PROVINCIAL CAPITOL</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Palawan Provincial Capitol is hard to miss. It is one of the dominating landmarks which you will see a few minutes from the airport. You will find a massive open space to lounge around and just enjoy a cool, and relaxing day after checking out the massive sculpture inside the Palawan Provincial Capitol.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4657} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/Things-You-Can-Do-in-Puerto-Princesa-in-24-Hours-01.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4657"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>PALAWAN HERITAGE CENTER</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Behind the Palawan Provincial Capitol is the Palawan Heritage Center. You will find the history of Palawan and the lives of the early inhabitants\' story -told in the exhibit. Depending on what exhibit is currently available, expect an entrance fee from PhP 100 –&nbsp;above per person.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4658} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/Things-You-Can-Do-in-Puerto-Princesa-in-24-Hours-02.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4658"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>PUERTO PRINCESA BAYWALK</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Puerto Princesa Baywalk is Puerto Princesa’s version of Manila de Bay. It is a long stretch of seaside, open area for strolling and leisure. you will find food vendors that will light up the space during at night offering local food. You will also find bicycles for rent, and enough space to stroll or sit around for hours.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4660} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/Things-You-Can-Do-in-Puerto-Princesa-in-24-Hours-04.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4660"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>IMMACULATE CONCEPTION CATHEDRAL OR PUERTO PRINCESA CHURCH</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With a touch of gothic look, these pointed symmetrical arches is the Immaculate Conception Cathedral. Located on top of a steep hill, this was said to be small old church built at the time of the Spanish occupation.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4659} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/Things-You-Can-Do-in-Puerto-Princesa-in-24-Hours-03.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4659"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>PLAZA CUARTEL</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Adjacent to the Puerto Princesa Cathedral is a historical landmark and a grim reminder of World War II and the torture that went along with it. The Plaza Cuartel appears ordinary in the outside. Going in and walking through the park, you will find a carefully told story of the infamous Palawan Massacre were 150 American prisoners were burned alive and only 11 escaped from the brutal forces of the Japanese invaders.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Puerto Princesa is a coastal city on Palawan Island in the western Philippines. It is home to the world-known Puerto Princesa Underground River National Park. It brings in massive loads of tourists every year and is one of the top tourist destinations in the Philippines. ','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/11/Copy-of-Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape-15.png','views' => '89','category_id' => '10','published_at' => '2019-12-08 00:31:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '371','title' => 'How To Keep Your Children Safe At Home','slug' => 'how-to-keep-your-children-safe-at-home','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A home is a safe-haven for families and it where children spend most of their growing years in. For homeowners that do not have children or have children who are still in the infant, you might not understand the importance of childproofing your home. Household accidents are the reasons kinds under 3 visit the Emergency Room each year.  It is smart to be prepared for the worst, childproofing your home not only <a href="http://filipinohomes.com/blog/childproofing-keeps-children-safe-harm-home/">keeps your children safe</a> but also gives you a peace of mind.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><b>Cover electrical outlets</b></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"width":592,"height":592,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large is-resized"><img src="https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn%3AANd9GcR5D1id6WXT-agY0zMpOJESLiP4qClPgS6lb35Ctc4pcN2h4LLr" width="592" height="592"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Kids naturally explore their surroundings. These include sticking their fingers to holes, and crevices. Make sure to cover your electrical outlets to prevent accidental electrocution.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><b>Secure television sets, bookcase, and other furniture and appliances</b></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://cdn.thewirecutter.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/anchor-furniture-00-630.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Trying to get their hands on anything, children tend to push and pull items. This includes large objects or wires, and anything they can get a hold of. Make sure to secure furniture, and appliances and other large objects that a child can easily pull or try to move around.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><b>Lock hazardous liquids, and medication</b></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://static.onecms.io/wp-content/uploads/sites/38/2017/03/12231611/child_poisoning_hazards_gettyimages-82860817.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Ensure your child\'s safety from harmful and hazardous liquids or solutions. These include cleaning solutions and even medications. Children not only explore with their hands but also putting things on their mouths. Lock any harmful solutions away from kids to prevent accidental poisoning.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><b>Tuck away tiny objects that a child could choke on</b></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://www.verywellfamily.com/thmb/vo9sG1t58DaXwt-Wu1OxKYYPlUM=/3864x2576/filters:fill(DBCCE8,1)/father-and-daughter-spend-time-together-at-home-995382266-5c16988046e0fb0001a51199.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Exploring things with their mouths, children tend to get a hold of any items and put them in their mouths. Tuck or hideaway tiny objects that could choke your child. Make sure that there are no household items that children would try to eat and choke on.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><b>Keep dressers closed when you\'re not using them</b></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"width":579,"height":579,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large is-resized"><img src="https://images-na.ssl-images-amazon.com/images/I/510gdXMGk7L._SX466_.jpg" alt="" width="579" height="579"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Children are naturally curious and would find ways to maximize their environment by exploring more of it. Keep dressers or drawers close. A child can see an opportunity to climb on the drawers to get to the top of it. Secure the drawers with a secure guard to keep of tiny hands from opening them.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><b>Cover sharp corners of furniture</b></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://welcomebabysl.files.wordpress.com/2014/03/bumpers.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It may not be attractive to have safety bumpers on your furniture but it is one of the important safety measures a parent could do and use. If you have young children who crawl and those who run around, cover corners of furniture with bumpers to soften the impact of your kids runs into them.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><b>Be fire ready.</b></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"width":584,"height":392,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large is-resized"><img src="https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcRjst0l4MuvlNjhV5cvbtYd5hyWxgA-bSOWaRYuljXSr0LNLcsW&amp;s" alt="" width="584" height="392"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Install smoke alarms with long term batteries, and keep a fire extinguisher at your home. This is not only a safety caution for your children but for the whole family. Create an evacuation plan and make sure everyone in the house knows it.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A home should be a place for safety but you can not stop accidents from happening. You can, however, prevent them from be being cautious and mindful of the surroundings for you and your children. Childproofing your home is one of the safety precautions one can do for the family.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2018/06/img_9156.jpg','views' => '46','category_id' => '13','published_at' => '2019-12-08 23:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '372','title' => '48th Filipino Homes Office Opens in Bajada, Davao City','slug' => '48th-filipino-homes-office-opens-in-bajada-davao-city','content' => '<!-- wp:image {"id":4745,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/80021049_605453466867199_7635261201454202880_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4745"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes opened its 48th office in Davao City last December 11, 2019. This office is managed by REB Marlou and REB Lanie Rea Hinay. The new office is located at  TMNT Building Donia Vicenta Drive, Bajada, Davao City. Marlou and Lanie also have an office in Butuan City and tit is also the first Filipino Homes Office in Butuan City. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4746,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/79514494_10215870880587664_1019004733555212288_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4746"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Davao City, the hometown of our current president, President Rodrigo Roa Duterte had a fast-growing investment opportunity over the years. Local and International investors have been eyeing Davao City as a good investment destination due to its good governance and also probably because the most influential leader continues to live in Davao despite having to fly back and forth from his home to Malacanang Palace.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4747,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/79279911_605453513533861_4449515475033915392_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4747"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The new office in Davao City is the 5th Filipino Homes Office in the City. This will help agents and brokers assist more clients in the future in preparation for the massive real estate projects that will be transforming the city. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Contact Details:<br></strong>Office  Secretary:  Darlyn Demetillo <br>Mobile Number: (0910) 150 5023 <br>Address:  TMNT Building Donia Vicenta Drive, Bajada, Davao City </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you are interested to jumpstart your career in Real Estate contact any Filipino Homes Agent/Broker to assist you. <a href="http://www.leuteriorealty.com/joinus">Join us!</a> </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Filipino Homes opens its 48th office in Davao City last December 11, 2019. This office is managed by REB Marlou and REB Lanie Rea Hinay. The new office is located at  TMNT Building Donia Vicenta Drive, Bajada, Davao City. ','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/12/80021049_605453466867199_7635261201454202880_n.jpg','views' => '42','category_id' => '14','published_at' => '2019-12-12 03:51:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '373','title' => 'Leuterio Realty Bags Top Realty Award from Cebu Landmasters Inc.','slug' => 'leuterio-realty-bags-top-realty-award-from-cebu-landmasters-inc','content' => '<!-- wp:image {"id":4751,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/79370258_1725293904267986_5296817157080875008_n-1.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4751"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Last December 12, 2019, Leuterio Realty &amp; Brokerage bagged the Top 1 Master Brokerage Award from the country\'s <a href="https://www.cebulandmasters.com/news/11205/"><strong>BEST PROPERTY DEVELOPER </strong>of 2019; Cebu Landmasters Inc</a>. (CLI). It was held at Rosario Pavilion, Limketkai Cagayan de Oro City. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4752,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/79111411_965230983861874_8646610035545210880_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4752"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>CLI, as mentioned by Ms. Marie Rose Yulo (VP of Sales), had exemplary sold Billion pesos sales for the year 2019 with the help of their broker partners. Out of a number of realties selling Cebu Landmasters projects in Cagayan de Oro, Leuterio Realty &amp; Brokerage had the highest total number of sales. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4753,4754]} -->
<figure class="wp-block-gallery columns-2 is-cropped"><ul class="blocks-gallery-grid"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/79500819_10215882349634383_266899403896258560_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4753" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/79500819_10215882349634383_266899403896258560_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4753" class="wp-image-4753"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/79149092_10215882350114395_4953532481379762176_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4754" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/79149092_10215882350114395_4953532481379762176_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4754" class="wp-image-4754"/></figure></li></ul></figure>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The award was given during CLI\'s Night of the Masters 2019. It\'s an event full of thanksgiving and recognition for a job well done in a year of selling Cebu Landmasters Inc. projects in Cagayan de Oro City. It was an invitational event that was attended by more than a hundred of their real estate partners. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4756,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/79834233_10215882346234298_9175812386517417984_n-1.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4756"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leuterio Realty Agents and Brokers also topped the project-based awards;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Top 1 Master Broker for Casa Mira Towers - Ms. Rowena Kho (REB) </li><li>TOP 2 Master Broker for Velmiro Uptown - Leo Ross Torralba</li><li>TOP 3 Master Broker for Velmiro Uptown - Kenneth Jun Pancito </li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4757,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/79024567_965230960528543_8699788967689584640_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4757"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The awards were personally handed by the CLI\'s CEO himself Mr. Jose Soberano III assisted by his daughter Ms. Joanna Marie Soberano-Bergundthal (VP and Marketing Director) and Ms. Marie Rose Yulo (VP for Sales). </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => ' Leuterio Realty & Brokerage bags the Top 1 Master Brokerage Award from the country\'s BEST PROPERTY DEVELOPER of 2019; Cebu Landmasters Inc. (CLI). It was held at Rosario Pavilion, Limketkai Cagayan de Oro City. ','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/12/Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape-5.png','views' => '44','category_id' => '9','published_at' => '2019-12-12 17:09:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '374','title' => 'Checklist for Buying a Home','slug' => 'checklist-for-buying-a-home','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Buying a home can be one of the best feelings in the world. Nothing beats that feeling of security and satisfaction when you open the door to a new home and are happy with your purchase. The question is, how can you best ensure that feeling is going to happen? There are a lot of pitfalls in the real estate world and naturally, you want to be able to avoid them and end up with a great home. Here are some great tips on how to streamline your home purchase and keep those little headaches from cropping up. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4739,"width":571,"height":316,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large is-resized"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/54053b647e6e50eb1a7ed882fe0ba39c.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4739" width="571" height="316"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><img class="wp-image-4737" style="width: 25px;" src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/tick-box-icon-6.png" alt="">Enough cannot be said about being financially secure and aware. If you spend some time organizing your finances before making an offer the process becomes much less stressful. Take some time and research your credit history and find out if there are any outstanding issues or problems and get them taken care of. This can negatively affect your chances of getting a good mortgage, so it\'s in your best interest to clear any credit issues up before the buying process starts. Most mortgage companies will offer you a pre-qualification, now this is nice to have but you are better off to take it a step further. Obtain the pre-approval for your mortgage. The pre-approval gives you an absolute number to work with. Not only does this make shopping for a home easier for you, but it gives you a significant amount of leverage in the actual sale. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4740,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/Depositphotos_41207211_xl-2015-1024x683.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4740"/><figcaption>Businessman signs contract behind the home architectural model</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><img class="wp-image-4737" style="width: 25px;" src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/tick-box-icon-6.png" alt=""> The next logical step is to begin working with your realtor on finding homes that suit your needs. Let your <a href="http://www.filipinohomes.com">realtor </a>know what things you cannot do without and those things that you would like and let them come up with a list that best fits you. During this time you can also research the available homes in your chosen area on the internet and find places that appeal to you. With this ammunition, you and your agent should be able to view homes and properties with confidence and easily find a place that is agreeable to your needs, wants, and wallet. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://cdn.balkanplumbing.com/wp-content/uploads/sewer-system-inspected-home-buyers.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><img class="wp-image-4737" style="width: 25px;" src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/tick-box-icon-6.png" alt="">Once you have located the perfect property, have an inspection done. This is a must! Be wary of sellers who are willing to sell to others on the "no inspection" clause. This is never a good thing and much of the time they don\'t want an inspection done for a reason. The inspection is an extremely important step in ensuring your protection as the new owner. After all, this is going to be your home right? Don\'t ever sell yourself short.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>However, if you are buying a property that is under pre-selling, which means the construction or land development has not yet started, make sure to visit the site at least, so that you will have an idea of the community or surrounding neighborhood of the property you are planning to buy. Sometimes, buyers\' decisions are influenced by the price of the property. Most especially when it\'s monthly payments are very affordable.  But if you are someone that has the right spending money, put on some weight on security and community in your buying decisions. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>I hope this helps you in starting your real estate investing or home buying journey! </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Buying a home can be one of the best feelings in the world. Nothing beats that feeling of security and satisfaction when you open the door to a new home and are happy with your purchase. The question is, how can you best ensure that feeling is going to happen? There are a lot of pitfalls in the real estate world and naturally you want to be able to avoid them and end up with a great home.','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/12/Copy-of-Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape-16.png','views' => '42','category_id' => '9','published_at' => '2019-12-13 17:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '375','title' => 'Avoid Legal Battles over Agent/Broker Commissions','slug' => 'avoid-legal-battles-over-agent-broker-commissions','content' => '<!-- wp:image {"id":4760,"sizeSlug":"large","className":"is-style-default"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large is-style-default"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/shutterstock_1170381406_1600-760x512-1.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4760"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Commission agreements that spell out how brokers or agents are paid typically use form documents.  The commission formula sometimes changes, but the terms and conditions usually stay the same.  Consequently, standard terms and conditions of commission agreements are often ignored by brokers and owners once the agreement is signed.  Since the broker’s/agent\'s income is tied to the terms of those agreements, close attention to details is vital to all parties involved.  Thus, it is best to have the owner stipulate, understand and sign the <strong><em>authority to sell before you start marketing the property </em></strong>to potential buyers. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Recent lawsuits stemming from disputes over broker commissions reveal tough lessons about the importance of paying close attention to commission agreements.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4761,"sizeSlug":"large","className":"is-style-default"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large is-style-default"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/43eb7685ec35f553bd4b8198aecdd2a2-1024x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4761"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A building owner in Iligan City was forced to pay a commission because the original agreement did not contain an expiration or termination date.  The building owner argued that there are a number of key terms understood and agreed to prior to signing the agreement that was not stated in the final written agreement.  The judge overruled this argument stating that the contract was clearly written.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There was an instance when owners were not willing to give out commissions after receiving the money for the property that they sold. The seller argued that since the sale took place after she decided to terminate the authority to sell because of personal reasons, she insisted that she doesn\'t have to pay. However, the client buying was already inquiring about the property before the said termination, agents/brokers are still entitled to claim the commission because of the clause in the agreement that "if the agent was able to bring a client for the property and buy it within six months after the termination of contract, the agent/broker is still entitled for the commission of the sale of the said property. The issue was not brought to court, but getting the commission was a bit a pain. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Judges and juries are not real estate professionals.  The term “procuring cause” may have a standard definition in the real estate business, but mean nothing to a juror.  All parties involved must make sure that the language is clear.  A judge or jury will not rewrite a contract to save either party from a bad business decision.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Even after a favorable commission contract is successfully negotiated and written, it’s not okay to simply toss it away.  Either party cannot claim they forgot about the agreement.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The lesson here is to carefully note important terms and conditions, especially those that relate to performance, compensation, and termination.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Legal disputes are more common than you would think.  Judges and juries nationwide are showing resistance to insert terms into commission contracts or allow parties to ignore the terms of a contract.  Recently there’s been an increase in the number of disputes.  Some have settled out of court, yet a fair number have gone to litigation.  This can be reversed through the efforts of brokers and owners who invest more time and effort putting together agreements and by abiding to the said terms.  This is the best method of prevention.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Clearly spelling out the terms of agreement is the first rule for owners and brokers.  This is the best way to prevent litigation.
','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/12/Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape-6.png','views' => '55','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2019-12-19 23:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '376','title' => 'Why Kababayans in Dubai Should Join the Philippine Property Roadshow?','slug' => 'why-kababayans-in-dubai-should-join-the-philippine-property-roadshow','content' => '<!-- wp:image {"id":4780,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/79846011_510274549576610_5636085656108138496_n-1024x536.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4780"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes partnered with the Philippines Best Property Developer of the year 2019; <a href="https://l.facebook.com/l.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Ffilipinohomes.com%2Fe%2Fduabai2020%3Ffbclid%3DIwAR2eoVNR9kQ6sF_-POYgkXnpuTk_MRUnm_vLaDAizBJ_PL1pejcm-xnI7b8&amp;h=AT1rSt1XqtDMT8kZ7l19gyohrRCntgBrmuESH_dxYFVkMyFjuKeMx0eZYsLQa1t29u5AG0dMyD1v4tVmZ1xTJageCvbSVBTeRhx-ORE-VDBYFfzJSGY7Pzg8lmcxgEQHg5w">Cebu Landmasters Inc</a>. They will be visiting our Kababayans in Dubai for <strong>FREE </strong>Investment talks and Philippine Property presentations. It will be on January 24 and 25, 2020 at Holiday Inn Bur Dubai Embassy District Al Hamriya Bin Waleed 20th St Dubai, United Arab Emirates. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Why OFW Kababayans should join the Philippine Property Roadshow in Dubai? </h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>1. It\'s FREE.</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4781,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/51132347_10214264448025184_6325852503288053760_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4781"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Registration for the event is FREE. All you have to do is sign-up to reserve a seat using this <a href="https://l.facebook.com/l.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Ffilipinohomes.com%2Fe%2Fduabai2020%3Ffbclid%3DIwAR2eoVNR9kQ6sF_-POYgkXnpuTk_MRUnm_vLaDAizBJ_PL1pejcm-xnI7b8&amp;h=AT1rSt1XqtDMT8kZ7l19gyohrRCntgBrmuESH_dxYFVkMyFjuKeMx0eZYsLQa1t29u5AG0dMyD1v4tVmZ1xTJageCvbSVBTeRhx-ORE-VDBYFfzJSGY7Pzg8lmcxgEQHg5w">link here </a>or contact your Filipino Homes Agent. Make sure you type in their name in the registration form. Or you may simply appear at the venue and look for the name of the person who invited you. There will be 120 Filipino Homes Agents who will be there to assist our fellow kababayans, so make sure you register so they would know who will assist you. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>2. It is a great opportunity to know first-hand information from the BEST PROPERTY DEVELOPER IN THE PHILIPPINES themselves. </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4782,4783,4788]} -->
<figure class="wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped"><ul class="blocks-gallery-grid"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/50613898_10214264447665175_4583092226409627648_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4782" class="wp-image-4782"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/50766632_10214264446745152_6274761943156785152_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4783" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4783" class="wp-image-4783"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/50808884_10213763758430927_1393205747789070336_n-1.jpg" alt="" data-id="4788" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/50808884_10213763758430927_1393205747789070336_n-1.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4788" class="wp-image-4788"/></figure></li></ul></figure>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Executives from Cebu Landmasters Inc. will be there to give you the information first hand, about their current and newest projects in the Philippine region that you might be interested to invest in. This is your opportunity to engage and be in the best investment sector in our country today. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Philippines has been tagged as the BEST COUNTRY to INVEST in, and foreigners are moving towards the Philippines and putting their money in it. Filipinos, on the other hand, are being left out because of the lack of information or the lack of venue to learn about it. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>3. It gives you the opportunity to meet face-to-face with your real estate agents or property investment endorsers. </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4785,4786,4787]} -->
<figure class="wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped"><ul class="blocks-gallery-grid"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/50905799_10213763761911014_8251106172501753856_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4785" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/50905799_10213763761911014_8251106172501753856_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4785" class="wp-image-4785"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/50913120_10213763761391001_4201285018368081920_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4786" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/50913120_10213763761391001_4201285018368081920_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4786" class="wp-image-4786"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/50494708_10213763760190971_3402253558932832256_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4787" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/50494708_10213763760190971_3402253558932832256_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4787" class="wp-image-4787"/></figure></li></ul></figure>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Real estate selling has been revolutionized. Technology is making it easier to search for properties and buy properties. And there are a lot of times that OFWs purchase their properties and never had the chance to meet their real estate agents or brokers online. Roadshows give you the chance to meet the human behind the property pages and real estate profiles you meet and interact in the Internet. It will give you the confidence to work with the real estate agent/broker to help you make the right decision and choose the best property for your family or for your investment. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4779,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/dubai-roadshow-xyzayape-filipino-homes.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4779"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>I hope this helps convince you to register. <a href="https://l.facebook.com/l.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Ffilipinohomes.com%2Fe%2Fduabai2020%3Ffbclid%3DIwAR2eoVNR9kQ6sF_-POYgkXnpuTk_MRUnm_vLaDAizBJ_PL1pejcm-xnI7b8&amp;h=AT1rSt1XqtDMT8kZ7l19gyohrRCntgBrmuESH_dxYFVkMyFjuKeMx0eZYsLQa1t29u5AG0dMyD1v4tVmZ1xTJageCvbSVBTeRhx-ORE-VDBYFfzJSGY7Pzg8lmcxgEQHg5w">Click this link if you haven\'t yet</a> or simply contact any Filipino Homes Agent you wish to work with. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/12/79846011_510274549576610_5636085656108138496_n.jpg','views' => '55','category_id' => '14','published_at' => '2019-12-20 23:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '377','title' => 'Highlights of  Filipino Homes 2019','slug' => 'highlights-of-filipino-homes-2019','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes has been amazingly blessed in the year 2019. From multiple international and national roadshows to new Filipino Homes Offices in Luzon, Visayas, and Mindanao, to National awards and International recognition for Real Estate, it has been a great year for all of us. Join us as we look back on the highlights of 2019. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4781,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/51132347_10214264448025184_6325852503288053760_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4781"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>International Property Roadshows</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It has become a tradition of Filipino Homes to partner with their very supportive property developers to reach out to our overseas Filipino workers and immigrants abroad to bring them the good news and wonderful stories of the Philippine Economy. It can\'t be avoided for some OFWs to be misinformed regarding our economy is doing and how the government is running the Philippines. Thus, Filipino Homes and its partners made it their mission to keep our kababayans/OFWs abroad up to date as to what is really happening in the Philippines. [<a href="http://localhost:3001/?s=property+roadshows">Related articles</a>]</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4782,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/50613898_10214264447665175_4583092226409627648_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4782"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>During <a href="http://localhost:3001/why-ofws-should-take-advantage-of-attending-philippine-property-roadshows/">property roadshows</a>, we usually talk about the accomplishments of our government and the real-time and true state of the Philippine Economy. We share about investment options available in the country that is suitable for OFWs/Kababayans. This International Property Roadshows registration is FREE, thus it is an event for Filipinos you should not miss. [<a href="http://localhost:3001/why-kababayans-in-dubai-should-join-the-philippine-property-roadshow/">Check for International Property Roadshow schedule for 2020 in Dubai here</a>]</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>8th Leuterio Realty National Real Estate Convention</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4603,4601,4599]} -->
<figure class="wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped"><ul class="blocks-gallery-grid"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73018193_2476669022579196_1028466181436080128_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4603" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73018193_2476669022579196_1028466181436080128_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/leuterio-realty-natcon-2019-opens/73018193_2476669022579196_1028466181436080128_n/" class="wp-image-4603"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/72906283_10159689117153018_7150351400801665024_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4601" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/72906283_10159689117153018_7150351400801665024_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/leuterio-realty-natcon-2019-opens/72906283_10159689117153018_7150351400801665024_n/" class="wp-image-4601"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73074811_2476802252565873_2162899015769784320_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4599" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73074811_2476802252565873_2162899015769784320_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/leuterio-realty-natcon-2019-opens/73074811_2476802252565873_2162899015769784320_n/" class="wp-image-4599"/></figure></li></ul></figure>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The 8th #LRNatcon2019 is the Grandest Leuterio Realty National Real Estate Convention ever in the history of Real Estate. Over 1,000 top-performing Real Estate Superstar agents and brokers of Leuterio Realty were recognized for their hard work and commitment to providing excellent service to clients. The PRC Chairman of Real Estate Madam Ofelia C. Binag and her husband graced the event. [<a href="http://localhost:3001/leuterio-realty-natcon-2019-opens/">Read Story here</a>]</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>National Awards Received</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4751]} -->
<figure class="wp-block-gallery columns-1 is-cropped"><ul class="blocks-gallery-grid"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/79370258_1725293904267986_5296817157080875008_n-1.jpg" alt="" data-id="4751" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/79370258_1725293904267986_5296817157080875008_n-1.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/leuterio-realty-bags-top-realty-award-from-cebu-landmasters-inc/79370258_1725293904267986_5296817157080875008_n-1/" class="wp-image-4751"/></figure></li></ul></figure>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For 2019, Filipino Homes and Leuterio Realty &amp; Brokerage received multiple awards all over the country.  In December 2019 alone, during the annual year-end Christmas Party and recognition, Leuterio Realty &amp; Brokerage received numerous awards and had been awarded as TOP 1 REALTY for almost; if not, all developers in the country. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>International Recognition During the National Association Of Realtors Conference</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4635,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/73415919_10215614918468771_7146092528410820608_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4635"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Last November 07, 2019, Leuterio Realty &amp; Brokerage and Filipino Homes were recognized during the Global Leaders Conference in San Francisco, California for having the most number of registered International delegates under one realty.  Leuterio Realty has 70 registered Realtors during the 3 days conference at Moscone Convention Center San Francisco California. [<a href="http://localhost:3001/filipino-homes-recognized-by-nar/">Read Story here</a>]</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>1st International Real Estate Awards in Las Vegas Nevada</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4730,4731,4732]} -->
<figure class="wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped"><ul class="blocks-gallery-grid"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/77100915_10215663704048380_8759129696140001280_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4730" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/77100915_10215663704048380_8759129696140001280_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/leuterio-realty-hold-its-first-international-awarding/77100915_10215663704048380_8759129696140001280_n/" class="wp-image-4730"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/76986933_10215716494848117_5656376404464369664_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4731" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/76986933_10215716494848117_5656376404464369664_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/leuterio-realty-hold-its-first-international-awarding/76986933_10215716494848117_5656376404464369664_n/" class="wp-image-4731"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/75380313_10215663807730972_8979311044245585920_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4732" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/75380313_10215663807730972_8979311044245585920_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/leuterio-realty-hold-its-first-international-awarding/75380313_10215663807730972_8979311044245585920_n/" class="wp-image-4732"/></figure></li></ul></figure>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leuterio Realty and Filipino Homes made history as they hold the first International Real Estate Awards last November 13, 2019, at the Plaza at Whitney Ranch Las Vegas Nevada. 120 Realtors of Filipino Homes was recognized for their excellent performance for the Fiscal year 2019. [<a href="http://localhost:3001/leuterio-realty-hold-its-first-international-awarding/">Read more here]</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>New Filipino Homes Offices Opened</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4556,4547,4541]} -->
<figure class="wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped"><ul class="blocks-gallery-grid"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73417764_442159659741243_5951045748341604352_n-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4556" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73417764_442159659741243_5951045748341604352_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/new-world-class-office-opens-in-cagayan-de-oro/73417764_442159659741243_5951045748341604352_n/" class="wp-image-4556"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73018612_425976118059352_3856772806654033920_n-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4547" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/73018612_425976118059352_3856772806654033920_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/47th-filipino-homes-office-opens/73018612_425976118059352_3856772806654033920_n/" class="wp-image-4547"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/fb_img_1571384846508364584979434862178-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4541" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/fb_img_1571384846508364584979434862178.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/fb_img_1571384846508364584979434862178-jpg/" class="wp-image-4541"/></figure></li></ul></figure>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In our commitment to service, Filipino Homes opened a total of 9 additional offices all over the Philippines to best serve our clients. [<a href="http://localhost:3001/?s=new+office">Related posts here]</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Year end highlights of 2019. Looking back at how well we were in 2019 to start working for our 2020.','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2019/10/73074811_2476802252565873_2162899015769784320_n.jpg','views' => '40','category_id' => '10','published_at' => '2020-01-02 06:25:54','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '378','title' => 'Fahstwalls Systems Technology; Aides Faster Construction','slug' => 'fahstwalls-systems-technology-aides-faster-construction','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes committed to helping the government in addressing the shortage of housing developments as fast as we can. Filipino Homes Plus, a build and sell company of Filipino Homes is now using Fastwalls Systems in its upcoming projects to build fast and quality house and lot projects in the Philippines. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4809,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/77200693_10215716871257527_7663302428749463552_o.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4809"/><figcaption> Meeting with Jay Yuvallos and Mike Basubas, whom we will be helping in marketing the Fastwalls System. Soon, everyone can benefit from one of the best in construction technologies utilized in the USA and Canada today.  11.21.2019</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href="https://fahstwall.com/">FAHSTWALL SYSTEMS</a> offers fast, cost-effective, and space-saving walling for homes, offices, and commercial buildings. Their pre-cast panels are made from a composite of concrete, EPS granules, organic and inorganic fibers, and coal powder; sandwiched by moisture-proof calcium silicate boards on both faces and fused together by high strength binders through a systematic curing production process that guarantees high quality and stable product.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Advantages of using<a href="https://fahstwall.com/"> Fahst Wall Systems</a></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4> THERMALLY EFFICIENT AND GREEN </h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The lightweight materials used in the panels are 1/6th the weight of normal 120mm thick brick walls and 60% lighter than traditional hollow blocks. This minimizes the load on the beams and columns which equates to significant cost reduction on the structural frame of the building. The panels are also moisture-proof, water-resistant and ready for painting as soon as they are installed and joined using our firm sealant and adhesive. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>STRUCTURALLY SAFE AND ECONOMICAL </h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The tongue and groove design of the wall panels are attached and secured using a firm sealant and adhesive. This transforms multiple wall panels into one sturdy wall with impact resistance and bending qualities that are better than traditional brick walls secured with ordinary cement. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>HIGHLY SEISMIC RESILIENT </h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A 42dB sound insulation test result complies with the National Insulation Test Standard GBJ121-88. Minimal sound t Minimal sound transmission and noise reduction are accomplished due to the higher density and unique composition of the wall panel material. This results in a more comfortable and quiet environment without the need to use any additional insulation products thereby saving on costs. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>ACOUSTICALLY EFFECTIVE </h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The precast wall panels feature a tongue and groove design that reduces installation times increase labor efficiency and save on costs. Electrical and plumbing installations can be completed 5 – 10 times faster when compared to using traditional hollow blocks. FAHSTWALL panels were also tested to withstand up to 1,000°C for 120 minutes and compliant to the standard for Grade A Fireproof Material. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4956,4957,4958,4959]} -->
<figure class="wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped"><ul class="blocks-gallery-grid"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/74911776_10215353402415632_3566503596642009088_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4956" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/74911776_10215353402415632_3566503596642009088_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4956" class="wp-image-4956"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/76609855_10215353402175626_4989672062785159168_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4957" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/76609855_10215353402175626_4989672062785159168_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4957" class="wp-image-4957"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/78596362_10215353401895619_386739338030874624_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4958" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/78596362_10215353401895619_386739338030874624_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4958" class="wp-image-4958"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/78647918_10215353402695639_692891517492133888_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="4959" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/78647918_10215353402695639_692891517492133888_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4959" class="wp-image-4959"/></figure></li></ul></figure>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>REB Marlou Hinay, one of the brokers of Filipino Homes in Butuan City who is also the CEO of Marrea Estates Corporation in Bayugan City, uses this technology in their projects, testified that the Fahst Wall Systems is making them efficient, cost-effective and fast building time of their houses. In a day, they can finish a cluster. It is easy to assemble and durable. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/02/Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape-2.png','views' => '43','category_id' => '11','published_at' => '2020-01-07 11:30:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '379','title' => 'Filipino Homes arrives in Dubai for the Philippine Property Roadshow 2020','slug' => 'filipino-homes-arrives-in-dubai-for-the-philippine-property-roadshow-2020','content' => '<!-- wp:image {"id":4844,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/filipino-homes-dubai.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4844"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes is committed to helping Filipinos own homes and give the best advice from the best real estate agents and brokers in the country. Filipino Homes in partnership with Cebu Landmasters Inc. once again visits Dubai, United Arab Emirates. Last January 23, 2020, the first batch of  130 agents and brokers Filipino Homes team arrived in Dubai UAE together with the Filipino Homes founder and the country\'s number one (1) broker in the Philippines, Mr. Anthony Gerard O. Leuterio. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4780,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/79846011_510274549576610_5636085656108138496_n-1024x536.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4780"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Dubai Experience wouldn\'t be complete without experiencing Dubai Safari, and so on our first day, just a few hours after our arrival we went for an adventure. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>Dubai Desert Safari Tour </strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Dune Bashing</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[4850,4848,4846,4845,4847,4849]} -->
<figure class="wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped"><ul class="blocks-gallery-grid"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/84273492_185238105867229_1240489758853955584_n-1024x824.jpg" alt="" data-id="4850" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/84273492_185238105867229_1240489758853955584_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4850" class="wp-image-4850"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/82911741_176382976797771_903394680782192640_n-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4848" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/82911741_176382976797771_903394680782192640_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4848" class="wp-image-4848"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/82854994_632553744168832_8020837123038904320_n-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4846" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/82854994_632553744168832_8020837123038904320_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4846" class="wp-image-4846"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/82822829_628149504612290_3874097089818394624_n-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4845" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/82822829_628149504612290_3874097089818394624_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4845" class="wp-image-4845"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/82910606_661081071377385_760834305227227136_n-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4847" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/82910606_661081071377385_760834305227227136_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4847" class="wp-image-4847"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/83023938_525842248137802_8926433210783498240_n-1024x768.jpg" alt="" data-id="4849" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/83023938_525842248137802_8926433210783498240_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=4849" class="wp-image-4849"/></figure></li></ul><figcaption class="blocks-gallery-caption"> The desert safari is a roaring example of Dubai’s tryst with both modernity and ancient culture . 14 Land Cruisers and Sequia for Filipino Homes batch 1 </figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Camel Ride &amp; the Arabian Eagle</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":["4856",4864,4865]} -->
