  array('id' => '390','title' => 'Official warns of illegal housing projects in Davao region','slug' => 'official-warns-of-illegal-housing-projects-in-davao-region','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A news was published last March1, 2020 about this, that you might be interested to read more about it here <a href="https://news.mb.com.ph/2020/03/01/official-warns-of-illegal-housing-projects-in-davao-region/">[LINK HERE]</a>. This is somewhat related to the previous post I have written here before about <a href="http://localhost:3001/buying-agricultural-lot-residential-yuta-data-data/">"Yuta Data-Data"</a> system that is very rampant online. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5058,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/o_1aqa5bjfa1ofqobh85qt38sok7.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5058"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We all know that it is almost everyone\'s dream to own a house that we can call home. The problem is, we would always look for and choose a property that is affordable and cheap. Hoping that what we got is something that is worth the price. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5059,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Residential-Subdivision-banner-Indovance.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5059"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Please don\'t get me wrong, I myself also wanted to own a property at a cheapest price possible. But I don\'t want to deal with the hassle of buying illegally put up subdivisions. People thought that by simply subdividing a property and have it partitioned and titled is the most legal thing to do. Selling it little by little to escape the taxes and possible fees of putting up a subdivision. If you wanted to do it the legal way, <a href="http://hlurb.gov.ph/wp-content/uploads/Transparency-Governance/manuals/PRLD_REGISTRATION.pdf">check the guidelines here. </a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As a buyer, you must protect yourself and your investment by doing due diligence. If someone is selling you a subdivided lot, here are the things that you need to check;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} -->
<ol><li>Check the subdivision plan. Notice if drainage system are in place and each lot has a right of way. </li><li>Look for individual titles of the property. If the property is still in it\'s mother title and not yet partitioned, BEWARE. </li><li>If the partition of lots is more than 8 lots, or marketed/sold commercially, Looking for the License to SELL Or LTS NUmber of the Subdivison. If it is something that they cannot and provide, consider it a RED Flag. Even if the property has the best location in town. You might end up in tears. </li></ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There are a lot of factors before this subdivisions can be called Legal. But selling and building a subdivision without a license is definitely illegal. Protect your hard earned money, buy only from Developers with license to sell and legit real estate agents and brokers. They will help you find the best investment all the way. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/03/awards-Filipinohomes-blog-xyzayape-1.png','views' => '40','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2020-03-03 23:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '391','title' => 'Real Estate Investing in the Philippines this year 2020','slug' => 'real-estate-investing-in-the-philippines-this-year-2020','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So&nbsp;far&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;Philippines,&nbsp;the&nbsp;real&nbsp;estate&nbsp;industry&nbsp;has&nbsp;been&nbsp;steadily&nbsp;growing&nbsp;and&nbsp;looks&nbsp;forward&nbsp;to&nbsp;going&nbsp;forward&nbsp;in&nbsp;2020&nbsp;and&nbsp;beyond.&nbsp;There&nbsp;are&nbsp;many&nbsp;ways&nbsp;to&nbsp;start&nbsp;investing&nbsp;in&nbsp;immovable&nbsp;property,&nbsp;and&nbsp;some&nbsp;of&nbsp;them&nbsp;require&nbsp;little&nbsp;effort&nbsp;other&nbsp;than&nbsp;a financial&nbsp;investment. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5213,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2020-03-27-at-12.53.30-AM-1024x473.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5213"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Check the options that are available with the budget you have on hand to start investing in the real estate market. You can buy land and rent it, buy and rent a residential area, or revamp and sell the cheap foreclosed property at a high price.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Because of its stress-free guarantee, projects such as <strong>condotel investment </strong>have gained popularity. Essentially how it works is to purchase a condo unit and rent it out on a long-term or short-term basis (such as a hotel). Realty companies are responsible for attracting tenants, providing the services and running the property while you enjoy all the benefits. Property Management Companies, however, like Ascott Limited, will strictly manage the property to ensure the quality of service and consistency of experience across all of their condotels in the world. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The thing about investing in real estate is that you will not only receive a stable income, but you will also have your own property that you can use if or when you decide to retire. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Condotels and Serviced Companies that you can invest in today;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} -->
<ol><li><a href="https://www.cebulandmasters.com/project/citadines-paragon-davao/">Citadines at One Paragon Davao of Cebu Landmasters Inc.</a></li><li><a href="https://filipinohomes.ph/condominium/tambuli-seaside-living/eg==/dXU=">Tambuli Seaside Living by Tytans Properties and Development, Inc.</a></li><li><a href="https://www.cebulandmasters.com/project/radisson-red/">Radisson Red at One Astra Residences of Cebu Landmasters Inc. </a></li><li><a href="https://worldwidecentralproperties.com/properties/">Vitale Suites of World Wide Central Property Developments</a></li><li><a href="https://worldwidecentralproperties.com/the-suites-at-gorordo/">Gorordo Suites of World Wide Central Property Developments</a></li></ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>and more. Contact your Filipino Homes Agent for your available options today. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/03/Filipinohomes-blogger-realtor-real-estate-agent-xyza-yape-3.png','views' => '44','category_id' => '10','published_at' => '2020-03-07 14:07:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '392','title' => 'Metro Manila Under Quarantine','slug' => 'metro-manila-under-quarantine','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>President Duterte in a press conference on 12 March 2020 gave updates on precautionary measures the government is taking to prevent further spread of COVID-19 in the Philippines after raising the Covid-19 Alert to Code Red SubLevel 2. <br><br>Covid-19  or “coronavirus disease 2019” is caused by “SARSCoV 2” has first been detected at Wuhan, China. With the increasing number or infected individual in the Philippines, the Philippine government had raised the Covid-19 Alert Code to it\'s highest level.<br><br>Below are the some of the important points pertaining to this alert &amp; precautionary measures:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Flexible work arrangement encouraged in private sector. Manufacturing and retail businesses encouraged to stay open with social distancing and minimal work force. </li><li>Mass public transport (MRT/LRT) shall continue operation with social distancing. </li><li><strong>Domestic air, sea and land transport suspended from March 15, 2020 (12 midnight) to April 14, 2020</strong>, subject to the review of inter-agency task force.</li><li>Stringent social distancing measures in NCR for 30 days. </li><li><strong>Suspension of classes in all levels in Metro Manila</strong> until April 12, 2020. </li><li>Mass gatherings, either planned or spontaneous shall be prohibited during this period. If rules in social distancing is not followed, it can be punishable under the penal code and can be arrested by military and police.</li><li><strong>Community quarantine is hereby imposed in the entire of Metro Manila.</strong></li><li>In other areas, LGUs can impose localized quarantine.</li><li>Provincial quarantine if more than 2 positive COVID-19 cases. </li><li>Municipality or city wide quarantine advised if 2 positive COVID-19 cases or more.</li><li>Baranggay-wide quarantine is advised if there are 2 or more COVID-19 cases.</li><li>LGUs outside NCR advised to exercise sound discretion to suspend classes, but does not allow you to suspend classes for trivial reasons. </li><li>PNP and AFP shall be called upon for effective and orderly implementation of above measures. This is not martial law. Do not be afraid of the PNP and AFP. They are there to help you.</li><li>OFWs allowed to travel to Mainland China except to Hubei. </li><li>Entry travel restriction imposed to all countries with COVID-19 cases, exept for Filipinos and their families, permanent visa holders and diplomats. </li><li>COVID-19 tests are free.</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It is best that we take the precautionary measures to prevent infection and spread of the disease.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/03/Metro-Manila-Under-Quarantine.png','views' => '31','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2020-03-13 05:25:42','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '393','title' => 'How to Keep Your Family & Home Safe from COVID-19','slug' => 'how-to-keep-your-family-home-safe-from-covid-19','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The news COVID-19 travel bans increasing number of infected cases with the respiratory disease outbreak caused by a novel (new) coronavirus is alarming. It has now been detected in almost 70 locations internationally and increasing number in the Philippines. <br><br>The virus has been named “SARS-CoV-2” causing the “coronavirus disease 2019” or “COVID-19” has first been detected at Wuhan, China. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>How can I make sure my family is safe from COVID-19?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} -->
<ol><li>Regularly wash your hands with soap and water regularly for at least 20 seconds.</li><li>If soap and water are not readily available, use an alcohol-based hand sanitizer that contains 60%–95% alcohol</li><li>Wash hands hands after going to the bathroom; before eating; and after coughing, sneezing or blowing your nose</li><li>If you can help it, don\'t touch or hold any public surfaces like elevator buttons, door handles, escalator hand railings, etc. If you need to, always wash your hands or use sanitizer that contains 60%–95% alcohol before touching your face</li><li>Maintain social distancing by avoiding large crowds</li><li>Maintain a healthy diet &amp; increase your body\'s immunity to prevent easy infection</li></ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/03/How-to-Keep-Your-Family-Home-Safe-from-COVID-19.png','views' => '43','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2020-03-14 02:45:35','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '394','title' => 'Stuck at home? 5 Tips to Actually be Productive When You\'re Working From Home','slug' => '5-tips-to-actually-be-productive-when-working-from-home','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> As&nbsp;<a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label=" (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/metro-manila-under-quarantine/" target="_blank">the national government has raised the COVID-19 alert to Code Red Sublevel 2</a> and placed the National Capital Region (NCR) under community quarantine to curb the spread of coronavirus (COVID-19), companies are encouraged to offer work-from-home options for their employees.  While the zero commute time, the ability to work in our pajamas, and flexibility over our work schedule may sound like a dream; working from home also has its challenges.  First on the list are the interruptions from children, family, neighbors, and friends that may be very disruptive to our work process. &nbsp;As someone who has worked remotely for a decade, I\'m sharing <strong>some tips on how you can stay productive while working from home</strong>:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1534166998141-a8746ef4ab6e?ixlib=rb-1.2.1&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;w=750&amp;q=80" alt=""/><figcaption> Photo by&nbsp;<a href="https://unsplash.com/@escape_from_reality?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">Djurdjica Boskovic</a>&nbsp;on&nbsp;<a href="https://unsplash.com/s/photos/work-from-home?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">Unsplash</a> </figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>1.  <strong>Make yourself a home office setup.&nbsp;</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Keep away from your bed or couch while working.  Taking your laptop to work on your bed or maybe plopping down on the couch in front of the television will definitely present many temptations.&nbsp; If you can, make yourself an office, or at least a work station area.  Dedicate a space for your work to create clear boundaries between your work and home life.&nbsp; <br><br>Make sure you\'ll have easy access to things that you might need to get your work done. You may need to consider access to wi-fi or LAN connection, phone line, or printer. &nbsp;If you can, invest in a good desk and chair so you’ll be comfortable enough to finish your tasks, but not too comfortable to be tempted to slack off.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513128034602-7814ccaddd4e?ixlib=rb-1.2.1&amp;ixid=eyJhcHBfaWQiOjEyMDd9&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;w=675&amp;q=80" alt=""/><figcaption> Photo by&nbsp;<a href="https://unsplash.com/@stilclassics?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">STIL</a>&nbsp;on&nbsp;<a href="https://unsplash.com/s/photos/planner?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">Unsplash</a> </figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>2. <strong>Create a to-do list for the tasks you need to accomplish.&nbsp;</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>To help you visualize your progress and keep you on task, having a checklist of the things you need to get done can help. Use apps if you need to. Personally, I find using <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="Getting Things Done | GTD Simple Free (opens in a new tab)" href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.dudziks.gtd&amp;hl=en" target="_blank">Getting Things Done | GTD Simple Free</a> and Trello helpful in creating task lists. Check out some other <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="FREE apps that help keep me organized and productive here.  (opens in a new tab)" href="https://lovettejam.com/productivity-apps-for-the-multi-passionate-freelancer/" target="_blank">FREE apps that help keep me organized and productive here. </a>  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1517292987719-0369a794ec0f?ixlib=rb-1.2.1&amp;ixid=eyJhcHBfaWQiOjEyMDd9&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;w=667&amp;q=80" alt=""/><figcaption> Photo by&nbsp;<a href="https://unsplash.com/@timbennettcreative?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">Tim Bennett</a>&nbsp;on&nbsp;<a href="https://unsplash.com/s/photos/blocked-social-media?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">Unsplash</a> </figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>3. <strong>Minimize distractions and set limits online.&nbsp;</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We all know how easy it is to get sucked into the distractions of the internet. Working remotely can make this temptation harder to resist. Before you get trapped into unproductive scrolling on social media sites, set limits on when you can wander off on your browser (or your phone!). &nbsp;When it’s work time, make sure to close any non-work-related tabs and websites. I use the Google Chrome extension <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="Nudge  (opens in a new tab)" href="https://chrome.google.com/webstore/detail/nudge/dmhgdnbkjkejeddddlklojinngaideac" target="_blank">Nudge </a>to block (or at least limit my access to some websites). On my phone, I installed the <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="Stay Focused app (opens in a new tab)" href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.stayfocused&amp;hl=en" target="_blank">Stay Focused app</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1490724500206-cd5482e02b9e?ixlib=rb-1.2.1&amp;ixid=eyJhcHBfaWQiOjEyMDd9&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;w=750&amp;q=80" alt=""/><figcaption> Photo by&nbsp;<a href="https://unsplash.com/@freestocks?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">freestocks</a>&nbsp;on&nbsp;<a href="https://unsplash.com/s/photos/work-time?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">Unsplash</a> </figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>4. <strong>Establish blocks of work time</strong>.</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>I can\'t stress this enough: While a work-from-home setup can give you flexible hours, disruptions can keep you unproductive. &nbsp;To help keep you on track, try to establish your work hours. You may need to follow your previous office hours to keep you in the zone, so to speak.  Of course, you can choose blocks of work time that best fit your schedule. For example, if you need to get in 8 hours of work per day, make 3 time blocks of 3 hours, 2 hours, and another 3 hours. &nbsp;This allows you to have time to take care of other things, like preparing meals for the family or cleaning the house, outside your work time or during your “breaks.” </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1471560090527-d1af5e4e6eb6?ixlib=rb-1.2.1&amp;ixid=eyJhcHBfaWQiOjEyMDd9&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;w=750&amp;q=80" alt=""/><figcaption> Photo by&nbsp;<a href="https://unsplash.com/@drewcoffman?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">Drew Coffman</a>&nbsp;on&nbsp;<a href="https://unsplash.com/s/photos/relax-home?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">Unsplash</a> </figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2> 5. <strong>Take care of yourself.</strong>&nbsp;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Don\'t forget to take good care of yourself.  Take breaks and keep your mealtimes sacred. Always remember to hydrate and find time to relax. Some also find it helpful to dress as if they were going to work to keep their productivity in check. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Related posts</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

