<!-- /wp:separator -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/03/Copy-of-filipino-homes-1.png','views' => '48','category_id' => '13','published_at' => '2020-03-15 00:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '395','title' => 'PH Property Sector Remains Optimistic Amid COVID-19 Threat','slug' => 'ph-property-sector-remains-optimistic-amid-covid-19-threat','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The year 2020 is looking to be a challenging year for the Philippine stock market and other equities markets across the globe to the negative impact of COVID-19&nbsp;[<a href="https://www.philstar.com/business/2020/03/09/1999164/philippines-braces-covid-19-impact">1</a>]. However, real estate firms and property market specialists remain positive that the industry will be resilient against this current threat [<a href="https://business.inquirer.net/292504/ph-realty-sector-remains-hopeful-amid-threat#ixzz6GciDEy00">2</a>]. &nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) is an infectious disease caused by a new strain of coronavirus (SARS-CoV-2) that had not been previously identified in humans. Since reports of the outbreak came out in December 2019, COVID-19 has since spread to 143 countries and territories, causing 5,735 deaths and affecting over 153,000 others as of 15 March 2020 [<a href="https://www.doh.gov.ph/COVID-19/FAQs">3</a>, <a href="https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/situation-reports/">4</a>].</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In a press briefing in Makati, Ms. Monique Pronove, Pronove Tai’s president and chief executive officer, said the impact of COVID-19 on real estate will already be felt in the first half of 2020, with the segments being affected differently [<a href="https://www.moneysense.com.ph/covid-19-to-impact-the-philippine-property-sector-in-first-half-of-2020-pronove-tai/?fbclid=IwAR3dD2NOe3aVz6-6nB1xC2YRFPSPCr4Fw9dkHisRuGc9o__sQUoFGrjVIfI">5</a>, <a href="https://www.bworldonline.com/hysteria-over-coronavirus-hurting-malls-hotels/?fbclid=IwAR2F4VWP6xnYVIG7EiYutFVBFWVjlHs-FyoII1NO3sWLO9K9C6RDMK3ufZ4">6</a>].</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5117,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/anmol-seth-hDbCjHNdF48-unsplash-1024x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5117"/><figcaption> Photo by&nbsp;<a href="https://unsplash.com/@anmol_seth?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">Anmol Seth</a>&nbsp;on&nbsp;<a href="https://unsplash.com/s/photos/hotel?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">Unsplash</a> </figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Hotels and Hospitality Market</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The hospitality sector, including hotels, resorts, and convention centers, will be heavily affected in the short- to medium-term. Occupancy levels are expected to drastically decrease due to lower tourist arrivals as well as the temporary postponement of large MICE (meetings, incentives, conferences, and exhibitions) events.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5119,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/2073442492_92a2f01605_h-1024x768.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5119"/><figcaption>   Photo by&nbsp; <a href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/acullador/">Jun Acullador</a> on <a href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/10435379@N02/2073442492/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="Flickr (opens in a new tab)">Flickr</a><br> </figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Retail Property Market</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Major retail, commercial, and
entertainment centers will likewise be
affected by COVID-19 as these areas are expected to experience lower foot
traffic. Mass hysteria will cause people to
not go out to eat, shop, or for entertainment. It’s really the retail centers
that are tenanted by non-essential items that will be affected.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In a recent RCBC Securities report, SM Prime Holdings Inc. expects a 10- to 20-percent fallout in average daily mall foot traffic and softer revenue for SM retail in the first quarter of 2020. Other mall operators, including Ayala Land Inc., Robinsons Land Corp., Double Dragon, Megaworld, and Rockwell Land will also likely feel the impact of less foot traffic as a result of the COVID-19 threat [<a href="https://www.philstar.com/business/2020/03/09/1999164/philippines-braces-covid-19-impact">7</a>].</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5120,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/cityscape-of-manila-philippines-from-a-balcony.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5120"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Office Property Market</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The office property market is generally seen to be resilient. Pronove disclosed that 54 percent of the office stock is occupied by traditional companies who have started—or expected to start—business continuity plans. Thirty-three percent of the office stock is occupied by BPOs, knowledge process outsourcing and IT, while 11 percent of the office market is tenanted by flexible workspaces [<a href="https://www.philstar.com/business/2020/03/09/1999164/philippines-braces-covid-19-impact">7</a>].</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Country Manager of International Workplace Group (IWG), Lars Wittig,  points out that business continuity can still be ensured should companies opt for a <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="work-from-home arrangement (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/5-tips-to-actually-be-productive-when-working-from-home/" target="_blank">work-from-home arrangement</a>. Witting said they have a network of flexible workspace close to people’s homes—not just in the central Metro Manila but also in the suburbs and other cities, from Pampanga all the way to Cebu and Davao [<a href="https://business.inquirer.net/292504/ph-realty-sector-remains-hopeful-amid-threat#ixzz6GciDEy00">2</a>].  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>However, the office take-up of Philippine offshore gaming operators (POGOs) is seen to slow down this year due to the pandemic, according to the real estate consultancy services firm Lobien Realty Group Inc. They are delaying expansion at the moment, probably until the situation improves [<a href="https://www.manilatimes.net/2020/03/14/business/business-top/pogo-office-market-to-slump-amid-covid-19/702923/">8</a>].   Prior to the Covid-19, POGO activities were propelling the real estate market, driving demands in both office and residential markets [<a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="9 (opens in a new tab)" href="https://www.pna.gov.ph/articles/1096231" target="_blank">9</a>].</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4571,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Citadines_Cebu_City_1BR_Living_Dining_750x490.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4571"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Residential Property Market</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Minimal impact is seen for the residential market, not slowing down despite the COVID-19 outbreak.  Catherine Ko, executive vice president of Federal Land Inc. and president of Sunshine Fort North Bonifacio Realty Development Corp., said they are not feeling the effect yet. Postponement of buying may be seen, but not to cancel outright.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>PHINMA Property Holdings Corp. Chief Executive Officer Raphael Felix noted that demand was still growing even outside Metro Manila.  Felix also pointed out the pent-up demand in the residential market.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>“We can’t supply it (the demand) fast enough. Despite what people think of the real estate industry producing so many units, on the contrary, it is not. Over the last two years, production has been dropping so it has made things more scarce,” Felix said. “Plus there’s a concentration of this virus scare in Metro Manila. There are so many other places out there. The regions are booming. In fact, there is more growth in the regions now. I don’t see it (real estate sector) slowing unless this (COVID-19) escalates rapidly.”   [<a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="10 (opens in a new tab)" href="https://www.manilatimes.net/2020/03/12/business/business-top/covid-19-wont-slow-down-residential-market/702583/" target="_blank">10</a>] </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>REITs </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Rick Santos, Chairman &amp; CEO of Santos Knight Frank,  said the Philippine real estate industry continues to have reasons to be optimistic despite the impact of COVID-19 and downturn in international stock markets. Santos cited various drivers, including the roll-out of REITs, continuous expansion of BPO companies, and strong consumer demand [<a href="https://business.mb.com.ph/2020/03/07/reits-reinforce-optimism-in-ph-real-estate-industry/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="11 (opens in a new tab)">11</a>].</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Santos Knight Frank believes that <a href="http://localhost:3001/millennials-can-invest-real-estate/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="REITs (opens in a new tab)">REITs</a> will unlock a number of opportunities in the property market, such as greater access to real estate investment and revitalization of capital markets.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>“We anticipate that REITs will drive an increase in acquisition, consolidation, and property development activities across the Philippines in the coming years. The new capital raised by the developers through REITs will enable expansion of the real estate sector not only in Metro Manila but also in the provinces, and with it generate jobs across many sectors,” says Kash Salvador, Associate Director for Investment &amp; Capital Markets, Santos Knight Frank  [<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://business.mb.com.ph/2020/03/07/reits-reinforce-optimism-in-ph-real-estate-industry/" target="_blank">11</a>]. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>What This Means For You</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Real estate experts confirm that the state of the Philippine real estate industry remains optimistic despite the COVID-19 threat.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you are looking for opportunities to increase your passive income, it is still a good time to invest in the real estate market. Talk to a&nbsp;<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/what-are-the-different-real-estate-professionals/" target="_blank">professional real estate service provider</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/03/Copy-of-Copy-of-filipino-homes.png','views' => '36','category_id' => '15','published_at' => '2020-03-17 22:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '396','title' => 'What Sites to Follow for Official COVID-19 Updates?','slug' => 'what-sites-to-follow-for-official-covid-19-updates','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As people are strongly advised to stay home and observe social distancing as much as possible to prevent the spread of the novel coronavirus, social media has, now more than ever, become a much appealing way to stay in contact with friends, family, and colleagues. However, whether we like it or not, social media can also be a  source of misinformation and bad advice. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In these trying times, we need to fight fake news and misinformation on the pandemic,  which could spread as quickly, and be as fatal, as the virus itself. We call on a more responsible use of social media and encourage everyone to check health-related information about the outbreak from established news and health sources rather than from shared stories in social media. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here are some websites and social media accounts to follow for official updates:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>World Health Organization</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="data:image/png;base64," alt=""/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Follow <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="World Health Organization (opens in a new tab)" href="https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019" target="_blank">World Health Organization</a> [link:  <a href="https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019">https://www.who.int/]</a> for official updates on the coronavirus outbreak. The site contains everything you need to know about COVID-19, including <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="answers to frequently asked questions (opens in a new tab)" href="https://www.who.int/news-room/q-a-detail/q-a-coronaviruses" target="_blank">answers to frequently asked questions</a>, <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="press briefing (opens in a new tab)" href="https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/media-resources/press-briefings" target="_blank">press briefings</a>, <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="situation dashboard (opens in a new tab)" href="https://experience.arcgis.com/experience/685d0ace521648f8a5beeeee1b9125cd" target="_blank">situation dashboard</a>, and tips and advice for the public on how to <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="protect yourself and others against the virus (opens in a new tab)" href="https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public" target="_blank">protect yourself and others against the virus</a>. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Social Media Sites:</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Facebook: <a href="https://www.facebook.com/WHO">https://www.facebook.com/WHO</a>/</li><li>Facebook (PH): <a href="https://www.facebook.com/whophilippines">https://www.facebook.com/whophilippines</a> </li><li>Tiktok:  <a href="https://www.tiktok.com/@who">https://www.tiktok.com/@who</a> </li><li>Instagram:  <a href="https://www.instagram.com/whophilippines">https://www.instagram.com/whophilippines</a> </li><li>Twitter:  <a href="https://twitter.com/WHOPhilippines">https://twitter.com/WHOPhilippines</a> </li><li>YouTube:  <a href="https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCADc3xF4LpddrTrOTfXE6mQ">https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCADc3xF4LpddrTrOTfXE6mQ</a> </li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>COVID-19 PH Government Portal</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5161,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/covid19ph-1024x693.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5161"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The site, <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://l.facebook.com/l.php?u=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.covid19.gov.ph%2F%3Ffbclid%3DIwAR2vQHaqHSr-LQOofRlNU-wsAuu8oTN_Fc76whrrD31B-YDXSXi3zPZ3f5Y&amp;h=AT3oHTn_AtqpaPsg8WWYGsWgJxB8oXaw9UE6Bo5G_TiFPcz6_QBo8-S5M0avr69tEejWlqDltwG-1II-YfhJc4NYQSr5wpUC9WF4FWVj4DxEC3CSyYvnMLSraVeWSQmcXD5LBjmQ_kC5V-FmVpp_O_olSiKJ" target="_blank">www.covid19.gov.ph</a>, is the government portal led by the Presidential Communications Operations Office (PCOO). The portal serves as:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} -->
<ol><li>News  aggregator (Phil News Agency, Phil Information Agency, PTV) ;</li><li>Issuances aggregator  (Presidential proclamations, department orders, memorandum circulars, etc.) ;</li><li>Heat map of confirmed cases and recovered patients based on latest DOH data;</li><li>Videos on demand (President Duterte’s messages, Laging Handa Public Briefings, and Press Briefings);</li><li>FAQs; and</li><li>Video campaigns.</li></ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Soon to be included in updated versions are:<br>1. IATF corner;<br>2. Bayanihan stories of HOPE; and<br>3. <a href="https://www.facebook.com/hashtag/dismissdisinformation?source=feed_text&amp;epa=HASHTAG">#DismissDisinformation</a> - correcting fake news.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>DOH Official Website</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="data:image/png;base64," alt=""/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Department of Health (DOH) [link:  <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.doh.gov.ph/2019-nCoV?fbclid=IwAR2JdSYlBxIg14Y00hNVOIfpvO_TKAYrJVN7mLzjmHsjRMBhbuhJhzkejKU" target="_blank">https://www.doh.gov.ph/2019-nCoV</a>] is our national health authority. The website provides updates on the status of COVID-19 here in the Philippines. Check the website for <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="FAQ published in Filipino (opens in a new tab)" href="https://www.doh.gov.ph/COVID-19/FAQs-Filipino" target="_blank">FAQs published in Filipino</a>, <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="public advisories also in Filipino (opens in a new tab)" href="https://www.doh.gov.ph/COVID-19/Gabay-sa-Publiko" target="_blank">public advisories also in Filipino</a>, <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="COVID-19 Case Tracker (opens in a new tab)" href="https://ncovtracker.doh.gov.ph/" target="_blank">COVID-19 Case Tracker</a>, <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="press briefing (opens in a new tab)" href="https://www.doh.gov.ph/2019-ncov-presscon" target="_blank">press briefing</a>, and some useful <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="infographics you can use to spread awareness (opens in a new tab)" href="https://www.doh.gov.ph/2019-nCov/infographics" target="_blank">infographics you can use to spread awareness</a> about the novel coronavirus.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Social Media Sites:</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Facebook:  <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label=" (opens in a new tab)" href="https://www.facebook.com/OfficialDOHgov/" target="_blank">https://www.facebook.com/OfficialDOHgov/</a> </li><li>Twitter: <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label=" (opens in a new tab)" href="https://twitter.com/officialdohgov" target="_blank">https://twitter.com/officialdohgov</a> </li><li>YouTube: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/channel/UChZQaAATaHjT_wG-kac3qfA">https://www.youtube.com/channel/UChZQaAATaHjT_wG-kac3qfA</a></li><li>Tiktok:  <a href="https://www.tiktok.com/@dohgovph">https://www.tiktok.com/@dohgovph</a></li><li> Viber: <a href="https://invite.viber.com/?g2=AQBloG%2B2iYcA9Ess%2BlEA7D6mSoLKBx642avqJSzYpecNd3Ah1SR%2FW1ZNR0K2OrQY&amp;fbclid=IwAR3pvPUxqrh9F13fjluApocoL9Pgoy4B9FU113CBhMEUKTcRNI-OeX-5BSk&amp;lang=en" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="Join DOH PH COVID-19 on Viber (opens in a new tab)">Join DOH PH COVID-19 on Viber</a></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Reliable News Sources</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://thenthattempt.files.wordpress.com/2015/08/logos.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We can also check established news sites for verified information about the global pandemic. Here are some web pages that compile updates. You may also opt to follow their official social media sites to keep updated:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><strong>CNN Philippines</strong>:  <a href="https://cnnphilippines.com/news/2020/3/17/Live-updates-coronavirus-covid-19-Philippines.html">https://cnnphilippines.com/news/2020/3/17/Live-updates-coronavirus-covid-19-Philippines.html</a> </li><li><strong>Inquirer.net: </strong> <a href="https://www.inquirer.net/novel-coronavirus-update">https://www.inquirer.net/novel-coronavirus-update</a> </li><li><strong>Philstar: </strong> <a href="https://www.philstar.com/tags/novel-coronavirus">https://www.philstar.com/tags/novel-coronavirus</a> </li><li><strong>Manila Bulletin: </strong> <a href="https://news.mb.com.ph/tag/ncov/">https://news.mb.com.ph/tag/ncov/</a> </li><li><strong>Rappler: </strong> <a href="https://www.rappler.com/nation/250663-novel-coronavirus-outbreak">https://www.rappler.com/nation/250663-novel-coronavirus-outbreak</a> </li><li><strong>Philippine Information Agency (PIA):  </strong> <a href="https://pia.gov.ph/news/search?q=covid">https://pia.gov.ph/news/search?q=covid</a> </li><li><strong>ABS-CBN News: </strong> <a href="https://news.abs-cbn.com/list/tag/coronavirus">https://news.abs-cbn.com/list/tag/coronavirus</a> </li><li><strong>GMA News:  </strong><a href="https://www.gmanetwork.com/search/?q=covid">https://www.gmanetwork.com/search/?q=covid</a> </li><li><strong>Interaksyon</strong>:  <a href="https://www.interaksyon.com/search/covid">https://www.interaksyon.com/search/covid</a> </li><li><strong>Sunstar:</strong>  <a href="https://www.sunstar.com.ph/COVID19">https://www.sunstar.com.ph/COVID19</a> </li><li><strong>Philippine News Agency: </strong> <a href="https://www.pna.gov.ph/articles/search?q=covid">https://www.pna.gov.ph/articles/search?q=covid</a> </li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Your Local Government Authority</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>To get updates about your COVID-19 in your locality, you may check the official Facebook accounts of your local government unit (LGU) or your local information and health offices. You can also follow local news agencies in your area on social media. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Let us all be responsible users of social media. Let\'s work together to combat fake news and disinformation while we all find ways to protect ourselves and others from the virus. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'In these trying times, we need to fight fake news and misinformation on the pandemic,  which could spread as quickly, and be as fatal, as the virus itself. We call on a more responsible use of social media and encourage everyone to check health-related information about the outbreak from established news and health sources rather than from shared stories in social media. ','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/03/Copy-of-Copy-of-filipino-homes-1.png','views' => '56','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2020-03-18 21:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '397','title' => 'Filipino Homes Founder Appeals to Developers to  Extend an Equity Holiday to Buyers','slug' => 'filipino-homes-founder-appeals-to-developers-to-extend-an-equity-holiday-to-buyers','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes founder Anthony Gerard Leuterio urged developers to consider relaxing on collections and extending an equity holiday to buyers. He is appealing to real estate developers to give buyers some leeway in paying their dues as they struggle to cope with the lingering effects of the Covid-19 global outbreak. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>“The coronavirus outbreak has posed a serious financial threat to thousands of our buyers. It’s no longer just about the difficulty of stocking up on alcohol and hand sanitizers but about their capability to pay their bills on time,” Leuterio said.<br></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>“In this challenging time, we urge your office to consider relaxing on collections and extending an equity holiday to buyers who are affected in this crisis. On a case-to-case basis, you may make collection forbearance available to some of them. This would involve no longer pursuing late charges or no interest for a certain time frame that you may set,” said Leuterio, in a letter he sent to developers Monday, March 16, 2020.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>“This critical situation provides us an opportunity to establish trust, do some social good beyond the interests of our firm, make a positive impact and showcase what our company represents for our buyers and the community,” the letter added.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leuterio said his company has received calls from overseas Filipino worker (OFW) buyers informing them of their late equity payments due to lockdown.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leuterio also expressed his concerns that many buyers may lose jobs due to the Covid-19 outbreak thus affecting their capability to pay or settle their bills on time.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>“But we know that these OFWs will not cancel their real estate purchases because they need an investment,” he said.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/03/Filipinohomes-.jpg','views' => '43','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2020-03-19 21:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '398','title' => 'Five Basic Requirements When Buying a Property','slug' => 'five-basic-requirements-when-buying-a-property','content' => '<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":5151,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/filipino-homes-leuterio-realty-brokerage-3-410x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5151"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Pick one and pay, how we wish it was just that easy, but the reality is, buying a house needs to be done legally. I often get complaints about the requirements a client must prepare when buying a home. Whether it\'s a house and lot or a condominium that you wish to purchase in the Philippines, you will be required to gather these things and provide to the developer. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Often times, we get these complaints from OFWs or citizens from other countries either former Filipinos or Foreigners. To set the expectations, these requirements are government-mandated or mandated by the Philippine laws that all citizens and investors of the country should and must follow.  Most especially, if you intend to borrow money from a financial institution to fund your purchase. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Here are the five basic requirements you need to prepare if you are buying a home; </h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>1. Two-valid Government-issued ID\'</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Prepare and bring a photocopy of this government-issued ID\'s with you during the reservation of the property. This is to make sure the proper documentation of the purchase. Each ID\'s should match and contain your real complete name.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>For</em> <em> <strong>married</strong> couples, your spouse is also required to provide all the listed requirements</em>. U<em>nless otherwise if you have a pre-nuptial agreement (document) that prohibits your spouse from co-owning the property you are about to purchase. If you\'re a widow or widower, you may be required later on to provide additional documents like the Death Certificate of your spouse as legal proof. </em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>If you are <strong>legally separated,</strong> you will also be required later on a proof of the Finality of marriage. However, if you are not legally separated (complicated status), you will be assumed and will remain married in the eyes of the law, thus will require documents of the spouse, regardless of the signed waiver of rights or number of years apart. </em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>2. Tax Identification Number(s)</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Make sure to bring your <strong><em>TAX IDENTIFICATION CARDS</em></strong> with you with the <em><strong>TAX IDENTIFICATION NUMBER</strong></em>.  You will be required to request the <strong>TIN Verification Slip </strong>issued by the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR). Make sure that the name in the TIN Verification Slip is the same as your legal name. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>If you are in a married status, Make sure you already changed or updated your marital status with BIR. If married, your record should state your married name in the record, unless you chose to still use your maiden name in a married status. [Because females/ladies, have the option to not change their maiden surname to their husbands\' surname name; but it should be consistent with all submitted documents. </em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Purchasing a property is taxable, thus TIN is required. The records of the property you will be purchasing will be attached to your TIN for proper accountability. Some developers require TIN prior to the reservation process. Some developers will allow you to apply for TIN later on, most especially for the OFW\'s or the foreign investors. However, you cannot own property without a TIN. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>3. Proof of Income</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Bring at least 3 months\' worth of payslip or a Certificate of Employment with Compensation if you are locally employed. If you are an OFW, a copy of your latest Job Contract will do. This is for pre-qualification for your home loan. Your agent and the developer will need to make sure that your household income is sufficient for the property you are eyeing to purchase. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If married, both spouses will provide proof of income to complete the household income.  If you are a <a href="http://localhost:3001/apply-housing-loan-online-worker/">FREELANCER or Online Worker, Click this article to help you out with generating your proof of income.</a> </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>4. Proof of Billing</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Bring a copy of your electric bill or phone bills registered to your home address or address where you wish your home loan notices and other purchase notice will be sent. This document is also required to make sure that we will be tagging the right address of the purchaser or buyer in the Contract to Sell, Deed of Sale, Title and other documents necessary for the legality of the purchase.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>5. Reservation Fee or Option Fee if pre-selling; Earnest Money for brokerage sale. </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Bring the required reservation fee or option fee of the property you wish to purchase. You can bring cash or check for the reservation of pre-selling properties. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For brokerage properties, the earnest money is required to show great interest in the property. Earnest Money can be cash or check and is deductible to the total selling price if the buyer decides to complete the purchase. However, just like reservation fees in pre-selling, if the buyer decides to not continue the purchase the reservation fee or earnest money is non-refundable.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Why do you have to prepare these things? </h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Whether you are buying spot cash or loan it from a financing institution, you will need to present these documents (1-4) for proper documentation of the purchase. Details of these documents are needed to make sure that the title of the properties will be transferred to the right person/buyer and that taxes will be paid accordingly. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Pick one and pay, how we wish it was just that easy, but the reality is, buying a house needs to be done legally. I often get complaints about the requirements a client must prepare when buying a home. Whether it\'s a house and lot or a condominium that you wish to purchase in the Philippines, you will be required to gather these things and provide to the developer. ','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/03/Filipinohomes-2.jpg','views' => '97','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-03-20 21:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '399','title' => '5 Easy Home Improvement Projects You Can Do To Keep You Busy','slug' => '5-easy-home-improvement-projects-you-can-do-to-keep-you-busy','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As most of us are stuck at home in efforts to help <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="#FlattenTheCurve (opens in a new tab)" href="https://www.livescience.com/coronavirus-flatten-the-curve.html" target="_blank">#FlattenTheCurve</a>&nbsp;with the ongoing <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="COVID-19 outbreak (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/what-sites-to-follow-for-official-covid-19-updates/" target="_blank">COVID-19 outbreak</a>, many are turning to hobbies and passion projects to keep boredom at bay. [*<em>Flattening the curve refers to community isolation measures that keep the daily number of disease cases at a manageable level for medical providers.</em>] In case you need a break from all the extra screentime you suddenly have, here are some home improvement projects you can do to help pass the time.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>1. Declutter</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5165,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/sarah-brown-oa7pqZmmhuA-unsplash-1024x683.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5165"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It may have been in your new year\'s resolution to declutter and organize your home after binge-watching "Tidying Up With&nbsp;Marie Kondo" earlier this year. Go ahead and commit to really doing it this time. You can do it. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>2. Organize your pantry</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1580116270858-8a0d62b15426?ixlib=rb-1.2.1&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;w=680&amp;q=80" alt=""/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>While you\'re on the KonMari project, consider organizing your pantry as well.  Who knows you might also reignite your passion for baking in the process? Check out some <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="tips on how to organize your pantry here (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/how-to-organize-your-pantry/" target="_blank">tips on how to organize your pantry here</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>3. Rearrange your furniture</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1558882224-dda166733046?ixlib=rb-1.2.1&amp;ixid=eyJhcHBfaWQiOjEyMDd9&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;w=749&amp;q=80" alt=""/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can give your living room a fresh look just by moving your furniture. It could probably be the tiny change that you need to help you get a little more enthusiastic about staying home. Here are some layout ideas you can try:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="https://i1.wp.com/www.simphome.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/how-to-efficiently-arrange-the-furniture-in-a-small-living-room-2-via-Simphome.com_.png?resize=1068%2C1078&amp;ssl=1" alt=""/><figcaption>[<a href="https://www.simphome.com/upgrade-small-living-room.html">source</a>]</figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>4. Create a vertical garden </h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://cdn.apartmenttherapy.info/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto:eco,c_fit,w_1060,h_1885/at%2Farchive%2F4512521d20dabfe95134e9b8f5ac0533f737fc7b " alt=""/><figcaption>[<a href="https://www.apartmenttherapy.com/indoors-or-out-tips-for-creating-a-vertical-garden-230139" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="source (opens in a new tab)">source</a>]</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You may also spruce up your home with a vertical garden --  indoors or in your balcony. You don\'t have to spend much on this project. Recycle your soda bottles. Whether you\'re growing decorative plants or herbs, studies have shown that interaction with plants&nbsp;helps in reducing psychological and physiological stress. Take on gardening -- it\'s good for your mental health.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>5. DIY Photowall</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="https://i.pinimg.com/564x/66/bb/e8/66bbe896e68a6ba5bfd73ba65d38bdc5.jpg" alt=""/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For those who are innately wanderlusts, you might be missing the road so badly. Gather your favorite shots and put up a photowall and personalize your space (and maybe start visualizing your next trip!). Here are <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="some design ideas to get you started (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/diy-photowall/" target="_blank">some gallery design ideas to get you started</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/03/Copy-of-Copy-of-filipino-homes-3.png','views' => '43','category_id' => '31','published_at' => '2020-03-22 21:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '400','title' => 'Steps to make a reservation for a pre-selling property ','slug' => 'steps-to-make-a-reservation-for-a-pre-selling-property','content' => '<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":5156,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/filipino-homes-leuterio-realty-brokerage-4-410x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5156"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The search is finally over. After all the site trips and meetings, you finally found the property that is for you and that fits you. Congratulations! You are now ready to reserve your unit with your real estate agent/broker. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>First time home buyer? Prior to coming to the developers\' office, make sure you have the five basic requirements for reservation with you. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Here\'s what will happen during the reservation day;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>1. Meet with your Real Estate Agent/Broker at the developers\' office for the reservation.</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>During this time, you may ask last-minute questions and some clarifications before you officially sign the reservation agreement. If everything is clear and okay with you, then you may proceed with the reservation. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>2. Completely sign the buyer\'s information sheet. </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Make sure all information is correctly spelled and coincide with the documents that you have. If married, both spouses must be present to sign the reservation agreement, unless if the other spouse is out of the country. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In cases where the spouse or the primary buyer is out of the country, the documents and reservation agreements may be accomplished by their chosen SPA (Special Power of Attorney).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>3. Choose your desired Unit.</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Make sure that you as the buyer agrees to the location and price of the unit to be reserved. Reservation fees are non-refundable and non-transferrable. If later on, you decide to move to another unit, another floor or another lot location, that will invalidate the first reservation and you will have to pay for the reservation fee of the other unit where you wish to transfer (assuming it\'s in the same project/condo).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>4. Pay the reservation fee or Option Fee.</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Make sure you have your cash or check for reservation. For pre-selling properties, The developers will give you the sample computation of the equity payments and break down of fees prior to the official reservation. Make sure you are aware of your obligations and you agree as to the amount and the term of the equity period or downpayment period before signing. Have your real estate agents/broker double-check the documents for possible typographic errors.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you agree with the term sheets and computations, that\'s the time that you will be ushered to the Cashier for the payment of your reservation fee. Make sure you are 100% sure because Reservation Fees are non-refundable and non-transferrable.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>5. Sign the term sheets. </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The term sheet will contain the Total Contract Price, The Reservation Fee, Transfer Charges or Miscellaneous fee and the breakdown of the equity monthly payments or what payment option you choose. Basically your monthly obligation to be paid directly to the developer as equity payment will be stated in a term sheet. Make sure you are signing the payment terms that you agreed with. It will also contain the payment schedule that you as a buyer need to follow. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Equity payments are most of the time in the form of post-dated checks that you as a buyer need to accomplish and submit. The developer will warehouse these checks and will deposit monthly. Check warehousing is done in a developers\' bank, thus the developers will not be storing these checks in their offices. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>6. Sign the Reservation Agreement</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This document will contain all the information about your purchase. Please read the agreement carefully and ask questions if there are things you don\'t understand or disagree with. This document will symbolize that the unit or location you choose is final. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>Reservation fees are for specific units. And most of the time it\'s non-refundable and non-transferrable. Even if it has the same total contract price. </em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>7. Claim copies of your documents with you before you leave. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Make sure you have the following documents before you leave the office. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Official Receipt of the reservation or Acknowledgement Receipt.</li><li>Buyer\'s copy of the Reservation Agreement</li><li>Copies of the Computation Sheets and Term Sheets</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Congratulations! You have just reserved your desired unit! </h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So basically we have just given you what will actually happen during the reservation day. How much time will be spent in this process varies from one developer to the other. That would really depend on their system, however, setting your expectation as to what will happen on that day, will give you an idea of what will transpire and probably schedule your time accordingly. Should there be misses at least you can give a reminder or inform the officer or your real estate agent/broker about it. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you have the desired property already or you still need to advise on what property to purchase, contact your Filipino Homes Agent/Broker today. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'First time home buyer? Just to give you an overview on what will happen during the reservation day. ','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/03/Filipinohomes-blogger-realtor-real-estate-agent-xyza-yape.jpg','views' => '51','category_id' => '10','published_at' => '2020-03-23 21:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '401','title' => 'Afraid of Covid-19? Ways to Boost Your Immune System','slug' => 'ways-to-boost-your-immune-system','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Afraid of Covid-19? The increasing number of COVID-19 infected individuals in Metro Manila and all over Philippines can be alarming.  World Helth Organization and the Department of Health has been vigilant in sharing information on how to prevent Covid-19. These includes proper handwashing and hygiene and boost your immune system.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here are ways to combat Covid-19 and boost your immune system against the deadly disease caused by the virus.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Personal Hygiene&nbsp;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://cdn.pixabay.com/photo/2015/04/23/13/15/hygiene-736051_960_720.png" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Personal hygiene is one of the basic preventive ways to prevent getting infected by the virus and from spreading it to your family. Taking a shower everyday and constantly washing your hands with soap for 20 mins is one of the few ways to keep the virus from spreading and infecting people who will most likely get Covid-19.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Eating Healthy Meals</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://www.usda.gov/sites/default/files/styles/featured_image/public/usda_blog_images/6235_6276704367_9e77b563bf.jpg?itok=n2-5uXhn" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Beside having good personal hygiene, eating healthy is one of the simplest things you can do to help boost your immune system. If possible, lessen processed foods so you will get the vitamins your body needs. Thoroughly clean your fruit, vegetables, and even meat right after you buy it from the market. Remember to also prepare your foods and cook it thoroughly to prevent any stomach upsets. Eating homecooked food ensures you safe meals without preservatives.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Get Enough Sleep&nbsp;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://storage.needpix.com/rsynced_images/sleep-1672945_1280.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Our bodies all require sleep in order to restore and rejuvenate, grow muscle, repair tissues, and synthesize hormones. It is one way the body recharges and rest after a long day. It is also the time when the body resets. Sleep plays a vital role in good health and well-being throughout your life. Make sure to get a good amount of sleep so it will not cause havoc on your immune system.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Take Your Multivitamins</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5209,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/89384156_10215404623218911_2111053404682846208_o-768x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5209"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Now is not a good time to get sick. So make sure your body is at a top health and getting the necessary vitamins and minerals to function well. Do not underestimate the power of multivitamins. Take Vitamin C, D and Zinc to help boost your immune system.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Exercise at Home</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"width":601,"height":400,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large is-resized"><img src="https://p0.pikrepo.com/preview/261/878/shallow-focus-photography-of-a-woman-meditating-thumbnail.jpg" alt="" width="601" height="400"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Being healthy also means being fit. A healthy body is not just putting in healthy food but making sure that we are getting enough body movements so that our body won\'t be weak and easily get sick. Try downloading fitness apps or watching exercise videos of routines that you can do from home. If you do not have any exercise equipment, find one that does not require it. You can get the whole family to exercise with you. Not only will you be healthy but you\'re also spending time with your family and building a healthy routine together</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/03/5-WAYS-TO-BOOST-YOUR-IMMUNE-SYSTEM-AGAINST-COVID-19.png','views' => '38','category_id' => '13','published_at' => '2020-03-26 22:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '402','title' => 'How to Help Homebuyers Find Their Dream Property in Time of Crisis','slug' => 'how-to-help-homebuyers-find-their-dream-property-in-time-of-crisis','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The coronavirus outbreak has caused the crash in the stocks market, closing off businesses, loss in income and job securities. How do a real estate broker or agent make the best out of the current crisis?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5213,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Screen-Shot-2020-03-27-at-12.53.30-AM-1024x473.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5213"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Update your online listings</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Most people are in their homes right now and have plenty of time in their hands. Most of them go online to get information or stay connected with family and friends. That is why it is best to be visible online where the future homebuyers are so they can see you. Make sure you optimize in your property listings on Filipino Homes. Make sure you have complete information on the description and highlight the property features. Keep in mind that these possible homebuyers are solely relying on visual context while browsing through the listing, so make sure to upload photos that can make the property sell.<br>
</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Keep in touch with existing clients</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With the current health crisis that is affecting the economy as well, your existing clients will have a number of concerns regarding their transactions with you. Make sure to be responsive to clients who had inquired or are inquiring about a property. Explain to them how they can move forward with the transactions despite the limitations of community quarantine. Address their concerns about the Covid-19 outbreak and its effect on real estate. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Make it easy to contact you</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Make sure your clients know what mobile number to call, email address to use, or official social media profiles to contact you. Don\'t forget to update your listings with this information so your future clients can easily get a hold of you. Adding these details will not only make it easy for your clients to contact you but also add reliability to your name and listing.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>Share property option</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Since everyone is at home and has time to look for property listings, make sure that you share property options in your profiles and your network. <br>Interested homebuyers are looking for better deals in the market. You can send or share several property options to them through your Filipino Homes property listing. Make sure to offer them different products of various price points to meet different types of budgets and those flexible payment terms. Always encourage your clients to look through your listing, and if they can\'t find anything they like, ask them the features they did not find in the properties you shared.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/03/Filipinohomes-blogger-realtor-real-estate-agent-xyza-yape-2.png','views' => '33','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-03-28 21:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '403','title' => '7 Self-Care Tips to Cope with Isolation and Stress During COVID-19','slug' => '7-self-care-tips-to-cope-with-isolation-and-stress-during-covid-19','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="outbreak of coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19) (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/what-sites-to-follow-for-official-covid-19-updates/" target="_blank">outbreak of coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19)</a> has raised stress and anxiety levels. There is much uncertainty surrounding this pandemic, strict <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="government measures (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/metro-manila-under-quarantine/" target="_blank">government measures</a>, and there is no clear timeline as to when this will end.  Many of us are under Enhanced Community Quarantine and may experience feelings of isolation, boredom, anxiety, stress, and panic. In ensuring we give our best care to the ones closest to us, it’s important that we don\'t forget to take good care of ourselves as well. Self-care is crucial, especially during this difficult period.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here are some self-care tips you can do as you #StayAtHome:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>1. Take care of your body.</strong>&nbsp;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1466637574441-749b8f19452f?ixlib=rb-1.2.1&amp;ixid=eyJhcHBfaWQiOjEyMDd9&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;w=800&amp;q=80" alt=""/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Practice good hygiene.  Exercise regularly. Get plenty of sleep. Eat healthy, well-balanced meals.  Keep a consistent schedule for meals, exercise, and bedtime. Establishing a routine can also help you feel more in control.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2> 2. <strong>Express yourself.</strong>&nbsp; </h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1434030216411-0b793f4b4173?ixlib=rb-1.2.1&amp;ixid=eyJhcHBfaWQiOjEyMDd9&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;w=750&amp;q=80" alt=""/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Take a few minutes to tune in to your feelings and pause and reflect.   Acknowledge your feelings.  Remember that it\'s okay to not be okay.  Find a way to express yourself. Keep a journal in whatever form you are comfortable with to help you cope with your feelings. You can keep a diary, blog, record a video, or make a scrapbook. Find the format that works best for you, and do it. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>3. Stay informed.</strong>&nbsp;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1560169897-fc0cdbdfa4d5?ixlib=rb-1.2.1&amp;ixid=eyJhcHBfaWQiOjEyMDd9&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;w=752&amp;q=80" alt=""/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The feeling of not knowing may cause added stress and anxiety. Watch, listen or read the news for updates from reliable sources. Be aware, however, that there may be fake news and fearmongering attempts out there, especially on social media. Make sure to validate your sources and turn to <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="trusted sources of updates and information (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/what-sites-to-follow-for-official-covid-19-updates/" target="_blank">trusted sources of updates and information</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>4. <strong>Avoid too much exposure to the news.</strong>&nbsp;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":5192,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/william-iven-SpVHcbuKi6E-unsplash-1024x680.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5192"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It can easily be overwhelming and unsettling to constantly see, read, or hear about the crisis.  Take breaks from watching, reading, or listening to news stories.  Try to turn off your radio, TV, and social media once in a while. If you can <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="work from home (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/5-tips-to-actually-be-productive-when-working-from-home/" target="_blank">work from home</a>, return to "normal life" as much as possible and check for updates between breaks.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>5. <strong>Take breaks.</strong>&nbsp;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1522008342704-6b265b543c37?ixlib=rb-1.2.1&amp;ixid=eyJhcHBfaWQiOjEyMDd9&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;w=750&amp;q=80" alt=""/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Take deep breaths, stretch, meditate, or take a short walk (around your house if you\'re under enhanced community quarantine). Try to do activities you usually enjoy. Catch up on your reading list, binge-watch your favorite show on Netflix, or sing to the top of your lungs. You don\'t necessarily have to be "productive" all the time. You need to rest.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>6. <strong>Connect with others.</strong>&nbsp;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1577897113292-3b95936e5206?ixlib=rb-1.2.1&amp;ixid=eyJhcHBfaWQiOjEyMDd9&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;w=681&amp;q=80" alt=""/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Humans are social creatures. Bond with your family or keep in touch with your friends online. Share your concerns and how you are feeling. Maintain healthy relationships and build a strong support system.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2> 7. <strong>Seek help when needed.</strong>&nbsp;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":5193,"sizeSlug":"large","linkDestination":"custom"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><a href="http://facebook.com/mentalhealthph" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/89764608_2782467091844908_4048724795011891200_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5193"/></a></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If distress impacts activities of your daily life for several days or weeks, you may need a professional to speak with. Call the National Center for Mental Health hotlines: 0917-899-USAP (8727) or 989-USAP (8727).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/03/Copy-of-Copy-of-filipino-homes-4.png','views' => '38','category_id' => '13','published_at' => '2020-03-29 21:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:20','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '404','title' => 'Making Money In Real Estate - 9 Basic Ways','slug' => 'making-money-in-real-estate-9-basic-ways','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Making money in real estate is an endless topic that includes all the various types of real estate investments. There are land, apartment buildings, homes, commercial buildings and more. Whatever the type, however, you\'ll make your profits in some of the basic ways listed below. Use this list to get yourself thinking of the possibilities.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Appreciation </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5180,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Filipinohomes-blogger-realtor-real-estate-agent-xyza-yape.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5180"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Making money in real estate can be as simple as holding on and waiting. To really get the most appreciation in value, however, you should buy in an area where demand is growing faster than the supply.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Depreciation</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://usercontent1.hubstatic.com/14109898_f1024.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Remember that after all the tax law changes, you still get to declare a loss for the depreciation that doesn\'t really exist. That can save you a lot at tax time, meaning more after-tax profit. To maximize this, buy a property that has its value primarily in the buildings,  because you can\'t depreciate the value of the land.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Loan pay-down</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://cdn.aarp.net/content/dam/aarp/money/budgeting_savings/2016/04/1140-pay-down-your-debt-intro.imgcache.reva22e12c4a0ac06823c3fe11c0bc1aa2c.web.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You gain equity with every payment you make. Get the lowest interest rate you can and more of each payment will go towards the principal. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Cash flow</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://www.moneycrashers.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/04/manage-increase-business-cash-flow.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When you buy income property the right way, you not only have your tenants paying all the costs and paying down the mortgage loan, but you also have positive cash flow.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Buy low</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://media.gettyimages.com/vectors/buy-low-sell-high-vector-id482272695" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When you buy the below-market you get instant equity that will be converted into a profit when you sell. Offer a reason for the seller to sell low: fast closing, cash, assume some debts or liabilities, etc. Or just make a low offer. The seller may have his own reasons to sell it cheap.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Sell high </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Clean it up nice, make it easy to buy, and find the right buyer to get top peso. The next four on the list cover ways to create value, so you\'ll get more when you sell. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Offer to finance</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://cdn.shortpixel.ai/client/q_lossless,ret_img,w_1038/https://www.successvalley.tech/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/accounting-3190208_1920-1038x686.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can often get substantially more for a property if you offer to finance. This is especially true if you let someone buy it with little money down. You can also get a good interest on the loan. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Change use</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://s0.geograph.org.uk/photos/23/75/237503_554f35b6.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If there is a higher use for the property, you can convert it to make it worth more to the next owner. Sometimes this means making condos into apartments, or apartments into condos. Maybe converting a home into office space will get the biggest return, some are even converting it to a restaurant or something. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Improve and repair</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://nebula.wsimg.com/f27f8b12db6dd4c5dd1869cd8a7e3bed?AccessKeyId=7FFC4F52434BD58B5B5D&amp;disposition=0&amp;alloworigin=1" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Repairing anything that needs it is obvious, but you need to look creatively and carefully to find improvements to make. Concentrate only on those that will raise the value several times more than what they cost you. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Making money in real estate can be a wonderfully creative process. Just look at the sources of profits listed here, and think of how you can use a few of them on your next real estate investment.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'What are the basic ways of making money in real estate? Buying low, selling high, and eight more are covered here.
