<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/06/Agents-can-now-enroll-to-FilipinoHomes-Institute-of-Real-Estate-F.I.R.E.png','views' => '46','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2020-06-26 03:52:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '449','title' => 'Looking for a new home? Tips on how to avoid rental scams','slug' => 'looking-for-a-new-home-tips-on-how-to-avoid-rental-scams','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Relocating, starting a family, moving and looking into a new home but not ready to buy? The best solution is to rent your future new living space. Finding a place to rent is not as difficult as it was 10 years ago. Now, we have property listings, apartment rental ads and social media make it easy for a lessor to post about a property for rent. But, unfortunately, not all home rental listings are legit as they say. There are people who take advantage when there is money involved. So how do you avoid rental scams? Here are some tips to help you identify and avoid getting a rental scam.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Consider the source</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Always look into where you found the information. Is it from a social media post, an ad online, a property listing, or a property agent?  Make sure to do your research by looking into reviews or complaints against that source. If you find bad reviews or find the information sketchy, you may want to look somewhere else.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Research about the property</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Rental home listings may appear anywhere including social media or free listing services. Make sure to double-check and search for the home address in the company\'s website. If you find a property agent post on social media, make sure to double-check the property showing up on the company\'s website as well.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Compare rental prices</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>By this time you will already know the going rental price in the preferred area you want to rent at. Is the rent significantly lesser compared to other rentals in the area? This could be a potential red flag.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Ask for a property tour</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you\'re interested, ask for a property tour and make sure you have someone with you as you take that tour. Ask for identification issued by the company the real estate agent works for. Ask about any available information about the property owner and why the property is up for rent.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Double checking</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Before signing the lease, check any mention of the real estate company or owner\'s name and look it up. Some property owner does not want their information readily available, so make sure to call the company to double-check if the property is on their listing.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When looking for a place to rent, make sure to look for properties in the right places. Check out the properties for rent on <a href="https://filipinohomes.com/properties/rent">Filipino Homes list of properties for rent</a> anywhere in the Philippines.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Relocating, starting a family, moving and looking into a new home but not ready to buy? The best solution is to rent your future new living space. Finding a place to rent is not as difficult as it was 10 years ago. Now, we have property listings, apartment rental ads and social media makes it easy for lessor to post about a property for rent. >>> Read more','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/06/Filipinohomes-bloggerrealtor-real-estate-agent-xyza-yape-cdo-cebu-iligancity-1.png','views' => '56','category_id' => '13','published_at' => '2020-07-10 22:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:53'),
  array('id' => '450','title' => 'A look at the Financial Crises in the Philippine Real Estate Sector','slug' => 'a-look-at-the-financial-crises-in-the-philippine-real-estate-sector','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>To better understand the economic downturn brought by the COVID-19 pandemic, we need to take a look at the different economic crises Philippines has gone through in the recent history. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Asian Financial Crisis [1997–1998]</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Asian Financial Crisis, which destabilized the&nbsp;Asian&nbsp;economy and then the world economy at the end of the 1990s, &nbsp;began in&nbsp;Thailand&nbsp;and then quickly spread to neighboring economies. It involved currencies collapsing and soaring interest rates [<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.britannica.com/event/Asian-financial-crisis" target="_blank">1</a>]. As a result, condominium prices declined to 14 percent and office rents dipped by 16 percent. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In 1998, GDP of our ASEAN neighbors dropped dramatically -- in Indonesia by 13.2 percent, Thailand by -10.4 percent, and Malaysia by -7.5 percent. In the Philippines, however, GDP dropped only by -0.5 percent [<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://opinion.inquirer.net/105497/recalling-asian-financial-crisis" target="_blank">2</a>].  The PH economy\'s resilience during this time was attributed to the regulatory reforms adopted by the Central Bank following the domestic financial crisis triggered by the political and economic turmoil following the assassination of Benigno Aquino, Jr. in 1983. Measures conducted to strengthen our banking system and forestall similar financial pressures in the future paid off well for us by the time the Asian Financial Crisis hit us in the late 1990s [<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://watermark.silverchair.com/2644357.pdf?token=AQECAHi208BE49Ooan9kkhW_Ercy7Dm3ZL_9Cf3qfKAc485ysgAAAnYwggJyBgkqhkiG9w0BBwagggJjMIICXwIBADCCAlgGCSqGSIb3DQEHATAeBglghkgBZQMEAS4wEQQMEcHB3BENJ4jgUwEeAgEQgIICKRq-ezLC3pzlo-VTdZTxm2nay3UzvYGpoQr2MNj_G-9EhdHbE4eGPXZDSysA0dE4OJp5IttDwAQ9YKFsMwpUnfaeGX7DYwq7jgFoHvwSZ1cPs1BPXG_QUsPO51brFsBYxmqLdPR12YQX4NBc-Ix8EKz4fpPk_7tNdVx3x9_-_FpVvnI-zwmXxUbrpDPTvwbCWj3Jocb8o0w9goVp9yKy94WXtLN3ecSWPMUC76gOfiPIdGwStyD6mE-RtbzDg0ozmDgPKenwnW39l7hCteZ12iZfQJmF6pup9Fjci9REnes95fbU6yFdJa0Ncp_ATvfefvm2yXoK4nsg2-DdtRJGfPGAp1vdGXO48GWoro7CsoElro9_mvdgnqUpTp3AYkyq7mTwbXWMZvl9an4VFv8XYTwcooegBsb0-E6z2d3S-G8BkmFepM1SwXVA-nrm90drWICo2nPgbs1Y9bVXzW1Ik5JwbLYeCHdQ31f8jk8uKYR70HMgPMgzVr1vvz1jsgbBVlwpwHtj-OwwDZEcg3l22ogm4GhMaWuOrF4X818sEFqpLxO5YWof62cXtZT7NxNmIn8rnwdA2-xGDs2OUX96hVQuEDp1yl_UlcTSO552eu1TFSvkhPr5IE9TfO_Up2eX3TD4nfX4iWRwqpqXn4hqepHTB0nELR9R6pIAdVdkKDWEpVHnYspXzHED6LwctEDIS26N_ux-8xG0jr3bP9Ll5SaryX0duLwc0PA" target="_blank">3</a>, <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://business.inquirer.net/242257/turning-points-ph-real-estate" target="_blank">4</a>]. <br><br>The Central Bank has imposed limits on banks’ lending to the real property sector in the aftermath of the domestic financial crisis in the 1980s. This, along with the Filipino developers\' financing approach of prominently funding their projects by preselling (rather than borrowing heavily from banks to construct their buildings), provided additional safeguards against a possible real estate bubble induced financial crisis [<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://opinion.inquirer.net/105497/recalling-asian-financial-crisis" target="_blank">4</a>]. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://cdn.pixabay.com/photo/2016/10/02/12/15/manila-1709394_960_720.jpg" alt="Manila, City, Manila Bay, Big City, Night, Sea, Sunset"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Global Financial Crisis [<strong>2007–2008</strong>]</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Philippine real estate industry was generally growing since the early 2000s and stabilized in 2003, primarily due to an unmet demand for housing, increasing household incomes for middle class families, as well as the reforms to relax the land ownerships. The upturn in the housing sector was driven by remittances from overseas Filipino workers (OFWs), momentarily dipping during the global financial crisis (GFC) [<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://business.inquirer.net/242257/turning-points-ph-real-estate" target="_blank">4</a>].</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Asian countries weren’t as severly affected during the GFC, which resulted to a quick, V-shape recovery. The BPO sector, however, halted expansion plans.&nbsp; Residential transactions also declined, but the values were generally maintained [<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.lamudi.com.ph/journal/colliers-trends-opportunities-quarantine/" target="_blank">5</a>]. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The PH economy bounced back stronger from 1.2 percent in 2009 to 7.6 percent in 2010. This increased investor confidence, manifested as sporadic construction of condominium, commercial and office buildings. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5695,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/stock-exchange-4878214_1280-1024x724.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5695"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>"The Great Lockdown" of 2020</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/WEO/Issues/2020/04/14/weo-april-2020" target="_blank">"Great Lockdown"</a>, as what IMF calls the&nbsp;current economic downturn, refers to the severe and global&nbsp;recession, arising as an&nbsp;economic consequence&nbsp;of the ongoing&nbsp;<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/what-are-the-global-real-estate-implications-of-covid-19-pandemic/" target="_blank">COVID-19 pandemic</a>.&nbsp; In its <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/WEO/Issues/2020/04/14/weo-april-2020" target="_blank">April 2020 World Economic Outlook</a>, IMF projected the global economy to contract sharply by –3&nbsp;percent in 2020, much worse than during the 2008–09 financial crisis.&nbsp;This financial crisis is the biggest crisis the world has confronted since World War II and the biggest economic disaster since the Great Depression of the 1930s [<a href="https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/WEO/Issues/2020/04/14/weo-april-2020" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">6</a>, <a href="https://www.ft.com/content/d5f05b5c-7db8-11ea-8fdb-7ec06edeef84" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">7</a>].&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Despite this threat, the Philippines remained resilient and optimistic. The country has been cited by <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/the-economist-ranks-ph-financial-strength-1st-among-emerging-economies-in-southeast-asia/" target="_blank">The Economist</a> among the emerging countries with the highest level of “financial strength,”&nbsp;ranking 6th among selected emerging economies in the world and the best among those ranked from Southeast Asia. This suggests that the country has the confidence of the international community, which will go a long way in helping us finance our COVID-19 response measures and help us attract investments and create jobs on our road to recovery.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>JLL’s comprehensive research of the <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/q1-2020-metro-manila-residential-property-market-overview-and-what-this-means-for-you/" target="_blank">property market in Metro Manila for 1Q2020</a> also showed a mixed performance across asset classes due to the impact of COVID-19. Industry experts remain optimistic, saying it is still a good time to invest in rental properties. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you’re considering investing, experts suggest going for&nbsp;a property in townships. These are probably the most <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/webinar-filipino-homes-plus-to-introduce-homes-that-are-designed-for-new-normal-living/" target="_blank">pandemic-ready</a> among developments.<br></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em>READ: </em>  <a href="http://localhost:3001/webinar-filipino-homes-plus-to-introduce-homes-that-are-designed-for-new-normal-living/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Filipino Homes Plus to introduce homes that are designed for new normal living</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'To better understand the economic downturn brought by the COVID-19 pandemic, we need to take a look at the different economic crises Philippines has gone through in the recent history. #FILIPINOHOMES

CLICK THE LINK TO READ MORE>>>','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/06/Copy-of-Copy-of-filipino-homes-5.png','views' => '63','category_id' => '11','published_at' => '2020-07-13 04:34:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '451','title' => 'Design Ideas for Your Dream Loft-Type Unit','slug' => 'design-ideas-for-your-dream-loft-type-unit','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The look of your home definitely plays a major role in determining the mood of your place. It tells people who and what you are. The beauty of a loft-type unit is, aside from having both the convenience of a condo and the airiness of a two-story home, it gives you advantage of efficient interior designing. Although space is your major enemy, there are also solutions for loft-type units to <a href="http://localhost:3001/making-the-most-of-the-small-living-space/">make the most out of the space you have</a> depending on your lifestyle and personality.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you still haven’t figured out what best design for your "dream" loft-type unit, well, look no further. Here are the most-hype interior loft design ideas to inspire you to redesign your home despite having limited space.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4><strong>Modern Minimalist Design</strong></h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/SZ2HJ15-9ZuPptCf9YqWCSFoZ3C4JwUcuyavf3Jful_NiwTRLsR5bk0AqHBeKFDbMx5GRZHOXIzyu2KraJSVL32fOpwEsH8J9C0vO52zIfe2yqLm76gnmjICN-xVUEss4nh0s_K5" alt=""/><figcaption>Photo courtesy of <a href="https://www.realliving.com.ph/shopping-services/service-directory/jean-suzanne-g-sy">Jean Suzanne Sy</a></figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you love gray-white palette as your backdrop and still want to maintain a clean and minimalist look on the side, then go with this one. Adding a drywall with glass panels can also make your loft unit look bigger and let natural light into the space.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4><strong>Plants Galore</strong></h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/QcFaqP7yAmdyfz3A-lzyVyRKvpEYnUBXFV_aL2sZELM6jqEEIVRpnS6ghQXQYHnwdJhwCvYqY_GU_RbKLDly4Gkl0L1RoFfKGD5XCcfSLqnXLuOnlufAn73emtWb0qHRblmylVrH" alt=""/><figcaption>Photo courtesy of&nbsp;<a href="https://www.apartmenttherapy.com/authors/esteban">Esteban Cortez</a></figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You may have heard about the <em><a href="https://www.realtor.com/advice/home-improvement/jungalow-style-defined/">jungalow trend </a></em>(the combination of jungle and bungalow)? If you haven’t, it is actually a modern bohemian-ish interior design that incorporates the blend of colors, different patterns, and of course, plants everywhere. And this is actually becoming a trend now! But depending on your taste and personality, you are free to customize the kind of vibe you want, as long as you are able to create a harmonious environment.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4><strong>Country-Inspired Style</strong></h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://images.summitmedia-digital.com/realliving/images/articles/2015/10/27/marinette-and-edmunds-60sqm-lofttype-condo-with-a-countryinspired-look/marinette-and-edmunds-60sqm-lofttype-condo-with-a-countryinspired-look/001.jpg" alt=""/><figcaption>Photo courtesy of<a href="https://www.realliving.com.ph/home-tours/condos/marinette-and-edmund-s-60sqm-loft-type-condo-with-a-country-inspired-look"> realliving.com.ph</a></figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you’re into warm and inviting feels, transform your home into a cozy country abode! Just work with upholstered pieces you can find online or feel free to DIY things. Just keep it from looking over decorated with colors and prints.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4><strong>Rustic Industrial Design</strong></h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://i.pinimg.com/564x/f9/96/bd/f996bdd2c221a7ab60bfe055a03e2493.jpg" alt="Take a look at the most dazzling interior design | www.delightfull.eu/blog #interiordesign #homeinteriordesigntrends #homedecor #architecture"/><figcaption>Photo courtesy of <a href="https://www.pinterest.ph/pin/25825397849771893/">delightfull.eu</a></figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This type showcases neutral tones, utilitarian and functional objects of wood and metal surfaces. Industrial designs also integrate textural interplay of grainy, earthy wood and lustrous metal for a strong rustic vibe.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4><strong>“Grand-Millennial” Style</strong></h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/7Br4iCuoyY666HH44JSuUQg_Vrq0BA5om0bepZKOOBYqBC5NGSUXrY_F_ipjzCn3B0op1SOiz2rBTHXKW_w2BdDVBOlHoyvOIz6w_Whn7Q829BV4VqTEYtKro9aV_TosCQX7tb7t" alt=""/><figcaption>Photo courtesy of <a href="https://www.realliving.com.ph/home-tours/condos/an-innovations-manager-s-50sqm-loft-with-small-space-solutions?fbclid=IwAR1PbzKW9nFIMnpJ8Z6J0nPiXkK4ML_NwBhI1dR0OBX5TKURP7AztmhybW0">Wilan Dayrit</a></figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Minimalism for millennial is a growing trend that preaches clutter-free and simple-living lifestyle. From the furniture, to the bed and accessories, this urban-style home design follows a clean and streamlined look as well as pops of color that serve as accents.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4><strong>Playful Chic Design</strong></h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://cdn10.bostonmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/12/colorful-condo-kendall-2.jpg" alt="colorful condo kendall"/><figcaption>Photo courtesy of <a href="https://www.bostonmagazine.com/property/2016/12/05/colorful-loft-kendall-otm/">Coldwell Banker Residential Brokerage</a></figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Now, if you love to play with colors, prints, and a bunch of global finds, go with creating your own Loft Wonderland! Playful patterns were used carefully in the soft furnishings (even in the seating pieces) to add more liveliness vibe.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4><strong>Classic Contempo</strong>rary Design</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/TFIRQN2P4VmDj8Gyz51SixInXSOa2LOER6NWFM9Ic59lsh9EoV3ZYZC7jiqCuCatqocTRZOyTw50hjfFP50is0wwiVUdQfT5es_uwnKL8iTL_buDM6BMk8kNfOdGLvvqCeFwEjJv" alt=""/><figcaption>Photo courtesy of <a href="https://www.realliving.com.ph/shopping-services/service-directory/allen-oblena">Allen Oblena</a></figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Classic never gets old! If you’re leaning toward the simple and homey look, then this might be best for you. It works with colors like light gray, beige, and cream to achieve a spacious fee to your loft unit. You can also try to pair classic elements like vintage prints with modern pieces to achieve the classic contemporary look.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There you have it. Again, your home design matters. It provides a soul to the place you call “home” and makes your space more functional, pleasant and livable. That’s why if you have a good budget, it would be wise to invest in the right people who can help you live comfortably and really add quality value to your unit.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>FURTHER READINGS:</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/studio-unit-design-ideas/">5 Design Ideas to Steal for Your Studio Unit</a></li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/room-dividers/">Small Space Hacks: Ideas for Room Dividers</a></li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/loft-bed-small-spaces/">Loft Bed Ideas for Small Spaces</a></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->','excerpt' => 'The look of your home definitely plays a major role in determining the mood of your place. It tells people who and what you are.','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/06/Loft-Design-Inspiration-Interior-Design-Ideas.png','views' => '44','category_id' => '29','published_at' => '2020-07-15 04:30:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '452','title' => 'Millennials are the "most entrepreneurial generation" yet: How do they save, spend, and invest their money?','slug' => 'millennials-are-the-most-entrepreneurial-generation-yet-how-do-they-save-spend-and-invest-their-money','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Millennials, born between 1981 and 1996 (current age 24-39), are often stereotyped as a generation of narcissistic, self-centered, and entitled young people, earning the title of "<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://www.nbcnews.com/id/17349066/ns/health-mental_health/t/college-students-think-theyre-so-special/#.XvLaWWgzY2y" target="_blank">Generation Me</a>." But there is definitely more to this group than meets the eye. Some of the most successful startups that redefined the 21st century were developed by millennials: Facebook, Pinterest, Uber, Shopify, Airbnb, among others. Studies have shown that millennials are the <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.smeweb.com/2019/02/27/millennials-entrepreneurial-generation/?cli_action=1592976091.535" target="_blank">most entrepreneurial generation </a>yet.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In this blog post, we\'ll see how this generation is dominating the modern investment race. Let\'s discuss about how they <strong>save, spend, and invest</strong> their money.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>On Savings</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Apparently, millennials are generally good financial planners, thinking about retirement even at a young age.&nbsp;There is a movement called <strong>FIRE</strong>, or <strong>Financial Independence Retire Early</strong>. By taking control of their finances at an early age, the FIRE movement has the millennial generation aiming to <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.forbes.com/sites/ericbrotman/2019/11/12/how-millennials-are-changing-the-retirement-conversation/#52f4156f6f07" target="_blank">retire as young as 30 or 40</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://cdn.pixabay.com/photo/2014/02/01/18/00/money-256312_960_720.jpg" alt="Money, Bills, Calculator, Save, Savings, Taxes"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Some interesting statistics compiled by the <a href="https://www.securitybank.com/blog/what-are-millennials-doing-with-their-money/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Security Bank Team</a>:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Millennials are more likely to save for retirement 4 to 8 years earlier than the Gen X or Baby Boomers group. (<a href="https://www.csmonitor.com/Business/Saving-Money/2017/0221/Why-Millennials-are-better-with-their-money-than-their-parents">CSMonitor, 2017</a>)</li><li>72% of millennials are retirement savers, with 40% savings rate increase among millennials, which means they’re saving a lot more every year. (<a href="http://www.nasdaq.com/article/what-millennials-are-doing-right-now-with-their-money-cm749820">Nasdaq, 2017</a>)</li><li>49% of millennials identify themselves as savers, while 25% consider themselves as spenders. (<a href="http://www.experian.co.uk/blogs/consumer-advice/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/Millennial-Me-and-My-Money-Report_FINAL.pdf">Experian, 2016</a>)</li><li>75% of millennials are actively tracking their expenses (<a href="https://www.forbes.com/sites/maggiemcgrath/2015/06/22/millennials-the-money-conscious-generation/">Forbes, 2015</a>)</li><li>67% of millennials are sticking to a fixed budget. (<a href="https://www.forbes.com/sites/maggiemcgrath/2015/06/22/millennials-the-money-conscious-generation/">Forbes, 2015</a>)</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>On Investing</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Data shows that more Filipino millennials are investing in stock market (<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.rappler.com/business/231850-more-filipino-middle-class-millennials-investing-stock-market" target="_blank">Rappler, 2019</a>).  In the PSE\'s 2018 stock market investor profile report, total accounts broke past the one-million mark, which is 25.4% higher than in 2017. Investors aged 18 to 29 comprised 21.5% of the total stock market account holders. Those in the 30-to-44 age range accounted for 43.1%, while 45 to 59 had 21.6%, and 60 and above for 13.9%. The increase in the number of younger people getting into the stock market was due to the growing popularity of online trading.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5706,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/austin-distel-EMPZ7yRZoGw-unsplash-1024x683.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5706"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Some more interesting statistics on millennials\' investment habit:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Almost 8 out of 10 millennials prioritize socially responsible and impactful investing (<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://businessmirror.com.ph/2020/01/12/most-millennials-now-prioritize-responsible-investing-survey/" target="_blank">deVere Group, 2020</a>)</li><li>74% of millennials find investing an attractive deal because they can grow their money manifold over time. (<a href="https://www.forbes.com/sites/maggiemcgrath/2015/06/22/millennials-the-money-conscious-generation/">Forbes, 2015</a>)</li><li>Millennials allocate about 25% of their income to investments. (<a href="http://blog.wallstreetsurvivor.com/2015/12/09/what-are-millennials-doing-with-their-money/">Wall Street Survivor, 2015</a>)</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The <a href="https://www.moneymax.ph/personal-finance/articles/best-investments-goals" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">best investment options</a> for millennials include: </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>For Short-Term Goals<ul><li>Time Deposit</li><li>Money Market Funds</li></ul></li><li>For Medium-Term Goals<ul><li>Balanced Funds</li><li>Equity UITFs</li><li>Pag-IBIG MP2</li></ul></li><li>For Long-Term Goals<ul><li>Stocks</li><li>Real Estate</li></ul></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em>READ:</em>  <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/millennials-can-invest-real-estate/" target="_blank">3 Ways Millennials Can Invest in Real Estate</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>On Spending</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Millennials are said to often splurge on travel, gadgets, numerous cups of coffee, and avocado toasts, <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://manilastandard.net/mobile/article/275495" target="_blank">a study conducted by Nielsen Holdings, Inc</a>. reported that this generation are actually very careful about their financial future.&nbsp;Despite their social media accounts showing their "extra" lifestyle, millennials are more likely to plan their spending, compared to the older generation.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5705,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/toa-heftiba-bvhEYmFU7ec-unsplash-1024x683.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5705"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Millennials tend to spend on real-life experiences that allow them to bond with family and friends. Shelling out cash on holidays or culinary classes is about experiencing life and pursuing passions.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>72% of millennials prefer to spend more money on experiences than on material things according to a Harris Group study. (<a href="https://www.cnbc.com/2016/05/05/millennials-are-prioritizing-experiences-over-stuff.html">CNBC, 2016</a>)</li><li>55% of millennials are willing to spend more on events like concerts, music festivals, and fun runs. (<a href="http://blog.wallstreetsurvivor.com/2015/12/09/what-are-millennials-doing-with-their-money/">Eventbrite, 2014</a>)</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Bottomline is:  This generation spend their money as they see fit. They save and investment to secure their future,&nbsp;while experiencing the world and making the most of their youth.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Millennials, born between 1981 and 1996 (current age 24-39), are often stereotyped as a generation of narcissistic, self-centered, and entitled young people, earning the title of "Generation Me." But there is definitely more to this group than meets the eye. Some of the most successful startups that redefined the 21st century were developed by millennials: Facebook, Pinterest, Uber, Shopify, Airbnb, among others. Studies have shown that millennials are the most entrepreneurial generation yet.
#FILIPINOHOMES

CLICK THE LINK TO READ MORE >>>','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/06/Copy-of-Copy-of-filipino-homes-6.png','views' => '85','category_id' => '11','published_at' => '2020-07-16 22:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '453','title' => '11 Modern Minimalist Home Office Design Ideas to Boost Your Productivity and Inspire Creativity','slug' => '11-modern-minimalist-home-office-design-ideas-to-boost-your-productivity-and-inspire-creativity','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The "new normal" has many companies embrace a flexible work arrangement for employees. While it seems to be an attractive idea to be working from home and spending a lot more time with the family, a work-from-home setup can be a bit challenging. Household distractions could potentially hurt your productivity and creativity. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A dedicated workspace in your home may help you better focus during work hours. In this blog post, we’ve gathered 11 home office ideas to inspire you to design a work-friendly space in your own home. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>1.  Wall-mounted desk</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Using a wall-mounted desk design leaves the floor less cluttered with the absence of desk legs. Just keep your wires hidden and your office space clean to maintain a minimalist aesthetic.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<center><iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=282178732891476807" height="550" width="450" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe></center>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>2. Folding desk </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A folding desk setup is a great solution when your home office is within a living room or bedroom. It closes up to conceal work equipment when not in use. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<center><iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=592927107173708070" height="1047" width="450" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe></center>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>3. Office in a closet</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With all the decluttering you\'ve been doing during quarantine, you may have freed up an area in your closet. You can easily convert this space to a home office with ample storage for your office supplies. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<center><iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=301248662579630585" height="775" width="450" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe></center>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>4.  Functional wall</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A <strong>corkboard wall </strong>provides a spot to pin some notes and reminders. You can also put in some inspirations to let your creativity flow freely.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<center><iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=240661173816702611" height="775" width="450" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe></center>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You may also opt for a <strong>whiteboard or dry-erase wall</strong>...</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<center><iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=69102175521233289" height="777" width="450" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe></center>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Or a <strong>chalkboard wall</strong> to keep you organized and on track with your task list and goals.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<center><iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=596023331920702955" height="700" width="450" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe></center>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>5. Ghost chair</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A clear acrylic chair in your home office makes an ideal minimalist choice, as it "disappears" out of sight, making your space appear a little larger and roomier. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<center><iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=50735933277019600" height="899" width="450" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe></center>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>6. Under the stairs</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can also create a dedicated home office space under your stairs.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<center><iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=467037423861902943" height="828" width="450" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe></center>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>7. Storage space options</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here\'s a brilliant small space solution:  Use a basic floating shelf as desktop and overlap it to a storage unit.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<center><iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=283163895298736631" height="717" width="450" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe></center>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>8. Window sill desk</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You don’t have to spend your work hours facing a wall. You can put your worktop across a window sill. This will let you enjoy the outdoor views and the natural lighting more. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Bonus points if you have a gorgeous view outside your home.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<center><iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=242842604893892811" height="550" width="450" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe></center>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>9.&nbsp;&nbsp;All-white office nook</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Transform an awkward nook in the house into a dedicated workspace. Paint it all white to make the space bigger than it is.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<center><iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=364791638543165109" height="691" width="450" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe></center>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>10. Ladder desk</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The ladder desk is a functional, efficient, and modern solution to set up a home office with very limited space.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<center><iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=447967494187566068" height="550" width="450" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe></center>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>11.&nbsp;&nbsp;Tropical settings</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The quarantine and stay-at-home directive had many of us embrace new hobbies, like gardening. Many had been transformed into "<em>plantitos</em>" and "<em>plantitas</em>" (or plant parents). Why not have an indoor garden in your home office? The calming effects of the potted plants could help you boost your creativity and productivity. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<center><iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=513128951293561822" height="777" width="450" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe></center>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>More Ideas:</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you have a small space, here are some more home office design ideas you can do: <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/7-home-office-design-ideas-small-spaces/" target="_blank">7 Home Office Design Ideas for Small Spaces</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/06/Copy-of-Copy-of-filipino-homes-8.png','views' => '43','category_id' => '31','published_at' => '2020-07-19 23:55:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '454','title' => '6 Simple ways to Make Your Bedroom into a Relaxing Haven','slug' => '6-simple-ways-to-make-your-bedroom-into-a-relaxing-haven','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Keeping a stress-free bedroom will make a huge difference to your self-care routine.&nbsp;Although bedrooms are oftentimes overlooked by many, there are good reasons for you to consider why it should be your top priority. First, your bedroom is where you begin and end every day of your life. It is where you allow yourself to rest and recharge to be ready again the next day. Second, bedrooms can also be your inner sanctum, where you find yourself reading, relaxing or just unwinding. Meaning it is impractical to keep the best self-care routine without actually making effort on investing a good <em>serene </em>bedroom. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So, now try to imagine your ideal relaxation scenario. Do you want a bedroom that is calm and peaceful? If yes, then it would make sense for you to read on. We have listed really simple ways how you can magically recreate your bedroom into a relaxing haven that makes you want to sleep in.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5714,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/Rashia-Bell-1024x576.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5714"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>1. <strong>Keep everything simple and organized</strong></h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/ZCSCYzkJOoqqs3S1ej2Rq6h9XdMVfADzsj4T5lOxOvBzbPPjfArzDgnKucy3pFurbDMjVFX4inAs1YsLbIwxXZnSs61MvEEuyPCu38zQdLO8K_r54Nwb4OEhNZGrf0qZgbnS4aG8" alt=""/><figcaption>Photo by<a href="https://unsplash.com/@chuttersnap?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText"> chuttersnap</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Your bedroom should be a restful place not your storage or exhibit room. Decluttering your bedroom to only the essentials can make it look and feel more relaxing. If you have lots of stuff that you can’t let go, try to remodel your bed or get convertible furniture to add more storage. Consider a platform bed with extra space for storage underneath. Making things simple diverts your mind on the bedroom’s purpose which is to <em>relax and rejuvenate</em>.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>2. <strong>Set the vibes with calming colors</strong></h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/dQDezYlXsLYOUZ0tcd8kGHsKuAZCGL94_qIF7KhON-syTIlRHUm9qpJvmhXy79-OEVFOdeE1z_uwqFYUJ2IQe0ScjnKapdAYuBl0XJsnSTT5qsMNjhVDpVNKpRS2pL86dBM8aQ4M" alt=""/><figcaption>Photo by<a href="https://unsplash.com/@blakepnw?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText"> Blake Carpenter</a></figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Light grey or off-whites are most-recommended. These neutral colors can give your room that calming and restful feel. It’s also clean and pure to look at. However, if neutrals don’t work for you, then try other colors like pale greens, purples and pinks. <a href="http://localhost:3001/black-and-white-bedroom/">Black and white combination </a>creates a timeless and peaceful look too. Just do some soul searching as to what colors you feel and find most relaxing. <em>You do you</em>.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>3. <strong>Make your bedroom a device and work-free zone</strong></h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/xKGgkHg31FFf7AhV6ZSy4r8qAhUELvGhH9Xh-L-TA7oY4d8aAy3R42wUhrWFZzNguFvHj9pXZsu7ui2Kgwsj1MzS3IfOIsdtsgrbV-faQxSDn12mo4LfjdB4HS03zs5SZESrbl50" alt=""/><figcaption>Photo by<a href="https://unsplash.com/@rhemakallianpur?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText"> Rhema Kallianpur</a></figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>According to Rashia Bell, your bed should be treated as a special and private space, allowing you to leave everything else behind while sleeping. That\'s why it is recommended to keep your bedroom device-free zone as much as possible, as they can energetically unbalance a room and disrupt sleep. Additionally, remove any stuff that reminds you of work and keeps your mind from unwinding. You may also consider adding a headboard to help make your bed feel extra special and indulgent. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>4. <strong>Change your old pillow and bedding</strong></h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/15m0K-kuxPazNJ5oIK6G3ctuv440tshNnnBCKfBCdEhpjaKG7ry6Ztl2abvrRQYwKjzaZnnKxw8CiJhEsnnUJPR3ZsvsKTv8cDlC6tjYJMRuNDcD3iz09Tc5EKnqpj12_UD6r0ff" alt=""/><figcaption>Photo by<a href="https://unsplash.com/@stevenungermann?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText"> Steven Ungermann</a></figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Now, don’t miss your bed essentials. Selecting calming colors can really make a huge impact. White bedding or any neutral color will surely give you that cozy feels. Apart from its calming effect, <a href="https://www.healthline.com/health/how-often-should-you-change-your-sheets#tips">regularly changing your essentials prevents the accumulation of bacteria you can’t see</a> like thousands of dead skin cells, dust mites, or even fecal matter. Though this won’t make you sick immediately. But in theory, it can.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>5. <strong>Put a rug around your bed</strong></h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/QOZ968YQjIv5rj59JWmmT81-Eyll33-PTXOh2cYtrsdmf-njUWy9CDR6ZwZSoDt34iqo9xoqC1deNVkd2RugqkxLpXGA_xn4ogA4NtM-JWwofiPzsZg6nlkQTlSVd8wOQ94SjuNP" alt=""/><figcaption>Photo by<a href="https://unsplash.com/@devano23?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText"> Devon Janse van Rensburg</a></figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Consider an area rug around your bed so your toes have something touch in the morning. It would feel good waking up with something soft under your feet especially during cold seasons. Rugs definitely make a huge difference.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>6. <strong>Put a personal touch</strong></h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/P3p2lv5YHKGaZqSoAGAFIvDrouEY9cncTV0wjaBcx7xSbKwoP2fIG4VI_PbEcf4BDaDzFTxKz5iyjdWxpHLhi5-2IOMlY4nGPPX2RLfbBuyatMjjEw3NqLPRV4nC5RIFH3D1Tax_" alt="pillows on bed"/><figcaption>Photo by<a href="https://unsplash.com/@byrdman85?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText"> DeMorris Byrd</a></figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Accent your room space with extra things that bring you joy! Whether it be your unforgettable travel picture, a beautiful painting, or a collection of succulents in a playful planter. Do not be afraid to incorporate a variety of details that you think may add a calming vibes to you. Just keep it to a minimum though to avoid too much visual stress.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Turning your bedroom into a relaxing sanctuary doesn\'t have to be expensive nor daunting. Your bedroom is where you begin and end every day of your life. It is where you allow yourself to rest and recharge to be again the next day.','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/06/6-Simple-Ways-to-Make-Your-Bedroom-into-a-Relaxing-Haven.png','views' => '43','category_id' => '31','published_at' => '2020-07-21 08:30:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '455','title' => '[Property Investing] The What, Why, and How of House Flipping','slug' => 'property-investing-the-what-why-and-how-of-house-flipping','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There are a number of ways to make money in real estate. &nbsp;Aside from the traditional route of buying rental properties, flipping houses -- though considerably risky -- is one of the popular ways of making money. In this blog post, we\'ll tackle the what, why, and how of house flipping as an investment strategy.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>What is House Flipping?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>House flipping is the process of buying, rehabbing, and selling properties for profit.&nbsp; Real estate investors buy properties below market price, make aesthetic improvements to increase its value, and then resell it for profit. &nbsp;It is, however, not a “get rich quick” plan.  House flipping takes a lot of work, a lot of investment, and perfect timing.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ</strong>:&nbsp;<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://filipinohomes.com/blog/flip-houses-for-profit/" target="_blank">How to Effectively Flip Houses for Profit</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>House flipping is best suited for investors with a large cash reserve, have a&nbsp;good eye for design, and great negotiation skills.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5770,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/nathan-fertig-FBXuXp57eM0-unsplash-1024x683.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5770"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Why House Flipping Can Be Profitable?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If done correctly, a successful buy-fix-sell can provide <strong>very large profits.</strong>  Flipping homes can be lucrative business. An investor can make a significant returns on investment relatively quickly, given the right timing.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>House flipping can help you <strong>develop your skills</strong>. It will take a lot of time and money, but there is a lot of valuable experience to be gained, including increasing your knowledge in construction and real estate. House flipping can also help you develop your negotiating skills as well as project management and time management skills, which will translate to all kinds of businesses you may dive into in the future.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>What to look out for</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Flipping houses can be fun, exciting, and inspirational, but <em>very dangerous </em>if you don\'t do it right. Make sure to calculate how much money you can spend on renovations and still make a return. Purchase properties sensibly and don’t spend too much on renovations.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Some factors to consider when buying a property for flipping include your target market’s needs, surrounding developments (distance to schools and universities, shopping centers, healthcare facilities, etc.), and future growth (future roads and commercial establishments).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://cdn.pixabay.com/photo/2018/04/05/17/31/renovate-3293498_1280.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>How to Effectively Flip Houses</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>Step 1: Plan</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Figure out what kind of property you are going to flip, how much you can afford, and how are you exactly going to complete it. Research about your target market. Where are they buying houses? What kind of properties are they buying? What are their non-negotiables when they go house hunting? Until you answer these questions and formulate a concrete plan, don\'t jump into house flipping. Do not base your decision on what they show on reality TV. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>Step 2: Buy smart</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It is important that you take time to study your local real estate market. Learn how to spot a good deal. &nbsp;Know your home financing options.&nbsp;Analyze <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/find-how-much-property-you-can-afford/" target="_blank">how much you can afford</a> and how much you can afford to lose on any deal.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em>READ:</em>  <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/find-how-much-property-you-can-afford/" target="_blank">How Much Property You Can Afford</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A good property to invest in should be in a <em>good location</em>, meaning in close proximity to place of work, good schools, and/or shopping areas; with convenient access to local transport hubs; with water access; and in a safe and secure neighborhood. As much as possible, purchase a house that in in general sound condition and will require only minimal upgrades or innovations.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>Step 3: Have a Timeline</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The objective of house flipping is to sell effective as quickly as possible. Create a realistic timeline and set times for contracting, renovating, and selling.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>Step 4: Renovate the house</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Prioritize the fixes that will quickly increase the value of the home you are flipping. Spruce up the property with renovations that would make it more appealing to your potential buyers.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em>READ:</em>  <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/condo-renovations-money/" target="_blank">5 Renovations That Make Money</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>Step 5: <strong>Sell the house</strong></h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Sell the property for a significantly higher price than the purchasing cost. Research the prices in the neighborhood, and seek the help of realtors. Hopefully, if you had a great plan and managed your flip effectively, you will sell it quickly.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Learn more:</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/a-beginners-guide-to-real-estate-investing-strategies/" target="_blank">A Beginner’s Guide to Real Estate Investing Strategies</a></li><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/money-real-estate/" target="_blank">How to Make Money in Philippine Real Estate</a></li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/condo-renovations-money/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">5  Renovations That Make Money</a></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/07/Copy-of-Copy-of-filipino-homes-10.png','views' => '51','category_id' => '15','published_at' => '2020-07-22 02:59:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '456','title' => '7 Best Home Office Colors to Boost Creativity, Happiness, and Productivity','slug' => '7-best-home-office-colors-to-boost-creativity-happiness-and-productivity','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Many studies have shown that color can seriously affect your mood. In setting up your <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/7-home-office-design-ideas-small-spaces/" target="_blank">home office</a>, choosing the right hues can work wonders for your creativity, happiness, and productivity. Here are some optimal colors for your dedicated workspace:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Blue</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<center><iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=84724036728838903" height="400" width="450" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe></center>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Blue is a professional and intellectual color. It represents trust, logic, communication, and efficiency. You may use blue as a dominant color for your home office, especially if your work require focus and mental strain, like legal or accounting.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Yellow</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<center><iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=34973334594459870" height="457" width="450" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe></center>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Yellow is an emotional color, representing creativity, optimism, and confidence. Incorporate yellow in your home office design when you want to stimulate creativity, positivity, and happiness in your space.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Green</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<center><iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=332773859969432100" height="663" width="450" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe></center>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Green represents balance, harmony, and restoration. Being the easiest color on the eyes, it is a great color for people who need to work long hours. Add green elements to add a sense of balance into your workspace.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Red</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<center><iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=93168286029729753" height="427" width="450" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe></center>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Red is a color that can&nbsp;invoke passion&nbsp;and&nbsp;raise mental energy flow.  It is also said to enhance human metabolism, increase respiration rate, and raise blood pressure. Be careful in using red, as it can be&nbsp;overpowering and may potentially lead to&nbsp;headaches. Red seems to work best as accent color rather than a dominant primary color for a space. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Orange</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<center><iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=269160515217968412" height="550" width="450" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe></center>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Orange blends the physical color (red) and emotional color (yellow), creating a sense of comfort. It is also a fun color, making it a good option for a casual feel in your office. Orange is a good color when you need to stay pumped for high-energy meetings or all-night hackathons. It\'s said to boost creativity and endurance.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>White</strong>&nbsp;</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<center><iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=72128031520870345" height="550" width="450" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe></center>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>White represents&nbsp;purity&nbsp;and&nbsp;cleanliness and your safest bet when you\'re going for a minimalist look. &nbsp;With lots of natural light, a white office can create a sense of spaciousness and promote creativity.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Grey</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<center><iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=4574037110744855" height="550" width="450" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe></center>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Grey represents neutrality. Its minimal appeal helps make your office look sleek or modern when used appropriately.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/07/Copy-of-Copy-of-filipino-homes-12.png','views' => '38','category_id' => '29','published_at' => '2020-07-23 01:09:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '457','title' => 'Buying a condo? Helpful tips before making that big purchase','slug' => 'buying-a-condo-helpful-tips-before-making-that-big-purchase','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A condominium is a building containing individually owned apartments. They system of ownership is having a full title of the individual unit or apartment. It has some advantages like location as condominiums are usually developed in a bustling part of a city. <br><br>If you are thinking of buying a condominium to live closer to your workplace or planning to buy one and have it rented for additional income. Here are some tips to help you in buying that property:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Research on the property your looking for</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5831,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/research-1024x514-1.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5831"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Research about the condominium you\'re looking into. Besides the floor area and the unit layout, this includes the amenities and facilities in the property, location, accessibility to shops, schools or workplace, as well as the safety features. Ofcourse you need to look in to the financing side of it as well. There are a lot of real estate agents who can help you with this one. Make sure to ask all the necessary information before making the call and making your purchase official. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Know your financing options</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":3949,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/03/helloquence-51716-unsplash-1024x683.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-3949"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Know the type of financing options available. Most purchases starts at 10,000 PHP reservation and a downpayment of 20-30%the property value. You can then apply for a bank loan or Pag-Ibig to cover the rest. If you\'re planning to for a bank loan, look for banks that offer the lowest interest rates. There are different home loans you can avail, like fixed rates for 5 years is the most popular choice but it have a 9%. Loans with yearly adjustments, however, only has 5-6% interest.  You have to ask the bank and see what are your options and if the monthly mortgage will fit your budget as well.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Additional expenses can occur</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":2342,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/pool-money-with-family-and-friends-real-estate-investment-filipinohomes.jpg" alt="pool money with family and friends real estate investment filipinohomes" class="wp-image-2342"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Besides the expenses of buying your appliances and furnitures, there are fees to expect before officially moving into your new place. Ask your agent if there are any additional expenses to expect. This includes Move-In Fees, installment fees for utilities like electricity, water and internet provider.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Learn about association dues</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://rdcnewscdn.realtor.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/12/HOA-fees-1024x576.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Unlike buying a home or a lot that is not within a developers community, condominiums like subdivisions have monthly or annual association dues to keep the community running. This covers maintenance of common areas, utility bills and the salaries of the the staff. Most developments, as early as the planning stages already have a pre-calculated amount for association dues. Expect to pay this on top of your mortgage and utility bills.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Research about the developer</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://www.businessnewsdaily.com/images/i/000/012/245/original/jobsearch.jpg?1472048462" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you\'re planning to use the property to live in or to have it rented, make sure you know the developer quality of work. Ask people you know who live or purchase a property from the same developer. Ask simple details like how is soundproofing, insulation, even plumbing and exhaust pipings. These are minor details that will save you from stresses in the future.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Ask about property maintenance and management</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://cdn.homedit.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/12/real-agent-talk.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There will be some community rules for all residents in the condominium and it can be a headache if you\'re dealing with property management services that are difficult to work with. Ask people you know who have experience living in properties developed and managed by the developer and property management. Ask how the deal with problems, how strict the are with regulations and how important safety is for them.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Talk to a real estate agent you can trust</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://myfamilylaw.ru/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/hq-main-couple-talking-to-agent-745x490.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The best way to know about information and details about a specific development is when you talk to a real estate agent. Work with someone you can trust or someone a family or a friend have worked with and can vouch for. Ask for honest opinions whether the property you are looking into can be a good investment or a best buy. The professional real estate agent will be honest with you and will put your terms, comfort and safety. At Filipino Homes we make sure that all Filipinos will be happy and secure in the purchases they make. We look into developments and work with developers with good standing with the best <a href="https://filipinohomes.com/agents">professional real estate agents in the country</a> who will look after you and your family\'s welfare.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/07/filipino-homes-realtor-blogger-xyza-yape.png','views' => '46','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-07-28 00:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '458','title' => '50th Filipino Homes Office Opens','slug' => '50th-filipino-homes-office-opens','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The 50th Filipino Homes Office officially opened in Legazpi City, Albay, Bicol Region yesterday, July 28, 2020.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[5845]} -->
<figure class="wp-block-gallery columns-1 is-cropped"><ul class="blocks-gallery-grid"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/114072904_10217806696421850_7775064055725901448_n-1.jpg" alt="" data-id="5845" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/114072904_10217806696421850_7775064055725901448_n-1.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=5845" class="wp-image-5845"/></figure></li></ul></figure>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The opening of this newest branch is a way to express Filipino Homes\' confidence in revitalizing the real estate market in the Philippines.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5854,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/111237716_10217806700021940_8005570966193071805_n-1-2.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5854"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Anthony Gerard Leuterio, CEO of Filipino Homes, said, "Despite the pandemic, we see our sales partners’ and their buyers’ high demand for actual service deserves this expansion."</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[5849]} -->
<figure class="wp-block-gallery columns-1 is-cropped"><ul class="blocks-gallery-grid"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/116634517_10217806697661881_9002375441078558757_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="5849" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/116634517_10217806697661881_9002375441078558757_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=5849" class="wp-image-5849"/></figure></li></ul></figure>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Legazpi City branch of Filipino Homes is located at the Ground Floor of Imperial Main Square, beside Ayala Mall Legaspi.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5850,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/113436787_10217806700461951_168954000386304756_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5850"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Congratulations, Team Legazpi! </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'The 50th Filipino Homes Office officially opened in Legazpi City, Albay, Bicol Region.','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/07/114244651_10217806699101917_1048646258662102920_n-1.jpg','views' => '45','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2020-07-29 05:19:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '459','title' => '10 Social Media Post Ideas for Real Estate Agents','slug' => '10-social-media-post-ideas-for-real-estate-agents','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Nowadays, if your business is not on social media, it may as well not exist.&nbsp; If you are not using social media to market your real estate services, you\'re missing out on the opportunity to connect with your clients (and future clients) on an intimate level. A solid digital presence is an opportunity to stay in touch with your client base and get repeat business and referrals.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The main purpose of social media marketing is for people to get to<em> know,</em> <em>like</em>, and <em>trust </em>YOU. In case you\'re at a loss at what type of content should you share as a real estate professional, here are some ideas to help you out:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>1. New Listing</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Make sure you update your social media with new listings. You’ll never know who are on the lookout for new homes.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Share a few key details about the house:  How many bedrooms? What does the interior and exterior look like? What are the other features and amenities? And don\'t forget to add your contact details.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://www.facebook.com/plugins/post.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Fcdohousingprojects%2Fposts%2F1392305794305082&amp;width=500" width="500" height="737" align="center" style="border:none;overflow:hidden" scrolling="no" frameborder="0" allowtransparency="true" allow="encrypted-media"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>2. Just Sold</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is a common real estate social media post, and to be honest, it may be tricky to not cross the line towards bragging. BUT, these posts can work if you share a relatable story about the sale. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Instead of posting:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Just sold this home for my wonderful client! Thank you for the trust. We worked so hard to get this done and can’t wait to help you next. Just call us at xxxx-xxx-xxxx!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Share a relatable story:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://www.facebook.com/plugins/video.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Fangie.kay.baguio.keys.godornes%2Fvideos%2F3105240912845322%2F&amp;show_text=1&amp;width=560" width="560" height="572" style="border:none;overflow:hidden" scrolling="no" frameborder="0" allowtransparency="true" allow="encrypted-media" allowfullscreen="true"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>If you can, include nice photos of the property.</li><li>Share a story other potential clients can relate to (for example, if client is an OFW purchasing a property for investment).</li><li>Make it personal.</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<figure><iframe src="https://www.facebook.com/plugins/post.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Ffilipinohomesiligan%2Fposts%2F518497068309961&amp;width=500" width="500" height="793"></iframe></figure>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>3. Helpful News or Information</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>While your ultimate goal is for your social media platforms is to get people to <em>know,</em> <em>like</em>, and <em>trust </em>YOU, you should not post all about YOU all the time. Offer value to your followers.  Be your clients’ go-to resource for helpful news and information. This could be local information, or it might be tidbits of info about buying or selling.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<blockquote class="instagram-media" data-instgrm-captioned="" data-instgrm-permalink="https://www.instagram.com/p/B_vgVmClRA2/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading" data-instgrm-version="12" style=" background:#FFF; border:0; border-radius:3px; box-shadow:0 0 1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.5),0 1px 10px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.15); margin: 1px; max-width:540px; min-width:326px; padding:0; width:99.375%; width:-webkit-calc(100% - 2px); width:calc(100% - 2px);"><div style="padding:16px;"> <a href="https://www.instagram.com/p/B_vgVmClRA2/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading" style=" background:#FFFFFF; line-height:0; padding:0 0; text-align:center; text-decoration:none; width:100%;" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"> <div style=" display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-items: center;"> <div style="background-color: #F4F4F4; border-radius: 50%; flex-grow: 0; height: 40px; margin-right: 14px; width: 40px;"></div> <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; flex-grow: 1; justify-content: center;"> <div style=" background-color: #F4F4F4; border-radius: 4px; flex-grow: 0; height: 14px; margin-bottom: 6px; width: 100px;"></div> <div style=" background-color: #F4F4F4; border-radius: 4px; flex-grow: 0; height: 14px; width: 60px;"></div></div></div><div style="padding: 19% 0;"></div> <div style="display:block; height:50px; margin:0 auto 12px; width:50px;"><svg width="50px" height="50px" viewBox="0 0 60 60" version="1.1" xmlns="https://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="https://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"><g stroke="none" stroke-width="1" fill="none" fill-rule="evenodd"><g transform="translate(-511.000000, -20.000000)" fill="#000000"><g><path d="M556.869,30.41 C554.814,30.41 553.148,32.076 553.148,34.131 C553.148,36.186 554.814,37.852 556.869,37.852 C558.924,37.852 560.59,36.186 560.59,34.131 C560.59,32.076 558.924,30.41 556.869,30.41 M541,60.657 C535.114,60.657 530.342,55.887 530.342,50 C530.342,44.114 535.114,39.342 541,39.342 C546.887,39.342 551.658,44.114 551.658,50 C