,79.673 528.631,79.82 C531.831,79.965 532.853,80.001 541,80.001 C549.148,80.001 550.169,79.965 553.369,79.82 C556.562,79.673 558.743,79.167 560.652,78.425 C562.623,77.658 564.297,76.634 565.965,74.965 C567.633,73.296 568.659,71.625 569.425,69.651 C570.167,67.743 570.674,65.562 570.82,62.369 C570.966,59.17 571,58.147 571,50 C571,41.851 570.966,40.831 570.82,37.631"></path></g></g></g></svg></div><div style="padding-top: 8px;"> <div style=" color:#3897f0; font-family:Arial,sans-serif; font-size:14px; font-style:normal; font-weight:550; line-height:18px;"> View this post on Instagram</div></div><div style="padding: 12.5% 0;"></div> <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: row; margin-bottom: 14px; align-items: center;"><div> <div style="background-color: #F4F4F4; border-radius: 50%; height: 12.5px; width: 12.5px; transform: translateX(0px) translateY(7px);"></div> <div style="background-color: #F4F4F4; height: 12.5px; transform: rotate(-45deg) translateX(3px) translateY(1px); width: 12.5px; flex-grow: 0; margin-right: 14px; margin-left: 2px;"></div> <div style="background-color: #F4F4F4; border-radius: 50%; height: 12.5px; width: 12.5px; transform: translateX(9px) translateY(-18px);"></div></div><div style="margin-left: 8px;"> <div style=" background-color: #F4F4F4; border-radius: 50%; flex-grow: 0; height: 20px; width: 20px;"></div> <div style=" width: 0; height: 0; border-top: 2px solid transparent; border-left: 6px solid #f4f4f4; border-bottom: 2px solid transparent; transform: translateX(16px) translateY(-4px) rotate(30deg)"></div></div><div style="margin-left: auto;"> <div style=" width: 0px; border-top: 8px solid #F4F4F4; border-right: 8px solid transparent; transform: translateY(16px);"></div> <div style=" background-color: #F4F4F4; flex-grow: 0; height: 12px; width: 16px; transform: translateY(-4px);"></div> <div style=" width: 0; height: 0; border-top: 8px solid #F4F4F4; border-left: 8px solid transparent; transform: translateY(-4px) translateX(8px);"></div></div></div></a> <p style=" margin:8px 0 0 0; padding:0 4px;"> <a href="https://www.instagram.com/p/B_vgVmClRA2/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading" style=" color:#000; font-family:Arial,sans-serif; font-size:14px; font-style:normal; font-weight:normal; line-height:17px; text-decoration:none; word-wrap:break-word;" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">🤔THINGS TO KNOW WHEN BUYING A HOUSE!💯🏠 ✔ 💰Budget - magkano ba kaya mong monthly? Kung magkano lang kaya mo doon ka magumpisa tumingin. ✔ 🛣️Location - consider mo parin budget mo. Kung mura lang siguradong malayo sa Downtown yan. 5 million na po up presyo sa Downtown. ✔ 💵Required Monthly Salary - Check mo na kaagad kung magkano sweldo mo kase doon lang magbabase kung magkano monthly pwede mo kunin! ✔ 🚻Marital Status - laging tandaan ang legalities kapag kasal ka sa papel kahit na hiwalay kayo sa mata ng batas conjugal property padin ang lahat ng pagmamayari ninyo. 😱Common Questions: 1. Saan po ba may mura? ✔ Depende sa location mo gusto, basta ang tandaan mo, basta mura malayo na talaga sa Downtown. 2. May Rent To Own po ba kayo? ✔ wala naman talagang rent to own. Maglalabas ka rin ng pera sa Equity or Downpayment at yung remaining pwede na maloan sa Bank/pagibig at magmomonthly ka nalang sa Bank/pagibig kaya parang rent to own ang labas. 3. May Lipat Agad po ba kayo? ✔ kung kaya mo magbayad ng cash maaring makalipat ka agad. ✔ kung installment hihintayin muna matapos Downpayment pagbayad na chaka palang maprocess sa Bank/pagibig na usually 3-6mos. (pwede mo bayaran ng cash ang Downpayment para maprocess agad sa Bank/pagibig) 4. Kelan pwede makalipat? ✔ kung na release na ng Bank/pagibig ang loan mo. 5. Ano ang Pre-selling? ✔ ibig sabihin nito itatayo palang ang bahay mo usually 18-24mos construction sa mga affordable or low cost housing. Ang maganda nito mura pa ang price ng bahay kase wala pang development. Maari mo din bayaran pa ng installment ang Downpayment or Equity. 6. Ano ang Equity? ✔ ito ay same lang ng Downpayment at required mong bayaran bago pwede maloan sa pagibig. How to Avail: 1. Join our Free Tripping! 2. Choose a unit after tripping and pay the reservation fee Initial Requirements: 1) 2 Valid ID(SSS, Company, TIN, Passport, PRC, etc.) -One month latest payslip 2) Within 30days ready the requirements then after that the downpayment will start 3) Submit the remaining requirements within 30days from reservation 4) After downpayment wait for Bank/Pagibig processing 3-6mos before the start of Monthly Amortization.</a></p> <p style=" color:#c9c8cd; font-family:Arial,sans-serif; font-size:14px; line-height:17px; margin-bottom:0; margin-top:8px; overflow:hidden; padding:8px 0 7px; text-align:center; text-overflow:ellipsis; white-space:nowrap;">A post shared by <a href="https://www.instagram.com/xyzayape/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading" style=" color:#c9c8cd; font-family:Arial,sans-serif; font-size:14px; font-style:normal; font-weight:normal; line-height:17px;" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"> Millenial Blogger Realtor®️</a> (@xyzayape) on <time style=" font-family:Arial,sans-serif; font-size:14px; line-height:17px;" datetime="2020-05-03T22:21:07+00:00">May 3, 2020 at 3:21pm PDT</time></p></div></blockquote> <script async="" src="//www.instagram.com/embed.js"></script>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Stay away from polarizing topics (like politics and religion)</li><li>Be a very careful curator and only share verified information on things that people will be actually interested in reading.</li><li>If you\'re linking to a source, make sure it is reputable and give credit.</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>5. Learning Sessions and Industry Events</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/10-free-online-courses-that-can-benefit-every-thriving-and-future-entrepreneur/" target="_blank">Learning never stops</a>. You can update your followers and potential clients of your activities in your real estate career. When you post updates about your personal milestones as you advance in your profession, you are also showing that you are striving to be better and that people can trust that you know what you are doing.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<figure><iframe src="https://www.facebook.com/plugins/post.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Frealtorhermisa%2Fposts%2F1213433155743420&amp;width=500" width="500" height="702"></iframe></figure>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Sharing your speaking engagements help establish your personal brand as an industry expert as well. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://www.facebook.com/plugins/post.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Fazela.realestate%2Fposts%2F349369199796282&amp;width=500" width="500" height="534" style="border:none;overflow:hidden" scrolling="no" frameborder="0" allowtransparency="true" allow="encrypted-media"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>6. Lifestyle and Community-Based Content</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Part of being a real estate professional is being a go-to person for resources about the local scene. This establishes you as a local expert. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Share  aspects of living in an area -- upcoming local developments, places to visit, restaurants worth trying, or even COVID-related local updates. As people planning on moving to a new area research the place on Instagram, it will work to your advantage if you have geo-tags and hashtags on your photos. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://www.facebook.com/plugins/post.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Fmarcgodornes%2Fposts%2F3201513679885746&amp;width=500" width="500" height="421" style="border:none;overflow:hidden" scrolling="no" frameborder="0" allowtransparency="true" allow="encrypted-media"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>6. <strong>Design Ideas, Household Tips, and DIY Projects</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can also share some design ideas, household tips and Do-It-Yourself (DIY) project ideas for beginners.  These are helpful topics that can help boost viewer engagement. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<figure><iframe src="https://www.facebook.com/plugins/post.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Fangie.kay.baguio.keys.godornes%2Fposts%2F2914414501927965&amp;width=500" width="500" height="729"></iframe></figure>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>7. Housing Market Info</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Show people that you know your stuff and are well-informed about what’s happening in your local real estate market. This helps build your expertise.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://www.facebook.com/plugins/post.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Ffilipinohomes%2Fposts%2F2711573112422118&amp;width=500" width="500" height="547" style="border:none;overflow:hidden" scrolling="no" frameborder="0" allowtransparency="true" allow="encrypted-media"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Use simple terms. Avoid using industry jargon.</li><li>Be brief and concise.</li><li>Provide a link to the original source.</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>8. Personal Post</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Every once in a while, people would love to see posts from your personal life. Let people know the real you. Don\'t be afraid to show snippets of your life outside real estate. This lets people know there is a real person behind the real estate posts.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<figure><iframe src="https://www.facebook.com/plugins/post.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Fangie.kay.baguio.keys.godornes%2Fposts%2F2941991409170274&amp;width=500" width="500" height="610"></iframe></figure>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>9. Your Own Home</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Talk about your experience of buying (or selling) your own home.  You can also share the process from purchase, to turnover, to furnishing, and moving into your new home. This will help you empathize better to what your clients are going through when they buy or sell their homes as well.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>10. Real-Life Work</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It’s always interesting to see what people actually do at work. As a busy realtor, you do a lot of things for your clients.  Show people what you’re doing -- from your current work space, to virtual or actual open house, to office visits, etc.  It helps your clients understand your scope of work better.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<figure><iframe width="560" height="315" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/ct1avuDfBRI" allowfullscreen=""></iframe></figure>
<!-- /wp:html -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/07/Copy-of-Copy-of-filipino-homes.png','views' => '40','category_id' => '16','published_at' => '2020-07-31 11:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '460','title' => '9 Studio Condo Improvements that Boost Property Value','slug' => '9-studio-condo-improvements-that-boost-property-value','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With the trend of small space designs and smart homes, many young professionals now are lured towards condo living. <a href="http://localhost:3001/rent-condo-right-young-professionals/">A studio condo unit is an increasingly valuable investment option for young professionals</a> who want to earn passive income. But when it comes to home upgrades, what studio condo improvements add the most value?&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you want to jazz up your property value or consider putting it in the market, keeping these simple home improvement tips will definitely increase your property’s value in a few years time.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Here are 9 Studio Condo Improvements to focus on:</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/6ki6xlEtGNhdf33raSd1Of6RXfLVq_Bx89kb2crhRBnQC3aw3eDSyPm74d4sF7ToeiF7Wk5IuxI1ir2jBls53q-1wInUqh9azNjVPfSwGTKtPwIVskOsNovMw0Nqru1wtusaGCz-" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Tip#1 Upscale your door</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Want to make an impression? Why not invest in a keyless entry? There are smart lock devices or keyless entry system that enables you to enter your home with only a card or a pin code through Smartphone. This will definitely give you the “wows” from potential home renters or buyers.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Tip#2 Paint Color Makes a World of Difference</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/Q2NEfh4Jpi-WhVFy1C3lH8IIVFfjM-N8uQlTIf2FHZSd9tIE2iHl9n3oVYLsgFMmBOcar_vCyLaRWmKIEb3J-cFub1rQDp15Ib_nJs5R3ZWuldlKoULh4CwtNDm8oNImqaJmOf5z" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Did you know that <a href="http://filipinohomes.com/blog/paint/">investing in quality paint job results in an average return of 141%</a>? A paint job is one of the easiest and quickest ways to earn more profit when you are selling your property. Applying a fresh coat with a trendy color of your choice can absolutely give your home a new look!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Tip#3 Invest in Security &amp; Surveillance cameras</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/38dpZwvpgyvegEtADUpY-Bh7THs8s9kBZbl6xxdhQXNdk75Ilswytj9l-cZScEUSWFI6z0ae1C4pG9RBCm6IQXRlUmy9KjDY27630E3_dZ41iz_P7_LM2MvfnxotEcDztrZVKwGY" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>According to the survey conducted by <a href="https://www.softwareadvice.com/resources/smart-apartment-technology-survey/">Software Advice</a>, <em>security </em>is one of the main deciding factors when considering to upscale a property. With this said, leveraging on modern technology would be a great way to increase your condo’s value. Invest in home security cameras and surveillance Systems that can be controlled remotely and get peace of mind 24/7.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Tip#4 Enhance windows for good lighting&nbsp;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/a8nVEGZmwiLodbnkMWzZaQ-ijsZ0kA7tln5bN_D4N5d-3gP2-ieL_bK5TswENFA-xSkn_1erfnatpCeqx20RVxFvLuyrd6sGRZJt2a3yO9qPyIPXDVVQqWwpnoBSaHAxmyCxVP5y" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Good lighting can easily enhance a studio condo unit’s look and market. Honestly examine your windows if it needs to replaced with bigger ones to allow more adequate light to enter the room.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Tip#5 Build a "secret" storage</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/86yJFNZ9LKOCGxdxSDE2Ud-QZaHO_E8XYyae8-u3DrOoh4If0AJo9xbAhzi48XypIBQjBgpW1oyQtH671glAJHOXIpuXABgEaleuXD_KvGZMyXhIK7rXnCSQ5l5H0aIedqsv5JQ8" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Functionality, not just design! Having too many wardrobes makes your home look too cluttered. Why not build a “secret” storage or multi-purpose furniture? You can also elevate your bed and take advantage of the space underneath. This could be a huge asset your potential home buyers may find appealing.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Tip#6 Pick up a large, wall mirror</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/QI5GBVJkHXgSIg_Kc1W9rFH0G1JUQOgTas1m7XQWEeYydRZF7-p4e06UVGDcJhaQhshD94ZGGczYTpI-8YQQHDgxvITGLnxc8hiF6r1dVDrWM2phjyluWsuCqS8MnosEJpzDY7XB" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A large, wall mirror is a great addition to any studio condo unit. It\'s highly versatile and works really well in different parts of your home.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Tip#7 Invest in Smart Home Technology</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/mbmyCmn3qYJEDpt-lFW9KLBfeM138mJZN5GXmAWrhNATdt5kAro5_jaYoxOT0nUzZGIt11gkzEd2DtdRWQMpw0CEwaYXRuUzTjpG4LNkLLPu_gOfyNs_2OYy2LKhOICJ2gOPQwwM" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A 2015 survey by <a href="http://www.upnest.com/1/post/7-smart-home-technology-upgrades-that-increase-the-value-of-your-home/">Better Homes</a> found that 64% of millennials are interested in smart home technology. Backed by data, investing in smart technology is a huge advantage that can surely increase a studio condo unit’s resale value. That will surely make potential buyers giggle and feel excited. Filipino Homes partnered with <strong>Lifesmart Philippines</strong>. If you are interested to make your home a smart home contact your Filipino Homes Agent and ask about Lifesmart. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Tip#8 Update Your Bathroom</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/6QxeEnNtbTmiUNnyEEAVGqwzVn3ZjOw5A4jycE0buABlMF1ORN7H1Cgi0RAKhNGAegVwO0IL8wtSh3FLFwYNpCIWk1KS2w-g4S9ua5gWz1yIBpfxO8NGg0JaJSKR2f2vlznlSaAN" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Updating your bathroom can also go a long way in raising your condo unit’s value. You may want to consider installing new countertops and replacing the stained sinks and leaky faucets.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Tip#9 Make sure the ceiling and floor in good condition</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/nerJheycWFjw4G8u4w7YjLkm3fb7hU2W4i__ESmtEW1SPKlGaJFkYvlsKrpBOI8HiVx51aGOq5YfJyLE0TCja0PX13ZJtSRX_zNhsdtKPdLjBcW18F2uZyGGJbvQR1GaUnCv-IxS" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Last but not the least, ceiling and floors. Remember that these two are the most important parts of any home because these reflect of who and what you are as a homeowner. Do a thorough cleaning of the tiles or get rid of that old, stained carpet. Replace plumbing fixtures and enhance the mirrors with frames and lighting (if necessary) and make sure they’re in perfect condition.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>SUGGESTED FURTHER READINGS:</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/how-to-increase-your-propertys-value/">How to Increase Your Property’s Value</a></li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/room-dividers/">Small Space Hacks: Ideas for Room Dividers</a></li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/loft-bed-small-spaces/">Loft Bed Ideas for Small Spaces</a></li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/add-value-property-sale/">How to Add Value to Your Property For Sale</a></li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/condo-renovations-money/">5 Condo Renovations That Make Money</a></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->','excerpt' => 'If you want to jazz up your property value or consider putting it in the market, keeping these simple home improvement tips will definitely increase your property’s value in a few years time. ','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/07/9-Studio-Condo-Improvements-that-Boost-Property-Value.png','views' => '51','category_id' => '13','published_at' => '2020-08-04 00:38:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '461','title' => 'Tips to help you find a superstar real estate agent','slug' => 'tips-to-help-you-find-a-superstar-real-estate-agent','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Looking into buying a house or a property? The real estate industry and the property purchasing details can be overwhelming for first-time property buyers. Which is why a real estate agent can be helpful when it comes to getting the right information and helping advise before any actual purchase. But how will you know if the real estate agent you\'re working with is a perfect match for you and your needs? Here is how to find the best real estate agent for you!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5892,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/1-1.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5892"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Ask for recommendations</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It is always better to hear from someone how a real estate agent performs. Ask for recommendations from family, relatives and friends if they have worked with a real estate agent and if they recommend working with them. It is most likely that you know someone who already have worked with a real estate agent and will share their working experience with them. You want to work with someone who is professional, knows about the ins-and-outs of the real estate industry. And you want to work with someone who can communicate well with you. So make sure to ask about their working ethics, knowledge about the industry and communications skills.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Ask and verify license</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Trusting a stranger you are not 100% familiar can be nerve-racking. There are also a lot of people who are knowledgeable about real estate and can pretend to be a real estate agents. Ask for the brokerage firm or real estate license so you can to look it up at Professional Regulations Commission or PRC. You can check <a href="https://onlineverification.prc.gov.ph">PRC Real Estate License Verification</a>  here to verify their license.&nbsp; You can ask them which brokerage firm they belong to - like <a href="https://filipinohomes.com">Filipino Home</a>\'s  <a href="https://www.leuteriorealty.com">Leuterio Realty &amp; Brokerage</a>. Make sure to look into the brokerage list of real estate agents to see his/her claim is legit. At Filipino Homes, we make sure to do background checks with all the agents we have on the list and make sure they are professional and well- trained before they make it to our list.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5890,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/2.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5890"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Connect with them online &amp; check their profiles</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Before fully committing to working with them, ask to be connected online and see what type of posts and interactions are online. If they have some red flag posts or online interactions that seems shady, reconsider working with them. Always look for professionalism from a licensed real estate agent.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Ask for references &amp; work history</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you come across a real estate agent online and you want to know about their previous work, ask for their portfolio and references. Their portfolio will show you their property listings and the developers they work with. And their references will also help you decide whether to work with them or not. If you\'re selling a property, it is also smart to ask for their sell history, if they have sold a property similar to yours and how long it took them. That way you know that the agent you\'re working with can help you sell your property or buy one.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5891,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/3.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5891"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Only work with a local expert</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Work with someone who is knowledgeable and familiar with the area you are looking into buying a property at. Working with a local expect will help you with details like location, commute and traffic situations, or even surrounding neighbourhood. These are some information that might be minor and less important but may also be a decision factor for you and your family. At Filipino Homes we have a list of well-trained <a href="https://filipinohomes.com/agents">local real estate agents &amp; experts</a> whatever city or province you\'re planning to buy or sell a property. You will find their profiles complete with contact details and you can also see the top real estate agents in your area.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Looking into buying a house or a property? The real estate industry and the property purchasing details can be overwhelming for first-time property buyers. Which is why a real estate agent can be helpful when it comes to getting the right information and helping advise before any actual purchase. But how will you know if the real estate agent you\'re working with is a perfect match for you and your needs? Here is how to find the best real estate agent for you!','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/07/How-to-choose-the-best-real-estate-agent-for-you-3.png','views' => '60','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-08-05 00:46:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '462','title' => 'How to find the ideal home for starting or growing  family needs','slug' => 'how-to-find-the-ideal-home-for-starting-or-growing-family-needs','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Whether you are starting a family, expecting another child, or simply upgrading your home to fit your family\'s needs, there are a lot of factors to consider when buying a home for a growing family. There are things that your family needs in order to have a comfortable lifestyle.  And this included looking for a new home to fit everybody\'s needs. There are a couple of things you need to keep in mind and here are some tips to help you make the right choice.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5880,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/How-to-find-the-ideal-home-for-starting-or-growing-family-needs-3.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5880"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Budget</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Let\'s be straightforward here, you should not buy a home that you can not afford. Don\'t go into debt just to buy a bigger house thinking you need extra space but you do not have an extra budget for it. Keep in mind your other financial obligations including paying utility bills that cover a large home, children\'s tuition fees, and even home association fees or maintenance fees. Be realistic in choosing your home. The important thing is buying a home that you can keep without dealing with financial stresses.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5881,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/How-to-find-the-ideal-home-for-starting-or-growing-family-needs-4.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5881"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Location is important</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Location is one of the important factors when looking for a home. And with that in mind, you have to think about matters that are important to you and your family. Do you prefer a home near a school or your work office? Do you like to live within the city or you\'re okay to live in the suburb? Are you looking for a place that is near the shopping centers and business district? There are a lot of things that you need to look into to make sure that you won\'t regret purchasing a home, and the location is on top of that list. Remember that you can change your home with upgrades or renovations but you can not change it\'s location once you make that purchase.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5878,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/How-to-find-the-ideal-home-for-starting-or-growing-family-needs-2.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5878"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Know the neighbourhood</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>One of the reasons why you are in the market of buying a home is considering a new or young member/s in the family. Knowing the neighborhood that you want your child to grow up in or surrounded with is important. You want to feel safe in your own community and you want to be comfortable living with your neighbors. You do not have to be friends with everyone in the block but there is a certain level of comfort when you know that your neighbors also prefer a peaceful community.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5882,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/How-to-find-the-ideal-home-for-starting-or-growing-family-needs-5.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5882"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Check for security &amp; safety measures</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Everyone wants a safe home. If you\'re buying new property always look for safety issues in the actual home and the surrounding areas. Is the door, windows, or stairs safe enough from break-ins or possible accidents? Are there security guards keeping the community safe? Is it near a river that overflows with heavy rain? Does it flood in the area? Is the front/backyard fenced? These are some of the questions and details you want to look into when buying a home for the family. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Whether you are starting a family, expecting another child or simply upgrading your home to fit your family\'s needs, there are a lot of factors to consider when buying a home for a growing family. There  are things that your family needs in order to have a comfortable lifestyle.  And this included looking for a new home to fit everybody\'s needs. There are a couple of things you need to keep in mind and here are some tips to help you make the right choice.','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/07/How-to-find-the-ideal-home-for-starting-or-growing-family-needs-6.png','views' => '56','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-08-05 23:17:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '463','title' => 'Pros and Cons of Building a New House','slug' => 'pros-and-cons-of-building-a-new-house','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Being in quarantine has had us thinking of building our dream houses,  where we can comfortably stay in over an extended period of time -- a <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/webinar-filipino-homes-plus-to-introduce-homes-that-are-designed-for-new-normal-living/" target="_blank">quarantine-friendly home</a>, so to speak. While it does sound like a dream to build your own house, but there are some very real-world disadvantages.  In this blog post, we\'ll tackle the pros and cons of embarking on a construction project.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Pros:</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>1. <strong>Customization (to an extent)</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5924,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/floor-plan-1474454_1280-1024x678.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5924"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The main advantage of building your own house is you get to build the home as you want and choose everything from the floor plan to the materials and finishing you like. You can literally have anything your budget, physics, and permits will allow.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>2. Quality Control</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5925,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/stencil-1508277_1280-1024x680.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5925"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Being the primary decision maker for the house you are building allows you to be hands-on to everything, from planning to building to furnishing. You can make sure everything you choose is up to your standard.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3> 3. No environmental or health worries</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>New homes are built to  current building codes. They are often more energy efficient, built with sustainability in mind and with environmentally friendly materials.  You also have the option to incorporate up-to-date technology, including solar panels or has modern insulation, in building your new home that will help you reduce energy costs down the line. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>4. &nbsp;Less likelihood of dealing with maintenance issues</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5926,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/milivoj-kuhar-Te48TPzdcU8-unsplash-1024x681.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5926"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Moving into a new home means you’re less likely to deal with big-ticket maintenance issues like leaky roofs or problematic walls and floors.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>5. Investment Potential </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5927,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/aaron-huber-G7sE2S4Lab4-unsplash-1024x678.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5927"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In terms of investment potential, building your home allows you the flexibility to future-proof your home. You can build a home with sustainability in mind that can potentially appraise for more than you spent building it. Doing this may attract a higher quality of tenant (or buyer if you decide to sell later), who will pay more for the luxury touches in newer homes.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Cons:</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>1.  A drawn-out process</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5928,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/etienne-girardet-sgYamIzhAhg-unsplash-1024x678.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5928"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here in the Philippines, it would typically take an average four of six months to finish a&nbsp;house&nbsp;construction project, depending on the size and design of the&nbsp;house. &nbsp;This time-frame may often need to be stretched out even more if there are any hold ups, mistakes, or clashing schedules with hired workers. You would also need about 6 weeks for blueprints and building permits. This means you won\'t be able to move in right away and you might need to be prepared to cover the cost of renting until you can move into your newly built place.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>2.   Location</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Location can also prove to be an issue with new builds. Most residential&nbsp;lots in the market are often on the outskirts of cities and not in central locations. This could mean longer commutes for your place of work, supermarkets, schools, etc.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>3.  Being your own project manager </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5929,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/daniel-mccullough-HtBlQdxfG9k-unsplash-1024x576.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5929"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Building your own house and being the key decision maker on the direction of the project from planning to financing can potentially be stressful. You would need to answer to the questions of your contractors, suppliers, etc and may have to deal with the unexpected change in scopes or change in materials.  Some people may have the skills for it, some unfortunately don’t. Ask architects, designers, or contractors who will manage the project if you are not able to. This may mean additional expense, but could help you keep your sanity. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>4.  Unpredictable weather </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here in the Philippines, we often have bad weather that can put delays on work getting started or completed. Be sure to ask your contractors what are the contingencies that they have in place in case it gets rainy for an extended period of time.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>5.  Unexpected out-of-pocket expenses</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":2342,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/pool-money-with-family-and-friends-real-estate-investment-filipinohomes.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-2342"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Unplanned expenses have a funny way of sneaking up on you when tackling new constructions. It may be very tempting to purchase better materials and go overboard in post-move costs like landscaping and furnishing.  Play it safe by budgeting for only those you can cover with cash.&nbsp; </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>FURTHER READINGS:</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/pros-and-cons-of-building-a-new-house/" target="_blank"><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/?p=5989" target="_blank">How to Apply for Building Permit in the Philippines</a></a></li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/?p=5920" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">5 Things to Do Before You Build Your New Home</a></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->','excerpt' => 'Being in quarantine has had us thinking of building our dream houses,  where we can comfortably stay in over an extended period of time -- a quarantine-friendly home, so to speak. While it does sound like a dream to build your own house, but there are some very real-world disadvantages.  In this blog post, we\'ll tackle the pros and cons of embarking on a construction project.','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/08/Copy-of-Copy-of-filipino-homes-1.png','views' => '48','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-08-07 00:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '464','title' => 'Condotels Meet Investors Business and Leisure Objectives in the Philippines','slug' => 'condotels-meet-investors-business-and-leisure-objectives-in-the-philippines','content' => '<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>What could be better than owning a vacation home and earning rentals when you aren\'t using it? Let me share you a story;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>John Smith with his Filipina wife from London, UK, owned a traditional vacation home, in Metro Manila, Philippines. But after a year away from the country; they arrived during the summer holidays to find the tenants that were renting the property had run away leaving the property abandoned. Unfortunately,  his caretaker is no longer to be found and pocketed the rent. So he sold the house and bought two condo-hotel units instead.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://myhouse.ph/wp-content/uploads/2019/03/Tambuli-Seaside-Living-Condominium-Update.jpg" alt="condotels philippines"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Now, Mr. Smith and his family own Condotel Suites in Manila and Cebu. They expect to earn money when the unit is rented out to other guests. Mr. Smith, his wife April, and their seven-year-old daughter spends their Summer Vacation in their unit at the Lancaster Suites in Manila, the Philippines. A 450-unit Condo Hotel built and managed by Pacific Concord Properties Inc under the Lancaster brand of Hotels.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Mr. Smith says. "If the condotel rents out the unit during 11 months of the year, I’ll make enough money to take my family on a second trip to the Philippines during the Christmas Holidays and go an extended way to covering the mortgage payments."</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Expectations like Smith’s are driving the marketplace for Condotels to new heights within the Philippines.</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"width":592,"height":333,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large is-resized"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/276724/pexels-photo-276724.jpeg?auto=compress&amp;cs=tinysrgb&amp;dpr=1&amp;w=500" alt="condotels philippines" width="592" height="333"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Owners of the Condotel units can decide to stay in their units and that they share 60% of any income. The Lancaster Atrium along with the finished Lancaster Suites Manila is the hub for Lancaster Condotels. The 42-story Lancaster Suites Manila, for instance, features studio, one-bedroom, and two-bedroom Condotel units, likewise as penthouse suites. The units are available for daily, weekly, or monthly rental.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In Cebu, Citadines of Baseline Residences is managed by Colliers International. Colliers is a world Property Management Company that handles condotels everywhere the globe. And there are lots of latest condotel projects within the country today.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://r-cf.bstatic.com/images/hotel/max1024x768/226/226432374.jpg" alt="condotels philippines citadines"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Several new Condotel projects are also within the works on the opposite side of the country. Anthony Leuterio, founding father of Filipino Homes said, a significant condo-hotel project is being considered by real estate development companies with several investors in Cebu, Philippines. We’ve got numerous clients requesting for Luxury Condotel Suites in Cebu and other areas within the country, he said. Its sort of a whole new era of Overseas Investments that are springing up isn\'t something that we’ve typically seen within the past. These Investors are all characteristically trying to find a five-star hotel resort, with all the features of a hotel that may be used for vacations and so lend the units when not in use.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There are new and exciting luxury five-star properties or high-end developments planned in Cebu Philippines and sold by invitation only. It will start within the 150,000 to 200,000 dollar range but can go all the far to 600,000 dollars for two-bedroom Penthouse suites and 800,000 dollars for a Grand Penthouse. Of course, International gateways from Europe, South East Asian, and therefore the US to Cebu-Mactan International Airport are within 10 minutes. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>All units have sea views, beach toys, and other lifestyle amenities like a spa and fine dining restaurants. It\'ll come fully furnished and finished to the very best European or US standards with fully fitted kitchens and fitted bedroom suites. Each unit sold includes all appliances, split type central unit air-conditioning, SMART TVs, and state of the art condotel management systems. Units are going to be significantly larger in size than a typical hotel room. Yet still a way better value for money investment option than paying 800,000 dollars for a studio suite in maybe Dubai or Panama or a cool million dollars for a condo in Chicago.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>A financing solution</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Condotels started within the Philippines still as within the US and Europe within the mid-1980s. But didn\'t become popular until after the Asian Crisis of 1997 made it difficult for hotel developers to get conventional financing for brand spanking new projects. They turned to the condotel concept, pre-selling rooms to individual investors, to lift equity.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In theory, the Condo Hotel meets two objectives that of the developer to urge a project built which of the client who, like Mr Thomas, wants a hassle-free place to vacation and also the chance to create a bit money on the side. Baby boomers are getting active vacation homebuyers, says Leuterio. If you purchase a condo in Manila, he says, you’re not going to use it quite 30 days a year. If you would like to rent it out, you’ll hire a management company and take your chances.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong><em>The attraction of a Condo Hotel suite is that you just can own a unit in a hotel, enjoy first-class amenities and standards of maintenance, then let the hotel company arrange all rentals for a percentage share of the revenues.</em></strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://myhouse.ph/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/Sheraton-Cebu-Pool-Area-Update.jpg" alt="condotels philippines"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Deciding whether a Condo-Hotel Suite meets your objectives is not really difficult or complicated. Condotels are a bit costlier, costing 10% to twenty over traditional residential condominiums in most markets. It\'s due to the nature of the income-earning investment potential. Generally, condotels have more amenities and facilities than in most residential condo buildings. The monthly maintenance costs, to pay your share of the hotel upkeep, run about $50/month for your 300-square-foot studio unit which is almost the same as a typical residential condo. The win-win clincher is that the percentage ROI expected through rental returns that the residential condominiums will never yield due to the Condotel Rental Pool concept of the event.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Buying a Condotel unit makes you an investor within the hotel industry. Leuterio says the Philippine hotel industry is currently hot. Shangri-La, Four Seasons, Marriott, and other resort and hotel developers are in build with several new hotels within the country. We\'ve got more heads than beds and therefore the industry should remain healthy for several years to come. Recently we have Hotel Condominium projects coming into the market, Like in Bohol, Davao, Iloilo and more.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Mr. Thomas says he purchased the smallest amount of expensive condotel units available within the Philippines. Spending less than $45,000 for his Lancaster Suites Manila studio unit and about $85,000 last November for a one-bedroom unit, expected rental revenues from his Lancaster units will quite cover his new 15-year bank mortgage payments. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Interesting, isn’t it? Contact your Filipino Homes Agent today to know your Condotel options. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Related Readings:</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/what-is-a-condotel-why-invest-in-one/">What is a Condotel and Why invest in one? </a></li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/condo-hotels-in-the-philippines-the-hottest-niche-in-the-philippine-investment-property-market/">Condo Hotels in the Philippines: The Hottest Niche in the Philippine Investment Property market</a></li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/real-estate-investing-in-the-philippines-this-year-2020/">Real Estate Investing in the Philippines this year 2020</a></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Condotels Meet Investorsí Business and Leisure Objectives, Offering First-Class Amenities and Share of the Revenues
','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/08/filipino-homes-realtor-blogger-xyza-yape.png','views' => '47','category_id' => '16','published_at' => '2020-08-08 00:00:35','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '465','title' => 'Foreclosed Property - Why people are buying these cheaper properties','slug' => 'foreclosed-property-why-people-are-buying-these-cheaper-properties','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you\'ve been researching "property investing" or "buying a home" or "property for your family", you might have stumbled on Foreclosed Properties and wondered what it is. Properties are considered foreclosed property when a lender, like banks or Pag-Ibig, get the property from the property owner (borrower) who fails to pay their amortizations or defaulted their mortgages. When you loan property or borrow money from the bank or Pag-ibig to purchase a property, the owner of the property is technically the bank (or Pag-ibig). You as the purchaser is a borrower. The only time, you can claim it yours is when you already fully paid the borrowed money. Thus, the bank (or Pag-ibig) will sell the foreclosed home for slightly less than it might be worth to get their investment back.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5901,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/What-is-a-foreclosure-property-Should-I-be-targeting-one-for-my-new-purchase-3.png" alt="foreclosed property " class="wp-image-5901"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Is it true that foreclosed properties are cheaper?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Foreclosed properties is sold below the market value because the bank is motivated to get the property sold and would negotiate more than a seller would. If you happen to find a foreclosed property in a subdivision, you can be sure that the foreclosed property is cheaper than the newly built unit or ready to occupy unit in the subdivision.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Why is a foreclosed property cheaper?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The seller of the property is the lender: bank or Pag-Ibig. These lenders are selling the property to get their investments back. They are not after the profit but more of the sale or disposal of the property. And since the property has been used, the conditions are not at par with the newly constructed units or homes.  These can not be sold at the same price as those newly built ones. The more run down the property is, the more likely it is sold for less.<br></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5902,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/What-is-a-foreclosure-property-Should-I-be-targeting-one-for-my-new-purchase-2.png" alt="foreclosed property search" class="wp-image-5902"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>How do I find foreclosed properties in the area or city I want?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Banks or Pag-ibig usually post their foreclosed property listings available online on their websites. Just to be sure, you can visit the bank or Pag-Ibig and check their foreclosed property listings. You can also find <a href="https://filipinohomes.com/properties/forclosure">Foreclosure Properties in the Philippines</a> is real estate listings like Filipino Homes.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Who owns the foreclosed property?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Once the property is foreclosed, the bank or Pag-Ibig is the absolute owner of the property. In some cases, previous owners still live in the foreclosed property. They will be notified to peacefully vacate and remove their belongings in the property within a grace period. It is highly recommended before you purchase a foreclosed property, that you check if the previous owners are still there. Preferably, choose the properties that are not being used by the previous owners anymore.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5904,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/What-is-a-foreclosure-property-Should-I-be-targeting-one-for-my-new-purchase-1.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5904"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Why should I consider foreclosed property in my next property investment move?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The more run-down the property is, the cheaper it is sold in the market. Most people who have the intention to buy the property as an investment is to buy a run-down foreclosed property. They do this so they can buy it for less and reconstruct or renovate the property after buying it. Renovating the property will give you an increase in the property value. Then you can have it rented or sold for a higher price or their current market value. Definitely higher than what you bought it for.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/07/1.png','views' => '44','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-08-10 01:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '466','title' => 'Real Estate for Filipina HomeBased Moms','slug' => 'real-estate-for-filipina-homebased-moms','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes Founder Mr.ANTHONY GERARD O. LEUTERIO, REB, and e-PRO®Founder, Leuterio Realty &amp; BrokerageFounder, Filipinohomes Institute of Real Estate - PRO® Certified Broker was recently invited by one of the largest online community for Filipino moms, <a href="https://web.facebook.com/fhmomscommunity/">Filipina HomeBased Moms</a> on Facebook for a free real estate webinar for Filipino HomeBased moms last 12 August 2020.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Along with Ms. AZELA HONOR an International Realtor Member who is also a Real Estate Broker and motivational speaker the live webinar discussed the great waiting opportunity for moms in the real estate industry.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5957,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Real-Estate-for-Filipina-HomeBased-Moms-02-1024x577.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5957"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Why real estate business is perfect for Filipina HomeBased Moms </h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Real estate is very flexible. It is not an 8H office job and can be done at home or anywhere else. Homebased moms may have some free time in between their chores and errands and can easily use this time productively.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>What educational background do moms need to be in real estate?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There are no set or strict educational attainment in order to be in the real estate industry. You can start being an accredited sales person and can undergo trainings and courses with the guidance of brokers to help you get a license and also be an effective agent. Extensive trainings are available to help moms through the first real estate online courses at <a href="http://realestatetraining.ph">Filipinohomes Institute of Real Estate</a>. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Do moms need gadgets if they plan to join real estate?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>What you need is a laptop or mobile phone and internet connetion. These are basic items and services that we already already have in our homes. With technology, it is easy to be connected to people online. Communication has become easier with its different forms. Not only can we just send text messages through emails and social networks, we can also send photos and videos as well. Phone and video calls is also an effective way to communicate online to talk with a client or to do your trainings without having to sacrifice your family time.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>"Mommies are the real winners" Lueterio said, further emphasing that with hard work and dedication, anyone can succeed in real estate and with booming real estate in the PH - Filipina HomeBased Moms best time to join is now.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/08/Real-Estate-for-Filipina-HomeBased-Moms.jpg','views' => '42','category_id' => '16','published_at' => '2020-08-17 01:10:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '467','title' => 'Home Owners Association: Pros and Cons for Homebuyers - Rules, Fees and Role','slug' => 'home-owners-association-pros-and-cons-for-homebuyers-rules-fees-and-role','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>House hunting? If you\'re looking into buying a new home or property in a subdivision or condominium, chances are you will find yourself moving into a home with home owners association. One thing to look it up and ask your real estate agent is whether there is an Home Owners Association involved in managing the community because this will entails a series of responsibility at your end.<br><br><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homeowner_association">Home Owners Association</a> is an organization within a community that oversees  it by enforcing community rules and maintaining the common areas. These are common in planned communities and apartment buildings. This will also entail added financial responsibility by the home owner with certain dues and fees to pay for. Often times, before purchasing a unit or home, the home buyer is informed of the rules that govern the community before he/she can fully commit to buying a property there.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5949,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><a href="https://filipinohomes.com/properties/sale"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/2.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5949"/></a><figcaption>Astra Centre at Cebu City</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>The Pros of having HOA</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Lifestyle Amenities</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Most communities with Home Owners Association will have access to recreational amenities such as swimming pools, parks, gyms and other shared facilities. These are free for use for all or limited number of household members. These charges visitors for using these amenities making it earn income for the community. Most of these amenities are community and family centered with adults and kids in mind. It encourages neighbours to commune in a safe place and offers activities for families without having to go out of the community</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Common Area Management</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Most communities have common areas that residents can enjoy but besides the management of the lifestyle amenities, there are some common areas that needs managing. These includes lawns, lobby and hallways that everyone uses. These areas are managed by the HOA from cleanliness to maintenance. So when you see a broken or shifted tiling on the lobby, you can be assured that HOA will fix that without added financial burden to the residents.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5950,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><a href="https://filipinohomes.com/properties/sale"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/3.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5950"/></a><figcaption>Lancaster New City Cavite</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Utilities included in your fees</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With your monthly fees, you not only can you avail and use of the lifestyle amenities but management of the basic utilities like sewer management, trash collecting, general maintenance, light and water use in common areas are covered.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Appeaser/Mediator</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you have a problem with a neighbour regarding loud noises or broken piping that leaks through your unit, you can be assured that HOA facilitate communication between both residents. There is no need for confrontation and with rules set by HOA, it\'s easy to have all residents exercise courtesy and respect to their neighbours.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5951,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><a href="https://filipinohomes.com/properties/sale"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/1.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5951"/></a><figcaption>Novona Lumbia</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Cons of having HOA</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Financial Obligations</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you\'re planning to buy a property in a community, make sure to ask if it\'s an Home Owners Association community. If it is, expect that you will have to pay monthly fees to not only enjoy the amenities but to also have everything else in the community managed and cared for. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Compliance to Rules</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>HOA not only manages the physical areas of the community but also manages the peace within the community. They make sure to maintain a peaceful community for the residents and make it an ideal place to live. This entails having rues and regulations set in place for all residents, staff and visitors. It can be a hassle to go through rules when you feel that you\'re entitled to do what you like in a community you\'re paying for but these rules ensures efficient management and peacefulness.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/08/Home-Owners-Association_-Pros-and-Cons-for-Homebuyers-Rules-Fees-and-Role.png','views' => '43','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-08-19 01:22:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '468','title' => 'How Much Should I Expect to Pay to Build a House?','slug' => 'how-much-should-i-expect-to-pay-to-build-a-house','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Many of us have spent much more time at home during quarantine, and many of us may have been daydreaming of building our ideal homes and start planning to make the <em>dream home</em> to a <em>real home</em>. If you\'re wondering how much it costs to build a house in the Philippines, this blog post is for you. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/2219035/pexels-photo-2219035.jpeg?auto=compress&amp;cs=tinysrgb&amp;dpr=2&amp;h=650&amp;w=940" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Rough Estimate by Area Method</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5998,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><a href="https://www.arcadis.com/en/asia/our-perspectives/research-and-publications/arcadis-construction-cost-handbook/"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/construction-cost-1024x503.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5998"/></a></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>According to the&nbsp;<em><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.arcadis.com/en/asia/our-perspectives/research-and-publications/arcadis-construction-cost-handbook/" target="_blank">2020 Construction Cost Handbook</a></em>&nbsp;by Langdon &amp; Seah Philippines Inc., the cost in building a house varies depending on the type and size. Terraced houses and average standard homes (one to two bedrooms) may cost from Php 48,111 to  Php 58,865 per square meter. Detached houses and high-end residences, on the other hand, may cost from Php 93,408 to Php 158,414 per square meter. These values are inclusive of the expenses for electrical, mechanical, and plumbing services.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Please note that the area method of estimation is advisable to be used to get a ballpark figure for budgeting purposes only. There are a lot of factors that can affect the actual cost of construction, including your location, types of materials used, types of finishes and fixtures, etc. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em><strong>READ:</strong></em>  <a href="http://localhost:3001/?p=6020" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">7 Factors that Affect the House Construction Cost</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>Permits and Other Paperwork Required</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/2058136/pexels-photo-2058136.jpeg?auto=compress&amp;cs=tinysrgb&amp;dpr=2&amp;h=650&amp;w=940" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Along with the cost of materials and labor, you also need to secure a number of permits and paperwork for your project to push through. Here are the common permits you need:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><strong>Architectural Plan</strong>&nbsp;– &nbsp;a design and planning for your home, containing&nbsp;architectural&nbsp;drawings, specifications of the design, calculations, time planning of the building process, and other documentation. This will be used as a reference in your construction project. This will be provided by your contractor.<br></li><li><strong>Barangay Permit</strong>&nbsp;– a permit from the barangay that has jurisdiction over the area you’re building a house in.<br></li><li><strong>Building Permit</strong>&nbsp;– a document issued by Department of Building Official that serves as your official consent to commence any construction, demolition, addition, or renovation of your property.&nbsp;<br><br>Fees may range from Php 6,000 and above depending on the your construction size, municipality/city location and the assessment plan. Fees in the provinces are usually cheaper than in the cities.<br><br><strong><em>READ</em></strong>:  <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/?p=5989" target="_blank">How to Apply for Building Permit in the Philippines</a>  <br></li><li><strong>Occupancy Permit</strong>&nbsp;– a document that signifies that a licensed building surveyor is satisfied with the completed building work and that the new house is suitable for occupancy. You will need to secure this when construction is finished.</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/08/Copy-of-Copy-of-filipino-homes-2.png','views' => '230','category_id' => '16','published_at' => '2020-08-21 00:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '469','title' => 'What happens during a recession and how to survive from it','slug' => 'what-happens-during-a-recession-and-how-to-survive-from-it','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It’s official! Last August 6, the Philippine government declared that the country has dived into <a href="https://www.cnnphilippines.com/business/2020/8/6/Q2-2020-PH-economy-recession.html">recession</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A recession occurs when economic activity declines, causing widespread job loss, weak trade activity, falling prices, and more government relief, which obviously caused by the COVID-19 global pandemic.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://cdn.pixabay.com/photo/2017/12/27/09/32/businessman-3042272_960_720.jpg" alt="What happens during a recession and how to survive from it" /></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>What happens during a recession?</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Typically, during a recession, businesses see less demand. There will be fewer availability of jobs and cost-cutting measures will follow, which unfortunately includes laying-off employees.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As people and businesses stop spending as much, the stock market may also go down. The share price of most companies will definitely decline, if not sideways.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Moreover, the government will most likely come out with several monetary policies to stimulate the economy. Among these is cutting interest rates for banks or lending institutions to encourage businesses to borrow money. Again, these measures are done to stimulate the economy.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: Take <a href="http://localhost:3001/a-look-at-the-financial-crises-in-the-philippine-real-estate-sector/">a look at the Financial Crises in the Philippine Real Estate Sector</a> to better understand the economic downturn brought by the COVID-19 pandemic</p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>How long will it last?</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The safest answer would be a year or more. Well, that’s how economists say it. But one thing is for sure, it will not last forever. Recessions are generally short-term and our economy will soon cope up with this.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6080,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/what-happens-during-a-recession-and-how-to-survive-filipino-homes-2.jpg" alt="What happens during an Economic Recession and how to survive from it?" class="wp-image-6080" /></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>What to do during a recession and how to survive from it?</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Rather than worry about recession, you can prepare yourself by taking precautionary measures to protect your finances and survive from it.&nbsp;The following are ways you can do to make sure your finances are in good shape even if the economy falters.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":6126,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/value-your-job-1.jpg" alt="value your job" class="wp-image-6126" /></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#1 <strong>Value your job</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As said above, during a recession, people may lose jobs, or find it difficult to secure jobs. So, if you have one, treasure it. Make an extra effort and provide quality outputs, but do not overdo. This might lower your chances of getting laid off or even might secure you a promotion. Plus it also helps your company to be productive and stay afloat.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#2 <strong>Minimize your spending</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://storage.needpix.com/rsynced_images/calculator-428294_1280.jpg" alt="minimize spending" /></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Lessen your expenses and find cheaper alternatives to your costs of living. Downsizing your lifestyle will definitely save you during this time. There are lots of ways you can start living frugally especially during quarantine. Since travel and going out is restricted, you can actually incur your travel or “personal” fund to your emergency or investment fund. Learning how to get by with less is your key to survive in recession.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#3 <strong>Avoid unnecessary debts</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://cdn.pixabay.com/photo/2017/06/08/12/32/wallet-2383496_960_720.jpg" alt="Be economical" /></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Paying down or avoiding unnecessary debt is one sure way to survive a recession or any economic storm. Carrying high levels of debt is very risky during this time because a slight change could actually affect your ability to pay your debt. If you have existing loans or long-term debts, then check if it makes sense to restructure them when the government cuts interest rates.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#4 <strong>Make ways to earn extra income</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://live.staticflickr.com/8436/28474822063_05f626694b_b.jpg" alt="Side Hustle Keyboard" /></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Having multiple streams of income can really help. If one income source starts to dwindle – or gets eliminated completely – you have other sources to fall back on to help keep you afloat. Investing during a recession isn\'t for the faint of heart.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#5 <strong>Diversify your investments</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://live.staticflickr.com/7163/6793832171_cc913a5f97_b.jpg" alt="Diversification" /></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In addition to having multiple income streams, it’s also important to diversify your investment. Remember that how you invest during this time can be just as important as what you invest in. Go through your investment portfolio. Honestly assess and look for ways to spread out your investments across different industries rather than trying to time the market.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When it comes to investment vehicles, real estate investing -whether it’s buying a home, a condo, or even land- <a href="http://localhost:3001/why-real-estate-is-a-good-investment-option-despite-a-crisis/">property investing is a good investment option despite a crisis</a> because it generally appreciates with time. If you don’t have enough funds yet to buy your own property, there are other ways to <a href="http://localhost:3001/millennials-can-invest-real-estate/">start investing in real estate</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>Takeaways</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A recession is a normal economic cycle. Although this one is caused by extraordinary reasons and is something beyond our control, what we can control is how we prepare for tough financial times.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Saving more. Downsizing lifestyle. Managing debt. Increasing cash flow and diversification are just a few tips that can help you survive a recession. Instead, have peace in mind knowing that while you can’t control the world, your finances are under control.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Further Readings:</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/how-to-invest-your-money-during-the-coronavirus-pandemic-5-questions-to-ask-yourself-before-investing/">How to Invest Your Money During the Coronavirus Pandemic: 5 Questions to Ask Yourself Before Investing</a></li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/what-are-the-global-real-estate-implications-of-covid-19-pandemic/">What are the Global Real Estate Implications of COVID-19 Pandemic?</a></li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/5-money-saving-tips-for-gen-z/">5 Money-Saving Tips for Gen Z</a></li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/is-it-best-to-look-for-a-home-despite-covid-19-crisis/">Is It Best To Look For a Home Despite Covid-19 Crisis?</a></li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/making-money-in-real-estate-9-basic-ways/">Making Money In Real Estate – 9 Basic Ways</a></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/08/What-happens-during-an-Economic-Recession-and-how-to-survive-from-it.jpg','views' => '47','category_id' => '11','published_at' => '2020-08-23 21:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '470','title' => '5 Things to Do Before You Build Your New Home','slug' => '5-things-to-do-before-you-build-your-new-home','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The process of building a new home starts long before the foundation is poured. The construction process can be more efficient and less stressful if you have a good plan and find an honest, competent builder. To avoid costly mistakes when building your new home, start with these five important steps.&nbsp;<br><br></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 id="mntl-sc-block_1-0-2">1. Plan your budget</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5981,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/kelly-sikkema-3-Tc_5LROrM-unsplash-1024x683.jpg" alt="5 Things to Do Before You Build Your New Home" class="wp-image-5981"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Start with a budget.</strong> Develop a realistic idea of how much you can afford and&nbsp;how much it will actually cost&nbsp;to build your dream home. This phase is really about balancing your wants with an honest assessment of what you need and can afford.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Also, consider the "hidden costs" of owning a home. There are many one-time costs associated with building a new home — furniture, landscaping, phone and internet set-up fees, etc. Recognize too that home ownership also comes with ongoing monthly expenses such as insurance, property taxes, and other maintenance costs. When budgeting for a new home, think about how much you\'ll need to spend to live comfortably in your home.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 id="mntl-sc-block_1-0-20">2. Pick a house plan</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5982,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/daniel-mccullough-HtBlQdxfG9k-unsplash-1-1024x576.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5982"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Next, <strong>define the project scope. </strong>It\'s time to think about what kind of home you want aligned to how much you can afford. Would you like to have a bungalow or a multi-storey home? How many bedrooms and bathrooms? What type of finish? Detailed specifications of your desired house can help you get more&nbsp;accurate quotes, a faster workflow, and prevent extra charges for add-on works during the construction process.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 id="mntl-sc-block_1-0-27">3. Assemble your team</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can now begin <strong>lining up the team of experts</strong> to design and construct your house.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Consult an architect, civil engineer, or interior designer before starting your home construction project. The professionals know more about&nbsp;building materials and methods, and they can help you avoid mistakes and save on time and money in the long run. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You may also need to hire a contractor who will assist in executing the design plans. The contractor will be in charge of the team of carpenters, electricians, and skilled workers for your home. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 id="mntl-sc-block_1-0-35">4. Prepare legal documents and clearances</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5983,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/scott-graham-OQMZwNd3ThU-unsplash-1024x683.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5983"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Make sure you <strong>secure all required documents, clearance, and permits. </strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A building permit is a permit to be applied by the owner to comply with the regulations set by the National Building Code. This has to be secured before construction will commence.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This permit usually comes with ancillary permits such as:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>The architectural permit</li><li>Civil/structural permit</li><li>Electrical permit</li><li>Mechanical permit</li><li>Sanitary permit</li><li>Plumbing permit</li><li>Electronics permit</li><li>Fire Safety Clearance, Barangay Clearance, bill of materials, ECC, PTR &amp; PRC of professionals</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Also, don\'t forget to get written, signed contracts for each hired professional involved in your home construction project. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>5. Give yourself plenty of time</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Building a new home is a drawn-out process. &nbsp;It typically takes an average four of six months to finish a&nbsp;construction project.  Give yourself time to research, time to compare the quality of materials, and time to find the best prices will save a lot of money.&nbsp; Don\'t rush and "just pay whatever amount to get things done." </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>FURTHER READINGS:</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/pros-and-cons-of-building-a-new-house/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Pros and Cons of Building a New House</a></li><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/?p=5989" target="_blank">How to Apply for Building Permit in the Philippines</a></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/08/Copy-of-Copy-of-filipino-homes.png','views' => '46','category_id' => '16','published_at' => '2020-09-02 01:14:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '471','title' => 'Faster & easier ways to pay-off your home loan','slug' => 'faster-easier-ways-to-pay-off-your-home-loan','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Buying a home is more than just finding a house you like, moving in and living in it. It is a long a tedious process for many homebuyers who do not have enough cash to buy a home in one payment. Most homebuyer apply for home loans with a payment scheme that can take at least 5 years to more. Depending on the homebuyer financial status the home loan payment can be a long financial burden to carry. Check out these tips to help you pay off your loan easier and faster:&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6054,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Filipino-Homes-Philippines-1.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6054"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Go for the right home loan payment term</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>One of the headaches in any kind of loan is the length you need to cover in order to fully settle your loan. There are two kind of payment schemes you might come across: long term loans or short term loans. The long term loans will allow you spread your payment for a longer period and for lesser mortgage every month. It does, however, means you have a higher payment total. You will be paying more than those who got a shorter payment term. On the other hand in short term loans, you need to pay higher monthly amortizations&nbsp; but have a lower payment total overall.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A short term loan allows you to save around 10-12% of the supposed payment because you don\'t have to keep paying monthly interest you will find in a longer home loan.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: <em>The <a href="http://localhost:3001/can-i-use-maceda-law-if-i-stopped-paying-my-loan/">Can I use Maceda Law, if I stopped paying my Loan?</a> article is helpful if you\'re having trouble paying your home loan</em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":3942,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/03/30023388800_3a62550c8d_b-1024x593.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-3942"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Check bank home loan offers and promos</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Make sure to do your research and compare what the banks are offering.  Not all bank loans are the same. So always check what bank promos before you decide and jump in. Most cases some banks offer promos for potential homebuyers with lower home loan interests. These can be time-limited, so make sure you follow the banks on social media or call the bank to ask if they have an ongoing loan promo. This will not only assure you that the bank will help you in your home loan application but it will also save your thousands in the long run.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5678,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/calendarcontemporarydigi_140295.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5678"/><figcaption>Calendar Contemporary Digital Device Concepts</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Consider making repayments</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you already bought a home and in the long process of paying off your home loan, making frequent repayment is a good strategy. Instead of paying your amortization every month, you can make fortnight repayments instead. You can divide you monthly amortization into two and pay it every two weeks. This will allow you to pay an extra one month worth or amortization each year without even realising it. There\'s a total of 26 fortnights and there are only 12 months a year covering an extra month annually.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Ofcourse you can increase the amount you pay every time  you have extra to spare that month or if you have gotten a raise and prefer to divert extra funds to your home loan.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: <em>A helpful article on</em> <a href="http://localhost:3001/what-you-need-to-know-about-housing-loan-refinancing/"><em>What You Need to Know About Housing Loan Refinancing </em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":2417,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/2-Finances.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-2417"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Pay lumpsums whenever you can</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Some homeowners do not know about this but you can actually make your amortization payments shorter and get interest savings. Lumpsums or big one-time payment can over a good percentage of your loan. It can either cover your monthly amortization in advance or it can pay off a significant portion of your principal amount loan. Lumpsums can be source from you 13th month pay, bonuses, inheritance, monetary gifts, or even savings. If you do not have anything to use the funds on, you can definitely use this for your home loan.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>READ: <em>Check out <a href="http://localhost:3001/company-life-insurance-housing-loan/">Can I use my company life insurance to pay for my housing loan?</a> article if you plan to pay a lumpsum with your life insurance</em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5901,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/What-is-a-foreclosure-property-Should-I-be-targeting-one-for-my-new-purchase-3.png" alt="Save, Finance, Home Loan, Budget" class="wp-image-5901"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Decrease your monthly expenses</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There are things you need to sacrifice for the greater good - which is to having a home you can call yours. Being frugal is knowing your priorities and using that to your advantage with your finances. You can set aside money from deciding to take the train versus the taxi, skipping on expensive coffee from cafes, buying clothes you don\'t really need, or upgrading a gadget when you really don\'t have to. Doing this will allow you to save more money to either pay more than the required monthly mortgage or to save and raise it to a significant amount and make a big one time payment.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: Self-employed and don\'t know wh<em>at to do? Check this out <a href="http://localhost:3001/apply-housing-loan-online-worker/">How to Score a Housing Loan if You Are Self-employed or an Online Worker?</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/08/Fast-and-easy-ways-to-pay-off-your-home-loan.png','views' => '44','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-09-03 01:08:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '472','title' => '10 Best Investment for Filipino Young Professionals [UNDER 100K]','slug' => '10-best-investment-for-filipino-young-professionals-under-100k','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For many young parents and professionals, it appears prudent to consider investment early on. Especially now, our economy is in a very tough situation and it left us no choice but to be financially frugal.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you’re looking for a long-term investment vehicle to put your money on this year, we’ve listed 10 best investment options to start for young parents and starting families in the Philippines with capital below Php100K.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: <a href="http://localhost:3001/how-to-invest-your-money-during-the-coronavirus-pandemic-5-questions-to-ask-yourself-before-investing/">How to Invest Your Money During the Coronavirus Pandemic: 5 Questions to Ask Yourself Before Investing</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/oXVXuYh9ivxw-KsQVKMt9ksHvVcs52xFVGvg-Z9VJZWg0UDOWf7kwdCBw-Pj2_IpyFgPRdjOz6_ahrp1_13PLqPajD_Iy1TtK37kAtW2jfQp8H2RjexW766RI_T93EJz3xNEQF0C" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>VUL Insurance</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Variable Universal Life (VUL) is one of the most popular investment options for young adults now. VUL is simply a form of cash-value life insurance that has investment value. Investing in VUL will get you protection for your family and access to stock funds.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","width":500,"height":500} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter is-resized"><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/3moigirm4NHs7uvy84Dl38Frky91LtbGFDhLQ5c2xu2zZnTdv2hebtXaknswzCcia5z-cVoY96wlb7Oc7_KOKrnht6dwlW0Qvk_0bgwhDU9ECOaTXdo-pVsfquVjIhWjOGZ3p_fK" alt="Advantages of Investing in VUL - Filipino Homes" width="500" height="500"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Advantages of investing in VUL:&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Low minimum investment</li><li>Tax-Free Death Benefit Payout</li><li>Liquidity (withdraw cash anytime)</li><li>Automate Savings</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>PAG-IBIG MP2</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Modified Pag-IBIG 2 or MP2 is a voluntary savings program available to existing and former Pag-IBIG Fund members. MP2 has a minimum savings requirement of Php500 that lets your money earn up to 7% in dividends. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","width":500,"height":500} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter is-resized"><img src="https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/fijYjxp8uiYQgBtIhkhzP94QqErliAhG1Hyuo3S7V7KItnY8j-tj7cG08dfI75jZRaynHfpe2b_5lZaK7NwDDzY9cPDCq7HfFIkrFGGEuGGNu38gtzqFhCobeDENNJYnE8Y0z4zw" alt="Advantages of Investing PAGIBIG MP2 - Filipino Homes" width="500" height="500"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Advantages of investing in Pag-IBIG MP2:&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Earnings are tax-free and guaranteed savings backed up by the government</li><li>You can withdraw any time (Terms apply)</li><li>Contributions are flexible</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>P2P Lending</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you’re looking for an easy and less complicated investment vehicle, P2P might work well for you. Peer-to-peer lending or P2P is a kind of investment that pools money from its members/investors and lends them to borrowers. Simply put, peers lend money to their peers and repay with interest. Plus, it does not require a huge amount of investment as well.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","width":500,"height":500} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter is-resized"><img src="https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/59hqEnTXjT-_skx4Lij-BOywX5uswvB9Gb_Bs_R81Ky79l_IAzA6YXz7m0nAeFONR8pv41aEH5OHVoacMG731u4r0GzHFM63V_rwFgbGe6RpH9LkvCQEc27_DvPAXSh7NYeZZfTC" alt="Advantages of Investing P2P Lending - Filipino Homes" width="500" height="500"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Advantages of investing in P2P Lending:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Requires little money to start with</li><li>Potential for better returns</li><li>Lower interest rates</li><li>More accessible source of funding</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>UITFs</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Unit Investment Trust Fund or UITF is simply explained as funds from different people facilitated by the bank to be used for different products (i.e stocks, bonds, or government securities).  UITFs can be a good vehicle for long-term investment goals. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","width":500,"height":500} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter is-resized"><img src="https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/txv7d6ggc87NAVa3Z66nlX_Ow2b15UphyWtwiLhe_JMXaC83Ex5Mc78oYCfJYhWz50-sZf5AQeuBmWIwmA9kZRJnymX8DTCMhm9xwV6GZVbfuwF9W3ntR9jBSHynN4Rhe1bSbnQm" alt="Advantages of Investing UITF - Filipino Homes" width="500" height="500"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Advantages of investing UITFs:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Low minimum investment&nbsp;</li><li>Professionally-managed funds&nbsp;</li><li>Ideal for all risk appetites</li><li>It is supervised by the Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas (BSP)</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>Stock Market</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Simply put stocks are units of ownership in a corporation. This means that if you own or invest in stocks of a company, you become one of its “owners”. You earn by getting dividends (can be in the form of cash or additional stocks) and selling the stock shares you bought at a higher price. And for as low as Php1,000, you can start investing in the stock market through <a href="https://www.colfinancial.com/ape/final2/home/pdfs/2012_eip_primer.pdf">COL Easy Investment Program</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","width":500,"height":500} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter is-resized"><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/s8dKwUK3uHnokWVsB6AmPHJvZnOgfdeHcFZsTrdH7E08syuPFULrR1LrEHNvwkbmP-sNynRHwtE7dw-2925TOKl-t0AQzEbGtLI4WT8gJWgNXyvi1jFcWP1S4r99ZVHROZKaytYo" alt="Advantages of Investing Stock Market- Filipino Homes" width="500" height="500"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Advantages of investing in Stocks:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Make money in two ways&nbsp;</li><li>Dividend Income</li><li>Diversification</li><li>Ownership&nbsp;</li><li>Take advantage of a growing economy</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>Small Business</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Why not start your own small business? Having your own business will yield greater potential for unlimited income. And if any case you already have one, we’ve written <a href="http://localhost:3001/7-things-you-can-do-for-your-small-business-to-survive-the-covid-19-pandemic/">practical tips you can do for your small business to survive the pandemic</a>. Remember in every business, it takes hard work, resourcefulness, and a good long-term plan to succeed.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","width":500,"height":500} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter is-resized"><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/Z1qncvkn_xo6W5WFsAIZV_IwDAEcwR8fpER8cVBOLFqvYqECtvnuRori5M8Upt5pjA0afp23z7uDf0U5HK4l-EZt_x6-nlusuNfKYKvwbEpBN62V4baz8eimXRInnmQV20V2SqTY" alt="Advantages of Investing in Small Business- Filipino Homes" width="500" height="500"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Advantages of investing in Small Business:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Potential for Unlimited Income</li><li>Greater Rewards for Higher Risks</li><li>Do Work You Truly Love</li><li>Collect a Big Windfall</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>Real estate</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href="http://localhost:3001/category/property-investing">Real estate property</a> is definitely a valuable investment option for young Filipino professionals, especially for the <a href="http://localhost:3001/why-ofws-should-take-advantage-of-attending-philippine-property-roadshows/">Overseas Filipino Workers</a>. The simple reason why it is an attractive investment is that property appreciates in value over time. Say, if you purchase a property at Php2M, the chances of its value doubling or tripling after five to ten years is high.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em>READ: </em><a href="http://localhost:3001/millennials-can-invest-real-estate/"><em>3 Ways Millennials Can Invest in Real Estate</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","width":500,"height":500} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter is-resized"><img src="https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/2Bbe-Wm_tvnEvR_sRBKZjqxe06dL20RMD18wkAohPGGtfJHubrTvfjcjnz3yDhp2v4EQCKf6JxXE10pQnge1I_g_0B0Yo2xX-drk59pTfpll-Tw2RgXQ2Hhx1ZDplu0TVKvG7fiR" alt="Advantages of Investing Real Estate- Filipino Homes" width="500" height="500"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Advantages of investing in Stocks:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Competitive returns</li><li>Dividend Income</li><li>Portfolio Diversification</li><li>Tax advantages and Ownership&nbsp;</li><li>Hedge against inflation</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>Cryptocurrency or Bitcoin</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Bitcoin is an increasingly ideal investment vehicle too among youngsters. Many financial analysts are saying that <a href="https://gbsge.com/bitcoin-future-money/">bitcoin could be the future of money</a>. Cryptocurrency or bitcoins are digital currency secured by cryptography that people on the internet use to trade. Money could be earned by mining and trading.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","width":500,"height":500} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter is-resized"><img src="https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/39sirnnh9vK4lA5Uein4taoPE4JjxEcLSSaeTx6Hj6I1awurChYj16X2ppO3D1QW2L3gI3ssyBHxLn8cApbAILS6IDdtwge3S2fxr644omdXMw6EW5VBm4WBAHhFMpzXNfteqT6f" alt="Advantages of Investing bitcoin- Filipino Homes" width="500" height="500"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Advantages of investing in Bitcoin:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Low transaction fees</li><li>High liquidity (easy to use in any situation)</li><li>Simplified International Payments For Merchants</li><li>Deflationary and decentralized currency</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>Personal Equity Retirement Account (PERA)</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>PERA is a voluntary savings plan established via RA 9505 to encourage Filipinos to invest for their retirement. You can contribute a maximum of Php100K per year and a Php200K maximum limit for those working overseas.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","width":500,"height":500} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter is-resized"><img src="https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/LGUgX_aGdLso8Zo82iVtYn_2A1vbcWpENd65lGmrWVpj9-POx2ISEXoDaFcVew9iy0kAfiAUocLgYEeo0pELGmjrx1Eis-tj_GJ-I2lm_6XUwwh8oxTg2odlTFwiYnCegx2A-vd0" alt="Advantages of Investing in PERA- Filipino Homes" width="500" height="500"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Advantages of investing in PERA:&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Tax exemption</li><li>More time to grow your retirement fund</li><li>Not subject to estate tax</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>ETF</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Just like Mutual Funds, Exchange Traded Fund (ETF) are managed investment funds, only that MF can’t be traded in real-time. Investing in ETFs means you’re owning shares from the top 30 companies in the stock market, including Ayala or SM Corp. As of 2020, the only available ETF in the country is the <a href="https://firstmetroetf.com.ph/">First Metro Philippine Equity Exchange Traded Fund (FMETF)</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","width":500,"height":500} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter is-resized"><img src="https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/XTWAxgUlNYBJfc_1LUzavsBAhh5J9vNWlkOsHDrrF2bWFkabaPYWDk1Q-p6f0DEXbnYsd5-7k1eAue8yrzmR9urZI7jWuaPvb5SYLbDslxSJygOl34vKcDkqvZg3ed0aC5XmXqH6" alt="Advantages of Investing ETF- Filipino Homes" width="500" height="500"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Advantages of investing ETFs:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Minimum Investment (Php2,000 – Php5,000)</li><li>Diversification</li><li>Profitable even in your retirement years</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/08/10-Best-Investment-for-Young-Professionals-Filipino-Homes.jpg','views' => '60','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-09-04 01:01:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '473','title' => 'Why you need a Real Estate Appraiser in selling your home?','slug' => 'why-you-need-a-real-estate-appraiser-in-selling-your-home','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There&nbsp;could be a&nbsp;massive&nbsp;reason why&nbsp;we have&nbsp;a Real&nbsp;Estate Appraiser and why&nbsp;they have&nbsp;to get&nbsp;a license to perform this&nbsp;vital&nbsp;task.&nbsp;If&nbsp;this is&nbsp;not an&nbsp;important&nbsp;job,&nbsp;we do not&nbsp;need&nbsp;licensed&nbsp;individuals&nbsp;to do&nbsp;it. However,&nbsp;people&nbsp;are&nbsp;typically&nbsp;stubborn.&nbsp;there is&nbsp;this Filipino mentality that we\'d&nbsp;opt for&nbsp;a couple of&nbsp;savings over obtaining what\'s wrongfully right. There is this "tipid-system" that overpowers doing what&nbsp;should&nbsp;be done right.&nbsp;real estate&nbsp;dealings&nbsp;is&nbsp;one in all&nbsp;the&nbsp;normally&nbsp;abused transactions&nbsp;in this&nbsp;"tipid-system".&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5902,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/What-is-a-foreclosure-property-Should-I-be-targeting-one-for-my-new-purchase-2.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5902"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Some sellers would prefer putting up their own price in selling their properties. Without considering if it\'s over-valued or under-valued compared to its current market price. Property owners can actually sell their own property and price it as to how they wanted it to be. However, if they ask other people to sell it in their behalf, you now need  a Licensed or accredited Real Estate Professional for that. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5891,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/3.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5891"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Real Estate Professionals like Real Estate Appraisers specifically are licensed to check on the value of each property base on its current market and zonal value, actual status or condition of the property and its neighboring lots. Real estate appraisers will look into different factors that will affect or greatly affect the value of the property. Sometimes, even if your property is a corner lot or along the highway, the price of the lot is not considered or qualified to be prime.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5878,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/How-to-find-the-ideal-home-for-starting-or-growing-family-needs-2.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5878"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Let your real estate transactions be done right the first time. If you are planning to buy a house, make sure that the value of the house was checked by a Real Estate Appraiser. That way, you will know that the property is not over-priced. If you are a seller of the property, work with a real estate appraiser for them to be able to give you the right value of your property. They will inspect the property and see to it that it matches the value of the City or Provincial Appraisers.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5120,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/cityscape-of-manila-philippines-from-a-balcony.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5120"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There are a lot of factors that affect the actual valuation of a property, <strong><em>location</em></strong> is just one of them. From supply and demand through to location, facilities and planned infrastructure projects, there are plenty of factors that can influence property value.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>What appraisers will do is check on these factors before actually arriving at the right value of your property. These same factors are also checked by the City and Provincial assessors through government standards. Real Estate Appraisers report should match or closer to the Government assessors value. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4522,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/triijqojsgqysgjaiubs.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4522"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A real estate appraiser will go through the home performing an evaluation, and then provide you with a written evaluation after he has gathered all necessary information. Appraisers will also take into consideration the replacement costs as well. Also, they will have to very land descriptions as well.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There is a lot of work involved with appraisals, which is why it’s so very important that each step of the process is performed correctly by a qualified real estate appraiser.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/09/Why-you-need-a-Real-Estate-Appraiser-in-selling-your-home.png','views' => '47','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-09-05 01:48:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '474','title' => 'How to Apply for Building Permit in the Philippines','slug' => 'how-to-apply-for-building-permit-in-the-philippines','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5994,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/0_WrWyA5hlCxeh83qK.jpeg" alt="" class="wp-image-5994"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>What is a Building Permit?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A&nbsp;<strong>Building Permit</strong>&nbsp;is a document issued by Department of Building Official that serves as your official consent to commence any construction, demolition, addition, or renovation of your property. <em>This has to be secured before construction will commence.</em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Why Do You Need to Secure a Building Permit? </h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As part of the Building Permit process, the Department of Building Official will look and analyze your submitted plans to guarantee that your application comply with the <strong>&nbsp;<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://www.chanrobles.com/republicactno6541.htm#.WAB9w-B94_4" target="_blank"><strong>National Building Code of the Philippines (PD 1096)</strong></a><strong>,&nbsp;<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://www.bfp10.net/download/irr-of-the-fire-code-of-the-philippines-ra-9514/" target="_blank">Fire Code of the Philippines (RA 9514)</a></strong></strong>, and your <strong>Local Building Code</strong>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Securing the building permit ensures that the home owner, architects and engineers follow the codes, standards, and minimum requirement for a construction. Proper architectural, mechanical, structural, electrical and sanitary plans should also abide by the codes.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>REQUIREMENTS IN SECURING BUILDING PERMITS</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5991,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/building-permit.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5991"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Applicants will be issued a list of requirements to fulfill. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The following are the requirements for securing a building permit:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>1. Ownership of the lot property<br>a. In case the applicant is the owner of the lot where construction will take place:<br>a1. Certified true copy of Transfer Certificate of Title, on file with the Registry of Deeds.<br>a2. Tax Declaration<br>a3. Latest Real Property Tax Receipt</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>b. In case the applicant is not the registered owner of the lot:<br>b1. Duly notarized copy of the Contract of Lease or Deed of Absolute Sale</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>2. Application forms</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Properly filled-up application forms duly signed and sealed by engineers concerned:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>a. Application for Building Permit (5 copies)<br>b. Electrical Permit Forms (3 copies)<br>c. Sanitary Permit Forms (3 copies)</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>3. Five sets of complete detailed plan</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>a. For construction of two-storey building:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Structural Design Analysis – signed and sealed by Civil Engineer at every page</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>b. For construction of more than two-storey building:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Boring and Plate Load Test</li><li>Seismic Analysis</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>Proof of Property</em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Photocopy of Transfer Certificate if Title (TCT)</li><li>Photocopy of tax Declaration of Property-lot (Certified True Copy) – 5 copies</li><li>Photocopy of Current Tax Receipt (5 copies)</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>Copy of License of Engineers and Architects</em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Photocopy of PTR # and PRC license of all involved&nbsp;engineers and architects</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 id="798b">PROCEDURES OF SECURING A BUILDING PERMIT IN THE PHILIPPINES</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>1. Prepare the list of requirements while you secure a checklist and application forms from the Office of the Building Official.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>2. Along with the filled out forms and required documents and clearances as outlined in the checklist, submit them to the Office of the Building Official.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>3. If the submitted requirements are complete, you will be granted an acknowledgement/follow-up slip.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>4. Within 10 working days, you will receive an order of payment from the Releasing Section of the building office. Settle the charge at the cashier’s office.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>5. After five days, the building permit will be released after the submission of proof of payment (official receipt).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>FURTHER READINGS:</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>FURTHER READINGS:</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/pros-and-cons-of-building-a-new-house/" target="_blank">Pros and Cons of Building a New House</a></li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/?p=5920" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">5 Things to Do Before You Build Your New Home</a></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/08/Copy-of-Copy-of-filipino-homes-1-1.png','views' => '444','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-09-07 01:13:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '475','title' => 'Why you should buy and invest in real estate property','slug' => 'why-you-should-buy-and-invest-in-real-estate-property','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Wanting to buy a property but not really sure if you want to make that purchase just yet? Not comfortable at buying a home or an apartment since you don\'t see that you and your family don\'t need it now? It is a long debate on when is the best time to buy your first property and you can come up with a hundred excuses not to. Below are some helpful points that you might have not thought about and will help you decide to buy and invest in real estate property before it is too late.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6055,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Filipino-Homes-Philippines-2.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6055"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Passive income when you buy and invest in real estate property</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Most people only see the money spent to acquire a property. However, properties when used well can generate income without having to continuously work on it day in and day out like a regular job. Having a property rented can give you income that will be either enough to cover the mortgage of the property or even have extra for additional income. Having an additional stream for income is a welcome during this economic recession. Make sure to find a unit that is "rentable" and found in a good location that is attractive to possible renters.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: <em>Check out <a href="http://localhost:3001/why-real-estate-is-a-good-investment-option-despite-a-crisis/">Why Real Estate Is a Good Investment Option Despite a Crisis</a></em> </p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6060,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Filipino-Homes-Philippines-9.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6060"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Increase in asset</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Not every one considers this when they buy and invest in real estate property. While renting a home is fairly good when you have just graduated or starting a family it does not increase your monetary value in the long run. It is still money going out of your pockets that can not be brought back. Owning a property can be expensive and may have monthly obligation. But with each mortgage payment is the assurance that the property is under your name and an addition to your assets. You can have it rented for a stable source of income or even sold if you wish to.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6059,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Filipino-Homes-Philippines-8.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6059"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Your own personal space</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>One of the joys of living in your own property is not be limited to a lease contract. You can do what ever you can in and on your home from drilling holes on the walls for wall decor to extending a kitchen to make more space. You can do whatever you want without having to constantly ask the landlord for approval. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4895,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/Insurance-Investments.png" alt="" class="wp-image-4895"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Value appreciates in time</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A reward to property ownership is having the property\'s value increase over time. It is one that makes this an attractive investment for investors. Most investors purchase a property and hold or wait for its value to appreciate over time before making their next big move. Hence, why buying-and-selling of property is one smart way to earn from property ownership. Ofcourse the same is true with rental rates. The higher the property value appreciates, the same way it is for rental fees.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>READ: <em>If you\'re concern about <a href="http://localhost:3001/buying-a-house-during-covid-pandemic/">Buying a House During COVID Pandemic</a></em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5878,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/How-to-find-the-ideal-home-for-starting-or-growing-family-needs-2.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5878"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Secure you and your family\'s future</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Every Filipino family\'s dream is to won a home of their own. This is because property ownership secures one futures either having it rented or knowing that your family will always have a roof above their head. And ofcourse, when worse comes to worst, selling the property which may have already appreciated in time is an option when finances is tight.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The real estate market is fast moving. People are getting smart and asing the right questions regarding new developments. If you don\'t act quickly, the property you\'re buying may get sold out before the day ends. Or you might see a new building being constructed at a vacant lot and find it unappealing to buy a unit in that development. A few month or years after, shopping or business districts pop up near or beside it and before you know it, it will be too expensive for you to buy a unit because the property value has increased. Real estate moves like that and it will not wait on you.The best time to purchase is not later when you will miss your chance or when it gets too expensive for you. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Check out <a href="https://filipinohomes.com/properties/sale"><em>Filipino Homes</em></a> for complete listing of hot-selling properties for sale. You might find the one that will make you says yes to that house!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/08/Why-Filipinos-Should-be-Investing-in-Real-Estate-Property-Now-4.png','views' => '59','category_id' => '9','published_at' => '2020-09-08 13:19:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '476','title' => 'Gaming Room Ideas to Steal for Your next Room Makeover','slug' => 'gaming-room-ideas-to-steal-for-your-next-room-makeover','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Gaming room or what streamers call it “battle stations” are growing in popularity for homeowners and renters alike especially during the quarantine. There have been a lot of posts about this on social media, and some even went viral. The funny thing is, it’s not only gaining momentum in the gaming world, but almost everyone is getting hooked on it and actually dreamed of having one.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Well, thanks to subscription games, free-play, and multiplayer online platforms (not to mention COVID). It allows us to create a gaming room space at home since we don’t have much to do during the lockdown.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: <a href="http://localhost:3001/ph-property-sector-remains-optimistic-amid-covid-19-threat/">PH Property Sector Remains Optimistic Amid COVID-19 Threat</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So, whether you’re a gamer, an avid streamer, or just someone who wants to upgrade an empty room space for family night or an entertainment spot for your friends to gather, let’s look at these amazing gaming room designs to put together your ultimate PC station.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6069,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Gaming-Room-Ideas-to-Steal-for-Your-next-Room-Makeover-1024x576.jpg" alt="Gaming Room Ideas to Steal for Your next Room Makeover" class="wp-image-6069"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>1. <strong>Simple Escape Room</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5973,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/gaming-room-design-filipinohomes.png" alt="Gaming Room Design Ideas" class="wp-image-5973"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you’re someone who just wants to recreate a studio into a simple gaming hideout, why not <a href="http://localhost:3001/room-dividers/">divide your room space into functions</a>. Just put some personalized stuff on your wall to add details on it. You may also want to upgrade your gaming chair with an elevated screen as this promotes a more comfortable, relaxed gameplay.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>2. <strong>Minimalist Workspace&nbsp;</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/Zdtlio3kkCeUSnOSxYL1vqWMYFUlU8hfo2H2QDKJ6Z434lUHs4pL4MV1wuodN091xtdQauSQv2C-8ogOc7tQG3eqrfGB-mguUZJ2lW2A5BOZxyhFx-jIGCdHOdgnRVNfa-tH9P4f" alt="Gaming Room Design Ideas"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This one is more of a <a href="http://localhost:3001/11-modern-minimalist-home-office-design-ideas-to-boost-your-productivity-and-inspire-creativity/">workspace </a>rather than a gaming console. While many gamers prefer playing close to eye level with their monitor, this minimalist design makes an ideal place to think and create. Feel free to adorn some artificial <a href="http://localhost:3001/7-best-plants-for-condo-living/">plants to freshen up space</a> without the need for a green thumb.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>3. <strong>Futuristic Gaming Room&nbsp;</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><a href="https://www.instagram.com/dopegamingsetup/"><img src="https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/dcmaw-UDuy93KrnkUDkvNgTvDS8rAr1y0OxZbN9HIT1RY_Os39Y3EwElHbcguIwsoA7xsoa5qTH7W2bQV4UxhZC7SM_Wy_E4Fy4fwBLztdzLABOKvfh17SMr57dVVHLDbgbtU1NB" alt="Futuristic Gaming Room "/></a><figcaption>Photo credit: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/dopegamingsetup/">dopegamingsetup</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Another amazing build by dopegamingsetup. If you want your room into a futuristic gaming and chill area, try this. As you can see, the setup wall may look pretty ordinary but it has niches inside to fix small patches using futuristic, customizable LED strip lighting. Combat the darkness by placing LED strip lighting along your ceiling or under the rim of your desk or shelving units. This gives you a space-age, ultra modern look. Dope right?&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>4. <strong>Bold and Sleek (Justice League-inspired office setup)</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/lhxzKlcjj7MzCR-xK7Uiaak3-sA5WJwt5Z0_IdSS5rsZtVam7waC4W1a8peFFnOhFq6tCBEI__dfkbEIXXBtU9EKA-JzF9kVSg6iGQuIdC8d-u1mM3cSWGMsnDYz1X0Pn7QwCcH5" alt="Bold Gaming Room design ideas"/><figcaption>Photo Credit: <a href="https://interiordub.com/best-gaming-room-setup-ideas-gamers-guides/">interiorhub</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This gaming room with four-screen monitor channels a collection of Justice League miniatures and funkos. In this design, you may want to choose a desk with a broad, flat surface that can comfortably accommodate your monitors, keyboard, mouse, and other accessories. Put your collectibles on display on floating shelves that will look cool and modern staggered at different places on your wall.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>5. <strong>Backlight Setup with Decorative Feature</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/GfxnovOzDbezdFxKSJukMfeIuSc_vQUlmPo72ppu30Vkdi7fSyM6s_tR-MzvbAGX6-TkJEhOv2tY_24fdmUKT2sxsIRPITk5qDb-vsBaNBurdZpGRmPHRi6VuFC2q4RupK7aeE-l" alt="Gaming Room Design Ideas"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Floor mats work really well with this one. If you want a nice bright room with good backlighting and decorative features, then it\'s worth a try. Just remember though it is important for your PC gaming setup to comfortably accommodate your monitor or monitors. This will prevent neck strain thus giving you the comfort you need while you hustle.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>6. <strong>Flying Coffin</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/JkcpWppKwG5FBYZ_SwjoE2s07fF706fyoGST7tG0RfkLT5FQ8HhfE5bp6PvpRDFPWtKaywauAZwKCDcYG98idDK3XqPEdswD1me_RPLlaq4DwU9jKd4WvfQalhRpWJcNnG0a-iSp" alt="flying coffin Gaming Room Design Ideas"/><figcaption>Photo Credit: <a href="https://www.thesun.co.uk/tech/10235311/ultimate-gaming-rigs-gamers/">Splitpics.uk</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Dubbed as the Flying Coffin, ths gaming room setup includes a built-in force feedback seat, steering wheel, flight stick, and rudder pedals. What’s cool about this is that when it\'s stowed away, you\'d never know it was there. Cool right? And sure, you can replicate the experience of piloting a jet with a keyboard, but it\'s a lot more fun with a flight stick and all the stuff.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>7. <strong>Blended Double</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/qch87oQ3oBP4PFWJ4_zDYZN8Ld3j9sue3n6wkvcwKJghYYOP8rbFMaWCpj_3KFKIYgs0p7bHwDVgkXrxDGw9yoxTcUbBROMZyQUvoiiIWUkkz8Uzyiv9Uh2hNZsZe9Ri_MDMpwId" alt="Gaming Room Design Ideas"/><figcaption>Photo credit: <a href="https://gramho.com/explore-hashtag/battlestation">gramho battlestations</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Take your game room decor to the next level by highlighting it with a novelty neon, just like Darien Cardenas Gaming haven! Although this design looks really simple, it actually has powerful gaming equipment. Plus, if you have an open space against one wall, you can go with simple rectangular shelves for your consoles and collection funkos.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>8. <strong>Six-Monitor Ultimate Streaming Setup</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/Km0ArTFp-1rGwVdUpYiD-P8Pbh7KOy8RsrYmD_IqPkGQsLCPWsonyw9YclsWzHhATQ4JrNcRE64y5ZcjjrnuzaA_XqYRdE2dyygVKlV-tjYIDK4GfBIlmv3kaiB0ByPFZq6fk_IA" alt="Gaming Room Design Ideas"/><figcaption>Photo credit: heartbraden</figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With the rise of affordable large screens, you can now explore panoramas of visual data just like this six-monitor setup with epic red backlights by Reddit user @heartbraden! This gaming room design features a large screen for a panoramic media view, a trio at the bottom for amazing graphics, and two other for monitoring security cameras, and other cool stuff. It’s like you’re in “the Hive” in Halle Berry’s movie<em> The Call</em>.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>&nbsp;9. Pink Perfection</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/Tq5K0OXygn5XuqsMnuvvpyM7DYB7Ws2crvbcg8WHX1T3cZ5MDzbQ3qwv5Ekq8aURTq_ZHFWf9zrIixVHaXDpXlsh2BCFY-OrNcc1EgC5ygOa9figotSHM5vTeCDmp5vZsTeelkMy" alt="Gaming Room Design Ideas"/><figcaption>Photo credit: arturoldan</figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This gaming room design by @arturoldan will definitely make every girl blush. It features a dual-stacked ultrawide monitor which is perfect for streaming! You can actually personalize this gaming setup by adding nano leaf lights or by plastering the walls with graphic prints or <a href="http://localhost:3001/7-diy-accent-wall-ideas-for-your-home/">DIY accent walls</a> that represent you.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>10. <strong>Battle Royale Warzone</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/0ctkZOHFtdWTKqX6Azqum1ZRnrjK2yXyIIadfZYzM0q25Jx-TxRCJIXcRLB65PUGOu-Iit42lYLBOyHc9wu7R5H-v5o8s3qnMhnFea63TwBr-W8ebFYTzY9xKqcJVVYkJKnWZKUt" alt="Gaming Room Design Ideas"/><figcaption>Photo credit: mar_cel88</figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Man, this is sleek! Did you know Battle Royale is currently the hottest genre in the video game industry and has the astonishing player count? This unique concept by <a href="https://www.instagram.com/mar_cel88/">mar_cel88</a> makes the inherent replayability of battle royale games and perfect entertainment space for your family and friends! Whether you\'re playing on an Xbox, PlayStation, or whatever, this perfectly suits your weekend game day!&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And that’s it! Hope these amazing gaming room ideas will help you get the dream gaming room you have always wanted. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Remember, the goal is to have some kind of breaks to refuel, unwind, and jump back in full throttle of life’s real game.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/08/Gaming-Room-Design-Ideas.jpg','views' => '43','category_id' => '28','published_at' => '2020-09-09 01:52:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '477','title' => '7 Factors that Affect the House Construction Cost','slug' => '7-factors-that-affect-the-house-construction-cost','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When planning to start a construction project, it is wise to start with a budget. You need to figure out&nbsp;<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/?p=5911" target="_blank">how much it will actually cost&nbsp;to build your dream home</a> and balance that with how much you can realistically afford.&nbsp;&nbsp;The most popular preliminary estimating method is the superficial area method, wherein you multiply your desired floor area with a cost factor, which can range from Php16,000 to Php150,000 per square meter.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong><em>READ:  </em></strong><a href="http://localhost:3001/wp-admin/post.php?post=5911" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">How Much Should I Expect to Pay to Build a House?</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>While it is commonly used for its simplicity, this is not accurate.&nbsp;There are a lot of factors that can affect the actual cost of construction. Here are some factors to consider:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>1. Floor plan and design</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Your desired floor area, number of rooms, and toilet and baths will obviously affect the cost of construction of your home.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5924,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/floor-plan-1474454_1280-1024x678.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5924"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>2. Height of structure</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Height of the structure also affects your construction cost. While higher floor or ceiling height makes a house appear more elegant and spacious, the additional height entails sturdier structural elements and more wall materials and finishes, which in turn leads to a higher construction cost.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=45036065012279958" height="795" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>3. Types of structural system </h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Your choice of structural systems, such as precast panels, load-bearing concrete hollow blocks, cast-in-place wall panels, and reinforced concrete frame will also greatly influence the total cost. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>4. Number and size of windows</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Glass is more expensive than masonry wall. The cost increases when more windows are added in your design. The cost difference is further amplified if specialized glass (tempered and laminated) is used.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=300263500159879848" height="700" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>5. Types of materials used </h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The types of materials you use for your pipes, wires, etc., also affect your construction cost. Branded materials of higher quality are expected to be more expensive. Cost of interior walls can also differ based on materials used, such as concrete hollow block versus fiber cement board.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=60517188730822699" height="1000" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>6. Types of finishes and fixtures </h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Your construction cost will vary depending on the type and brand of finishes and fixtures used in your house. Method of installation and warranty period for those items may also affect the cost.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=352688214570365569" height="700" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>7. Location </h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Location will also greatly impact your total construction cost. For example, construction projects in the provinces around Metro Manila is generally cheaper compared to constructions within the metro itself. On the other hand, accessibility and availability of construction materials may become a problem in some farther areas, potentially adding up cost.  Also, a property inside a high-end subdivision is expected to have higher cost considering the strict construction regulations.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>FURTHER READINGS:</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/wp-admin/post.php?post=5914&#038;action=edit" target="_blank">Pros and Cons of Building a New House</a></li><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/wp-admin/post.php?post=5920" target="_blank">5 Things to Do Before You Build Your New Home</a>&nbsp;</li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/wp-admin/post.php?post=5911" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">How Much Should I Expect to Pay to Build a House?</a></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/08/Copy-of-Copy-of-filipino-homes-3.png','views' => '50','category_id' => '16','published_at' => '2020-09-10 01:08:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '478','title' => 'Should you buy a home during Covid-19 economic recession?','slug' => 'should-you-buy-a-home-during-covid-19-economic-recession','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Covid-19 broke out early 2020 and it has been a few months being stuck at home with limited movements outside the homes. There has also been changes on work set-up as well has school set-up for the kids with everyone following quarantine restrictions. Covid-19 has definitely disrupted our life as well as our plans for this year as well as the <a href="http://localhost:3001/what-happens-during-a-recession-and-how-to-survive-from-it/">Covid-19 economic recession in the Philippines</a>. If you\'ve been planning to buy a house, it is understandable if you have some reservations to move forward. After all, the recession could mean a lot of financial changes. Here are some factors to help you decide to buy a home during Covid-19 economic recession and why it is still best to buy now despite the pandemic outbreak.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6063,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Filipino-Homes-Buying-a-Property-Philippines-3.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6063"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Do people buy a home during Covid-19 during recession?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Yes. In fact, Bangko Sentral has lowered the interest rates for loans including home loans to help the Philippine economy.  But make sure to be diligent in preparing your documents as banks have become stricter with credit standards. Filipino Homes have been busy with work as people making the best of their time to look for a better house for the family. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em>READ: Check out <a href="http://localhost:3001/what-happens-during-a-recession-and-how-to-survive-from-it/">What happens during a recession and how to survive from it</a></em> </p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6065,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Filipino-Homes-Buying-a-Property-Philippines-5.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6065"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Is real estate stable?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Real estate is one of the stable form of investment you can get for yourself and your family.&nbsp; Property market value is not directly affected by the pandemic. Finding a home that is ideal for the current situation is gaining attraction for some people. Having realised their growing needs after staying at home for a few months, people are more adamant to buy a home during Covid-19. A property close to the marketplace, malls and banks is the most ideal. You do not have to travel far to buy supplies for the family.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6055,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Filipino-Homes-Philippines-2.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6055"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Can I afford it with or without recession?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>One the things being stuck at home has brought us is the ability to stay at home and not spend too much. Going out and eating out takes a good percent of your money without you even realizing it.&nbsp; Having that option taken away from you will give you more room for your savings to grow.&nbsp;But buying a house is not just have the money and the ability to save. It is also knowing that your income stream is not easily disrupted. If it does, you need to have enough money to cover the financial obligations. Do you have enough saving or funds to pay for the mortgages if your income stream is affected? If yes, you are in a better position than those you might be affected. It is the best time to look into your finances and work on saving and raising funds when needed.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em>READ: Take&nbsp;</em><a href="http://localhost:3001/a-look-at-the-financial-crises-in-the-philippine-real-estate-sector/">a look at the Financial Crises in the Philippine Real Estate Sector</a><em>&nbsp;to better understand the economic downturn brought by the COVID-19 pandemic</em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5882,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/How-to-find-the-ideal-home-for-starting-or-growing-family-needs-5.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5882"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Will buying a house do good to my family?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Since you\'ve been staying at home more, you tend to see the limitations you have in your current home. You find the need to have bigger outdoor space, an extra room for your growing kid, a larger living space for your family and etc.&nbsp;A house is not just a space to sleep and eat at but also safe-haven where your family can grow and be nurtured. It not only gives you a new space but it is a better and bigger space that will fit the needs of each of your family member.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/08/Should-you-buy-a-home-during-the-Covid-19-economic-recession.png','views' => '44','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-09-11 01:29:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '479','title' => '7 Budget-Friendly Bedroom Makeover Ideas You Can Do in a Weekend','slug' => '7-budget-friendly-bedroom-makeover-ideas-you-can-do-in-a-weekend','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For most of us, we have been spending a lot more time inside our homes for the past few months. If you have become bored with your space, it may be the best time to change things up a bit. In this blog post, we\'ve rounded up some easy, budget-friendly makeover ideas for your bedroom that you can do in a weekend. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>1. <strong>Rearrange your furniture.</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=317222367506839420" height="877" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Changing the layout of the bedroom is the most cost-effective thing you can do to give your space a fresher look. It’s free! You just need to put in a little time and energy. Don\'t forget to declutter as you do this and remove the things you don\'t need or want in the bedroom. This can help you free up some space as well and make your bedroom look and feel bigger and airier. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em><strong>READ</strong></em>:  <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/feng-shui-bedroom/" target="_blank">How To Feng Shui Your Bedroom</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>2. Update your lighting.&nbsp;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=117797346492187127" height="700" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Lighting can have a major impact on your bedroom\'s design,  especially in creating a relaxing atmosphere. Fixing outdated or inefficient lights and updating fixtures, bulbs, and switches can help brighten your room, save energy, and give your space a refreshed look.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>3. Change your pillowcases and bedding.&nbsp;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=524247212877653424" height="700" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Choosing pillowcases and sheets in a color that is different from what you currently have can be the change you need. You can never go wrong with the classic all-white bedding, which can easily be layered for pops of color. And don\'t be afraid to use patterns.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>4. Walls</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=211174971872259" height="900" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Paint, wallpaper, and artwork pieces can give your bedroom a new look. An accent wall can give a focal point in your space. Consider adding a gallery wall as well. Display special photos that will give your room a homey and cozy feel. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>5. <strong>Hang a mirror or two.</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=440367669819611762" height="700" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Mirrors can do wonders to help make a small room appear brighter and feel larger. A floor mirror leaning up against the wall can do wonders.  You can also opt to use a mirror as a headboard or furniture with reflective surfaces.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em><strong>READ: </strong></em> <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/making-the-most-of-the-small-living-space/" target="_blank">Making the Most of the Small Living Space</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>6.&nbsp;Add or change a rug.&nbsp;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=391109548895052555" height="880" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Your floor is a great place to get creative with patterns.&nbsp; Consider adding a soft rug in your room to pull a space together. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>7. Storage&nbsp;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=99431104264504557" height="1000" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Your bedroom should be a relaxing place, so clutter should be kept to a minimum. This means there should be adequate storage. Closet organizers, storage bins, and baskets can help keep miscellaneous items from piling up. If your dresser, cabinets, and nightstand need a little updating, consider sanding them down and painting it a fresh color. Installing new hardware (or spray painting your old ones) can also give your old furniture an updated look.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em><strong>READ: </strong></em> <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/7-clever-storage-solutions-for-small-spaces/" target="_blank">7 Clever Storage Solutions for Small Spaces</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/08/Copy-of-Copy-of-filipino-homes-4.png','views' => '45','category_id' => '28','published_at' => '2020-09-14 03:27:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '480','title' => 'Buying a home? What to consider before buying','slug' => 'buying-a-home-what-to-consider-before-buying','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>#ForeverHome is a goal and a dream for mostly everyone. Everyone has it in their goals list. But buying a home more than just looking qt pretty houses, it is commitment. A lot of thought and seriousness is needed before one can fully decide on it. It\'s is not something you do out of whim or mood. It needs deliberate research before actually making the purchase. The whole home buying process is also a tedious process and can take from months to years. Not only do you need to financially prepare yourself but also mentally and emotionally ready as well. Below are some helpful points you need to consider before buying a home.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5770,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/nathan-fertig-FBXuXp57eM0-unsplash-1024x683.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5770"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Make your money worth it</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Home buying and its process is expense driven. You need an amount upfront to pay for downpayment or equity. Besides the mortgage area additional fees like move-in, utility connection fees, and even Home Association fees. You need to be financially capable to buy a property and be confident that you will have the capacity to pay for the mortgage. So make sure you make the purchase worth your money.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Choose a property that will make you and your family\'s life convenient. Be it closer to work, business district, or school for the kids. That way you not only save time commuting but also have lesser spending. If you\'re just starting a family, it would be ideal to buy a property that you can grow in. Something that you can see yourself living when your family grows.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: <em>Check out and <a href="http://localhost:3001/find-how-much-property-you-can-afford/">Find How Much Property You Can Afford</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5927,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/aaron-huber-G7sE2S4Lab4-unsplash-1024x678.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5927"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Know what you need when buying a home</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Every kid has a long list of what their house would be when they grow up. Make a list similar to that. List down the things you need from a house that will make your life easier. This includes location, community features like parks, swimming pools, or gym. It can also be a two-car garage or an extra space for an outdoor living area. That way you know what to look for and you do not get easily swayed with hundreds of properties listed every day.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can check on listings to see what are the new developments around the area you want to buy at. <a href="https://filipinohomes.com/properties/sale">Filipino Homes</a> has numerous properties for sale for both commercial and residential properties listed on the site. You might need to look at several properties before you can find your forever home.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: <em>You might want to read</em> <a href="http://localhost:3001/how-to-find-the-ideal-home-for-starting-or-growing-family-needs/"><em>How to find the ideal home for starting or growing family needs</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6057,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Filipino-Homes-Philippines-6.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6057"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Its different when you see it in person</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Photos can be deceiving. It does not show how hot it will get in the middle of the day, how the building units on the building beside it gets a full view of the unit, and so much more. It is best to visit a property and see the details with your own eyes. Make sure to accompany a reliable person you can ask opinion from This could be your spouse, a family member, or close friend who can give you an unbiased opinion. It will help you envision you and your family living there or make you see some issues or limitations instead. Make a pros &amp; cons list to help you weigh it out before deciding to go with the purchase.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5880,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/How-to-find-the-ideal-home-for-starting-or-growing-family-needs-3.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5880"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Long-term financial commitment</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Buying a home is a long-term financial commitment. you need a large amount of cash to settle it fully in just one go. But in the case that you need financial assistance, there are banks that have home loan plans to fit your needs. Not all home plans are the same, so it is best to do your research on which bank has the best offer that you can stick with. Consider looking into interest rates and flexible payment terms that fits your financial needs. You can visit any banks ask for their requirements for home loans and check out the best home loan plan for you. Remember think ahead of the future and not just consider the reality of you financial status at the present. But to make sure you will be capable to fulfill the financial responsibility.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>READ: <a href="http://localhost:3001/are-you-ready-for-a-home/"><em>Are You Ready For A Home?</em></a> article financial considerations to make note of before you start looking for a home</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'The whole home buying process is also a tedious process and can take from months to years. Not only do you need to financially prepare yourself but also mentally and emotionally ready as well. Below are some helpful points you need to consider before buying your forever home.','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/08/What-to-consider-when-buying-a-home.png','views' => '47','category_id' => '15','published_at' => '2020-09-15 01:37:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '481','title' => '[Kitchen Organization] 5 Ways to Create Open Pantry Space in your Home','slug' => 'kitchen-organization-5-ways-to-create-open-pantry-space-in-your-home','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The "new normal" calls for us to stay at home as much as we can and if possible, minimize supply runs. This means we need to stock up on food and other essentials, which means we need more storage space. One way to create space without having to do major home renovations is having open shelving pantry. This is a great solution for people who like to have ingredients and small appliances at arm’s length yet still have a stylish kitchen.&nbsp;If you are looking for ways to organize your kitchen without breaking the bank, this post is for you. We round up 5 easy ways you can create an open-shelf pantry in your home.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=25966135340074968" height="1150" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>1. Full-wall pantry</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=290552613462232806" height="850" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Devote an entire wall to an open pantry. You may customize the shelf length and width to hold a variety of items. It will serve as a great space to display your favorite glassware, pottery, etc., while also keeping your ingredients and small kitchen appliances easily accessible. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>2. Open-shelf kitchen nook</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=338192253269567729" height="999" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Carve out extra storage space in your kitchen by creating an open-shelf pantry in an underutilized nook you might have. This solution is a way to create a pantry that doesn’t necessarily become a focal element in the kitchen. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>3. Pantry near the prep sink</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=611715561878836369" height="1000" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Create an open pantry above a counter where you usually do prep work when cooking or baking. It\'s a good location for your pantry essentials. This type of open pantry could work well as part of a dedicated prep station, or baking station.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>4. Freestanding shelves to a wall</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=37506609384959880" height="999" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Adding freestanding shelves to an available wall could be a good storage solution for your kitchen. Repurpose old bookshelves or bookcases. Use containers and baskets to make a pantry look organized. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>5. Use floating shelves</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=294422894385538975" height="700" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Floating shelves is an easy way to create an open-shelving pantry. And it\'s such a rad way to organize your dinnerware and ingredients.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>BONUS TIP: </h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you\'re considering some light renovation in your space, here\'s a great renter-friendly idea: Build a wood feature wall in your kitchen. It functions as a divider to break up spaces, while also providing space for storage. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=111604897004427482" height="940" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/09/filipino-homes-blog-post-cover-.png','views' => '45','category_id' => '28','published_at' => '2020-09-16 13:49:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '482','title' => 'Investing your OFW savings in real estate','slug' => 'investing-your-ofw-savings-in-real-estate','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>One of the many questions OFW\'s ask is how to build their family\'s security and grow their money. Most cases, OFW\'s look into real estate for substantial and long-term investment but have limited knowledge on how the real estate industry works. And while there are a lot of information available in the internet, one of the least common talked about are the tough questions OFW\'s face when considering of buying a home or a property. Check out some questions that you may have asked to yourself before fully investing your OFW savings in real estate.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Is investing your OFW savings in real estate a good idea?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5904,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/What-is-a-foreclosure-property-Should-I-be-targeting-one-for-my-new-purchase-1.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5904"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Why am I buying a property?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The first but not so obvious question you should ask yourself is why you are buying the property before you can start investing your OFW savings in real estate. Some find this easy to answer, having dreams as a kid to own a home of their own. Which their main reason of buying a property is securing a home for their family. Others however, maybe find it difficult to ask this because they want a property they can earn from. This can come in two forms: have the property rented or holding on to it until the market value increases and selling it with the intent of earning from the sale. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is the first question to ask because it will help you determine what kind of property you need to buy. If you intend to use it as a family home, you might need to consider your family\'s needs. This includes location of the property, the community, size of the home, etc. If you plan to have it rented, you might need to consider what type of renters you prefer. If you are targeting university students, young professionals or starting family then you need to consider their needs when looking for a property.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: <em><a href="http://localhost:3001/what-is-pagibig-overseas-program-pop/">What is Pagibig Overseas Program (POP)</a> for OFWS</em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6065,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Filipino-Homes-Buying-a-Property-Philippines-5.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6065"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>How should I know which developers to look into and new developments in the area I want to purchase a property at?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Buying a property is not just picking a home because it is pretty. You need to consider the developer of the property. This will ensure you of the quality of the unit as well as the additional facilities in the building or community. Every developer has its strengths that will work for the homebuyer and it is best to talk about those with a professional about it. At Filipino Homes, it is our vision to make every Filipino find their homes. You can check out our <a href="https://filipinohomes.com/properties/sale"><em>property listing for properties on sale anywhere in the Philippines</em></a>. you can also connect with any of our <a href="https://filipinohomes.com/agents"><em>well-trained and knowledgeable Filipino Homes real estate agents</em></a> to help you with any questions you may still have. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ:<em> Not sure if you can purchase while you\'re still abroad? Check out <a href="http://localhost:3001/can-an-ofw-buy-a-property-while-outside-the-philippines/">Can an OFW buy a property while outside th</a></em><a href="http://localhost:3001/can-an-ofw-buy-a-property-while-outside-the-philippines/"><em>e Philippines?</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5924,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/floor-plan-1474454_1280-1024x678.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5924"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Should I do the actual site visit or can I get someone else to do it for me?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Preferably you need to do an actual site visit. It is important to see the property you like because it can be different in photos or videos. You might find that the property you like does not cater to your family\'s needs. See the property and the community where its at is always a good way to visualize your plans.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Make sure to schedule property viewing during your next vacation. Or you can get your spouse or parents to do site viewing for you, if you really can\'t. Make sure the person you ask to view it for you will give you reasonable opinions and without bias that way you can make an informed decision.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6064,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Filipino-Homes-Buying-a-Property-Philippines-4.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6064"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Who will manage &amp; look after the property?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In some cases, OFW\'s prefer buying a property in the city proper with the intent of having it rented. And while that is an excellent way to have a passive income, it also has additional burden like managing it. Working from abroad and having you family cities away from the property can be a problem. You might want to hire a property manager to look after the property and see all the business side of property leasing on it. This included helping you find people to rent the property to and placing your property on listings. They can also do background check &amp; interview, work on the legalities like creating a lease contract and discussing payment schemes for both you and the renter.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: <a href="http://localhost:3001/why-ofws-should-take-advantage-of-attending-philippine-property-roadshows/"><em>Why OFWs should take advantage of attending Philippine Property Roadshows?</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Home not only have a list of top-caliber real estate agents but also have professional property managers. You can find assurance that your property is well-managed and you can talk with someone who not only give you updates about the property but also in managing paperworks. This is an ideal set-up if you have a young family or elderly parents who will find it hard to constantly travel to interview a prospect renter every time. Check out the <a href="https://filipinohomes.com/agents"><em>list of real estate agents and property managers</em></a> we have in the Philippines.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/08/Questions-OFW’s-Should-Ask-Before-Buying-a-Property.png','views' => '81','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-09-17 03:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '483','title' => '5 Places to Add Backlighting in Your Home','slug' => '5-places-to-add-backlighting-in-your-home','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Backlighting </strong>is one of the popular home interior designs nowadays. People were kind of fascinated with the backlight accent that adds an element of mystique and drama of a room or a decor.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>However, not every area of your home needs backlighting as every other.&nbsp;Although its function is purely aesthetic, backlighting offers an amazing mood-boosting advantage than <a href="http://localhost:3001/maximize-natural-light/">other lighting techniques</a>. It helps to brighten up dark corners, highlight an object and illuminate home spaces.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So, let’s take a look at 5 places to introduce backlighting within your own home without having to spend a ton of time and money.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/BVvfn8uP9Ae5WQtmyisTGQxPi3TWEJk9zEh4WySgFr6UFS9hwcxyRGsWErNBHSmgkCgCDnty_Li6awtYBWqpqAvry0har6XbTJt4XCe2pIN9hiCCnA3aPuojnDEq1XHqB3tJVvxJ" alt="Places for Backlight Accents in Your Home"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":1} -->
<h1>Bedroom Ceiling</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Your bedroom is the perfect place to introduce backlighting because it’s less intense, and gives you a <a href="http://localhost:3001/6-simple-ways-to-make-your-bedroom-into-a-relaxing-haven/">perfect zone-out vibe</a>. It eliminates the need for ceiling lighting which can shine directly into the eyes when lying down and wanting to relax. It also gives you a decorative influence and eye-catching feature into your bedroom. Looks cool right?&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ:  <a href="http://localhost:3001/diy-bedroom-weekend/">7 DIY Bedroom Projects for the Weekend</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Around the TV</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/kAfBEOTl3gyJmJhrLrRULqgdsnpAyJwQSFfocAU1VifT5-dhuE75Y4ePovJehfUNkkZts89KN6w3Kxi4dU9TTVlCZkL8KJhcAHuC-T0Rw-OIKypsqWcoBVnKaPlwK08gU2Ii0D8G" alt="Places for Backlight Accents in Your Home"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can highlight your television area by adding a LED backlight behind the wall panels to fill it with an illuminating glow. It somehow draws the eye and creates a beautiful focal point to your room. In this way, your eyes won’t hurt when the lights come back on after the movie.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Home Office and Gaming Room desk</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/JSeyvhA1NPlh3xGMwKnDudPHEHVlj_8le_eDvxYgzyKc-oCqYysz7io_Wo0lu8pXsQHjLlV66nzRJ3hlpNZGHVvIfMIKta-CG0rNTzYX2mnDrzaNEPJyDzZ1jrKPbwL5v5iQ2_uV" alt="Places for Backlight Accents in Your Home"/><figcaption>Photo from <a href="https://manofmany.com/living/masculine-home-office-ideas-inspirations">ManofMany</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This too is becoming more and more popular. Backlighting your gaming room is also a great idea to reduce excess light in a room and wash out the sharpness of your computer screen. As said above, watching a screen in a dark room can strain your eyes. Backlighting helps reduce eye strain since you move from bright to dark gradually.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Bathroom mirror highlights</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/2FPHIDc73SvnoV5S6L_AbWlbylpIoP9G6Ft9wLUKjdpuXpd3y8_pTNiusuvmBmRWn9HkVojruU0vsUqAXXTShCrBGAzmpOkEMEgzT2E7RO9RvkDKlZoTRGieVkQ-JOkrLVaiWztS" alt="5 Places for Backlight Accents in Your Home"/><figcaption>Photo credit: <a href="https://www.houzz.in/hznb/professionals/interior-designers-and-decorators/the-bnk-group-pfvwus-pf~663878948?">The BNK group</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here’s a trick to make your bathroom look more dramatic. Backlighting your bathroom mirror adds to the stylish look of the space. It casts an illuminating glow throughout your bathroom making it look glamorous and elegant.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Stairway</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/nDCnRP7sD9H3q9OVV6eqB5qse9EsZ7FXBfhHLapnIlVYEslmpiZ0t981tINwkRn2IysjzSZVTDOEtJsKg3TyuZRSJC5lNp3-l6v-YfHDwuaEqIkpkJJM2FP5CC4vP56AEXOm52Xz" alt="Places-for-Backlight-Accents-in-Your-Home"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Aside from its aesthetic purpose, adding a LED strip backlight in your stairway creates a guide when you walk upward. Such lighting ensures a well-lit passage especially during night or blackouts. You can also add it on dark areas, where you don’t want to switch on bright lights throughout the day.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Home cabinets</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/xpcFsz6ltlVDufSp58ltpQOU-MLDHlxreQeCXppqcyTY5mMV4JFHUu4ExflvOg3rivdlEmPeQRiLbI6CYWkXrjl3HXydHfC7ee4HFl_qIfC2VxQoeuMC0AtmqmVzNhG9ld7Z_uWF" alt="5-Places-for-Backlight-Accents-in-Your-Home"/><figcaption>Photo by <a href="https://unsplash.com/@nicolasjleclercq?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText">Nicolas J Leclercq</a>&nbsp;</figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Backlighting your cabinet interiors can actually lighten up its contents when the door opens.&nbsp; Just a tip, mount a light under the individual shelves as it gives you an illumination. You can also use a softer light in your cabinets to make it much easier on the eyes. This works really well on cabinets with doors.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>That’s it! You see how backlighting plays an important role in enhancing the mood of a home. It affects the ambience and mood of a space. Aside from it’s aesthetic glows, backlighting subtly gives us an illuminating home interior without flooding too much brightness which is perfect for zoning out.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Have you tried backlighting too? Or do you have other ideas how backlighting can be integrated within a home? Let us know so we can feature it.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/09/5-Places-for-Backlight-Accents-in-Your-Home.jpg','views' => '49','category_id' => '13','published_at' => '2020-09-18 08:54:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '484','title' => '7 Wall Christmas Tree Ideas You Should Try for Your Small Space This Year','slug' => '7-wall-christmas-tree-ideas-you-should-try-for-your-small-space-this-year','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We\'re halfway through September! For us Filipinos, the beginning of "ber" month signals the fast-approaching Christmastime. It\'s time we start thinking of Christmas decorations. If you don’t have room for a traditional Christmas tree, a wall Christmas tree might be for you! This DIY project is a smart way to get the effect of having a Christmas tree in your home without having the bulk of one. Here are some ideas for wall-mounted Christmas trees using garlands, strings, fairy lights, washi tapes, or even family photos.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>1. Wall-mounted Christmas tree</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=10273905387597304" height="1000" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you are interested in a wall Christmas tree that really looks and feels like a traditional Christmas tree but doesn\'t take much floor space, then this DIY project is for you. It is easy to put up, has a 3-dimension feel, and it\'s something your kids or furbabies can topple over. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em><strong>Tutorial here:  </strong></em><a href="https://www.hometalk.com/25358546/wall-mounted-christmas-tree" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Wall Mounted Christmas Tree</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>2.&nbsp;<strong>Ornament tree wall</strong>&nbsp;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=46021227430379504" height="1164" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can go the minimalist route and create a Christmas tree on a wall using Christmas ornaments and nothing else. Love the ombre effect of this one!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em><strong>Tutorial here:  </strong></em><a href="https://www.purplehuesandme.com/2013/12/ornament-wall-tree.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Ornament Wall Tree</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>3. <strong>Christmas Light Christmas Tree</strong>&nbsp;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=26810560268006844" height="839" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here\'s another easy and festive idea to try:  Simply shape and tape a strand or two of fairy lights to the wall. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em><strong>Tutorial here:  </strong></em><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.purplehuesandme.com/2013/12/ornament-wall-tree.html" target="_blank">Fairy lights wall Christmas tree</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>4. Kid-Friendly<strong> Christmas Tree</strong>&nbsp;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=85146249178872944" height="565" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you have kids, then space probably isn\'t your primary issue when putting up a Christmas tree. Some kids just need their own tree to play with.  This felt Christmas tree is perfect for families with kiddos. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em><strong>Tutorial here:  </strong></em><a href="https://www.icanteachmychild.com/kid-friendly-christmas-tree/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Kid-friendly felt Christmas tree</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>5. Photo Christmas Tree</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=6544361946653057" height="1300" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>At a time when reunions are uncertain considering possible travel restrictions, a more personalized Christmas tree with photos of people you care about is a great idea. Here\'s how to make this:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<figure><iframe width="560" height="315" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/_kH2wRwElWo" allowfullscreen=""></iframe></figure>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em><strong>Tutorial here: </strong></em> <a href="https://www.lilyardor.com/photo-christmas-tree-alternative/">Photo Christmas tree</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>6. Washi Tape Christmas Tree</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=263742121899492967" height="500" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is also another great idea to have a Christmas tree using washi tapes. Washi tape is a Japanese tape often used to decorate planners, journals, packages, etc. It peels off quite easily making this an ideal material for the walls. You can go with a colorful holiday palette or go minimalist with metallic washi tape like this:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=11399805284578630" height="1000" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em><strong>Tutorial here:  </strong></em><a href="https://www.brit.co/washi-tape-trees/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Washi tape Christmas tree</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>7. String Art Christmas Tree</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=529665606176855066" height="555" width="345" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you\'re up for a string art on your wall, this one is a good alternative Christmas tree. You can use Christmas cards or photos as ornaments. You\'d need clear hooks, colored yarn or string, scissors, ruler, pencil, and small pegs.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em><strong>Tutorial here:  </strong></em><a href="https://mypoppet.com.au/makes/how-to-string-art-christmas-tree-card-display/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">String art Christmas tree and card display</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/09/filipino-homes-blog-post-cover-1.png','views' => '43','category_id' => '29','published_at' => '2020-09-21 08:47:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '485','title' => 'What are the "Hidden Charges" when buying a property?','slug' => 'what-are-the-hidden-charges-when-buying-a-property','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Buying a property is a big financial move for anyone. Looking at the market and selling value of a home, apartment or condominium can already be nerve-racking. And going through the buying process can be overwhelming as well. To add to that are hiccups and difficulties along the way. This includes some unexpected expenses required from the homebuyer.  What first-time home or property buyers do not know are the some fees and payments that needs attention throughout the home purchase process. This is what most people call "Hidden Charges", it got its term "<em>hidden</em>" because some homebuyers believe they are only expected to pay the upfront value posted on a listing and  that these payment were "hidden" from them. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>One of Filipino Homes top real estate agent, <em><strong><a href="https://filipinohomes.com/xyzayape">Charmaine Xy-Za Yape</a></strong></em> had some experiences with people who messaged her and sought advise regarding "hidden charges" they did not expect. These home-buyers expressed their confusion over additional fees and charges that were not explained to them by their real estate agents. The <em>upfront value a homebuyer sees</em> is the market value of the property you are buying, this does not include the several process like getting the electricity installed &amp; registered to your name for example. She expertly shares what these additional fees every homebuyer must look-out and expect for and why these are not included in the upfront value on the property listings.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5901,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/What-is-a-foreclosure-property-Should-I-be-targeting-one-for-my-new-purchase-3.png" alt="Save, Finance, Home Loan, Budget" class="wp-image-5901"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>1. Transfer charges</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Before you can finally say that you own the property or home, it needs to be officially transferred to your name. There are a lot of paperworks needed to transfer the property to your name and that requires administration and processing payment. These fall under Transfer Charges.<em> "While some developers already include Transfer Charges on your total payment but it is always best to ask upfront.&nbsp;That way there is room for you to set money aside for this.</em>"</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>2. Move-in fees</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Moving in is an exciting time for each homebuyer. They get excited to finally use the home and live there. But before doing so, they get surprised with some move-in requirements that are needed with additional costs. Like every new home, the electrical wiring and plumbing is already in place. But the homeowner still needs the electricity, water and other utilies installed and registered to their name.  This is covered under Move-In fees. "<em>Move-in fees are not included in the total payment. This covers the water, electricity and an advance payment for real property tax. Developers can not give you an exact and fixed amount on how much this can be but a sample calculation can be provided.</em>" This may vary for each development depending on the water and electricity service provider in the city and are beyond the scope and control of the developer. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":2334,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/How-to-Add-Value-to-Your-Property-For-Sale-03-1024x682.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-2334"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>3. Pag ibig advances</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you are planning to get a home loan from Pag-Ibig it is best you ask for any additional fees as well. These include "<em>MRI, fire insurances, etc. This figure will be given to you by Pag-Ibig</em>." In the case of the death of the insured,<strong> MRI or Mortality Redemption Insurance </strong>pays off  a part or the whole outstanding mortgage balance so his survivors will not have to pay for it. These additional fees will insure you and your family from untoward circumstances. These are fees under Pag-Ibig before finally approving your home loan. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>4.&nbsp; Bank Loan processing fee</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you decide to get a home loan from the bank, also consider a bank loan processing fee.&nbsp; This cover the processing of your documents and may vary from bank to bank. "<em>Every bank has its own processing fee and only they can give you how much this costs. The developers don\'t have any hand or control over this since this is charged by the bank you are applying loan from</em>." You can do your research on which bank offers the home loan payment you like and ask for their bank processing fee as well. This will give you a clue on how much you need to set aside when processing the bank loan.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6063,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Filipino-Homes-Buying-a-Property-Philippines-3.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6063"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>5. Condo dues or Home owners association dues</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Condominium and subdivisions have Condo Dues or Home Association Dues. This is set by the property management or HOA to covers the management of the property, including facilities and the utilities in the common areas. This includes maintenance of gym, swimming pool and the light sand water use in common areas to name a few. "<em>Real estate agents can only give an estimated amount upon reservation or sometimes upon move-in.</em>"</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>6. Building insurance and real property tax</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You also have to know that all real estate properties have either building insurance or real estate property tax. "<em>Condominiums pay annual building insurance and properties with land titles like houses needs to pay real estate property tax. You are subject to tax evasion if you do not pay for these</em>."</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/09/What-are-the-22Hidden-Charges22-when-buying-a-property.png','views' => '44','category_id' => '9','published_at' => '2020-09-22 01:54:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '486','title' => 'Back-to-School: Tips for Setting up a Home Learning Space during COVID-19','slug' => 'back-to-school-tips-for-setting-up-a-home-learning-space-during-covid-19','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A home learning space has been a talk of the town among parents, students and teachers during the \'new-normal\' virtual <em><a href="https://www.deped.gov.ph/2020/05/31/depeds-first-virtual-brigada-eskwela-oplan-balik-eskwela-set-to-promote-bayanihan-amid-covid-19-situation/">Brigada Eskwela</a></em> last month. It is upon the directives of the Department of Education (<a href="https://www.deped.gov.ph/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/DO_s2020_012.pdf">DepEd Order No. 12, s. 2020</a>) to find ways for learning to continue amidst the threat and uncertainties brought by COVID-19 pandemic.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>One of the highlights of DepEd’s order is the encouragement of all Filipino households to create a learning space or study area in preparation for the upcoming academic school year. Parents and their children were advised to prepare themselves for a blended type of learning which will employ different modalities such as Modular Distance Learning (MDL), Online Distance Learning (ODL), and television (TV) or Radio-Based Instruction.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In this set up, the teacher and students do not necessarily have to meet in person. Instead, classes are conducted online and in remote locations. Classes meet via online learning platforms based on identified schedules as well. Hence, creating a learning space at home is highly encouraged .&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/pVRT9n9pA5O0UNhfJtTWLFv3DF9L1V9Lh6ZzBzci6KUiQww10FKoNbEe61cFqil2GmP9hpesuefYmXd9Jn5PtwFcC321KiHIEbnlrtrAlyiNh3tCLKSNQGdl8xSovEbJi1Teq2xH" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>A learning space involves educational, environmental, physical (engineering), and socio-emotional factors to maximize learning potential.</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A learning space is not only about the dedicated desk or table at home. It involves different factors that provide a blueprint for learning, behavior, and attitudes. Hence, strategic use of home spaces can be a great asset that enables your child to flourish with their studies.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>How to create a learning space at home</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Whether your children are in preschool, elementary, high school or college, here’s how to create a learning-friendly space that works best for every Filipino Homes.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6215,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/How-to-create-a-Learning-Space-for-your-child-at-Home-1.jpg" alt="How-to-create-a-Learning-Space-for-your-child-at-Home-" class="wp-image-6215"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#1 Location- Designate an area for learning</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Just like in <a href="http://localhost:3001/">real estate investing</a>, location is very important in homeschooling. Try to put your child in a quiet, organized, and distraction-free area where they can focus on their school work and nothing else. If you have a home office or a spare bedroom, that’s perfect. But if you happen to live in a <a href="http://localhost:3001/making-the-most-of-the-small-living-space/">small house</a>, then a dedicated space in the kitchen or in the bedroom, would be fine. Remember this is where the learning takes place, and it should meet the following essentials.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>A learning space should be:</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Quiet</li><li>Away from distractions</li><li>Close to School supplies</li><li>Has comfortable temperature</li><li>Has an outlet for charging laptop (if there’s any)</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It would also be best to include your child when decorating because it will stimulate excitement and a sense of ownership. These essentials can help them develop routines, master self-regulation and value learning.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#2 Lighting- Make sure it’s well lit!</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Of course, who would want to study if the area is too dark? Otherwise it might make your child prone to nodding off rather than learning. It is advisable to make use of as much natural light as you can. Studies have shown that natural lighting in learning environments boosts performance, wellbeing, and creativity. The more natural light, the more conducive the environment is for learning. Natural light from windows or doors can do wonders for livening up a space. Plus, its saves energy and lowers your electricity bill.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: <a href="http://localhost:3001/maximize-natural-light/">How to Maximize Natural Light in Your Home</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#3 Prioritize comfort</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A learning space that\'s clutter-filled and has uncomfortable furniture won’t allow your child to get the most out of their study time. Do a quality check of the furniture --chair, table and light-- in your child’s proposed space at various times of the day. <a href="http://localhost:3001/how-to-keep-your-children-safe-at-home/">Childproofing your home not only keeps your children safe but also gives you a peace of mind</a>. Ask if they’re comfortable studying/working with it. This will reduce chances of discomfort such as getting back pain, leg cramps, and eye strain.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Moreover, if you have two or more kids, ask them if it’s okay for them to mix up. Would you consider alternate usage depending on class schedule? Perhaps you can innovate ways with them. The more kids you have, the more room you’ll need to have it designed properly.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#4 Keep things organized and set learning norms</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Students can learn best in an organized, clean, and clutter-free learning space. An ideal study space provides order that is simple for any child to grasp, for instance, materials are organized on low shelves so they are easy to reach. It’s also important to set learning norms for your child to get into a regular habit of getting work done such as:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>What to do first?</li><li>When to start</li><li>How long will it take?</li><li>Is food allowed?</li><li>What are the technology rules?</li><li>How can you (as a parent) help?</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#5 Encourage your child to personalize things</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When a study area is customized to the specific passions and interests of your kids, they will feel as though they have ownership of the space and will be more likely to engage in and care for it.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Try to encourage them to help you decorate or improve the space. Perhaps adding their artwork to the wall, or painting the desk their favorite color. Many studies have shown that <a href="http://localhost:3001/7-best-home-office-colors-to-boost-creativity-happiness-and-productivity/">color can seriously affect your mood</a> especially when studying. Adding ornamental plants could be a great idea too! <a href="http://filipinohomes.com/blog/benefits-of-decorating-your-home-with-indoor-plants/">It makes the study area more cozy and increases levels of positive energy</a> around.&nbsp; Just don’t overdo the personal touches so they won’t get overly distracted.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#6 Be flexible and realistic</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As a parent (at the same time teacher) at home, you have to be flexible. You’re not having a 7-hour school day like the regular class in school. You can\'t expect your child to be sitting there for a whole day. It’s highly-encouraged to have short breaks and snack times. Since online learning will mean much more screen time for students than they normally spend on schoolwork, it’s imperative also&nbsp; to schedule daily physical activities.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And be realistic too. You’re at home and of course, expect that there will be unnecessary things to come out or will happen throughout that day. Having a schedule is important, but it’s okay to alter it sometimes.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#7 Celebrate successes</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Finally, always make sure to reward or praise your child for their successes. It doesn\'t need to be a material thing. A simple “great job” or “very good” can definitely uplift a child’s morale. It makes them feel motivated and boosts their emotional being. Acknowledging your child’s effort accelerates the learning process.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Wrapping up</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As Sec. Briones said, <em>“Together, let us face the challenges of the ‘new normal’ with the virtues of the ‘old normal’—courage, faith, adventure, and discovery!</em>”&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Do you have other tips to share on how you create a child-friendly learning space in your home? Let us know in the comment section.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/09/Back-to-School_-Tips-for-Setting-up-a-Home-Learning-Space-during-COVID-19.png','views' => '47','category_id' => '13','published_at' => '2020-09-23 03:23:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '487','title' => 'Helpful Tips to Improve Work-From-Home Work-Life Balance','slug' => 'helpful-tips-to-improve-work-from-home-work-life-balance','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Work life balance is a goal everyone wants to achieve. Being stuck mostly at home and having adjusted working from home in the last months, now we want to have a healthy balance of work and home life. Having the ability to enjoy time with family and not be constantly bothered by work is hard to get when you work from home. Here are some few helpful tips to achieve a work-from-home work-life balance:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":3891,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/03/planning-calendar-1024x683.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-3891"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Plan out your day and week</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There is no better way to separate different tasks or errands than alloting time for each. This is highly applicable when planning your family time throughout the week. You can schedule some movie or family dinners during the days you do not have much on your plate at work. That way you do not constantly shuffle from work and family time.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ:<a href="http://localhost:3001/5-tips-to-actually-be-productive-when-working-from-home/"> <em>Stuck at home? 5 Tips to Actually be Productive When You’re Working From Home</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6123,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/value-job.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-6123"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Set a time for work and stick to it</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Having a set time for work programs your brain to fully focus during those time. This is also helpful on keeping you organise and efficient during workhours. Because you know that you only have a few hours in a day to finish your tasks. Now that everyone is working from home and expected to stay mostly indoors, it is so much easier to contact you and get you to work on something. Be firm on your work hours and do it first thing in the morning during your work hours instead. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: <a href="http://localhost:3001/is-it-best-to-look-for-a-home-despite-covid-19-crisis/"><em>Is It Best To Look For a Home Despite Covid-19 Crisis?</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5902,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/What-is-a-foreclosure-property-Should-I-be-targeting-one-for-my-new-purchase-2.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5902"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Let your family know about your working hours</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Being at home and easily accessible to everyone in the family can be tough. You kids wanting to play or your spouse asking a favour from you are minute things that will set off your work time. Since you spent some time with family during work, you may tend to extend your work hours to get more things done. So instead of doing that, inform your family when you\'re at work even when you are home.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5869,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/designers-home-filipino-homes.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5869"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Have a designated work area</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Having a work area tricks your brain that you are in full work mode once you sit on that home office desk or even at the dinning table. It is also helpful when family members not to bother you when they see you sitting down on your work desk. Setting up your work desk or sitting down to start work also mimics the pattern you do when you get to your office desk and starts work. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Whether or not your work calls for you to work from home, it is always best to have a small space intended for work station, studying area for the kids or simply a place where you can do admin stuff at home like paying the bills and keeping everything in order.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: <a href="http://localhost:3001/do-you-work-from-home-buy-your-next-home-with-your-office-in-mind/"><em>Do you work from home? Buy your next home with your office in mind</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/09/Helpful-Tips-to-Improve-Work-From-Home-Work-Life-Balance.png','views' => '50','category_id' => '13','published_at' => '2020-09-24 01:25:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '488','title' => 'Low-budget Swimming Pools You Can DIY at Home','slug' => 'low-budget-swimming-pools-you-can-diy-at-home','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Still feeling the summer heat? Well, putting in a small swimming pool at home might be a sure-fire idea to fend off the scorching temperatures. If you are looking for something simple and more budget-friendly, worry no more because we have found a solution for you!&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With the <a href="http://localhost:3001/what-are-the-global-real-estate-implications-of-covid-19-pandemic/">COVID-19 situation</a> continuing to develop in the country, our only and best defence to avoid its spread is to <a href="http://localhost:3001/how-to-keep-your-family-home-safe-from-covid-19/">stay at home and practice social distancing.</a> Going a day trip to a beach, resort or swimming pool is definitely not a good idea to do this time. So, better yet create your own at home.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here are 5 awesome DIY swimming pool ideas to turn your backyard into a dose of refreshment!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/wUpiFtSlbjPiW1g10KlVXaylLFSNmQhE6YujxJuBs_9vtYDA0kusVLjx1m_d2U7nBwnSHEsqxFHkdtNG-q3Sj1dAQrC0JKPbOW9QCECKzixG4UhN7GbVH5R-M8EWevG6krYFQV7u" alt=""/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":1} -->
<h1>#1 Pallet Swimming Pool</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There is no better way to cool off on a scorching summer day, especially in the Philippines than to relax in a nice cool pool. This wooden pallet swimming pool has seen viral on Facebook since 2015. Its perfectly looking structure has inspired millions of netizens to create similar structures in backyards across the world which is very ideal for summer weekend projects on a budget.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Check out the original post, from Torben Jung, below:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:group -->
<div class="wp-block-group"><div class="wp-block-group__inner-container"><!-- wp:html /--></div></div>
<!-- /wp:group -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can start building one by positioning wooden pallets upward and arrange to make your circle on a sheet of tarpaulin. Next, hold together with two ratchets and then nail it. Finish it by adding some comfy lining in the form of old towels, sheets, decors and finally the water.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Definitely amazing enough to spend quality time with the family, plus enjoy some summer snacks!&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":1} -->
<h1>#2 Concrete Backyard Swimming Pool</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/SRjq2jV6c7kx-rpoSGXpyPVkf6oykvGyCzt0h9UBNXPb7KUg3oipVPIvBlwcTKIzo2kti7ZgXk4HxDKTk1kn0qlfapXfc4t_DWSA7bxOcbQQDyUROXBRjVDGYpDLr21zvDlRZlIZ" alt=""/><figcaption>PHOTO BY ROSE ANN BAUTISTA</figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you’re up into a more fixed and secure construction pool, better yet create concrete ones.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Michael and Rose Ann shared their own version of a DIY swimming pool that is made out of hollow blocks, cement, and steel. It has a depth of around 3 ft. and drainer at the side. Accordingly, they used leftover tiles from their previous projects for the sides. They are also using a water pump to fill the pool and they drain it every 2-3 days.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/wZhMvaPOZ8wFSbrl8zOtkpVkTnyNboErkZ-nHniPZ8ge1uEfQ-_BglI7RTt5DmIFi13vBtg_-VgokOdhlSdHCXAU_IOjeEcZc9-E7jXiWd45DifdwVoXkqNEG6XryCJDWcIuetNV" alt=""/><figcaption>How the pool looks from above. PHOTO BY ROSE ANN BAUTISTA</figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This might take a bit of work so you might need the whole family for help. Take it as a way to spend quality time with the family and relatives. By just about anyone and it saves you thousands over buying a new inground pool.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":1} -->
<h1>#3 Unused Shipping Container Pool</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/v_fq6gg7EfpR07a6Sbdw-KyV4NkjKWl1xjKXZj1wjAaOtNsBlKsHinSeQcJee3gN4yzrq0uZcq8-MiZLg7yPLnRsCQR2Sryq9taNcc-YVazxQOcU2CX5LVPssLvQgLmAd8EP4hXA" alt=""/><figcaption>Photo from <a href="https://www.pinterest.ph/pin/518054763378763148/">besideroom</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Got an empty shipping container at home? Why not transform it into this amazing backyard swimming pool!&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can do this by digging a huge hole in the backyard to fit the dumpster in, then adding some primer and paints. This is followed by softening the structure’s rough edges to make it suitable for the whole family to use. The only disadvantage of using a shipping container is it rusts. But it can be painted anyway, so push!&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":1} -->
<h1>#4 Natural Swimming Pool</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/5wZmpbEntOuGgZooAP86oI1M1JDRp_HxmvTdjJUdS5AZ84vWYSTW4WAjH424DjLNcqvsyGZQbVrs_mSzqgy86kBqQFPwwRpTBzHX2xwweyyfvnNSZ8GNu9jyPDN-snkJTtdqN0TQ" alt=""/><figcaption>Photo by Robins Nest Aquatics</figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you are blessed to have <a href="http://localhost:3001/pagadian-city-waterfalls/">a natural water landscape</a> near you, take advantage of that and turn it into a classy backyard swimming pool. Whether it be near the river, a waterfall or seashore. You can build your own all-natural swimming pond and share the fun with nature.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Your only investment here would be gravel stone and clay instead of concrete, and natural aquatic plants in place of harsh chemicals. This is definitely a beautiful transformation for your backyard area.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":1} -->
<h1>#5 Repurposed Water Tank Swimming Pool</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/2aRnLezD8kKd-EgkV1phszMfJ__qmlX2JyJuudD7rF16HdshHCP1jhRkiMWLtWC93Lul7zzrX7AAklruvZ8JWHuOdsBgADyRnenWRf796gzMvTePA9kPaXNtnvfLaBp09Cxd3whw" alt=""/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Another cool idea is to repurpose an empty large container or a stock tank into an above-ground swimming pool. It’s quite a valuable investment for a swimming pool when you take into consideration all the benefits and enjoyment it can give you in the future. Nothing can add the much-needed flair of freshness to your family bonding time and comfort those scorching heats of summer!&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Hope these simple, easy to construct DIY Home Swimming Pool Ideas turn your backyard into a real deal! Building these requires creativity, construction skills, and of course, assistance and support from your loved ones. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/09/Low-budget-Swimming-Pools-You-Can-DIY-at-Home-Filipino-Homes.jpg','views' => '79','category_id' => '13','published_at' => '2020-09-25 08:35:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '489','title' => '10 Budget-Friendly Living Room Makeover Ideas','slug' => '10-budget-friendly-living-room-makeover-ideas','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The simplest room makeovers are often the best ways to give your space a fresh look.  Little changes like new&nbsp;paint, updating your throw pillows, or&nbsp;repurposing worn-out furniture are some budget-friendly ways to rework your living room. Here are some of our favorite ideas for quick and easy living room makeovers:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>1. Rearrange the furniture</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=1266706133210257" height="1000" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>An alternative layout of your living room is a quick and cheap makeover idea. Consider moving your furniture around and probably use an artwork as a focal point. Sometimes, a good de-cluttering and clearing out of tired furniture can make your space look and feel airier and larger.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>2. Create a gallery wall</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=19069998411796361" height="550" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Gallery walls are a great way to personalize a space and also showcase your artwork or favorite family photos. You can choose frames of the same color for a cohesive look or really mix it up with frames in a variety of colors and sizes.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=563018692330092" height="1000" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>3. Showcase your favorite souvenirs</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=517491813435016751" height="1000" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you miss traveling, then maybe it\'s about time to showcase your collection of souvenirs from a favorite vacation for a happy reminder of an enjoyable getaway.  Whether it\'s little trinkets you collect, postcards or subway maps, a display area in your living room can help you reminisce about the memories of travel and look forward to a future when we are all able to explore again without restrictions.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>4. Manage the clutter</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=241787073734108958" height="998" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If your living room is everyone\'s favorite <em>"tambay" </em>area, you probably got used to seeing toys, chargers, books, etc. crowding the space. Tidy up and help everyone in the family stay organized by providing a dedicated area for stashing toys, cables, and other items.&nbsp;Bookcases and basket drawers can help add extra storage space to keep the room feeling relaxed and tidy.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>5. Give new life to tired, old furniture</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=346636502570137822" height="1042" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Most of the time, a fresh coat of paint can give a new look to items you already have. You can go with any color, or for a fun twist, use painter\'s tape to add stripes.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>6. Update the walls</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=430093833164793750" height="700" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>One of the easiest makeover-on-a-budget ideas is to paint your walls. There are a lot of good-quality, low-priced paint options out there.  You can go for plain colors or go for fun patterns using a patterned paint roller to create an accent wall. For renters, you can use removable wallpaper.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>7. Change your cushions</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=15762667435921965" height="760" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Cushions / throw pillows are probably the most versatile of soft furnishings. Available in so many different sizes, shapes, colors, and textures, a few new cushions could easily transform the look and theme of your living room.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>8. Modernize lights </h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=315463148902830730" height="1000" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Give your outdated light fixtures a fresh look. You may need to update your bulbs to help brighten your room and save energy.&nbsp;Or update your existing light fixtures with matte black paint using spray paint.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>9. Paint the ceiling a different color</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=264586546847043864" height="700" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>While you\'re changing the look of the living room, consider updating the ceiling as well. Painting the ceiling a soft shade of blue that brings to mind the sky, draws the eyes up naturally, making your room feel more airy and open.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>10. Add a touch of nature</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=456693218465396365" height="1000" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Adding even a small touch of the outdoors is sure to make your living room feel more alive. Potted plants are ideal because they clean the air but, if your thumb is brown, bring a cut branch indoors and pop it into a sturdy container for maintenance-free greenery.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/09/filipino-homes-blog-post-cover-2.png','views' => '57','category_id' => '13','published_at' => '2020-09-26 02:04:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '490','title' => 'Tips to Get You in Good Financial Shape to Buy Your Dream Home','slug' => 'tips-to-get-you-in-good-financial-shape-to-buy-your-dream-home','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Buying a house is mostly a financial responsibility. You need to be in good financial shape to make a purchase with the downpayment and be able to pay the mortgage month in and month out. It is not about good market conditions but more about your personal financial readiness. Here are tips to get you in good financial shape to buy your dream home:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":2417,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/2-Finances.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-2417"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Pay down or pay off your debt</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You needs to pay down or totally pay off any existing debt. Buying your dream home most likely get you into one through home loan. You need to be able to pay any existing loan or debt to show that you are will be able to handle the financial responsibility of paying the monthly mortgage. It will also help in your debt-income ratio and most likely will be approved to get a home loan. This is why lending institutions asks for any existing loans (personal, home, car, etc.) and how far along are you. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: You can also check out<em> <a href="http://localhost:3001/are-you-financially-ready-to-buy-a-house/">Are You Financially Ready to Buy A House?</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5617,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/budget.jpg" alt="Save, Finance, Home Loan, Budget" class="wp-image-5617"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Maintain a good credit score</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Most of the time a bank looks into your credit score. A credit score is a numerical expression that reflects a borrower\'s repayment of debt. This can be source through banks, credit card companies, government offices, etc. It shows your ability to pay your financial obligations one time. Make sure you pay your credit card or other loans in time. That way you not only stay on top of your financial obligations but also work on making a good credit score.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5618,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/EF-1024x683.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5618"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Have an emergency fund</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Paying off your debt is the first thing to do to achieve that good financial shape. The next thing is saving up for an emergency fund. An emergency fund is 3-6 months worth of your monthly expense. You need to calculate all the necessary expenses you incur every month and multiply that to 3-6 times - that is the amount you need to raise for your emergency fund. Emergency funds is intended for the times you lose your income stream. It gives you 3 to 6 months worth of expenses until you get back on track. That way even when you lose your job, you will still funds to be able to pay your financial obligations like loans, etc.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: You might also find<em> <a href="http://localhost:3001/renter-to-owner/">How to Transition From Renter to Owner: 7 Helpful Tips</a> </em>helpful</p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5901,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/What-is-a-foreclosure-property-Should-I-be-targeting-one-for-my-new-purchase-3.png" alt="Save, Finance, Home Loan, Budget" class="wp-image-5901"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Calculate what you can afford</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You have to be realistic and do the math diligently. Calculate your income and your expenses (including savings) to check if you you can realistically afford to buy the house you want. You do not want to raise the large amount for downpayment but will find a hard time paying off your monthly mortgage. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6123,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/value-job.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-6123"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Speak to a professional</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There is no better way to get good property deals than through a real estate broker or agent who knows promos offered by developers. Get in touch with a real estate agent in your area and speak to them about your goals. Let them know the type of property you\'re eyeing and how much you can afford. They will let you know if your are in the right track or you need to work on your budget more. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: Check out <em><a href="http://localhost:3001/tips-to-help-you-find-a-superstar-real-estate-agent/">Tips to help you find a superstar real estate agent</a></em> to help you get in touch with a professional</p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>No other best time to start working on a dream but now. Check out the top <a href="https://filipinohomes.com/agents">real estate agents in the Philippines</a> and get some professional real estate advice and direction.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/09/Tips-to-Get-You-in-Good-Financial-Shape-to-Buy-a-House.png','views' => '45','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-09-28 01:38:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '491','title' => 'Cebu Landmasters completes P1.2 billion three-tower residential condo in CDO','slug' => 'mesaverte-garden-residences-in-cagayan-de-oro-officially-turned-over','content' => '<!-- wp:image {"id":6345,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/Mesaverte-Residences-2020-07-1-1024x768.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-6345"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leading VisMin residential developer Cebu Landmasters Inc. (CLI) recently marked the completion of the three-tower P1.2 billion Mesaverte Residences in Cagayan de Oro City and has started to turnover more&nbsp;than half of the development’s 700 units to their owners.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Mesaverte Residences is expected to generate about P2 billion gross revenues for CLI which posted record reservation sales from housing projects of P7.43 billion in 1H 2020, a growth of 41% year-on- year.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Mesaverte Residences is the third completed project of CLI’s mid-market Garden Series, the listed&nbsp;company’s top revenue contributor in H1 2020. Construction work governed by strict safety guidelines&nbsp;continued even during the lockdown period in Cagayan de Oro and a number of other CLI sites in Vismin cities where quarantine restrictions were minimal.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6347,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/Mesaverte-Residences-2020-07-2-1024x768.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-6347"/><figcaption>Construction of Cebu Landmasters’ three-tower Mesaverte Residences in CDO is completed and the listed company is now starting to turnover the units to its owners. The development is CLI’s first project outside of Cebu and the third of its top-selling mid-market Garden Series.</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Launched in 2016, Mesaverte was CLI’s first project outside of its home turf Cebu. Offering 20-40 sqm studios and one-bedroom units, the first phase of the project sold out in less than a year. This prompted the launching of the second phase the following year.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The three-tower Mesaverte Residences occupies a 8,740 sqm property. Sixty percent of the lot is devoted to open space complimented by generous amenities like a clubhouse, function rooms,&nbsp;swimming pools, fitness gym, children’s playground and a multi-purpose court.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6346,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/Mesaverte-2020-09-2-1024x768.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-6346"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Jose Soberano III, CLI CEO observed that VisMin buyers in general are on the lookout for good value&nbsp;housing. “We’re happy that the quick takeup&nbsp;of our units affirms we are meeting their needs for residences that are priced right and in strategic city locations. Moreover, our residences are part of well- managed communities that offer individuals and families personal safety and security they need during&nbsp;these uncertain times.”</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Cebu Landmasters is focused on serving the undiminished demand for affordable and mid-priced housing in VisMin with a total of 14 projects in 2020 worth Php 19 billion. The listed company currently has 70 developments in 15 key VisMin cities across the region. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/09/Mesaverte-Residences-2020-07-1-1.jpg','views' => '42','category_id' => '9','published_at' => '2020-09-28 04:16:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '492','title' => '7 Kitchen Makeover Ideas on a Budget','slug' => '7-kitchen-makeover-ideas-on-a-budget','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Having spent much more time preparing your meals at home during the quarantine season, you might have considered updating your kitchen. You don\'t really need a deep pocket to give your space a fresher look. In this blog post, we have compiled 7 ways to upgrade the look of your kitchen without breaking the bank:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>1. Paint your kitchen cabinets</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If your kitchen cabinets are still in relatively excellent condition, a fresh coat of paint can be all you need to transform your kitchen. Here\'s a great before-and-after example of how paint can change your kitchen from dark and outdated to bright, airy, and modern.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=651685008572327562" height="1000" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>2. Replace your cabinet door handles</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Replacing your kitchen cabinet door handles can help transform your kitchen. High-quality handles can make your cabinets look expensive. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=98164466867794346" height="991" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>3. Install open shelves</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If your cabinet doors are in bad shape, consider removing the doors and keep your open shelving. It\'s trendy and a great way to display your favorite pieces. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=351421577176667004" height="1000" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong><em>READ:  </em><a href="http://localhost:3001/?p=6143" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">5 Ways to Create Open Pantry Space in your Home</a></strong></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>4. Update your taps</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Updating your old taps with new options can easily give your sink area a facelift.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=2885187246999570" height="1000" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>5. Improve your lighting</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Lighting can make a huge difference to a kitchen makeover. Make sure you have ample lighting. Placing pendant lights over a bench can add extra interest to your room. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=18858892175964344" height="1000" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>6. Refresh the splashback</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Your splashback is a relatively small area where you can go all out on your makeover project without spending too much.  There are several ways that could be done at low cost, but with significant impact. You can either replace with new tiles if you have the budget, or you can just use tile paint and paint over your existing tiles. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=1970393575465182" height="1400" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em>Tips on painting your splashback here: </em><a href="https://designertrapped.com/painting-tile-backsplash/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">How to Paint Your Tile Backsplash in 5 Simple Steps</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>7. Update chipped floor tiles </h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you have chipped floor tiles and you have the budget to upgrade, replacing the tiles can be a great idea. If there\'s hardwood beneath the old tiles, removing the tiles altogether and refinishing the wood can be a great option.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=21110691993170720" height="1000" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/09/filipino-homes-blog-post-cover-3.png','views' => '56','category_id' => '9','published_at' => '2020-09-29 13:58:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '493','title' => 'The Top 3 Costs of Owning a Home','slug' => 'the-top-3-costs-of-owning-a-home','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Everyone dreams of having a house they can call their own. Having their own space to decorate it the way they wish and having a home that they will always have the final say on everything. Buying a house is a goal for every Filipino family and who wouldn\'t want to have a property under their name? But buying a house is a financial responsibility. More than the upfront value of the house you like to buy, there are other costs when it comes to owning a house and managing your own household. Below are top 3 costs of owning a home that you need to know:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6275,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/Filipino-Homes-Homes-Buy-or-Sell-a-Home.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6275"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Downpayment and other necessary fees</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>One of the roadblocks for people wanting to buy a house is the large amount of money needed to get the purchase journey started. Before you can purchase a property you need to come up with 10-20% of the selling value of the property as a downpayment. Besides that you might also come across of necessary fees like reservation fee, insurance fees paid at the bank, processing fees and even move-in fees.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Make sure to do your research. Find the bank that offers a good home load payment scheme that you can afford. Do not be shy to ask questions about how much the calculate mortgage would be and if there are current home loan promos the bank or lenders is offering. Also make sure to ask the real estate agent on the necessary fees you need to expect. That way you know around how much you need to save or set aside during the homebuying process.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6283,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/Filipino-Homes-Homes-Selling-a-Home.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6283"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Paying the utilities</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It is a big moment for a first-time homeowner to finally be able to use and live in the the newly bought house. Besides paying your monthly mortgage, you also need to take care of the utilities to keep the home running. Paying the electricity, water, internet and cable connection are a few bills you need to pay. Ofcourse, your bill will reflect your consumption of these services.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Make sure to go easy on water use and turn off the lights when not in use. You also need to research on the type and brands of appliances that will help you save. LED lights for example is more expensive that regular light bulbs but it uses less energy and last longer. These are simple ways to help curb the expenses you have having your own home.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6279,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/Filipino-Homes-Homes-Selling-a-Home-Buying-a-Home-Homebuyer.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6279"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Repairs or renovating your home</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Every home when well-lived will have some need of fixing. There might be leak in plumbing, the roof gutter needs cleaning, the roof is leaking and all sorts. These are some problems the homeowner will at some point face. Make sure you have an emergency fund or a house fund set aside for home repairs. That way when something needs fixing, you have some money set aside for it.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/09/Buying-a-Home-Top-3-Costs-of-Owning-a-Home.png','views' => '46','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-09-30 13:55:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '494','title' => 'The Value of Concrete Countertops: Customization Increases Aesthetic Appeal and Real Estate Investment for Homeowners','slug' => 'the-value-of-concrete-countertops-customization-increases-aesthetic-appeal-and-real-estate-investment-for-homeowners','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Concrete countertops are now becoming popular again. As minimalist and industrial designs are being chosen by minimalist Millennials. In fact, concrete countertops have become somewhat of a status symbol for kitchens, rivaling granite, and other high-end countertop surface options. Consumer Reports Magazine ranked concrete highest for its customization and exclusivity among high-end kitchen countertops.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6328,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/Concrete-Counters-2-4-1024x732.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-6328"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As a custom product, the amount of time and craftsmanship required to produce concrete countertops places them as the most labor-intensive and priciest among leading countertop materials. My late Dad was a civil engineer and the majority of his projects even before is using a concrete base countertop. However, clients most of the time would prefer tiled countertops of granite. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>However, concrete countertops are becoming more accessible for those on a modest budget. The latest do-it-yourself (DIY) trend to captivate homeowners and builders is building your own concrete countertop. There is little monetary investment in making concrete countertops, yet the creative gains of working with concrete are plentiful.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>THE SHOWSTOPPER</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6329,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/custom-color-red-orange-concrete-countertop-2_fp4pnf-2.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-6329"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Increasingly, homeowners are moving away from the monotonous, manufactured look of traditional countertop surfaces. They are now choosing concrete for its earthy, timeless appeal. Plus, the options for personalizing concrete countertops are endless.  One can color, polish, stamp and stain concrete or imbed personal objects like stones, seashells and fossils into the countertops surface, adding sentiment and character. Functional features such as drain boards, soap dishes, and trivets can also be incorporated to suit the homeowners own needs and lifestyle.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Concrete is slowly becoming demystified as characteristically cold and industrial. On the contrary, this age-old material is warm and surprisingly tactile; people cannot help but touch their smooth, polished surfaces. You can build a pour-in-place concrete counter for the home kitchen and bathrooms. The sand-colored concrete countertops were polished smooth, then paired with a natural slate of varying colors  like charcoal, rust, and gold tones that forms the backsplashes in the kitchen and baths. As a design accent, small rectangular slate tiles were added to the rim of the bathroom sinks, which provided a unique detail to the custom vanities.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6331,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/OIP.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-6331"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The concrete countertops were easily the most unique and impressive of all the finishes. I believe they were a huge part in adding value to the home. In the Philippines, all you see in homes are granite countertops. And I really think homebuyers are getting quite numb with granite.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>BREAKING THE MOLD</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6330,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/maxresdefault-1-1024x576.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-6330"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Another advantage of concrete is its adaptability in either modern or traditional settings. This is true especially when coupled with other materials like varied metals, wood, or stone. Concrete adds so many [possibilities] to stone, and the combination with slate, which is hugely popular here, gives the mountain homes an overall warm, natural touch, says Joy.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The L-shaped concrete countertop has a rough, rustic stone appearance, complementing its rugged country surroundings. An integral drain board and trivets provides function and added interest to the concrete countertop. Natural slate backsplashes, distinct wall accents, and a butcher block countertop at the kitchen island all resonate with the traditional warmth and earthiness of the concrete countertops.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Concrete countertops can add tremendous aesthetic and financial value to a home. Concretes customization and a show-stopping appeal are like no other countertop surface. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/09/filipino-homes-realtor-blogger-xyza-yape.png','views' => '49','category_id' => '10','published_at' => '2020-10-01 01:53:29','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '495','title' => 'Buying Property Online? Tips for Safe Real Estate Transactions','slug' => 'buying-property-online-tips-for-safe-real-estate-transactions','content' => '<!-- wp:image {"id":5878,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/How-to-find-the-ideal-home-for-starting-or-growing-family-needs-2.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5878"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Browse through online listings</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Buying a home starts off by looking at available houses or units in your preferred community or area. And while being limited in the comforts in your homes can be quiet a challenge when looking for a new home, online listings are the best bet. Check out online listings of real estate portals in the Philippines. These listings work alongside professional broker and real estate agents as well as real estate developers to provide all the important information of a new condo or subdivision development. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes has thousands of property listings in nearly every city and towns in the Philippines. From condominiums to houses in subdivisions and even large empty land for your dream agriculture or business ideas.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: <a href="http://localhost:3001/is-it-best-to-look-for-a-home-despite-covid-19-crisis/"><em>Is It Best To Look For a Home Despite Covid-19 Crisis?</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5891,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/3.png" alt="Filipino Homes, professional real estate agents in the Philippines" class="wp-image-5891"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Connect with professional real estate agent or broker</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Still wanting to buy that dream property but don\'t know where start? Connect with real estate agents to help you start your home buying journey. Professional real estate agents or brokers are knowledgeable of the ins and outs of the home buying process. It is also good to have advise from a professional on the requirements you need and the steps you need to take to make the purchase. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: <a href="http://localhost:3001/tips-to-help-you-find-a-superstar-real-estate-agent/"><em>Tips to help you find a superstar real estate agent</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5553,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/man-using-stylus-pen-for-touching-the-digital-tablet-screen-6335.jpg" alt="Filipino Homes, real estate portal" class="wp-image-5553"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Research on the web</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With everyone stuck at home and encouraged not go out from their homes, a lot of businesses and offices had adapted to making their services accessible online. These also meant you can easily research about the property you want to buy or simply research about home loans from the safety of your home. Here are some information you can gather while doing your research on the web:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Property owners experiences: If you\'re lucky you will fin people sharing about their property purchase journey online. You can find these on their personal blogs, social media posts or in vlogs on YouTube. You can gather information based on how they went through the process to help you decide on whether to buy that property or not.</li><li>Home loans from banks: Banks these days have made home loan information accessible online. You can research the home loan schemes the banks have and also compare the interest rates before making a sound decision. If you need more information, bank officers now entertains appointment through calls to give you a better understanding of the home loan you are planning to get.</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6276,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/Filipino-Homes-Homes-Buying-a-Home-Selling-a-Home.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6276"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Go on virtual tours</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you find that it is a challenge to hop visit every home or property you are interested in during this pandemic, consider doing a virtual tours. Real estate agents can walk you through a virtual tour for the properties that your are eyeing without having to leave your home.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: <a href="http://localhost:3001/buying-a-house-during-covid-pandemic/"><em>Buying a House During COVID Pandemic</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/10/Buying-Property-Online-Tips-for-Safe-Real-Estate-Transactions.png','views' => '43','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-10-02 01:21:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '496','title' => '7 Makeover Ideas for Small Dining Rooms','slug' => '7-makeover-ideas-for-small-dining-rooms','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipinos love to eat; food&nbsp;will always be something that brings us together. Make every meal a more beautiful experience by sprucing up your dining area. Even if you don’t have a big budget or a big space, you can create a beautiful dining room. You can make it appealing and inviting. Here are some tips and ideas to help transform your dining room into a more desirable room to bond with the family in.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>1. Clean and declutter</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=367465650851893665" height="500" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If your dining room has become a catchall for the stray papers and other random items in the home, a good decluttering session could be a great place to start. It\'s free and can potentially give your space look and feel fresher, bigger, and airier. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>2.  Shop your house</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=398216792055135742" height="907" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Check other rooms in your house&nbsp;and bring in something into the dining room. Maybe there\'s a potted plant that can bring life into your space or an artwork that would just be perfect in the area.  You can spruce up your dining area with framed postcards or heirloom pieces inherited from a family member.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>3. Fresh Wallpaper</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=24206916736160520" height="1000" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Wallpapers are a great solution if you don\'t have the luxury of time or budget for a fresh coat of paint. This can also be the perfect opportunity to create a focal point and explore patterns in your space.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>4. Circular Table</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=357895501640314184" height="901" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A sleek, round table in your dining room can help make a small area appear much larger.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>5. Mirrors Galore</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=127297126946467864" height="885" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Natural light is very crucial for small spaces. If you can, place your dining set directly in front of the windows. If it\'s not feasible, one great solution is to use mirrors. Mirrors can help a cozy area feel much brighter. Strategically hanging mirrors behind your dining area can help allow light to bounce around the space.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>6. Bold Lighting</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=329396160251575125" height="1000" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Bold lighting can also help elevate the overall look of your dining space. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>7. Colorful Seating</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=453948837438673004" height="961" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Don\'t be afraid to use colors in your dining area. Refresh your space with colorful chairs that best represent your design aesthetic.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/09/filipino-homes-blog-post-cover-4.png','views' => '40','category_id' => '31','published_at' => '2020-10-03 00:55:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '497','title' => 'Want To Sell Your Home Faster? Try Home Staging!','slug' => 'want-to-sell-your-home-faster-try-home-staging','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Home staging tells homeowners how to prepare and market their home for sales in the real estate market. Professional home stagers are professionals that help you in preparing your home for sale. They help you create a very good first impression on potential homebuyers by taking care of your house and its appeal. In the Philippine market, home stagers are frequently used by owners and sellers of High end or luxury houses. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://images.homify.com/c_fill,f_auto,q_0,w_740/v1515534194/p/photo/image/2384089/Foto_Fabio_Peixoto_2044.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Professional home stagers rearrange your home’s furniture, making it more organized. They help you redesign your house so that it appeals to potential homebuyers in the market. They can also suggest and in some cases, purchase furniture or fixtures to make your home show it’s absolute best!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>To put it differently, they <a href="http://localhost:3001/4-effective-ways-to-sell-your-property-listing-tips-for-real-estate-agents/" data-type="URL" data-id="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/4-effective-ways-to-sell-your-property-listing-tips-for-real-estate-agents/">make your house sellable</a> with their design experience and expertise. Home staging is particularly useful where prices appreciate slowly and finding a buyer takes a lot of time.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>The Home Staging Process</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://www.photoup.net/wp-v4/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/Virtual-Staging-Sample-Living-Room.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> The first impression is the key to a good offer and quick sale. Most buyers make up their mind even before entering the house! That is why it becomes so vital to create a winning first impression. A real estate agent may be good at marketing your house, he/she may know what makes it sell but in all probability he may not be able to help you do it. This is where professional home stagers come in. They help you prepare your house for the best first impact.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> Zeroing in on a professional home stager is not difficult. You can ask your friends and acquaintances who have recently sold a house for reference. Your real estate agent or company can also help you in this regard. In all probability they might have already utilized the services of the professional home stagers in your area.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> Once you have zeroed in on a few home stagers, the next step is to find out the cost. It is always good to get an estimate from a few home stagers. Mostly it is a quick and accurate process. You should then make calculations and comparisons. It is always a good idea to discuss estimates with them before making a final decision.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://blog.homejab.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/09/Livingroomb4andafter-copy-764x1024.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> It is also important to take into account others factors like the state of your home, asking price and average time the houses are on sale before a deal is clinched. Asking price is the most important factor. If the asking price is low, it may not be feasible to hire professional home stager, more so when the higher price is not in tandem with the cost involved. All these factors go a long way in helping you make an informed decision of hiring a professional home stager.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> On occasion your real estate agent may also contribute to the charges of your professional home stager. This is done when your real estate agent is convinced that the charges are reasonable and the investment is worthwhile.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Doing It On Your Own</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://www.thespruce.com/thmb/t8VBKQDK_LWtxz5rLu8M34iAt1o=/735x0/HP-Midcentury-Inspired-living-room-58bdef1c3df78c353cddaa07.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you don’t want to spend money and hire professionals you can do home staging on your own. Here are few tips on do-it-yourself home staging:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>1) Clean your house, yard, kitchen bathrooms, drapes, and carpets. Wash the windows.<br>2) Make your home organized and less cluttered. This will make your home look neat and spacious. Remove all the unnecessary objects.<br>3) Get your home repainted.<br>4) Check the floor. It might need refinishing.<br>5) Change furniture and fixtures to make your house more appealing. You can buy try borrowing or renting.<br>6) Remove unnecessary pictures. Rearrange others.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Home staging can help your house sell faster and at a better price than you probably would be able to without any preparation. The thing to remember is that your home should appeal to a wide variety of buyers. The best way to do this is to use neutral colors and rich fabrics.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/10/filipino-homes-xyza-yape-real-estate-agent-.png','views' => '36','category_id' => '16','published_at' => '2020-10-04 23:58:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '498','title' => 'Buying a house? Signs you\'re not financially ready & how to fix it','slug' => 'buying-a-house-signs-youre-not-financially-ready-how-to-fix-it','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>One of the huge financial decision a person or family make in their lives is buying a house. Home buying is an exciting journey but it also brings with it an overwhelming financial responsibility. Hence why people are scrutinizing their finances first before fully deciding to it. Are you planning to buy a house but not sure if you\'re financially ready? </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":1876,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2017/05/finances.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-1876"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>You have low credit score</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You may have always heard about credit score and not sure what that means. Credit score is a numerical figure that reflects your ability and likelihood to pay credit back. Banks&nbsp; and other lenders calculates and looks into credit score to see the level of risk in lending to you.<br><br>A good credit score means a higher chance of approving your loan. It also may mean significantly lower monthly payments and better interest rate on your mortgage. If you do not have a great credit score, consider delaying your plans until you built up your credit.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5617,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/budget.jpg" alt="Save, Finance, Home Loan, Budget" class="wp-image-5617"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>30% of your income goes towards monthly payments</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Personal finance experts say that the total monthly payment should not consume more than 30% of your take home pay. these payments include monthly rent, insurance payment, utility bills, monthly tuition for the kids and the such. Any more than the 30% for monthly payment will put you in a tight position should those financial obligations increase. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Step back and examine your finances. Check where you can cut off your spending and see how it goes from there. Sometimes you just need a lifestyle to check to realize where your money is going and you have to be smart moving forward. You can also consider asking for a raise or adding a side hustle to increase your monthly income.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5618,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/EF-1024x683.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5618"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>You don\'t have emergency funds</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Buying a house is a huge financial responsibility. It is not something that you can easily walk away from if you are having difficulty with your finances. Unlike renting where you can find another house with lesser rental fee, owning a house with a mortgage ties you up for a long time.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Emergency fund is money set aside should you find yourself without work or income. It is your buffer savings to help you out with your finances with sudden income loss. Having emergency fund or savings for emergencies like such will help cover financial obligations like mortgages.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you do not have emergency fund yet, consider starting now. Not only will it help you achieve your financial freedom but it will also give you a peace of mind knowing you have back-up funds to cover your expenses for the unforeseen circumstances in the future.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>READ: <em><a href="http://localhost:3001/how-do-you-know-if-you-are-ready-to-buy-a-property-7-financial-questions-to-ask-yourself-before-buying-a-house/">How Do You Know if You are Ready to Buy a Property? [7 Financial Questions to Ask Yourself Before Buying a House]</a></em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6055,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Filipino-Homes-Philippines-2.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6055"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>You are not actively setting money aside for savings</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Even with an emergency fund, you should still be able to set aside money to put on savings. If you don\'t have extra money after you paid your bills and mortgage, you might be placed in a tight spot. Owning a home is also knowing that there will be maintenance or upgrade costs. Having just enough money to cover your means might get you deeper into debt.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You don\'t need to set aside huge money every time but it does pay to start putting money into savings account to help fund some of your goals or for your future self. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>READ: <em><a href="http://localhost:3001/5-things-to-do-before-you-build-your-new-home/">5 Things to Do Before You Build Your New Home</a></em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":3666,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/01/hire-professional-mover-1024x684.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-3666"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>You\'re planning to move elsewhere</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you have plans to move to another province or country, it would not be a smart move to put yourself in a financial constraint by buying a house. The first few years of your mortgage mostly covers the interest and not the principal loan. Instead pool and save that money for the time you will purchase a home when you eventually move.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>READ: <em><a href="http://localhost:3001/ready-buy-home/">How Do I Know if I’m Ready to Buy a Home?</a></em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4893,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/Real-Estate-Property-Investments.png" alt="" class="wp-image-4893"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>You think you the only expense you need to worry is the one on the real estate listing or ad</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Buying a house comes with a large cost. Keep in mind that there are additional charges and fees that comes when purchasing a home. Do not expect to only pay the selling price of house, there are more expenses to it. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Research on the additional charges you might encounter when buying a home. These includes bank fees, processing fees, move-in fees and the likes. You can ask your real estate agent on how much to prepare on top of the selling price of the property your eyeing. These additional charges and fees are not covered or included in your loan, so you need to prepare for it.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>READ: <a href="http://localhost:3001/what-are-the-hidden-charges-when-buying-a-property/"><em>What are the “Hidden Charges” when buying a property?</em></a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/10/Buying-a-house-Signs-youre-not-financially-ready-how-to-fix-it.jpg','views' => '64','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-10-06 00:24:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '499','title' => 'Podcast Launch | Real Estate Spotlight','slug' => 'podcast-launch-real-estate-spotlight','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Pursue personal growth in your Real Estate Career. Feed your thoughts with the best practices shared by accomplished Real Estate Professionals. Wherever you are, at home, in your car, or during your daily commute, you can now listen to the Real Estate Spotlight. Anthony Leuterio will be hosting this live podcast on how to become a Real Estate Superstar. Catch the first episode tomorrow. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6403,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/120841816_10218348823894698_7404114022619067911_o-1024x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-6403"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/10/120841816_10218348823894698_7404114022619067911_o.jpg','views' => '35','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2020-10-07 10:32:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '500','title' => 'Condo vs House: Not sure whether to buy a condominium or a house?','slug' => 'condo-vs-house-not-sure-whether-to-buy-a-condominium-or-a-house','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Real estate investing is an exciting milestone but it can be very difficult and overwhelming. So much so that most people get stuck longer on the deciding process of whether to buy a property or not. One of the pain points when buying a property is also deciding what kind of property you\'re going to buy. Will it be house in a subdivision or a condominium in the middle of the city. There\'s really no general right or wrong answer to this. It all depends on how you want to use the property, your preferences and your family\'s needs.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Fortunately buying a property does follow some factors to consider to make a sound decision. For example, if you\'re looking for a property with the purpose of using it to invest and earn from, condominium is a better choice. But if you want to use the property for a growing family with the intention of having an extra outdoor space for kids to run and play around, a landed house is a great way to go.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Getting a Condominium</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":2307,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/How-to-Make-Your-Condominium-Unit-Look-Bigger-07.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-2307"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Condo apartments cost for upkeep is not as big compared to a landed house. You don not have to worry about keeping the gardens well-maintained. Safety and security is taken cared for. Condominiums are also easier to lease and rent out especially if the location is near universities or offices. Renters can come and go and not have to worry about huge rent when they only intend to stay there for a few years or so.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>However, one of condominiums biggest disadvantage is having additional fees to worry about. Association fees to help with building maintenance, amenities like swimming pool, playground and gym depends on how big your unit is. It is directly proportional to the floor area of the unit you\'re intending to buy. If you plan to buy a bigger condo unit, expect a high association fee compared to the small units in the building. These fees can increase over time depending on the upkeep needed. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5878,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/How-to-find-the-ideal-home-for-starting-or-growing-family-needs-2.png" alt="buying a hone, buy a home, property, home, house, interior design" class="wp-image-5878"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Buying a house</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A house is attractive to starting and growing families. It is most often a larger place with some outdoor space for the family. It provides privacy and freedom to have the whole place for yourself. Unlike condo you do not have to worry about your neighbour with just a wall separating you. You also can decide whether to have a pets or to do major remodeling or renovating without having to constantly ask approval from the home association or building admin. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>However, a landed property costs more than a condominium. You need to take care of its upkeep, utilities and the lot area is bigger than a condo. You also have to worry about security with only guards at the subdivision gate and limited visibility to the houses in the community.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Regardless of whether you buy a condo or a house, you need to first figure out what you intend to use the property for and what  your needs are.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/10/Condo-vs-House_-Not-sure-whether-to-buy-a-condominium-or-a-house.jpg','views' => '64','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-10-08 00:45:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '501','title' => 'What to Know About a Community Before Buying a Home','slug' => 'what-to-know-about-a-community-before-buying-a-home','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Most people, when buying a home, prefers a titled lot inside a community where the family can enjoy.  The like to have  a sense of belongingness in a community where families know each other and where they feel most safe. There are a lot of things to consider before buying a house - how much more if it\'s in a community you are new to. Are you thinking of buying a home in a subdivision or within a community? Here are some of the questions you might need to ask yourself to find out more about the community before buying a home there.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5059,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Residential-Subdivision-banner-Indovance.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5059"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Is it safe and secure?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When looking for a house the number one priority should be safety and security. You want to feel safe and secured in your own home and you want to know that your family is in good hands. Make sure to ask for security measures in the community. These includes shifting and roving guards, 24/7 CCTV in the common areas, well-lit roads and exclusive residential access. These are some of the factors that make you want to buy a house in that community.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5536,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/Going-Back-to-Work-after-lifted-ECQ-Tips-to-keep-you-your-family-safe-from-Covid-19-4.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5536"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Does it have a pedestrian and is it commuter-friendly?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>One of things to look for in a neighbourhood is if it is commuter friendly. You know that you and your family will spend years living there, make sure you know that you or your children when they grow up won\'t have any problem commuting when needed. It is important that you will be able to get to work or elsewhere without having to worry how to commute. Also check if the neighbourhood roads have pedestrian lane and crossings. That way you will also feel safe from vehicles when you\'re walking in the neighbourhood.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Does it match your lifestyle?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You also need to consider if the community fits your lifestyle. If it\'s close to the school or workplace, shopping areas or lifestyle districts. You don\'t want to travel hours to get to work or to get to places you frequently go to.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6346,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/Mesaverte-2020-09-2-1024x768.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-6346"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Are there community amenities for your family to enjoy?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Check the amenities the community offers. Most communities offer lifestyle amenities like swimming pools, parks, community gym, playground and the likes. These allows you and your family to bond during the times you can not travel elsewhere. If you have kids, it would be great to buy a home with playground for them to play at and even meet new kids. You want a community where you and your family can enjoy and spend time together without having to go far from home.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5537,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/Going-Back-to-Work-after-lifted-ECQ-Tips-to-keep-you-your-family-safe-from-Covid-19-5.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5537"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Does it offer convenience?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Always check if the community not only has nice house and amenities, it should offer conveniences for the family. It should have access to the grocery shops and farmers market, near some clinics or hospitals and banks and other places. These are some of the places that are also important for the family and  to keep the home running.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/10/What-to-Know-About-a-Community-Before-Buying-a-Home.png','views' => '44','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-10-09 00:29:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '502','title' => '10 Tips to Buy Real Estate Without Breaking Your Budget','slug' => '10-tips-to-buy-real-estate-without-breaking-your-budget','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you want to buy a home, but aren’t sure if your budget can handle soaring real estate prices, we’ve got good news. There are things you can do to stretch your buying power. With the help of your real estate agent – and these 10 tips – you can become a savvy home buyer without breaking your budget.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://kmcmaggroup.com/ImageGen.ashx?image=/media/664761/investing-in-residential-real-estate-deciding-factors-when-buying-a-condominium-as-an-investment-compressor-new.jpg&amp;Compression=60" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>1. Get pre-approved for your home loan.</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This means, fill out a loan application and go through the process of securing financing. That way, when you’re ready to seriously evaluate real estate, you’ll know exactly how much home you can afford. In the Philippines, brokers/agents will usually knows how to prequalify. But if you really want to know how much is your allowable loan from your chosen lender or bank, you can have yourself pre-approved so you will know what type of house you can afford or more likely be approved by the lender.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>2. Explore creative financing options.</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>During the home loan pre-approval process, ask about ways to get creative with your financing. Low down payment options, first and second mortgage combinations and first time buyer programs might help you afford more funding. Many lenders are now offering interest-only home mortgages; just make sure you thoroughly evaluate the terms for this type of home loan. Down payment grants are also available in some instances and might be worth investigating or discussing with your realtor.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>3. Sell your existing home first.</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Although selling your existing home before finding new real estate to buy can be a little nerve wracking, any inconvenience will be offset by your ability to make an offer with cash in hand. Contingent purchases are not the best when negotiating to buy a home. Having your financing in order and your bags packed will give you the advantage in a competitive market.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>4. Look for vacant real estate.</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Perhaps a seller’s job has transferred him out of the area. Or maybe a family purchased a new home before putting their existing one on the market. In any case, a vacant home could be just the deal for a savvy home buyer, so have your realtor look for vacant property in your preferred neighborhoods. And keep in mind, the longer a house stays empty, the greater your negotiating power will be.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>5. Consider cosmetic fixers.</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you’re handy with a paintbrush, a toolset and gardening equipment, consider buying real estate in need of cosmetic fixing. Property that lacks curb appeal needs minor handiwork or the yard overhauled could end up being the home of your dreams for a price you can afford. You just need to look beyond the ho-hum to see the potential of a cosmetic fixer.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>6. Buy a home that’s a major remodel project.</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you want to live on Lake Washington, but can’t afford a $2M home mortgage, consider buying a dilapidated cottage on a fabulous lot with western exposure. In time you’ll need to gut the existing home and build from the ground up or contract significant home improvements. But in the end your property value will skyrocket. And if your carpentry and other construction skills are well-developed, you can save even more and accrue “sweat equity” during your remodel by doing much of the work yourself.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>7. Don’t discount bank foreclosures.</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>One person’s loss could be your gain if you buy real estate in foreclosure. Although the search for a decent foreclosure may take a while, your realtor should be able help. The U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (http://www.hud.gov/) can be an excellent resource for foreclosed properties. Because HUD houses are sold at market value, your best bet will be homes that need cosmetic work or even major repair.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>8. Land with a manufactured home.</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Sometimes, to buy a home on a budget, you need to look beyond convention. Even if your wish is to buy real estate, you may have to settle for a piece of property in an outlying area with a mobile or manufactured home. Discuss this option with your real estate agent and try to keep an open mind about this possibility.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>9. An older, smaller home.</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Older homes are typically priced much less than newer construction and don’t tend to create buyer bidding wars. If you can enjoy life in an older and smaller home in a neighborhood or suburb off the beaten path, this could be your ticket to real estate ownership.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>10. The cheapest house in the best neighborhood.</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You have your heart set on a specific – and expensive – neighborhood. Maybe it’s the schools that you’re interested in. Or perhaps it’s the close proximity to downtown or the waterfront. In any case, a budget-savvy buyer will look for the least expensive home for sale in the neighborhood. If you’re not in a hurry, you can even play the waiting game to see what properties come on the market. Your real estate agent can be a real asset in this case by investigating potential sellers.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Buying real estate without breaking your budget will require research and compromise. On moving day, however, you’ll have the satisfaction of knowing that your homework paid off!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/10/filipino-homes-realtor-blogger-xyza-yape.png','views' => '60','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-10-11 23:36:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '503','title' => '5 Budget-Friendly Makeover Ideas for the Small Balcony','slug' => '5-budget-friendly-makeover-ideas-for-the-small-balcony','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In this time of quarantine and stay-at-home orders, we value the time we are able to stay outside. The balcony could be the closest we can have to the \'outside world.\'  If your balcony is a place used as a storage or utility area, then perhaps it’s time for a quick makeover. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The balcony is a good source of fresh air and sunlight, but it is also one of the most unused spaces in the home. To get the most out of your balcony, consider these <strong>5 budget-friendly balcony makeover ideas</strong>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>1. Add a vertical garden</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=651896114806450640" height="1095" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Adding a vertical garden is an easy way to bring nature into your home. Embrace your "plantito/plantita" self and decorate your balcony with lush potted plants or probably some herbs and aromatics for your kitchen. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>2.  Add a cozy seating area</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=781726447804094495" height="904" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If space permits, consider adding a tiny table and a couple of chairs in your balcony. This can transform your space into a cozy nook where you can enjoy your morning coffee (or wine at nighttime).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>3. </strong> <strong>Get the floor pillows out</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=255368241349798681" height="742" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Floor cushions can also make a space cozy. It\'s a budget-friendly way to deck out your balcony with pops of colors and interesting patterns. They’re easy to wash and maintain too.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>4. Install a hammock</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=131026670395460375" height="850" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Daydream of your beach&nbsp;life, chilling in&nbsp;hammocks while at home. Transform your balcony into your own private reading nook or just a sanctuary to relax in.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>5. Switch up the lighting</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=159455643034210472" height="1000" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Lighting can affect the mood of a space. Swapping your boring bulbs to a more dramatic pendant light can give your balcony an instant makeover. A few scented candles and maybe some fairy lights, and you’re all set for a relaxing evening outside.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em><strong>READ:  </strong></em><a href="http://localhost:3001/creative-ideas-for-your-balcony/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Creative Ideas for Your Balcony</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/10/filipino-homes-blog-post-cover-5-1.png','views' => '43','category_id' => '28','published_at' => '2020-10-13 00:28:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '504','title' => 'Housing Developers urges BIR to suspend VAT on low-cost housing projects','slug' => 'housing-developers-urges-bir-to-suspend-vat-on-low-cost-housing-projects','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In light of the Covid crisis, the housing and real estate developers are urging the office of Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR) to consider the suspension on  the imposition of the value added tax (VAT) on low-cost housings that will take effect on 2020.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Chamber of Real Estate and Builders’ Associations Inc. (CREBA) urged the BIR to issue a ruling suspending the imposition of VAT on low-cost housing units immediately as the three-year reprieve under the Tax Reform for Acceleration and Inclusion (TRAIN) law for low-cost housing ends by December 2020. Under this TRAIN law, homebuyers of P1.9 million-worth residential lots and P3.2 million-worth house and lot units are exempted to pay VAT. By the start of next year, only those worth P2 million and below would be VAT-exempt.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Chamber of Real Estate and Builders’ Associations Inc. (CREBA) urged the BIR to issue a ruling its suspension with Filipino homebuyers who are struggling to purchase their homes due to the crisis in mind.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>According to CREBA, there is a 6.57 million units housing backlog and that there is an increasing by 300,000 units per year gap between supply and demand.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Charlie Gorayeb</strong>, <em>CREBA National Chairman</em>, said that imposing VAT on low-cost housing would make the prices go up and making it hard for Filipinos homebuyers to purchase their desired homes. <em>“Real estate developers have no choice but to fully pass on VAT to homebuyers. When obtained through a long-term loan, the 12 percent VAT of about P360,000 for a P3.2 million home actually translates to P1 million over a 30-year mortgage life,”</em> he said. Gorayeb said that to make it necessary for Filipino families to have decent homes, there should be a fixed, low-interest long-term housing loans from the government.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Noel Cariño</strong>, <em>CREBA National President</em>, added that these additional taxes that will be collected by the government from housing will not help the slowdown of the real estate sector during this crisis. “<em>But with housing being globally-recognized for its economic multiplier effects, a robust housing industry will be a primary catalyst for economic recovery to help the entire country heal as one,</em>” he said.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/10/Housing-Developers-urges-BIR-to-suspend-VAT-on-low-cost-housing-projects.png','views' => '41','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2020-10-14 00:38:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '505','title' => 'Where Should We Live? Checklist on Choosing a Good Neighborhood','slug' => 'checklist-on-choosing-a-good-neighborhood','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Many homeowners would agree that finding a good neighborhood is as important as choosing a home itself. Well, it’s pretty understandable though. Who would want to live in a noisy, troublesome neighbourhood? Considering you’d be living with them for the rest of your life, so it’s better to think the way forward before everything messes up.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here’s a quick checklist to consider:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6427,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/Factors-to-Consider-When-Choosing-a-Good-Neighborhood.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-6427"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#1 Crime rates&nbsp;</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Safety should be your top priority when choosing a neighborhood. Living in a neighborhood with a low crime rate is not only safer, but can help keep property values afloat in the years to come.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you’ve watched the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ep8iKiQNSrY"><em>Netflix film American Murder: The Family Next Door</em></a><em>, </em>then that is a chilling reminder that brutal crimes can happen in real life too.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>How to check:</em> Do some research online and offline. Interview the people around or ask some friends what they know about the place. Social media is a good place to get more information too! But most importantly, work with real estate agents you can trust or someone a family you can vouch for. Ask for honest opinions whether it’s really safe or not.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#2 Proximity to workplace</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Next is location. Where you work in relation to where you live is also an important factor to consider. How far is the commute from home to your workplace? Will you commit to a long travel time for work? If not, be sure to look into public transportation options that are in close proximity.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>How to check</em>: Visit the place yourself before sealing the deal. Instead of just asking people around, test out your commute at the time of day you typically go to work.&nbsp; Although choosing the right neighborhood takes some legwork, it\'s important to choose a place to live where you want to come home every night.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#3 School quality</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Even if you don’t have a child, choosing a community with good schools can be a smart investment. Because homes that are situated near high quality schools generally have higher property values and huge resale potential. In fact, many home buyers are willing to forgo certain home amenities just to have access to quality schools.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>How to check:</em> Create a checklist of your <em>negotiables and non-negotiables</em> (i.e school qualities or values) that are important to you and your child\'s education. Once you\'ve narrowed down your lists, then ask any of your network to get insights. Parents, perhaps?&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#4&nbsp; Quality of Community Services Around</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When choosing a neighborhood, the quality of the community\'s services (i.e. police and fire protection, department stores, education and health care) is something that you may give a lot of thought to. Is the neighborhood close to hospitals, supermarkets, church, public transportation, and other necessities of urban living? Make sure to consider choosing a location that’s close to where you will be running a majority of your errands.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: <a href="http://localhost:3001/what-to-look-for-when-condo-hunting-for-your-growing-family/">What To Look for When Condo Hunting for Your Growing Family</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#5&nbsp; Character of the community</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Lastly, give yourself and your kids a headstart in life by surrounding them with people who have the same values and aspirations as your family. You can get a good sense of the community surrounding simply by talking to them and asking what they like or proud of the community. There’s nothing that beats a neighborhood who takes pride in their community.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/10/Checklist-on-Choosing-a-Good-Neighborhood-for-Your-Family.jpg','views' => '52','category_id' => '13','published_at' => '2020-10-15 00:24:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '506','title' => 'Home Staging Tips & Tricks to Sell Your Home Fast','slug' => 'home-staging-tips-tricks-to-sell-your-home-fast','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Planning to sell your home? Selling a home can be tricky with a lot considerations to have if you want to sell it fast and at a good price. You do not have to do a major renovation to increase the price of the home if you do not have budget for it. You can, however, style and stage it well to make it easier for potential homebuyers to imagine themselves living in the house. Here are some home stage tips and tricks to sell your home fast:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6279,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/Filipino-Homes-Homes-Selling-a-Home-Buying-a-Home-Homebuyer.png" alt="home, house, interior design" class="wp-image-6279"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Boost the outdoor appeal</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Most people drive by or check out the property from the outside before actually setting an appointment for a home tour or viewing. It is best be prepared by cleaning the driveway and trimming bushes in the garden. Make sure your gate looks good and have it repainted it needed. Clean the sidewalk or the outside of your fence.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Clean &amp; declutter your home</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you\'re really serious about staging your home, you have to make it look like it came from a magazine. You need to tidy up your personal belongings and make sure that clutter must go. Cleaning the home also includes making sure there are no lingering smoke or pet odors as well. A clean and tiny home will allow them to visualize how to make the house their own and imagine themselves living there.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6056,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Filipino-Homes-Philippines-5.png" alt="home, house, interior design" class="wp-image-6056"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Take a good look at your floors.&nbsp;</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The well-maintained floor is a good indicator of a well-kept home. Check out your floors if there is the need for tile tough-up if there\'s a missing one. The floors is a huge thing because having to redo the floors will be costly for the new homeowners. So better you fixed a missing tile than having potential homebuyers offering a much lower rate if not walk away from buying your home.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Rearrange your furniture</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Staging a home is making it look inviting. So if you must, rearrange the furniture to suit a better layout for the potential homebuyer. If gives the room a fresh look and also making it appealing to the homebuyer.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6277,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/Filipino-Homes-Homes-Buying-a-Home.png" alt="home, house, interior design" class="wp-image-6277"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Choose sophisticated neutral colors</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It is not wise to experiment with colours when staging your home. Most people love colour but what they like may not match what your home has. It is all better to go neutral when staging. It makes the room airy and clean looking. It also gives a somewhat blank canvas for the potential homebuyer to imagine how he/she likes the room to turn out. A neutral palette is also a a top buying factor for those people who are not looking into remodeling or renovating the house when the buy it. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/10/Home-Staging-Tips-Tricks-to-Sell-Your-Home-Fast.png','views' => '46','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-10-16 00:35:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '507','title' => 'Investing in Real Estate in Your 20s: Possible or not?','slug' => 'investing-in-real-estate-in-your-20s-possible-or-not','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Investing in real estate in your early 20s? What? That’s insane!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This may sound a little absurd, but <a href="http://localhost:3001/why-you-should-buy-and-invest-in-real-estate-property/">investing and making money in real estate</a> in your 20s is not only possible but also one of the wisest decisions you can make for your financial future. In fact, most real estate investors often wish they could have started earlier.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Most young people would also agree that the idea of investing during this time may seem not realistic (if not impossible). Youth at their 20s view real estate investments as something that should be undertaken only when they’re older. Life on this stage should be about finding a good job, building a career, having fun and definitely not about ending it. Plus given the circumstances that the world is going through this year, is it still good to invest in real estate for young people.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Here’s Why You Should Start Real Estate Investing in Your 20s&nbsp;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>First of all, you’re never too young (or old) to invest. The fact is, investing early helps you build an early safety net. It appears prudent now to have multiple streams of passive income that can be of assistance in times when things aren’t so clear. Second, starting early allows you to have more time to build your wealth. It gives you more time to learn, grow, and navigate through the waves of real estate investment. And third, investing in real estate is actually not about making money alone. You will also learn other life skills which will be very helpful to you throughout your life.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>Related: <a href="http://localhost:3001/why-gen-z-should-start-planning-investment-now/">Why Gen Z should start planning investment now</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"left","id":6422,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="alignleft size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/How-to-Start-Investing-in-Real-Estate-while-Youre-Young.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-6422"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>How to Start Property Investing in Your 20s [Filipino Homes]</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>Start Small</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Many newbie real estate investors get overexcited and try to shoot for the stars on their first investment. It is important to start simple and small and gradually grow your real estate portfolio so that you don’t end up regretting and discouraging yourself.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>Come up with a long-term plan</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Developing a long-term plan for real estate is very important. Because having a vision is what keeps you from straying too far from a certain path. More importantly, you must be aware that you can’t reap the benefits of real estate investing by tomorrow. Time is your friend in real estate investing and it’s what paves the road to your future financial security.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>Educate yourself through those who’ve done it</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Sometimes, when you are young, your focus is often divided to do many things. But in order to be a successful property investor, you must learn to find the true value of what you’re doing by <a href="http://localhost:3001/successful-real-estate-investor-tips/">learning from the mistakes of expert real estate investors</a>. Simply put, you can avoid mistakes at a fraction of the cost by doing so. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can also enrol yourself at FIRE or the <a href="http://realestatetraining.ph/">Filipinohomes Institute of Real Estate</a>, a program created by Filipino Homes that aids in developing the skills and talents of a real estate practitioners through various online courses.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>Learn to Save</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Some investors would say don’t save money, the money you save will not work for you and your money will not increase in value from what you saved. Well, that’s partly true. But <a href="http://localhost:3001/5-money-saving-tips-for-gen-z/">learning how to save is the foundation of all financial success</a> especially in real estate investing. Life is uncertain, thus saving money is very important.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>Pay your dues and be responsible with your credit</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is also a MUST for every investor. If you wish to take a start investing and you have a terrible credit score, chances are you’re going to get denied or compromised. To <a href="http://localhost:3001/tips-to-get-you-in-good-financial-shape-to-buy-your-dream-home/">maintain a clean credit history</a>, you need to be responsible with your bills and loans. Make sure to pay on time! OR maybe this time forward, try to motivate yourself to downgrade your lifestyle even if it means turning your back on some luxuries from time to time.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>Start networking</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Networking is one of the most significant aspects of investing in real estate. Whether you are just starting out or already in business, <a href="http://localhost:3001/tips-for-millennials-who-want-to-invest-in-real-estate/">knowing the right people is one trick in the book that you should definitely do</a>. You can begin this journey by attending local events like workshops, seminars, and open house events to meet with agents, developers and other investors. With the technology we have nowadays, social media has also become one of the most convenient methods of networking.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4><strong>Answer: Yes. Investing while you’re young can offer you big gains in the future.</strong></h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Cliche as it may sound but, <em>“The best time to buy a home is always five years ago.”</em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you’re interested to know more, we’ve compiled some useful tips and guides about <a href="http://localhost:3001/?s=money">personal finance</a>, <a href="http://localhost:3001/category/business/">business</a>, and <a href="http://localhost:3001/category/property-investing/">property investing</a>. We hope that these tips will take you far!&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You may also check out the <a href="https://filipinohomes.com/agents">top real estate agents in the Philippines</a> and get some professional real estate advice and direction.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/10/Filipino-Homes.jpg','views' => '56','category_id' => '15','published_at' => '2020-10-17 00:41:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '508','title' => 'Cerise Tower Breaks Ground','slug' => 'cerise-tower-breaks-ground','content' => '<!-- wp:image {"id":6490,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/121635289_2908037909461465_7086767403880472324_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-6490"/><figcaption>📸: <a href="https://www.facebook.com/alejandro.manalac1?__cft__[0]=AZXGCG75Jk7YbPutiImNFqXCHIqEKGD1m77_-LJsSxJkkKoelkCFmj-ucUwxhQ3GSbM52wy1464amq136-HdVdfAi65UPoGErsAm8PW2Bi877jAQvvi_4DwbWyQwCscG6X4&amp;__tn__=-UC*F">Alejandro Manalac</a> / HAVITAS Developments</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Cerise Tower</strong> broke ground on October 15, 2020, marking the start of construction of this project in the Southwoods City, Laguna. This residential &amp; office development&nbsp;is owned by Malveda Properties and Development Corporation and managed by <a href="https://www.facebook.com/HavitasDevelopments" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">HAVITAS Developments</a>. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6491,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/121647711_2720254704913064_4478118792912501881_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-6491"/><figcaption>📸: <a href="https://www.facebook.com/markchristopherreyes0001?__cft__[0]=AZURC9WkH0HEZ_TN9VrxXWjtEcbX7XVoqTy_dKiX6SSFeEGi9EN0YG0APZUHMWRCzZB_6F5ITd_v9-4y1USLk7p1ngvmGNZ_rvARk2UH2HWjc4RCh3wL_7ZYyKzcHxh7mMM&amp;__tn__=-UC*F">Mark Reyes</a></figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Cerise Tower </strong>is strategically located 2 blocks from a hospital, a 5-minute walk to the mall, a 5-minute drive to the Collegio San Agustin-Biñan, and is less than 10 minutes away from the world-class Southwoods Golf Course. This will be managed by one of the biggest brands in the world when it comes to serviced apartments.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This low-density development (with less than a hundred units) is "new normal" ready, with a lot of open spaces, in a low-pollution environment, and walkable to essential destinations.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Keep posted for more information about Cerise Tower. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

