<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/10/filipino-homes-blog-post-cover-9.png','views' => '51','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2020-10-18 08:13:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '509','title' => '6 Lead Generation Tips and Tricks for New Real Estate Agents','slug' => '6-lead-generation-tips-and-tricks-for-new-real-estate-agents','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>New agent? Here are six simple lead generation tips that can help you get unlimited leads.</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Have you ever thought, <em>“What if I don’t have the right market to sell properties? What if I ran out of people to talk to? Would I still be able to get sales?”</em>&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>To tell you honestly, it’s not easy to make marketing work in real estate now, as most agents follow the same online strategy that makes it harder for new agents to stand out. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>But <strong>don’t let this discourage you</strong>. In fact, there are ways you can do to generate quality leads by simply using social media. Even if you’re just new in the industry and you don’t have a strong community following or a network of strategic partners, these simple lead generation tips can help you flood your inbox with inquiries.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em>Related: </em><a href="http://localhost:3001/4-effective-ways-to-sell-your-property-listing-tips-for-real-estate-agents/"><em>4 Effective Ways To Sell Your Property Listing: Tips For Real Estate Agents</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>6 Simple Ways To Do Real Estate Lead Generation</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":6448,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/6-Ways-To-Do-Real-Estate-Lead-Generation-1024x1024.jpg" alt="real estate lead gen" class="wp-image-6448"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Tip #1 Create a Professional Facebook Account&nbsp;</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As a new agent, you need to go where people spend so much of their time online and on social media. And according to Statista, <a href="https://www.statista.com/statistics/1127983/philippines-leading-social-media-platforms/#:~:text=As%20of%20the%20third%20quarter,hours%20online%20on%20social%20media.&amp;text=In%202020%2C%20Facebook\'s%20user%20population%20was%20over%20800%20million%20in%20Asia.">Facebook is the most popular social media platform in the Philippines</a> where most Filipinos spent nearly four hours online.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Your Facebook profile (in the world of business) is already considered as your online business card. Have you noticed that <em>before people accept you as a friend, a lot of them scroll through your profile before deciding to accept your friend request</em>? So make sure your online business card looks neat and professional.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6441,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/6-Simple-Lead-Generation-Tips-Tricks-for-New-Real-Estate-Agents-1-1024x576.jpg" alt="6 Simple Lead Generation  Tips &amp; Tricks for New Real Estate Agents" class="wp-image-6441"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Facebook Profile Essentials</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>Profile Picture: </em><strong>Must be on high-quality</strong> with a clean background.<br><em>Cover Photo:</em> <strong>Must leave an impression</strong> (e.g. Corporation name).&nbsp;Remember that this is the biggest portion that people will see first.&nbsp;<br><em>Bio: </em><strong>2-3 statements that define you</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Examples:<ul><li>Licensed Real Estate Agent</li><li>Business Coach</li><li>Entrepreneur</li><li>Online Marketer</li><li>etc.</li></ul></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Tip #2 Learn to Qualify, Add and Compliment</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>An effective formula that online marketers have been using now is the “qualify-add-compliment.” But actually, the rule is pretty simple. The first step is to qualify them as a lead based on the niche you are looking for. Second is to add them as your friend on your Facebook account. And lastly is to compliment leads so you can start a conversation. But make sure to compliment them once they add you back (not before they accept your friend request). Basically, think of it like virtual farming, where the ultimate goal is to build your name recognition as well as help you capture potential property buyer and seller leads.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Tip: It is always a great idea to start off with a compliment so you can say something like:&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:verse {"textAlign":"center"} -->
<pre class="wp-block-verse has-text-align-center"><em>“Hey ______! Glad to finally connect. Just touching base with fellow property enthusiasts in this account. Awesome profile btw!”</em></pre>
<!-- /wp:verse -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If they are responsive, take the initiative to reach out and spark a conversation. But if not, that’s fine since you will want to exert your energy conversing only to those people who are positive and responsive. Just be friendly and remember that your purpose is to genuinely connect with these people.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Tip #3 Join Facebook Groups</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Now you may wonder <em>where do these leads come from?</em> To tell you the truth, online places like Facebook groups are the best networks where you can always find leads and never run out of people to talk to. So what you have to do is look for real estate niche-specific Facebook groups and go through as many members as possible. Reason is you won’t waste your time on groups with the least number of people because most likely they’re inactive.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6446,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/6-Simple-Lead-Generation-Tips-Tricks-for-New-Real-Estate-Agents-2-1024x576.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-6446"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Tip #4 Add your property list on Marketplaces</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>One amazing feature of Facebook you can take advantage with is the <a href="https://www.facebook.com/marketplace/"><strong><em>marketplace</em></strong></a><strong><em>. </em></strong>This page is specifically meant for you to put up listings. You can directly post about your property and get interested leads right into your inbox. Furthermore, if you happen to live in metro cities like Manila, Cebu, Davao or Cagayan de Oro, you must have come across numerous groups like “Properties for Sale in Cagayan de Oro”. These are also meant to advertise properties located in the area that are up for rent or lease. So feel free to join these local marketplaces and post your property.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Tip #5 Explore real estate events and tradeshows</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There are a number of <a href="http://localhost:3001/category/events/">virtual real estate events and tradeshows</a> in the country happening almost every month. You can attend these online events as it is a wonderful place to get quality leads and increase your list. And amazingly, you can even choose to exhibit your property listings at these events to attract potential buyers.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Tip #6 Utilize Paid Advertising</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Last option would be using paid ads. The benefit of content boosting or ads is to streamline your lead acquisition process. Using social media ads (Facebook for example) can help you reach quality leads based on their interests, behaviors and demographics. In addition, you can geotarget people based on their location which helps you when you want to focus on the area you\'re farming.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>Related posts:</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/10-social-media-post-ideas-for-real-estate-agents/">10 Social Media Post Ideas for Real Estate Agents</a></li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/5-tips-for-real-estate-agents-on-how-to-stay-productive-during-community-quarantine/">5 Tips for Real Estate Agents on How to Stay Productive during Community Quarantine</a></li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/how-to-be-a-prc-accredited-real-estate-salesperson/">How to be a PRC-accredited Real Estate Salesperson</a></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/10/6-Simple-Lead-Generation-Tips-Tricks-for-New-Real-Estate-Agents.jpg','views' => '46','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-10-19 00:25:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '510','title' => 'Filipino Homes CEO Anthony Leuterio shares about "Marketing in the New Normal" on SHDA Kapihan','slug' => 'filipino-homes-ceo-anthony-leuterio-shares-about-marketing-in-the-new-normal-on-shda-kapihan','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes founder and CEO Anthony Leuterio presented during SHDA Kapihan via Zoom Meeting on <em>Sales and Marketing in the New Normal: Pivoting onto Digital Platforms</em> last September 30, 2020. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[6497,6507]} -->
<figure class="wp-block-gallery columns-2 is-cropped"><ul class="blocks-gallery-grid"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/122005506_10157924685093318_5331424644978054468_n-1.jpg" alt="" data-id="6497" class="wp-image-6497"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/121815747_10157924685133318_8616336770216372024_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="6507" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/121815747_10157924685133318_8616336770216372024_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=6507" class="wp-image-6507"/></figure></li></ul></figure>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leuterio shared about the trends in the real estate industry as we move towards the new normal. He talked about how Filipino Homes utilizes technology and innovation to be digitally ready. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6498,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/image-10-1024x576.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6498"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>Mr. Ken Stern</em> of Lamudi Philippines was also a speaker for the event. Also present were the reactors, <em>Mr. Franco Soberano</em> of Cebu Land Masters and <em>Mr. Cesar Wee</em> of Wee Community Developers Inc. The kapihan session was hosted by <em>Mr. Rene "RJ" Ledesma Jr.</em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In case you missed this SHDA Kapihan session, you can watch it here: </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<center><iframe src="https://www.facebook.com/plugins/video.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Fshdaph%2Fvideos%2F613481315993566%2F&amp;show_text=0&amp;width=560" width="560" height="315" style="border:none;overflow:hidden" scrolling="no" frameborder="0" allowtransparency="true" allowfullscreen="true"></iframe></center>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>About Subdivision and Housing Developers Association</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"left","id":6503,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="alignleft size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/image-12.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6503"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With over 160 members from chapters in Luzon, Visayas, and Mindanao, the Subdivision and Housing Developers Association (SHDA) is the major and leading organization of housing developers in the Philippines. SHDA is at the forefront in promoting and safeguarding the interests of its members through continued coordination and linkages with government agencies and allied professionals. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Among its most significant contributions to the industry are the group’s efforts in amending Sec. 20 of Republic Act No. 7279, deemed a game changer in addressing urban homelessness as it introduced a new category, which is socialized condominiums. The amended Sec. 20 introduced incentives “to encourage greater private sector participation in socialized housing and further reduce the cost of housing units for the benefit of the underprivileged and homeless.”</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/10/filipino-homes-blog-post-cover-10.png','views' => '53','category_id' => '14','published_at' => '2020-10-19 13:40:41','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '511','title' => '13 Superstitions That Are Considered Bad Luck to Filipino Homes','slug' => '13-superstitions-that-are-considered-bad-luck-to-filipino-homes','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Let’s admit it. No matter how modern or civilized we consider ourselves to be, <strong>superstitions (or <em>pamahiin</em>)</strong> are part of our day to day lives. From the moment of birth, adulthood, to death and even to afterlife, many of us still believe in these things even though the Philippines is known to be a religious nation.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Most <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superstition#:~:text=A%20superstition%20is%20%22a%20belief,or%20God%20resulting%20from%20superstition.%22">superstitions exist for thousands of years</a>. It extends beyond our belief in supernatural forces whether it be on things, numbers, life, ideas, and imaginations. But what really stands out among superstitions is when it comes to building our homes. As Filipinos, we make sure that we follow and adhere to these things which according to our ancestors will give prosperity and safety for us.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em><strong>Question</strong>: Do you believe them? </em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Well, whether you’re superstitious or not, knowing these won’t hurt you anyway. Since <em>Halloween </em>is almost upon us, <strong>let’s explore some of the superstitions that are considered bad luck to Filipino Homes</strong>. And please let us know in the comment section if we missed anything. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em>Related: </em><a href="http://localhost:3001/feng-shui-moving-new-house/"><em>Feng Shui for Moving into a New House</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/buemjnznPC4edeHn5HgytOwTuXHf5Zd92Gr_ef79FrJXT6seUeCWrv96FpEEfkM79Ozz4EbwMTAWrzuEORQ0ZIcGlSdJpyLUy5v5Pw8KJIV0oU53qaI2Ma6tQmKSGU8vssFODOa4" alt="filipino superstitions" /></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Sweeping at night</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is probably the most common superstition among all. Many of us still believe that sweeping the floor with a broom at night will bring bad luck. Although there’s no logical explanation for this, many Filipinos still believe that this can spur away good blessings. You can sweep anytime during the day, but not after sunset.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Staircases</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Staircases should have an even number of steps and be counted in a series of threes called “<em>oro, plata, mata”</em> which literally translates to “<em>gold, silver, death</em>.” This is because many Filipinos will go to great lengths to avoid ending in <em>mata (death) </em>which denotes bad luck. Moreover,&nbsp; having a 13-steps staircase is not advisable, as 13 is believed to be the number of the devil or <em>bilang Hudas</em>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Lighting a Trio of Candles</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The superstition of lighting three candles comes from the belief that the person who stands closest to the shortest candle will be the first to die. There is also a belief that a couple whose candle goes out first during a wedding will be the first couple to die.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Butterflies</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A Black Butterfly inside the house is believed to bring death to the household. Meanwhile, if a Brown butterfly comes in, that’s your dead loved one.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Wall Clock &amp; Bed Shouldn’t Face the Door</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Our lolo and lolas keep telling us that the home’s wall clock and bed should not face the door’s entry. Or else, bad spirits or the “<em>kamatayan</em>” will come knocking in.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>House Remodelling</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Two storey houses that are remodeled into a one-storey structure will shorten the lives of the occupants.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Home Mirrors</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The legend tells that the glass mirror facing the bed is bad luck because it can steal your soul. Also, a mirror placed on the wall facing the main door of a house will deflect good luck that enters the house.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Saying “Tabi-tabi po”</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Whenever you pass through an unfamiliar area of an abandoned place, never forget to say “<em>tabi-tabi po” </em>or else elementals and demons might play and come with you at home.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Whistling indoors</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>People who whistle indoors are said to be whistling for the devil or whistling up a storm. So, best to avoid that.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>The Kitchen&nbsp;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Kitchen shouldn\'t be next to the toilet or septic tank. This is believed to bring illness to the family members.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Wake/Funeral Mirrors</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If a wake is being held at home, it is recommended that all mirrors should be covered with cloth because the <em>dead </em>might try to show themselves in those mirrors. You must also avoid looking at yourself in the mirror and combing your hair during this time, as these are bad luck.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Avoid the Group of 3’s in Pictures</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Grouping yourselves in sets of 3s (especially in pictures) is considered bad luck. Many Filipinos believe that the one in the middle might <em>actually </em>die.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Bringing Home Food from Funeral</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>While it’s customary to offer food to fellow mourners at Filipino funerals, it’s also believed that any food brought in to the wake should not be taken out of it. You can only bring the food after the <em>9th day of novena</em> or what we call “<em>pagsisiyam</em>” or “<em>tapos</em>” in Cebuano. Visitors who hoard proffered snacks during wakes are frowned upon.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Did we miss anything? Feel free to share home-related superstitions you know in the comment section.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Are you looking for a new home? Contact any <a href="https://filipinohomes.com/agents">Filipino Home’s top real estate agents (that might be residing near you) now</a> and get some professional real estate advice and direction.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/10/What-to-Know-About-a-Community-Before-Buying-a-Home-768x427-1.png','views' => '222','category_id' => '10','published_at' => '2020-10-20 13:32:42','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '512','title' => 'How to Know You\'re Buying a Well-Made Condo','slug' => 'how-to-know-youre-buying-a-well-made-condo','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Planning to buy a condo but not sure how to know if the one you\'re looking at is well-made? It can be a headache to find that the condo you like did not turn out the way you expected it to. Some real estate ads can be misleading so it is best that you know how to spot a well-made condo when you see it.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6283,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/Filipino-Homes-Homes-Selling-a-Home.png" alt="home, house, interior design" class="wp-image-6283"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Well-thought of home layout and High quality finishing</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Whether you are looking for a studio apartment, a multiple bedroom unit, a well-made condo should have a good layout already. It should be planned and built with the homeowners in mind and how they would probably use the space. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Most condo come in and delivered to homeowners as unfurnished. Make sure to be mindful of the finishings used and how it is done. A great condo not only uses aesthetically pleasing finishing and filler but will also use high-quality materials. That way you do not have to remove or redo the finishing when you move in and you will be assured that it will last you years.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5928,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/etienne-girardet-sgYamIzhAhg-unsplash-1024x678.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5928"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Structurally safe and <strong>professionally designed</strong> interiors</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It is important to look at the structural safety of a condo before considering buying a unit there. A well-made condo does not have loose electrical wirings, flood-free and designed with safety in mind. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>High-end condos are professionally designed by a team of interior designers. They not only design the common areas like the lobbies and amenities but each unit are designed to fit the over all theme of the condo. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5770,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/nathan-fertig-FBXuXp57eM0-unsplash-1024x683.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5770"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Good lighting &amp; ventilation</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can tell that a condo is well-made when it has proper lighting and good ventilation. Good quality condos are designed and built with light and air wells so the units will not feel stuffy. This is also a good way to attract potential homeowners.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>Built by reputable developer </strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you\'re planning to buy a condo, make sure you know the developer behind and the quality of work they do. People you know who live or purchase a property from the same developer can vouch on how their properties have turned out and aged. Details like how the soundproofing, insulation, even plumbing and exhaust pipings are very minute and small details that a good developer will not ignore.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5924,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/floor-plan-1474454_1280-1024x678.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5924"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>Lifestyle amenities to choose from</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It should also have the future homeowners lifestyle in mind. These reflects in the amenities they offer, such as gym, swimming pools, playgrounds, pet grounds, or open gardens, etc. You can also see if these amenities are maintained and managed well and if the current homeowners are enjoying these.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Well-managed property</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Some condos rules for all residents in the condominium and it can be a headache if you\'re dealing with property management services that are difficult to work with. You can tell that a good condo is well-managed when you check the surroundings and how it it is maintained.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/10/How-to-Know-Youre-Buying-a-Well-Made-Condo.png','views' => '58','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-10-21 01:44:15','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '513','title' => 'Metro Manila Residential Property Market Report [1H 2020] and What This Means For You','slug' => 'metro-manila-residential-property-market-report-1h-2020-and-what-this-means-for-you','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Jones Lang LaSalle (JLL), the country\'s leading real estate and investment management firm, has released the <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="Philippine Property Market Report (opens in a new tab)" href="https://www.jll.com.ph/en/trends-and-insights/research/1h19-philippine-property-market-overview" target="_blank">Philippine Property Market Overview</a> for the first half of 2020.  The comprehensive report highlights key movements and updates in the office, residential, retail, and hospitality sectors of the real estate market in the country. This blog post focuses on the <strong>state of the residential property market in Metro Manila.</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6462,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/image-1024x575.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6462"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Residential<strong> Property Market</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong><em>Supply</em></strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>More than 8,000 units were added to Metro Manila\'s residential supply in the first half of 2020, with only 1.3% completed. With the extension in the community quarantine and halt in construction activities, 80% of the second half of the year pipeline is more likely to slip to 2021. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6463,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/image-1-1024x577.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6463"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Of the 394,600 existing residential supply, top districts maintain their share, with 50% of 1H20 completions concentrated in subdistricts of Makati City and Taguig City, and fringes of Quezon City.  Pasay City is expected to have the second-largest share to total supply pipeline within the next three years, with the completion of projects in SM MoA Complex.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6464,"className":"size-large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/image-2-1024x571.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6464"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong><em>Demand</em></strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Metro Manila vacancy rate almost doubled to 6.7% in 2Q20 against 3.5% in 1Q20. It was 2% in 2Q19.  This is primarily contributed by higher occupancy reductions in the cities of Makati, Taguig, and Quezon.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6465,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/image-3-1024x571.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6465"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Lease Market</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":5} -->
<h5>Demand Drivers</h5>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The leasing market for upper mid to luxury developments source demand from corporate housing needs of expatriate employees who were not reassigned and frontliners and BPO employees for secondary or halfway homes located near their workplace.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":5} -->
<h5>Rent Prices</h5>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Average Metro Manila residential rent reached a double-digit decline of 14.9% q-o-q to PHP 41,000/month as leasing activities continued to weaken with the prolonged community quarantine.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The cities of Taguig (ranging from Php13,000 to Php220,000 per month) and Makati (Php20,000 to Php180,000 monthly) continue to have the highest average rents across districts.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>Sale Market</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":5} -->
<h5>Residential Sales</h5>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In terms of selling, the average cumulative sales rate of ready-for-occupancy developments in Metro Manila reached 99.7% as of 2Q20, translating to a q-o-q net take-up of 29 units during the period.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Meanwhile, the pre-selling market experienced a slowdown in 2Q20. The average cumulative sales rate of pipeline developments recorded a lower level  at 94.2%, translating to a negative q-o-q net take-up of about 4,000 units.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":5} -->
<h5>Demand Drivers </h5>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Local high-net-worth investors or affluent families and/or corporate executives who buy for investment remain to be the major demand contributors for upper-mid to luxury developments.&nbsp;Upper middle-class who take advantage with the flexible terms to purchase units of typically upper-midscale residential condominiums also drive the residential sale market.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":5} -->
<h5>Selling Prices</h5>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The average selling price of ready-for-occupancy developments experienced a flat q-o-q growth at PHP 180,300/sqm, but the average selling price of pipeline developments started to dip by 0.8% q-o-q to PHP 205,200/sqm due to weaker pre-selling market performance.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>What This Means For You</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The prolonged community quarantine has further weakened the residential condominium lease and preselling markets of midscale to luxury segments, despite the landlord’s openness for term negotiations to improve takeup performance.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The market remains optimistic to revive demand. There is greater accessibility of residential real estate in the country. In response to the ongoing crisis, several property developers have introduced financial programs to boost the buying power of the market by offering more flexible terms and discount promos.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Likewise, the government has stepped up its efforts to make property buying easier.&nbsp;Pag-IBIG launched promo rates for housing loans in July, which will be available until the end of the year. Members can secure a special low-interest rate of 4.985 percent per annum under the one-year repricing period and a 5.375 percent per annum under the three-year repricing.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you are looking for opportunities to increase your passive income, invest in a condominium, and make it a self-liquidating asset, talk to a <a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="real estate provider (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/what-are-the-different-real-estate-professionals/" target="_blank">professional real estate service provider</a> and assess your options.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Related Articles</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Learn more about property investing. Read more:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="Why Invest In Real Estate Property (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/why-invest-in-real-estate-property/" target="_blank">Why Invest In Real Estate Property</a></li><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="10 Projects in Manila worth investing (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/10-projects-in-manila-worth-investing/" target="_blank">10 Projects in Manila worth investing</a></li><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="Is It Better to Hire a Property Manager or Manage My Rental Property Myself? (opens in a new tab)" href="http://localhost:3001/is-it-better-to-hire-a-property-manager-or-manage-my-rental-property-myself/" target="_blank">Is It Better to Hire a Property Manager or Manage My Rental Property Myself?</a></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Full report: <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.jll.com.ph/en/trends-and-insights/research/philippine-property-market-overview-1h20" target="_blank"> https://www.jll.com.ph/en/trends-and-insights/research/philippine-property-market-overview-1h20</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
