  array('id' => '520','title' => '7 Filipino Youtube Channels to learn Home Design and Renovating Tricks','slug' => '7-filipino-youtube-channels-to-learn-home-design-and-renovating-tricks','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you enjoy watching home design Youtube videos, budget home makeovers, DIY decors, or anything related to <a href="http://localhost:3001/category/home-renovation">home renovations</a>, then these Filipino YouTubers are definitely the perfect people to follow!&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In today’s digital era, online video platforms such as Youtube have become home to the world’s up-and-coming influencers and vloggers. As easy as one-two-three, you only need to type out whatever question you have in mind, and voila! You have a myriad of answers and recommendations.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So it’s no wonder why <a href="https://www.statista.com/statistics/259477/hours-of-video-uploaded-to-youtube-every-minute/">almost 5 billion videos are watched on YouTube every single day</a> --where YouTube gets over 30 million visitors per day. Insane right? If you’re interested to know about <a href="http://localhost:3001/category/tips-guides/">home redecorations and makeovers</a>, then hit the subscribe button of these awesome Filipino Youtubers and make sure to have your notepad with you.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6543,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/7-Filipino-Youtubers-to-learn-Home-Design-Makeovers-and-Renovating-Tricks-1024x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-6543"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>#1 Elle Uy Décor</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:group -->
<div class="wp-block-group"><div class="wp-block-group__inner-container"></div></div>
<!-- /wp:group -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Elle Uy is probably one of the most followed Pinoy home stylists on Youtube now. Elle is an Interior Designer Decorator based in Manila. She does home furnishing, budget room makeover, redecorating, DIYs and the results are always amazing!&nbsp;Check the video below how she redecorated Baninay Bautista’s condo unit.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:core-embed/youtube {"url":"https://youtu.be/Jxx9CjfV-iw","type":"video","providerNameSlug":"youtube","align":"center","className":"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-embed-youtube aligncenter wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
https://youtu.be/Jxx9CjfV-iw
</div></figure>
<!-- /wp:core-embed/youtube -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>#2 Karlo Marko</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This former Overseas Filipino Worker (OFW) from Singapore found his other passion which is motivational speaking and content creation. <a href="https://architectkarlo.wixsite.com/portfolio">Arch. Karlo Marko Aboganda</a> is an architecture professional who has a strong passion and appreciation in architecture, the details and aesthetics.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:core-embed/youtube {"url":"https://youtu.be/NMnPj6sO-w4","type":"video","providerNameSlug":"youtube","align":"center","className":"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-embed-youtube aligncenter wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
https://youtu.be/NMnPj6sO-w4
</div></figure>
<!-- /wp:core-embed/youtube -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>#3 Gila Salvador</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Gila, an entrepreneur, beauty queen, interior designer, and vlogger is definitely one to check out for. Did you know this young entrepreneur <a href="https://www.manilastandard.net/business/biz-plus/289090/24-year-old-ateneo-dropout-now-employs-more-than-100.html">earned her first million at 18 and established an interior design company employing engineers and architects at 20</a>? Just wow! Know more about how she handles business, life and everything in between on her channel.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:core-embed/youtube {"url":"https://youtu.be/bn6XP9I5u3g","type":"video","providerNameSlug":"youtube","className":"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-embed-youtube wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
https://youtu.be/bn6XP9I5u3g
</div></figure>
<!-- /wp:core-embed/youtube -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>#4 Cara Fajardo Interiors</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Cara Fajardo is also a licensed interior designer based in the Philippines. Although she’s fairly new to YouTube, her videos on home makeovers and interior designs are a reflection of her talent and all of it are super lit.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6552,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/image-15-1024x576.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6552"/><figcaption><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2MXURtBFf8A">EXTREME MAKEOVER! Coastal Chic | THE HOUSE RENO: Ep 3 + Tips On How To Style Shelves</a></figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>#5 Slater Young</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The builder of the ever-famous <em>Skypod</em>, Engr. Slater Young. This former PBB Big Winner is now back on Youtube after a long hiatus. Thanks to his very beautiful and supportive wife Kryz (who is also a famous Youtuber) for convincing him to create his own channel. Right now, Slater has over 200k subscribers where he posts videos of him inspiring viewers to appreciate engineering even more.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:core-embed/youtube {"url":"https://youtu.be/F8MEdIfQxc4","type":"video","providerNameSlug":"youtube","align":"center","className":"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-embed-youtube aligncenter wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
https://youtu.be/F8MEdIfQxc4
</div></figure>
<!-- /wp:core-embed/youtube -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>#6 Tidily Ever After by Mica Canto</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you’re into minimalism, zero-waste home organization and design, then better check out Mommy Mica Canto’s channel. Watch her videos on how to simplify life, live purposely, and find your own <em><a href="https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCHxCf0J6tmjOx2xylGqPr7Q">Tidily Ever After</a></em>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":6551,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/image-14-1024x576.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6551"/><figcaption>Tidily Transformation - <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ALAmpP6AWaA">Maximizing a Studio Unit</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>#7 Oliver Austria</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And last but not the least, the famous “Big Brain” Pinoy architect Lyann Oliver Austria whose reaction videos, house-building wisdom and mildly amusing humor have attracted netizens. Although he is not new on Youtube, it was only this year that he got a major spotlight and reached over a million subs. So, if you want good vibes at the same time so much learning, you may check his channel and join the <em>Mah Dudes Army</em>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:core-embed/youtube {"url":"https://youtu.be/CwAjKLJM0mc","type":"video","providerNameSlug":"youtube","align":"center","className":"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-embed-youtube aligncenter wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
https://youtu.be/CwAjKLJM0mc
</div></figure>
<!-- /wp:core-embed/youtube -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Have any of these YouTubers inspired you to start your own YouTube channel? If you want to become an influencer or give your design business a boost online, it’s time for some DIY. Develop your online presence and build a content marketing system to showcase your skills and products.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/10/Filipino-Youtubers-to-learn-Home-Design-and-Renovating-Tricks-1.jpg','views' => '128','category_id' => '9','published_at' => '2020-10-28 01:15:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '521','title' => 'Providing the departed one a home of their own','slug' => 'providing-the-departed-one-a-home-of-their-own','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipinos take the time of the work and school days to honor All Saints Day and All Souls Day. These days are dedicated for remembering the dearly departed siblings and loved-ones. It is in the Filipino culture to visit and spend time wit the departed loved ones in the cemetery. These are the days of commemorating and remembering the memories when they were still on earth. Traditional visits to the cemetery and other parks are done to commemorate their happy memories when they were still on earth. In lieu of the IATF decision to close the various cemetery and columbarium from Oct 30 to November 4, 2020, remembering our death can be done through prayers from home and churches.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Last&nbsp; November 1, 2020, 2020 at 3pm to 4:30pm <strong>Dr. Eduardo "Doc EG" Ong</strong>, Ph.D, DPA, DBA along with featured guests <strong>Veronica Lim</strong> and <strong>Dennis M. Booth Ph.D. </strong>talked about providing homes for the departed loved ones via<em> Ikonsulta Mo Kay Doc EG </em>FB &amp; YouTube Live.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>Ikonsulta Mo Kay Doc EG </em>is a a real estate and business page where <strong>Doc EG</strong>,  the First Chairman PRBRES and also the 2020 Outstanding Professional of the Year for Real Estate Service talks about the Philippine real estate and businesses.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In this episode, they shared the different personalities in the memorial parks business. It was also discussed how to purchase a memorial lot and provide other services to honor our siblings and loved ones because providing the departed one a home of their own is an act of love for them.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you missed the episode, an online event streamed was and also available via <a href="https://www.facebook.com/103896854665810/posts/177194434002718/">Facebook Live</a>  or at <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z23CfeljL2Q">YouTube Live</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:</strong><em><a href="http://localhost:3001/why-you-should-care-about-the-properties-of-your-deceased-parents/">Why You Should Care About The Properties of Your Deceased Parents?</a></em><br><strong>READ:</strong> <a href="http://localhost:3001/transfer-title-deceased-parents/"><em>Transferring a Property Title From Deceased Parents in PH</em></a><br><strong>READ:</strong> <a href="http://localhost:3001/will-testament-why-is-it-important/"><em>Will &amp; Testament | Why is it important?</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/11/Ikonsulta-Mo-Kang-Doc-EG.png','views' => '50','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-11-03 01:10:32','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '522','title' => 'How to Build an Earthquake and Typhoon-Proof House in the Philippines','slug' => 'how-to-build-an-earthquake-and-typhoon-proof-house-in-the-philippines','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Philippines is a country prone to natural disasters. Located along the typhoon belt in the Pacific, the country is visited by an average of 20 typhoons every year. It is also situated in the Pacific Ring of Fire, making it vulnerable to frequent earthquakes and volcanic eruptions [<a href="https://www.adrc.asia/nationinformation.php?NationCode=608&amp;Lang=en" data-type="URL" data-id="https://www.adrc.asia/nationinformation.php?NationCode=608&amp;Lang=en">src</a>].  In the recent years, typhoons have hit the country, causing deaths, flooding, and damaged properties.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><a href="https://news.sky.com/story/typhoon-goni-hits-philippines-worlds-strongest-storm-of-2020-leaves-four-dead-as-nearly-350-000-are-evacuated-12120447" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src="https://e3.365dm.com/20/11/2048x1152/skynews-goni-typhoon-philippines_5157357.jpg?bypass-service-worker&amp;20201101111554" alt=""/></a><figcaption>Super&nbsp;Typhoon&nbsp;Rolly (Typhoon Goni) | Albay, November 2020 [<a href="https://news.sky.com/story/typhoon-goni-hits-philippines-worlds-strongest-storm-of-2020-leaves-four-dead-as-nearly-350-000-are-evacuated-12120447" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">src</a>]</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>One primary cause of deaths during these disasters are poorly built buildings that collapse, forming hazards rather than shelters. Most of the damaged buildings are built with traditional methods and materials, usually without regard to ensuring the structures withstand strong winds or major earthquakes.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>While a house made of wood generally fares better than a concrete house in an earthquake, the opposite is true for a typhoon. This makes building earthquake and typhoon-proof homes in the Philippines a bit tricky.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:  </strong><a href="https://nextcity.org/daily/entry/can-a-house-be-typhoon-proof-and-earthquake-proof-at-the-same-time" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Can a House Be Typhoon-Proof and Earthquake-Proof at the Same Time?</a><br></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Tubigon_2_earthquake.JPG/1200px-Tubigon_2_earthquake.JPG" alt=""/><figcaption>Earthquake | Tubigon, Bohol; 2013 [<a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tubigon_2_earthquake.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">src</a>]</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>How do you build safer homes?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here\'s a list of recommendations from a paper written by Louise Mattsson. Check the link below if you want to read further.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Source: <a href="https://businessdocbox.com/Construction/87001613-How-to-build-earthquake-and-typhoon-resistant-buildings.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">https://businessdocbox.com/Construction/87001613-How-to-build-earthquake-and-typhoon-resistant-buildings.html</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Avoid building in a disaster-prone area, if possible</li><li>Build on hard soil</li><li>Build on flat land</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6641,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/image.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6641"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Provide for good drainage in the site</li><li>Plant trees to protect from wind</li><li>Choose a square or rectangular shape, or divide asymmetric shapes into several separated rectangles</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6642,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/image-1.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6642"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Have small and few opening</li><li>Place openings on the opposite sides of the building</li><li>Have the same size and placement of opening on all floors</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6643,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/image-2.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6643"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Anchor wooden house in a heavy and deep foundation</li><li>Connect all wooden members with straps, brackets, and gusset plats</li><li>Use diagonal trusses or plywood to brace the wooden framework</li><li>Reinforce masonry both vertically and horizontally around openings and in corners</li><li>Tie all masonry walls together with a continuous steel band or concrete beams placed in the top of the walls</li><li>Make sure that all connections are strong, especially the connection between walls and roof</li><li>Shape the roof pyramidal with a pitch of 30-40 degrees</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6645,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/image-4.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6645"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Use light materials for the roof, such as wood and corrugated iron</li><li>Anchor the roof overhang to the walls.</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6644,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/image-3.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6644"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:  </strong><a href="https://businessdocbox.com/Construction/87001613-How-to-build-earthquake-and-typhoon-resistant-buildings.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">How to Build Earthquake and Typhoon Resistant Buildings? Guidelines for the low-income housing</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/12/filipino-homes-blog-post-cover-13.png','views' => '65','category_id' => '13','published_at' => '2020-11-28 03:04:11','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '523','title' => 'NCIP reiterated that lands within ancestral domain cannot be sold','slug' => 'ncip-reiterated-that-lands-within-ancestral-domain-cannot-be-sold','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The National Commission on Indigenous Peoples (NCIP) has issued advisory number NA-2020-08-001 Series of 2020, reiterating that lands within ancestral domain cannot be subject to commerce.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[6581,6584]} -->
<figure class="wp-block-gallery columns-2 is-cropped"><ul class="blocks-gallery-grid"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/118768029_366122724790690_1614846342988311851_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="6581" class="wp-image-6581"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/118590093_366122748124021_5714285286585789755_n-1.jpg" alt="" data-id="6584" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/118590093_366122748124021_5714285286585789755_n-1.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=6584" class="wp-image-6584"/></figure></li></ul></figure>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The advisory cites Section 5 of the Indigenous Peoples Rights Act (IPRA) which states that “Indigenous concept of ownership sustains the view that ancestral domains and all resources found therein shall serve as the material bases of their cultural integrity. The indigenous concept of ownership generally holds that ancestral domains are the ICC’s/IP’s private but community property which belongs to all generations and therefore <strong>cannot be sold, disposed or destroyed</strong>. It likewise covers sustainable traditional resource rights.”</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It has come to the attention of the Commission that there is continued selling off of portions of ancestral domains despite the effort of the NCIP to educate and inculcate the nature of ownership of the indigenous peoples to their ancestral domain, thus the issuance of the advisory.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>All NCIP regional and provincial offices, Community Service Centers, Indigenous Political Structures (IPS), Council of Elders (COEs), Indigenous Peoples Organizations (IPOs), Indigenous Peoples Mandatory Representatives (IPMRs), and Tribal Councils are enjoined <strong>to stop, prohibit, and report any transaction dealing in, and/or negotiating the transfer and selling off portions or parcels of ancestral domains.</strong> These pertain to any form such as Deed of Sale, Transfer of Rights, and the like.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The heads of Local Government Units, the barangay, barangay legislative councils, and realtors are advised to refrain from facilitating, dealing, and negotiating transactions involving the transfer and sale of portions of the ancestral domain or any illegal intrusion into the ancestral domains.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Violations are punishable by imprisonment of not less than nine months but not more than 12 years or a fine of not less than Php100,000 nor more than Php5000,000. In addition, the guilty party shall be obliged to pay the indigenous cultural community/IP concerned of whatever damage may have been suffered by the latter as a consequence of the unlawful act.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 id="page-title">List of Identified Ancestral Domain (ADs) per Region</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>Source:&nbsp;</em>National Commission of Indigenous Peoples (NCIP)</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><a href="https://www.doe.gov.ph/sites/default/files/pdf/eicc/ad-car.pdf">CAR</a></li><li><a href="https://www.doe.gov.ph/sites/default/files/pdf/eicc/ad-region01.pdf">Region 1</a></li><li><a href="https://www.doe.gov.ph/sites/default/files/pdf/eicc/ad-region02.pdf">Region 2</a></li><li><a href="https://www.doe.gov.ph/sites/default/files/pdf/eicc/ad-region03.pdf">Region 3</a></li><li><a href="https://www.doe.gov.ph/sites/default/files/pdf/eicc/ad-region04.pdf">Region 4</a></li><li><a href="https://www.doe.gov.ph/sites/default/files/pdf/eicc/ad-region05.pdf">Region 5</a></li><li><a href="https://www.doe.gov.ph/sites/default/files/pdf/eicc/ad-region06_07.pdf">Region 6 and 7</a></li><li><a href="https://www.doe.gov.ph/sites/default/files/pdf/eicc/ad-region09.pdf">Region 9</a></li><li><a href="https://www.doe.gov.ph/sites/default/files/pdf/eicc/ad-region10.pdf">Region 10</a></li><li><a href="https://www.doe.gov.ph/sites/default/files/pdf/eicc/ad-region11.pdf">Region 11</a></li><li><a href="https://www.doe.gov.ph/sites/default/files/pdf/eicc/ad-region12.pdf">Region 12</a></li><li><a href="https://www.doe.gov.ph/sites/default/files/pdf/eicc/ad-region13.pdf">Region 13</a></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

