<!-- /wp:separator -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/11/filipino-homes-blog-post-cover-9.png','views' => '39','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2020-11-30 03:40:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '524','title' => 'Realtors can now be sanctioned for hate speech','slug' => 'realtors-can-now-be-sanctioned-for-hate-speech','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The <a href="https://www.nar.realtor/">National Association of Realtors (NAR)</a> board of directors finally approved to expand the Code of Ethics Article 10, making it a violation for Realtors who use harassing or hate speech toward any of the protected classes even outside their real estate duties. The trade organization said on Friday, November 13, during the 2020 <a href="https://www.conference.realtor/">Realtors Conference &amp; Expo</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>NAR President Vince Malta called the approval of the changes <em>“a monumental moment”</em> in reaffirming NAR’s commitment to fair housing and ensure the Realtors Code of Ethics extends beyond real estate-related activities. <mark>It is said that the changes will <em>“raise the bar on the professionalism and private speech”</em> of America’s 1.4 million Realtors.</mark></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/on97kUnPBFZ1Wpuv5iUYVopLENId_Ttcau2acaEVKwwtUA4rslFy6V_r1Dl1Z8qMRx7EBexSslKHE5ZjSq4UzAlPGzfZTkv1t0dCUIIaO74YH4aQE6RDFPJLrIgoqbf7mxmf_LZ-" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>What this means for realtors</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Under current rules, realtors and organization members who engage in hate speech or any discriminatory remarks --whether on their business or personal social media account-- can be subject to disciplinary action. The amendments took in effect immediately, but do not retroactively apply to members’ past activities or actions i.e online comments and postings.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>The new, expanded Realtors Code of Ethics</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>According to the Article 10 of the REALTORS® Code of Ethics that realtors are prohibited from discriminating without a consequence on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, handicap, familial status, national origin, sexual orientation, or gender identity in the provision of professional services and in employment practices. But the centerpiece of these changes is the addition of a new Standard of Practice 10-5, which says:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em>“Realtors must not use harassing speech, hate speech, epithets or slurs based on race, color, religion, sex, handicap, familial status, national origin, sexual orientation or gender identity.”</em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Anyone can file a complaint against a realtor alleging the use of harassing language or hate speech in public. However, complaints will be considered on a case-by-case basis by the local realtor association in which the agent is a member, according to NAR.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And yes, consequences for violators of the code of ethics vary from fines to requirements to attend educational courses. But in most cases, a realtor’s membership can be suspended or revoked.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href="https://www.nar.realtor/national-leadership/committee-members-liaisons/code-of-ethics-professional-standards-policies"><strong>Read more about NAR\'s additions to their Code of Ethics here</strong></a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Philippines’ Real Estate Code of Ethics</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Meanwhile, in the Philippines, there’s also a Code of Ethics for real estate practitioners known as RESA or the Real Estate Service Act. Officially took effect in 2009, the law protects the rights of those who call themselves real estate professionals. It also lays down the rules which these professionals have to adhere to, so that they may be registered under the Professional Regulation Commission (PRC) and be allowed to continue their practice.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here’s a copy of the <strong><a href="https://www.prc.gov.ph/sites/default/files/RealEstateServiceCOE.pdf">Code of Ethics and Responsibilities for Real Estate Service Practitioners</a>.</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6599,"sizeSlug":"large","linkDestination":"attachment"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><a href="http://localhost:3001/10-things-you-need-to-understand-resa-law/" target="_blank" rel="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/10-things-you-need-to-understand-resa-law/ noopener noreferrer"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/resa-law-philippines-1-1024x576.jpg" alt="resa" class="wp-image-6599"/></a></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em>Related blog: </em><a href="http://localhost:3001/10-things-you-need-to-understand-resa-law/"><em>10 things you need to understand RESA Law</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":1} -->
<h1>Bottomline:</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The amendments of the Realtors Code of Ethics serve as a reminder for real estate professionals (not just in America but all over the globe) to always uphold professionalism in the industry, abide by the code of ethics and swear to protect the interests of the persons they work for. Because diligence and integrity are the characteristics that will reap good dividends, not hate and bigotry.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6598,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/resa-law-philippines-1024x576.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-6598"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"align":"center","level":1} -->
<h1 class="has-text-align-center">Let us know in the comment section.</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Note: The term "REALTOR®" is a registered collective membership mark which identifies a real estate professional who is a member of the National Association of&nbsp; Realtors (NAR), the largest real estate trade association in America.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/11/Realtors-can-now-be-sanctioned-for-HATE-SPEECH.jpg','views' => '42','category_id' => '16','published_at' => '2020-12-01 03:47:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '525','title' => 'DHSUD goes after real estate scammers & bogus brokers','slug' => 'dhsud-goes-after-real-estate-scammers-bogus-brokers','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Department of Human Settlements and Urban Development (DHSUD) said it will pursue illicit home developers and false brokers doing unlawful selling of land properties. DHSUD having the regulatory power over real estate developers and brokers and salespersons is doing this campiagn to clean the real estate from these illegal activities.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Sec. Eduardo del Rosario said the DSHUD will have an intensified campaign against illegal selling of housing and human settlement projects.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>“<em>We need to put a stop to these illegal activities through pro-active efforts in collaboration with our stakeholders, including legitimate developers, who are also falling victims to these scammers, and other government agencies,</em>” he said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Del Rosario have ordered DHSUD\'s regional offices to come up with campaigns against real estate scammers These includes illegal developers, brokers, and agents engaged in the illegal selling of real estate properties.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This campaign will strengthen the DHSUD\'s relationship with otehr government agencies including the Department of Justice (DOJ), Department of the Interior and Local Government (DILG) and partner-developers in pursuing efforts to eliminate these illegal activities.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This initiative is brought about from numerous reports of unregistered developers and real estate brokers engaging in property selling illegally.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Based on the Housing and Land use Regulatory Board (HLURB) under Presidential Decree 957—no real estate broker or salesman shall engage in the business of selling subdivision lots or condominium units without being registered.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>“<em>We should protect our home buyers, especially overseas Filipino workers, from these scammers,</em>” said del Rosario.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Del Rosario reminded the public to avoid falling prey to unlicensed developers and other bogus brokers or salespeople.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>This article was first published by https://www.pna.gov.ph</em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/12/DHSUD-goes-after-real-estate-scammers-bogus-brokers.png','views' => '40','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2020-12-02 01:47:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '526','title' => '5 Things to Consider for Your Post-Pandemic Dream Home','slug' => '5-things-to-consider-for-your-post-pandemic-dream-home','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The COVID-19 pandemic has emphasized the importance of our home environment. The home is not only a place to sleep in but must also serve as a place of work (home office), a full-time kitchen, a place for entertainment, and a place for relaxation. Having a home that can act in all these roles can be challenging, but is also achievable.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This quarantine has led us to reevaluate the role of the home and how to best prepare for the future. Here is a list of strategies and methods to create the best environment for post-pandemic living.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>1. Access to a Variety of Spatial Experiences</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Spending all your time at home can take a toll on your mental health and productivity.&nbsp; Having access to a variety of spatial experiences is important to potentially avoid burnout and unnecessary stress.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=3659243435207969" height="850" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Bright and airy spaces can be great as places for relaxation, but these can be too distracting for work. While there may be people who prefer to have the dining area double as a co-working space with the rest of the family, there are some who would need to have established quiet corners that boost productivity. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For the post-pandemic ideal home, it may be best to have a variety of spaces for a change of environment when needed.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>2. Flexible Spaces</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Not every house can have a dedicated space for all types of activities within the home.  It is crucial to incorporate flexible spaces.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=22166223157229318" height="500" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For example, instead of having a guest room that is rarely used, it may be a more practical option to consider building a multi-purpose room that can also be used for other activities.&nbsp; A home office + guest room combination is a great idea. You can use the bed as a lounging area when you don’t have people over.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>3. Designing for Cleanliness</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Clutter can easily make your home look and feel disorganized, chaotic, and stressful. You can encourage cleanliness by taking into consideration spatial organization and material choices in your design. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=389702174010911536" height="437" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A garage with a sink and a table can be a dedicated space for disinfecting packages and groceries. In terms of materials, non-porous, smooth materials are much easier to clean and disinfect.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>4. Space for Physical and Mental Health</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A space that encourages exercise can help maintain a sense of normalcy in the home. Home gyms (or even an area cleared for movement and meditation) have become increasingly popular during the quarantine period. Creating a simple home yoga space reinforces the importance of self-care.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=133278470212533016" height="700" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>5. Access to Outdoor Space</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Access to outdoor space is also a great thing to consider for your post-pandemic dream home. While it is tempting to utilize all available space for a building, do not forget to carve areas for landscape and access to light and air. Having something close to nature can help with your mental health. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=1055599901393082" height="1001" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
z
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/11/filipino-homes-blog-post-cover-10.png','views' => '50','category_id' => '31','published_at' => '2020-12-03 01:35:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '527','title' => 'How Gen Z homebuyers are impacting Real Estate Market','slug' => 'how-gen-z-homebuyers-are-impacting-real-estate-market','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Millennial is out, Gen Z is in! There is a new generation of home buyers and renters that’s coming to the real estate market and they’re changing the game!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Known as the <em>Digital </em>or the <em>iGeneration</em>, <strong>Generation Z or Gen Z</strong> comprise those born from about 1996 to 2010, of which the oldest among them is now in their early 20s. They are the generation who grew up with the internet and social media. They’re educated, forward-thinkers, and competitive in their careers. And even though they’re young, many of them have already bought their first homes or at least are starting to enter the housing market.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So if you’re a real estate agent, broker, property investor or someone’s selling a property, it’s timely to note Gen Z’s housing habits and learn how to connect with this generation and gain their trust.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/EBSYRkEn14cWqk2e7R29MpG6WsizaLy4ku2--xkBobLPGPrhjwx8yDDxa_0R0kQERzNhPN7juYTQUNt78_r7QdPjgu9lU_IxlDggVKaPOW5iv9XblT4BCUt7Xr2rasYcNTs0GQz4" alt="Gen Z on Real Estate"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>How Generation Zs are impacting the housing market</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Researchers have found that the concerns and belief systems of this generation differ radically from both the Baby Boomers and the Millennials. Let’s take a look at how Gen Z is making an impact on the real estate market.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#1 Gen Z is Frugal</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A <a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B1Axm9XHqBDgek10eTBkb3BKb051R3U4aXZKd0d0NjRzVEZB/view">survey</a> reports that Gen Zs are forward-thinkers and driven to plan for the future compared to their older generations i.e Millennials, Gen X, and Boomers. They are serious about money, investing, and career choices. They care about the cost and quality of an item or product, while also valuing their time. Probably because they remember their parents struggling to make ends meet which they don’t want to happen again.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Considering Gen Z’s frugal mindset, it’s important that you build trust with them through transparency. Be genuinely honest in transacting with them and explain the pros and cons, especially when confidential details are revealed. The more you’re transparent with them, the more likely you win their trust.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>Related:<em> <a href="http://localhost:3001/how-genz-invest-work-and-cope-financially/">How Gen Z Invest, Work and Cope Financially</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#2 Gen Z aspires homeownership</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>According to a <a href="https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/move-over-millennials-better-homes-and-gardens-real-estate-reveals-homebuying-dreams-of-gen-z-teens-274452691.html">survey</a> conducted by Better Homes and Gardens in 2015 that ninety-seven percent (97%) of Gen Z believes they will eventually own a home. It is seen that they are more likely to buy than their Millennial counterparts, so it’ll be interesting to see over the next five to ten years how that plays out.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With this million strong generation already moving into their home buying years, it’s important to craft the right message and begin connecting with them now. Gen Z consumes most information and interacts via the internet, so you need to be creative, fast and responsive, and tech-savvy too. If you’re still relying on traditional ways of marketing and doing business, then you’ll be left out and Gen Zs won’t spend time with you. Building a connection is key.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#3 Gen Z moves in and out</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It is also found out that Gen Z doesn\'t have deep roots. They’re willing to move in and out, look for career opportunities that they are passionate about or just experience a new area. They think they don\'t have anything major to lose, so a lot of them don\'t even want to stick around the same place and they’re willing to move across to find their own path.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>To connect with Gen Z where they’re most comfortable, you must use your social channels consistently. This means you have to be online, have a consistent message, and have a regular posting schedule. You don’t need to meet them personally to build a connection. A solid digital presence is an opportunity to stay in touch with them and get repeat business and referrals.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>Read: <a href="http://localhost:3001/10-social-media-post-ideas-for-real-estate-agents/"><em>10 Social Media Post Ideas for Real Estate Agents</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#4 Gen Z hates commute</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Gen Z hates commutes. They want to be near work airports and amenities. They want to be within walking distance of restaurants of nightlife bars a lot of things to do. They\'re young and looking to have a good time so how do you sell to them well.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As a real estate practitioner, you must position yourself into this growing group of potential homebuyers by staying up-to-date on what’s latest, updating your value proposition to appeal to this generation’s needs and desires, learning all you can about this demographic, and understanding their home buying habits. It’s your ticket to keeping with the Gen Z trend.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#5 Gen Z do it for the gram</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Social media is part of everyday life for Gen Z. They’re used to documenting their lives and sharing their experiences with their peers. And because Gen Z live in a time where everything is immediate, this will most certainly impact how they shop for and buy a house.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As a property salesperson, you have to <a href="http://localhost:3001/4-effective-ways-to-sell-your-property-listing-tips-for-real-estate-agents/">level up your social media game</a> too. Make sure your property is Instagram-worthy! Hiring a professional photographer to take photos of your property listing is definitely a good investment to make. Remember too that they’ve been marketed throughout their lives, so they can differentiate what’s genuine or fake. Feel free to explore more budget-friendly <a href="http://localhost:3001/category/home-renovation/">home renovations</a>, <a href="http://localhost:3001/category/home-improvement/">DIY home improvements</a>, and <a href="http://localhost:3001/category/tips-guides/">real estate tips</a> from Filipino Homes.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>But take note that as they become homeowners, expect Gen Z to document it every step of the way. For real estate agents and brokers, this could be a game-changer in real estate marketing. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6609,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><a href="https://filipinohomes.com/properties/sale#"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/property-filipino-homes-1024x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6609"/></a></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Are You Looking for a Property?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you are one of the Gen Z who is considering <a href="http://localhost:3001/category/real-estate-101/">real estate investing</a> as an option, you may talk to a <a href="http://localhost:3001/#">professional real estate agent</a> who knows the ins and outs and the current real estate trends of today.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/11/genz-on-real-estate.jpg','views' => '48','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-12-04 07:18:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '528','title' => '2021 PH Real Estate Trends Homebuyers are Looking Out For','slug' => '2021-ph-real-estate-trends-homebuyers-are-looking-out-for','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Beautiful and efficient spaces affects both mood and productivity not only in the workspace but also in the home. With the Covid pandemic still limiting the movements of people and the highly encouraged work and study from home set-up, our homes should be ready for the demands of the new normal. Here are the trends that people will most-likely look for in the finding a home in 2021:<br></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Location matters all the more</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With everyone at home and limited to go out. Having a home with a convenient location is something people would want to get a hold off. Not having to travel or commute to get to to the grocery shops, banks, malls, pharmacy, hospitals and etc. These matters these days especially to families who prefer to be in the the center of the city for its convenience. Some families may go for homes in the outskirts of the city. So subdivisions is a hot property as well. So families can be away from the busy city and have more freedom from the concrete jungle.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Spacious home for work/study from home set-up</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With this pandemic, companies had set up work from home for their employees to avoid infection in the workplace. And while this is good, our homes are not set up to have home office or study rooms for the working or studying family member. This is something people would want to consider when buying a property</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Plant and pet friendly homes</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>What the pandemic has given people is the chance to care for plants and pets while coop up at home. People have become plantitos and plantitas and have grown to love pets when the haven\'t before. Having a home for the new family members is a considerations for these homebuyers.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Some bit of outdoor space</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Having to stay indoors most days of the week can get pretty tiring and cabin fever can be a struggle to fight off. It is not a surprise that homebuyers will look for a little bit of outdoor space in the house they are looking. Even a balcony is a good extra outdoor space to fill up with plants and other whatnots to make one feel more attached to the outside world.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Online house hunting</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Finally, online house hunting is a thing these days. People are browsing online from one property listing to another finding the perfect home they can call their own. These homebuyers are also looking for qualified real estate brokers and sales agent who can assist them and guide them in their homebuying journey. At Filipino homes, you will find numerous real estate brokers and sales agent in your area. All of which are professional not only in their dealings but very knowledgeable to the properties in the current market that would suit a homebuyers needs.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/12/2021-PH-Real-Estate-Trends-Homebuyers-are-Looking-Out-For.png','views' => '58','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-12-05 02:07:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '529','title' => '10 Balcony Garden Ideas for Tight Spaces','slug' => '10-balcony-garden-ideas-for-tight-spaces','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This pandemic has had nearly everyone nest really hard and worked on transforming spaces within the home. Many have learned to embrace their inner plant mom (or dad!) selves. If you are hesitant to join the plant party because of space issues, know that you don\'t need a yard or a large wide area to live the garden life. Your balcony can hold more plants than you think. Check out these cozy balcony garden ideas that you can use for your tight condo balcony:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>1. Plants in little pots</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=249527635590114279" height="1000" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Using different plants in small pots can help you fill your space neatly. Whether it is flowering plants, herbs, or vegetables that you want on your balcony, little pots can make your balcony less cramped.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>2. Use ladder planters</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=103723597656554384" height="1001" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Make use of the vertical space in your balcony and install a ladder-style planter. This can help make your balcony feel lush and green but not overcrowded. You can grow herbs and stack them instead of spreading them across your balcony floor.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>3. Add a living wall</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=418131146660329994" height="1059" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Another way to maximize your vertical space is to utilize your balcony wall. This makes a gorgeous statement piece for your space and provides you the greenery you need.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>4. Add a comfy chair</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=466615211391947018" height="953" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Add a comfy chair to your balcony, and you can have a space to enjoy the glorious view of the city. It\'s a perfect spot for relaxing with a cup of coffee (or a glass of wine!) and a good book as well.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>5. Add a string of lights</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=821555157019815538" height="850" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A string of bulbs can help make your balcony look really great at night.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>6. Use the balcony ledges</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=260364422193289608" height="1001" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Balcony ledges provide extra space for growing your small garden.<strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>7. Hang up your plants</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=188306828152312731" height="1001" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Hang up your pots for a less invasive yet still quite divisive privacy screen for your balcony. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>8. Add a hammock</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=138204282303747038" height="926" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For a more relaxing vibe, add a hammock, and transform your balcony into a cozy reading nook.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>9. Greenhouse in the balcony</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=320459329739692606" height="1021" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you are up for a DIY project, consider building a greenhouse for your balcony.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>10. Use varied pot sizes and plant types</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://assets.pinterest.com/ext/embed.html?id=397020523405729023" height="888" width="600" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Minimalists can also keep balcony gardens. A few carefully curated pots and plants can make a huge difference and still bring green into your space.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/11/filipino-homes-blog-post-cover-11.png','views' => '49','category_id' => '31','published_at' => '2020-12-06 01:37:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '530','title' => 'Wee Community Developers wins big at the 2020 PropertyGuru Philippines Property Awards!','slug' => 'wee-community-developers-wins-big-at-the-2020-propertyguru-philippines-property-awards','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Congratulations to <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://weecommph.com/" data-type="URL" data-id="https://weecommph.com/" target="_blank">Wee Community Developers Inc.</a> for a remarkable Luzon, Visayas, and Mindanao winning feat! </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://www.facebook.com/plugins/post.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Fweecommdevelopersinc%2Fposts%2F3796839960326138&amp;show_text=true&amp;width=552&amp;appId=1900316703582796&amp;height=833" width="552" height="833" style="border:none;overflow:hidden" scrolling="no" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen="true" allow="autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture; web-share"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>During the 8<sup>th</sup>&nbsp;PropertyGuru Philippines Property Awards on November 25, Wee Community Developers Inc. was recognized as the <strong>Best Breakthrough Developer of 2020 PropertyGuru Philippines Property Awards</strong>. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://www.asiapropertyawards.com/wp-content/webp-express/webp-images/doc-root/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/50646994101_64b5e47883_b.jpg.webp" alt=""/><figcaption>source: <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.asiapropertyawards.com/en/2020-propertyguru-philippines-property-awards-first-virtual-edition-marks-the-8th-anniversary-of-celebrating-the-nations-finest-in-real-estate/" target="_blank">Asia Property Awards</a> website</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Some WeeComm projects also garnered awards in the following categories:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><strong>Harbour Park Residences:</strong> Best Affordable Condo Development (Metro Manila) &amp; Highly Commended for Best Lifestyle Development</li><li><strong>The Diamond Heights: </strong>Best Housing Development (Mindanao), Best Housing Architectural Design &amp; Best Housing Development (Philippines)</li><li><strong>Emerald Estates: </strong>Best Housing Development (Visayas) &amp; Highly Commended for Best Housing Architectural Design</li><li><strong>Grand Mesa Residences:</strong> Highly Commended for Best Condo Architectural Design</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The company was also recognized for the following efforts: </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Special Recognition for Building Communities </li><li>Special Recognition in Sustainable Construction </li><li>Special Recognition for CSR</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>All of these are affirmations of WeeComm’s commitment to create robust communities that are beyond ordinary, not just in Metro Manila, but in key Metro Cities all over the country. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Congratulations again, and kudos for garnering the most number of awards for a single developer in this year’s edition of the Property Guru’s Annual Philippine Property Awards.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>About the Property Guru\'s Annual Philippine Property Awards</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The annual <strong>PropertyGuru Philippines Property Awards</strong> honored the country’s finest developers during its first-ever virtual gala on November 25, 2020 to celebrate the best projects, design, and innovation within the industry in the past year.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Presented by global brand Kohler, the 8th Annual PropertyGuru Philippines Property Awards are the most respected and most sought-after real estate industry honors. The event is part of the regional PropertyGuru Asia Property Awards program established in 2005. With a professionally run judging system supervised by BDO, one of the world’s largest auditing and accountancy firms, the Asia Property Awards is the gold standard in real estate.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ</strong>:  <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.asiapropertyawards.com/en/award/philippines-property-awards/" target="_blank">Full list of winners HERE.</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/12/128798848_3796835010326633_9151623531252929311_o.jpg','views' => '43','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2020-12-09 05:02:07','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '531','title' => 'How to Apply for Registration of Real Estate Broker (DHSUD)','slug' => 'how-to-apply-for-registration-of-real-estate-broker-dhsud','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In November 2020, the Department of Human Settlements and Urban Development (DHSUD, formerly HLURB) has started to accommodate annual renewal for registration of real estate brokers and salespersons.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":6685,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/Renewal-_-Application-for-Registration-of-Real-Estate-Broker-Infographic-410x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6685"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here is the application process:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>Step 1. Prepare the requirements.</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} -->
<ol><li>Signed and filled out Application for Registration of Real Estate Broker. </li><li>Two (2) 2x2 colored pictures; one for the application form and the other one for the photo signature sheet.</li><li>Photo signature sheet</li><li>Photocopy of PRC ID and Certificate of Registration (COR)</li><li>Photocopy of your last year’s DHSUD (HLURB) official receipt (OR).</li><li>Photocopy of the Php 5,000 Cash bond OR or Surety Bond.</li></ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>Step 2. Present all the requirements to the personnel in charge for evaluation. </h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Be ready with your original copies for verification if asked.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Remember to renew at the DHSUD(HLURB) branch where you originally registered.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>Step 3. Present your Order of Payment slip to the cashier and pay Php 720.</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If all requirements are satisfied, you will be given the order of payment slip to be presented upon payment at the cashier. Make sure to bring the exact amount of Php 720 to avoid delays.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>Step 4. Submit a photocopy of your receipt</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Submit a photocopy of your Official Receipt to the personnel in charge and keep the original copy. You will be asked to fill out your details. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>Step 5. Wait for your Provisional Certificate of Registration to be sent via email.</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The provisional certificate of registration will be issued through your email.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Download the <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://dhsud.gov.ph/downloadable-forms/" data-type="URL" data-id="https://dhsud.gov.ph/downloadable-forms/" target="_blank">APPLICATION FOR REGISTRATION OF REAL ESTATE BROKER </a>here.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>READ: </strong><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/?p=6692" target="_blank">How to Apply for Renewal of Registration of Real Estate Salesperson</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Office Address:</strong> DHSUD Building, Kalayaan Avenue corner Mayaman Street, Diliman, Quezon City<br><strong>Email:&nbsp;</strong><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="mailto:ncr@hlurb.gov.ph" target="_blank">ncr@hlurb.gov.ph</a> <br><strong>Contact numbers:</strong> 0916 378 0531 or 0921 757 3383</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/12/Registration-renewal-real-estate-broker-philippines-2.png','views' => '184','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2020-12-26 21:04:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '532','title' => 'How to Apply for Renewal of Registration of Real Estate Salesperson (DHSUD)','slug' => 'how-to-apply-for-renewal-of-registration-of-real-estate-salesperson-dhsud','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Department of Human Settlements and Urban Development (DHSUD),&nbsp;formerly called Housing and Land Use Regulatory Board (HLURB), has issued a set of revised implementing rules and regulations (IRRs) for Presidential Decree 957 in efforts to promote safe and legitimate real estate transactions in the Philippines.&nbsp; Under PD 957 as amended, is empowered to register real estate salesmen dealing in condominiums, farm lots, memorial parks, and subdivision projects.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Brokers and salespeople are mandated to get DHSUD accreditation or license before they can engage in Philippine real estate services. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>No real estate broker or salesman shall engage in the business of selling subdivision lots or condominium units unless he has registered himself with the Authority in accordance with the provisions of Sections 11 &amp; 12 of Presidential Decree No. 957 and Sections 13, 14, and 15 of Rule V of Implementing Rules and Regulations as Amended and Other Related Laws and Regulations of the HLURB.</p><cite>Source: <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://dhsud.gov.ph/broker-agent/?doing_wp_cron=1608983297.7126820087432861328125" target="_blank">DHSUD website</a></cite></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you are under the license of a real estate broker selling projects from developers then you are required to register with DHSUD too.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In November 2020, DHSUD has started to accommodate annual renewal for registration of real estate brokers and salespersons.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":6693,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/Renewal-_-Application-for-Registration-of-Real-Estate-Salesperson-Infographic-410x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6693"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here is the application process:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>Step 1. Prepare the requirements.</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} -->
<ol><li>Signed and filled out Application for Registration of Real Estate Salesperson.</li><li>Two (2) 2x2 colored pictures; one for the application form and the other one for the photo signature sheet.</li><li>Photo signature sheet</li><li>Photocopy of your PRC ID (or claim slip if ID is not yet available) and Certificate of Registration (COR).</li><li>Photocopy of your last year’s DHSUD (HLURB) official receipt (OR).</li><li>Photocopy of your&nbsp;<strong>real estate broker’</strong>s PRC ID and Certificate of Registration (COR).</li><li>Photocopy of your&nbsp;<strong>real estate broker’s</strong>&nbsp;latest DHSUD (HLURB) official receipt (OR).&nbsp;Your broker must renew his/her DHSUD registration first starting Nov 2020.</li><li>Photocopy&nbsp;Letter of Engagement / Employment by an HLURB-registered dealer or broker. This should be signed by your broker.</li><li>Photocopy of Bond or Security (Original copy must be presented for comparison as faithful reproduction). It is advisable to pay a cash bond of Php 1,000 which you can use lifetime (as long as you do not have any violations) rather than paying a surety bond of around 400-500 yearly.</li><li>Photocopy of the Official Receipt (Application fee) Php 288.</li></ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>Step 2. Present all the requirements to the personnel in charge for the evaluation. </h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Be ready with your original copies for verification if asked.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Remember to renew at the DHSUD (HLURB) branch where you originally registered.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>Step 3. Present your Order of Payment slip to the cashier and pay Php 288.</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If all requirements are satisfied, you will be given the order of payment slip to be presented upon payment at the cashier. Make sure to bring the exact amount of Php 288 to avoid delays.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>Step 4. Submit a photocopy of your receipt</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Submit a photocopy of your Official Receipt to the personnel in charge and keep the original copy. You will be asked to fill out your details. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>Step 5. Wait for your Provisional Certificate of Registration to be sent via email.</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The provisional certificate of registration will be issued through your email.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Download the <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://dhsud.gov.ph/downloadable-forms/" data-type="URL" data-id="https://dhsud.gov.ph/downloadable-forms/" target="_blank">APPLICATION FOR REGISTRATION OF REAL ESTATE SALESPERSON </a>here.&nbsp; </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ: </strong><a href="http://localhost:3001/how-to-apply-for-registration-of-real-estate-broker-dhsud/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">How to Apply for Renewal of Registration of Real Estate Broker</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Office Address:</strong> DHSUD Building, Kalayaan Avenue corner Mayaman Street, Diliman, Quezon City<br><strong>Email:&nbsp;</strong><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="mailto:ncr@hlurb.gov.ph" target="_blank">ncr@hlurb.gov.ph</a> <br><strong>Contact numbers:</strong> 0916 378 0531 or 0921 757 3383</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2020/12/Renewal-_-Application-for-Registration-of-Real-Estate-Salesperson-FilipinoHomes.png','views' => '267','category_id' => '16','published_at' => '2020-12-27 21:12:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '533','title' => 'Work-from-home Desk Tips to Increase Productivity','slug' => 'work-from-home-desk-tips-to-increase-productivity','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Covid-19 gave everyone a hard time and gave us a new way to look at our normals. With community quarantine put in placed that has limited our movements, it has not been good to all of us. We have to make adjustments from the way we commute, go out from our homes, and including our work situations moved to home set-up.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We have to make adjustments at home and this includes making space for a desk step up to work from home.  Here are some simple tips to increase your work-from-home productivity by making your work desk and environment get in you the work mood.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6724,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Work-from-home-Images-10.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6724"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>Choose the right spot</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Choosing the right spot for your work desk is crucial. It not only sets the mood for work but also gives you a distinctive place to turn on your brain for work. Setting up a work desk or area trains your brain to focus and start work. Finding the right spot can be tricky though. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Make sure to place your work desk in a well-lit area like beside a window. It is also good that the area is ventilated to keep you comfortable throughout the day. Choose a spot where there is less traffic and noise to help keep you focused.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:</strong> <a href="http://localhost:3001/do-you-work-from-home-buy-your-next-home-with-your-office-in-mind/"><em>Do you work from home? Buy your next home with your office in mind</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6722,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Work-from-home-Images-08.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6722"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>Use a stable table &amp; comfortable chair</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Your work table and  chair will probably be one of the most used furnitures you have at home right now with work occupying 8hours a day. Make sure to use a steady and sturdy work table. It should be stable enough to hold your computer and other work items you need on hand all the time. If you can find an ergonomic chair would also give your back some comfort while sitting all day.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Being seated in front of your computer all day can give you some bad back. It is best to address that early on by making sure you have both a stable desk and comfortable chair to work on all day long.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:</strong> <a href="http://localhost:3001/5-tips-to-actually-be-productive-when-working-from-home/"><em>Stuck at home? 5 Tips to Actually be Productive When You’re Working From Home</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6721,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Work-from-home-Images-07.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6721"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>Organize your office supplies &amp; make it accessible</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Make your workspace yours by being creative with in and also organizing your work items. That way you do not have to constantly look for items that you need and disrupt your work.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:</strong> <a href="http://localhost:3001/2021-ph-real-estate-trends-homebuyers-are-looking-out-for/"><em>2021 PH Real Estate Trends Homebuyers are Looking Out For</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6725,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Work-from-home-Images-11.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6725"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>Set-up with video meetings in mind</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Everyone is doing video meetings while working from home. Make sure to always have a clean and organized background to prepare for any video meetings. This will not only make you look professional but also help your colleagues from being distracted with what is at your background.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Make sure to also have a good lamp to help you with the lighting. You do not need one if the room is well-lit.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:</strong><em><a href="http://localhost:3001/5-things-to-consider-for-your-post-pandemic-dream-home/"> 5 Things to Consider for Your Post-Pandemic Dream Home</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6715,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Work-from-home-Images-01.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6715"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>Liven up the room </strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A home office don\'t need to boring. It is also good to give it a personality t help motivate you to work. Allow your workspace to reflect your character and make it lively. That way you will always look forward to starting work every workday.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:</strong> <em><a href="http://localhost:3001/buying-a-home-what-to-consider-before-buying/">Buying a home? What to consider before buying</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Working from home can be challenging with all the distractions of comfortable bed, or activities done by other family members. A good work environment will not only motivates you to work but also keeps you focused, makes it comfortable and efficient and increases your productivity.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/01/FILIPINOHOMES-BLOGS-XYZA-YAPE-1.jpg','views' => '49','category_id' => '31','published_at' => '2021-01-11 03:23:26','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '534','title' => 'Choosing the Best Type of Condo Unit for You','slug' => 'choosing-the-best-type-of-condo-unit-for-you','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Young adults these days are slowly moving into adulthood and experiencing independence to certain degrees. One of which is moving out of the "nest" to live closer to the workplace and also to be independent in both finances and survival. There\'s nothing more than moving out from your parents condo buying/renting that screams out independence.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Knowing what type of condo you need is challenging, especially if you\'re a first property or homebuyer. But here are helpful tips to consider on what type of condo units to choose from whether you are buying or renting one:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":2311,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/Smart-Small-Condo-Design-Ideas-02.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-2311"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Studio Unit</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A studio unit is basically a one room apartment without bedroom, kitchen or dining partition. It is an open space where you can assign where your bed, table or desk to go and you can see everything from any part of the unit. The only partition you will find is the bathroom and in some cases the kitchen if it is located near the entry door.<br><br>This condo is good for people who are looking for a place of their own but do not have the budget to go for a more spacious unit. You have to be okay with small spaces to consider this unit.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>Check out</strong>: <a href="https://filipinohomes.com/properties/sale"><em>Condo units in Metro Manila</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":2308,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/How-to-Make-Your-Condominium-Unit-Look-Bigger-06-1024x768.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-2308"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>1 BR Unit</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A one bedroom unit is a unit with provision and separated room for the bedroom. You will find a living room, comfort room and bedroom in this unit. It is much bigger than the studio unit and gives define boundaries for living spaces and your sleeping area.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This type of unit makes it perfect to get home and relax. It is also for people who likes to entertain and can host parties over since the bedroom is separated from the dining and living room. This will be a little pricey than a studio unit but definitely gives more room for storage and you can get more privacy in this unit.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>Read:</strong> <a href="http://localhost:3001/how-to-know-youre-buying-a-well-made-condo/"><em>How to Know You’re Buying a Well-Made Condo</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":2305,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/How-to-Make-Your-Condominium-Unit-Look-Bigger-02.png" alt="" class="wp-image-2305"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>2 Bedroom Unit</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The two bedroom unit is a bigger condo unit layout with 2 bedrooms, a comfort room and a living area where you can place your living and dining areas and kitchen. You can use the other bedroom as a spare or guest room for family or friends pending the night there. Or you can have it rented out by someone you know to help with the mortgage and upkeep.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>Read:</strong> <em><a href="http://localhost:3001/condotels-meet-investors-business-and-leisure-objectives-in-the-philippines/">Condotels Meet Investors Business and Leisure Objectives in the Philippines</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>3 Bedroom Unit</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is condo layout may be too large of a space for solo living. Condo units with multiple rooms is ideal for starting families to have separate bedrooms for the kid/s.&nbsp; You will find ample space for living and dining areas and private spaces for the family. It will give you enough to grow in with your growing family.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>Read:</strong> <em><a href="http://localhost:3001/9-studio-condo-improvements-that-boost-property-value/">9 Studio Condo Improvements that Boost Property Value</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":2307,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/How-to-Make-Your-Condominium-Unit-Look-Bigger-07.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-2307"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Loft Unit</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Loft units are not typical condo layout in the Philippines but you can find some developers offering this type. It is a half room unit with an upstair area that may serve as your private sleeping space. You can have all the downstairs are for living and dining spaces. It does offer distinction in spaces even though the unit is small.&nbsp;It maybe quite challenging to design a small space to be functional but it can be rewarding.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>Read:</strong> <em><a href="http://localhost:3001/buying-a-condo-helpful-tips-before-making-that-big-purchase/">Buying a condo? Helpful tips before making that big purchase</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Whether you are buying or renting a condo unit. It is best that you know what you are looking for so you can decide what type of condo unit layout that fits you and your lifestyle.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/01/Choosing-the-Best-Type-of-Condo-Unit-for-You.jpg','views' => '53','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2021-01-13 02:49:03','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '535','title' => 'Pre-nuptial Agreement | Why is it important?','slug' => 'pre-nuptial-agreement-why-is-it-important','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Marriage is one of the most important and eventful milestone in one\'s life. A couple\'s union is not limited to the marriage contract signed but also in their goals &amp; dreams, in finances &amp; properties. When they say "two becomes one" in marriage, the same is true with the assets and properties owned by these individuals before getting married.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>What is a Prenutial Agreement?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A pre-nuptial agreement is a conditional agreement regarding the ownership of assets and properties before marriage. It is a legal document prepared &amp; signed before the wedding takes place and takes effect from the moment of celebration of the marriage. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:</strong> <em><a href="http://localhost:3001/five-basic-requirements-when-buying-a-property/">Five Basic Requirements When Buying a Property</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Why is prenuptial agreement important?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Under the<strong> Family Code of the Philippines, Executive Code No. 209</strong>, signed into law by then-President Corazon Aquino, it states that <strong><em>all properties acquired before or during the marriage will automatically be considered conjugal properties for those who got married on or after August 3, 1988.</em> </strong>This also means that all income that property owned prior to marriage will also be conjugal. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And in the event of legal separation, the property &amp; the income it generated will be equally divided by both parties. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>Now let us consider the marriage of <em><strong>Spouse A </strong></em>to <em><strong>Spouse B</strong></em>. They met one day in an event and they clicked. It was a "whirlwind romance" and both would say that they were madly in love with each other. <strong><em>Spouse A</em></strong> came from a middle-class earning family, recently graduated and just started working. <em><strong>Spouse B</strong></em> is from an affluent family and has worked for several years in one of their businesses.</p><p>If <em><strong>Spouse A</strong></em> marries the rich &amp; successful <em><strong>Spouse B</strong></em> who do not have any prenuptial agreement in place. <strong><em>Spouse A</em></strong>, by law, has the right to half of the properties and money <em><strong>Spouse B</strong></em> has. And if they separate, <strong><em>Spouse A</em></strong> will get half of the property and money even if these were inherited or worked for by <strong><em>Spouse B</em></strong>.</p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Will the properties be considered conjugal property after marriage?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In the absence of a Prenutial Agreement, the Family Code will be followed, where <strong>all existing properties owned by an individual will become conjugal property with his/her spouse upon marriage</strong>. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>Read:</strong> <a href="http://localhost:3001/property-ownership-before-during-and-after-marriage/">Property Ownership | Before, During and After Marriage</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Why do you need prenuptial agreement?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Pre-nuptial agreements are generally entered for several reasons:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li> Significant age difference</li><li>Considerable difference in wealth &amp; assets</li><li>Co-owner of a business/asset</li><li>To protect children from previous marriage/relationship</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>While conjugal ownership of all property is good in some cases, especially in handling and managing these. In some cases, it may present issues in some unions, and sometimes, a prenuptial agreement is a good instrument to address those issues even before they arise. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/01/Pre-nuptial-Agreement-Why-is-it-important-.jpg','views' => '52','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2021-01-14 02:02:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '536','title' => 'Will & Testament | Why is it important?','slug' => 'will-testament-why-is-it-important','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You might have heard some families after each others neck after the loss of a parent or a relative because of whom the properties go to. It is not always a good scenario and it can cause rift within the family.<br><br>Making sure that there won\'t be any conflict to arise within one family after one\'s death can be done. And this is through a legally binding contract called a will &amp; testament written by the person prior to an event of death.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:</strong> <a href="http://localhost:3001/transfer-title-deceased-parents/"><em>Transferring a Property Title From Deceased Parents in PH</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>What is a Will &amp; Testament?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Last will and testament</strong> outlines how the deceased person\'s possessions is to be managed. This is a binding contract that will say how these possessions like money and funds, real estate properties and assets will be distributed to a family member, a charity or any institutions the deceased person may have wished to leave it to. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:</strong><em><a href="http://localhost:3001/why-you-should-care-about-the-properties-of-your-deceased-parents/">Why You Should Care About The Properties of Your Deceased Parents?</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Why is will &amp; testament important?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Article 783 of Republic Act No. 386</strong>, or otherwise known as the Civil Code of the Philippines (“Civil Code”) defines the will as an "<em>act whereby a person is permitted, with the formalities prescribed by law, to control to a certain degree the disposition of his estate, to take effect after his death.</em>"</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Writing a will must be a personal act according to Article 784 and must not be forceful. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And in the event of death, all existing estates like properties and assets will be given or handed over to the person or institutions the deceased person may have stated it is given to. This ensures conflict and controversies regarding his estates is prevented.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>Read: </strong><em><a href="http://localhost:3001/providing-the-departed-one-a-home-of-their-own/">Providing the departed one a home of their own</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Why do you need a will &amp; testament?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>If you have a specific property that you want a person or family member to have, this makes sure that it is given to that person. A Will &amp; Testament is legally binding and ensures that your last wishes are carried out.</li><li>You get to decide on whose care your (minor) children will be left to and avoid that your children will be taken cared of by an institution or a some you do not like.</li><li>It also helps to take care of your children by assigning trust funds or estates placed in their names for financial support.</li><li>You can decide who your executor can be. An executor will carry out your wishes for you. It should be someone you trust with your estates and your wishes to be carried out.</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/01/Will-Testament-Why-is-it-important-.png','views' => '41','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2021-01-15 10:02:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '537','title' => 'Bukidnon ranks 5th in the list of richest provinces in the Philippines','slug' => 'bukidnon-ranks-5th-in-the-list-of-richest-provinces-in-the-philippines','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For the second consecutive year, Bukidnon has ranked as the 5th wealthiest province in the Philippines with total assets reaching P18.294 billion, according to the latest Commission on Audit\'s (COA) Annual Financial Report (AFR) for Local Government.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6758,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/137330176_1616964918495385_3583313669488561335_n.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6758"/><figcaption>[image credit: <a href="https://www.facebook.com/DTI.Region10/photos/pcb.1616966795161864/1616964915162052" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">DTI Region 10</a>]</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Based on the <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.coa.gov.ph/local-government-units-lgus/category/8757-2019#" target="_blank">COA’s 2019&nbsp;Annual Financial Report on LGUs</a>,&nbsp;the province\'s assets grew by P3.016 billion in 2019 from total assets of P15.278 billion in 2018. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://www.facebook.com/plugins/post.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2FDTI.Region10%2Fphotos%2Fa.545567935635094%2F1616964981828712%2F&amp;width=750&amp;show_text=true&amp;appId=180470228681693&amp;height=498" width="750" height="498" style="border:none;overflow:hidden" scrolling="no" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen="true" allow="autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture; web-share"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><br>Topping the list of richest provinces in the country are Cebu (P203.9 billion), Batangas (P20.793 billion), Rizal (P20.275 billion), and Davao de Oro (P20.099 billion).  Completing the list were&nbsp;the provinces of Surigao del Norte (P16.684 billion), Negros Occidental (P15.901 billion), Leyte (P13.54 billion), Palawan (P13.036 billion), and Iloilo (P13.034 billion).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The AFR also ranks the wealthiest cities and provinces in the country for 2019. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The top 10 list of richest cities for 2019 are Makati (P233.78 billion),&nbsp;Quezon City (P96.423 billion), Manila (P64.805 billion), Pasig (P45.639 billion), Cebu City (P34.711 billion), Mandaue City (P32.157 billion), Taguig (P29.065 billion), Caloocan (P20.599 billion), Pasay (P19.795 billion) and Davao City (P19.783 billion).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The top 10 richest municipalities are Cainta, Rizal (P4.933 billion), Limay, Bataan (P4.065 billion), Silang, Cavite (P3.842 billion), Mariveles, Bataan (P3.076 billion), Sual, Pangasinan (P2.989 billion), Caluya, Antique (P2.904 billion), Binangonan, Rizal (P2.336 billion), Tanay, Rizal (P2.209 billion), Calaca, Batangas (P2.12 billion) and Carmona, Cavite (P2.075 billion).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ: </strong><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.coa.gov.ph/index.php/local-government-units-lgus/category/8757-2019?download=44043:annual-financial-report-for-the-local-government-volume-i" target="_blank">Annual Financial Report for the Local Government</a>  </p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/01/filipino-homes-blog-post-cover-14.png','views' => '46','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2021-01-16 04:42:26','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '538','title' => 'Real Estate Salesperson | Do we have the right to choose a real estate broker?','slug' => 'real-estate-salesperson-do-we-have-the-right-to-choose-a-real-estate-broker','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Are you a real estate salesperson or are you planning to get into a real estate career?  The first step to a successful real estate career is to make sure you are making the right decisions. Since selling real estate property without a real estate broker license is prohibited by the Philippine Law, you are then required to find a real estate broker to "sponsor" you. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Do we have the right to choose a real estate broker?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A real estate agent can not work independently. Technically you are selling properties by yourself so you must work in behalf of the real estate broker or a real estate brokerage to be able to legally sell real estate property in the country.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You have the right to choose the real estate broker or agencies you are going to work with. You will find that real estate brokerage or companies are always recruiting salespeople. Just know that there are differences among real estate companies in its structure, and operations. Make sure to find a broker or agency that you like and with values that is also a right fit for you.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>How to find the right brokerage for you</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>First, you need to know what area/s you want to work in or cover. This may include the current city you live in and the neighbouring cities around it.</li><li>Check local real estate listings and find what brokers/brokerages that covers these areas and gauge the number of developers are on their listings.</li><li>Check the reputation of the brokerage and how established it is in the local area. In as much as you can, talk to salespersons under the brokerage to get the opinions on the working environment and culture in the company.</li><li>Check the location of the office if it is accessible to you and if the brokerage has local office branches in different cities you also want to cover. And if they have a large market and covers the area where you want to work in.</li><li>You may also need to ask the type of listings they have and the resources you can use. And if they effectively promote properties and agents alike.</li><li>Ofcourse you need to ask if there is any onboard trainings and requirements needed from you to become a salesperson under the brokerage. Also ask for the commission split and the benefit packages</li><li>Lastly, make sure to ask what are your obligations/responsibilities to the brokerage.</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":5891,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/3.png" alt="Filipino Homes, professional real estate agents in the Philippines" class="wp-image-5891"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Where to find Licensed Real Estate Brokers in the PH?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong><a href="https://rebap.com.ph">REBAP ( Real Estate Brokers Association of the Philippines)</a> </strong> is a group of dedicated licensed real estate brokers dedicated to professionalizing the real estate industry and raising the level of ethical standards of licensed real estate practitioners. The Real Estate Brokers Association of the Philippines, Inc. (REBAP) was established with this noble caused and has been around for more than forty years already. The organization has every chapter in each region of the Philippines.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href="https://realestatedirectory.org.ph"><strong>Philippine Real Estate Directory</strong></a> has specific contents like directories, main and profile directory, listings, Brokers’ manual, Buyer and Seller guides, tools and resources for real estate practice among other service that needed for real estate daily practice</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href="https://filipinohomes.com/"><strong>Filipino Homes</strong></a> is the largest comprehensive real estate solutions portal in the Philippines. It provides one-stop-shop services for real estate buyers and sellers and powered by its growing 10,000 property agents. Filipino Homes provides a full range of services including property management, in tandem with affiliate Rent.ph; foreclosure listings; and real estate insurance and consultancy services.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Finding the perfect brokerage for you can be challenge. You need to do your own research and make sure it is the best one for you. Your career growth and success starts with what brokerage you want to work and be affiliate with.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/01/Real-Estate-Salesperson-Do-we-have-the-right-to-choose-a-real-estate-broker.png','views' => '34','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2021-01-16 05:12:34','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '539','title' => '5 Social Media Sites for Real Estate Agents this 2021','slug' => '5-social-media-sites-for-real-estate-agents-this-2021','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Social media has become part of the daily lives of every Filipino. From the moment we wake up, to the dining, to work, and even the time we go to bed, <em>social media</em> just seems like everything. In fact a survey by Statista shows that <a href="https://newsinfo.inquirer.net/1362892/survey-filipinos-connected-to-social-media-almost-4-hours-daily">Filipinos connected to social media almost 4 hours daily</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>But as a real estate agent, you have to level up your social media game. Choosing the best social media platform is vital for you to find a wide audience, in the right platform and at the right time. As they say, <em>Fish where the fish are and save the rest for personal use</em>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Here are 5 best social media sites for every Filipino real estate agents this 2021:<br></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6787,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/pasted-image-0-1024x1024.png" alt="social media real estate
" class="wp-image-6787"/><figcaption>Data based on information from Global Web Index via DataReportal.&nbsp;</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#1 Facebook &amp; Messenger</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Facebook is still the most used social media platform in the Philippines. According to Statista, Facebook’s user population was over 800 million in Asia in 2020. And in the country alone, there were almost 74 million Facebook users as of 2019.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Having the widest reach of any of the social media for real estate agents, Facebook is ideal for real estate agent marketing. Filipinos rely on social media app as a primary source of news whilst entertainment and leisure.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#2 Instagram</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The top tier of Facebook is Instagram but more of a photo and video-sharing social network.. Accordingly, there were more than 10 million Instagram users in the Philippines in February 2020, which accounted for 9.6% of the population.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The beauty of Instagram is it allows you to get really creative about how you promote your listings. You can share an eye-catching photo of your listing that makes you look like a pro even if you don\'t have much experience. You can also use relevant hashtags for SEO, promote your personal brand and get really interactive with IG story &amp; IGTV.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>Related: <a href="http://localhost:3001/6-lead-generation-tips-and-tricks-for-new-real-estate-agents/">6 Simple Ways To Do Real Estate Lead Generation</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#3 Youtube</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>What most real estate agents failed to realize is that YouTube is a huge platform that gives you the opportunity to reach every kind of audience through interactive video marketing. Video is very much a significant part of the future of marketing as it has become and continues to be so popular in the country, especially with the <a href="http://localhost:3001/7-filipino-youtube-channels-to-learn-home-design-and-renovating-tricks/">growing trend of Vloggers and Influencers.</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Looking at the successful Youtubers now, there are three ways you can leverage on this platform as a real estate agent. It’s either you <strong>Entertain, Educate </strong>or <strong>Inspire</strong>. If you feel like you’re entertaining or funny or you have that alluring look that could catch people’s attention without even speaking, then create a channel for entertainment. But if you feel like you’re inspiring or you have knowledge to share that people don\'t know about, then do an educational channel. With videos that teach, entertain and enlighten, there’s no doubt you’ll achieve Youtube’s Silver or Gold Button!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#4 LinkedIn</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>LinkedIn is an ideal social media platform for estate agents as well. Not only can you establish connections and find quality leads, but it is one of the best networks where that allows you to build your professional portfolio and increase your credibility as a realtor.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In 2019, there were over 8 million Linkedin users in the Philippines, which accounted for 7.3% of the entire population. So there’s no denying that LinkedIn has successfully found its niche as the social platform for professionals like you.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>#5 Tiktok&nbsp;</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Despite its controversies concerning user privacy, <a href="https://www.onenews.ph/tiktok-still-the-most-downloaded-entertainment-app-in-phl-retains-global-popularity-despite-controversies">Tiktok still emerged as the Most Downloaded Entertainment App in the Philippines</a> and retained global popularity. And as a real estate agent, you have to keep with the trend as well.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Tiktok is not like Facebook, where you can post about your life or your business. You only have 15 seconds or 60 seconds to get your message across, so you have to strategically encapsulate your content but maintain the value. Because what you’re doing in the video doesn’t matter as much as the content. But the value that you’re bringing to the video is what wins your audience.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>Related: <a href="http://localhost:3001/10-social-media-post-ideas-for-real-estate-agents/">10 Social Media Post Ideas for Real Estate Agents</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/01/5-Best-Social-Media-Platforms-for-Real-Estate-Agents-2021.jpg','views' => '41','category_id' => '13','published_at' => '2021-01-18 07:46:18','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '540','title' => 'Where to apply or request for Birth Certificates, CENOMAR, and/or Marriage Certificates Online?','slug' => 'where-to-apply-or-request-for-birth-certificates-cenomar-and-or-marriage-certificates-online','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In the past, Filipinos have somehow gotten used to going to government agencies early in the day to acquire the service they need. Fortunately, for a couple of years now, various government agencies have started offering their services online. &nbsp;Applying and paying for civil registry documents (including birth certificates, marriage certificates, or Certificate of No Marriage Record (CENOMAR) from the Philippine Statistics Authority or PSA (formerly National Statistics Office or NSO),  for example, can now be done over the internet. Your requested certificates will be delivered to your home or office after several days.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Where to Request for Your Civil Registry Documents Online?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Philippine Statistics Authority’s&nbsp;<strong><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://www.psaserbilis.com.ph" target="_blank">PSA Serbilis</a></strong> is an online facility that allows you to submit requests for civil registry services.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6770,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><a href="https://www.psaserbilis.com.ph/Default.aspx"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/image-1024x576.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6770"/></a><figcaption><a href="https://www.psaserbilis.com.ph/Default.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">PSA Serbilis</a></figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipinos can request&nbsp;for a <strong>birth certificate</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>marriage certificate</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>death certificate</strong>, or&nbsp;<strong>CENOMAR</strong>&nbsp;(Certificate of No Marriage Record) online from the PSA (NSO), for delivery anywhere in the Philippines or abroad.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Birth Certificate</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A&nbsp;<strong>Birth Certificate</strong>&nbsp;is a vital record that establishes the birth of a child. It is an official form that gives details on the time and place of a person\'s birth, and his or her name, sex, mother\'s name, and (usually) father\'s name.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Information to be provided for the issuance of Birth Certificate:</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} -->
<ol><li>Number of copies you are requesting</li><li>Name (maiden name if married female)</li><li>Sex</li><li>Place of birth</li><li>Date of birth</li><li>Father’s name</li><li>Mother’s maiden name</li><li>Date of registration, if the birth certificate was late registered</li><li>Purpose of your request</li><li>Your relationship to the birth certificate owner</li></ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Birth certificate requests must be duly authorized as per&nbsp;<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.psaserbilis.com.ph/Secure/FAQs.aspx#D4" target="_blank">The Child and Youth Welfare Code (P.D. 603)</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:buttons {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-buttons aligncenter"><!-- wp:button -->
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link" href="https://www.psaserbilis.com.ph/default.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Click here to request now</a></div>
<!-- /wp:button --></div>
<!-- /wp:buttons -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Marriage Certificate</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A&nbsp;<strong>Marriage Certificate</strong>&nbsp;is a document that shows social union or a legal contract between people that creates kinship. This document contains the important details of the marriage, signed by the couple and by all in attendance. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Marriage certificates can be requested by the interested party by providing the following information to facilitate verification and issuance of certification:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Information to be provided for the issuance of Marriage Certificate:</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} -->
<ol><li>Number of copies you are requesting</li><li>Name of husband</li><li>Maiden name of wife</li><li>Place of marriage</li><li>Date of marriage</li><li>Date of registration, if the marriage certificate was late registered</li><li>Purpose of your request</li></ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:buttons {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-buttons aligncenter"><!-- wp:button -->
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link" href="https://www.psaserbilis.com.ph/default.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Click here to request now</a></div>
<!-- /wp:button --></div>
<!-- /wp:buttons -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Certificate of No Marriage (CENOMAR)</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A&nbsp;<strong>Certificate of No Marriage Record (CENOMAR)</strong> is a certification issued by the PSA stating that a person has not contracted any marriage. Also called a certificate of No Record of Marriage or Certificate of Singleness.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Information to be provided for the issuance of Certificate of No Marriage (CENOMAR):</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} -->
<ol><li>Number of copies you are requesting</li><li> Name </li><li> Sex</li><li> Place of birth</li><li> Date of birth</li><li> Mother’s maiden name</li><li> Father’s name</li><li> Purpose of your request</li></ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:buttons {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-buttons aligncenter"><!-- wp:button -->
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link" href="https://www.psaserbilis.com.ph/default.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Click here to request now</a></div>
<!-- /wp:button --></div>
<!-- /wp:buttons -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>How much do I pay?</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>LOCAL REQUEST: If delivery destination is within the Philippines</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>PHP 330.00</strong> per copy for copy issuance of birth or marriage certificates, and <strong>PHP 430.00</strong> per copy for Certificate of No Marriage Record (CENOMAR). The additional PHP 30.00 serves as the Documentary Stamp Tax (Sections 173 and 188 of the Tax Code, Revenue Memorandum Order 13-2008 and Revenue Regulations No. 4-2018) per copy issued.<br></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>FOREIGN REQUEST: If delivery destination is outside the Philippines</strong>:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>USD 20.30 </strong>per copy for copy issuance and <strong>USD 25.30</strong> per copy for CENOMAR.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>Important Note:</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>These civil registry documents can only be issued to:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} -->
<ol><li>The owner himself or through a duly authorized representative</li><li>His/her spouse, parent, direct descendants, guardian or institution legally-in-charge of him/her, if minor</li><li>The court or proper public official whenever absolutely necessary in  administrative, judicial or other proceedings to determine the identity of a person</li></ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you are the document owner and you are unable to receive the document, you may authorize a representative to do so on your behalf. Your authorized representative will have to present<br>the following to the courier:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>a. your signed authorization letter<br>b. your valid ID (with photo and signature)<br>c. the valid ID (with photo and signature) of your authorized representative</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:</strong> <em><a href="https://www.psaserbilis.com.ph/Secure/FAQs.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">PSA Serbilis | Frequently Asked Questions</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/01/filipino-homes-blog-post-cover-15.png','views' => '51','category_id' => '13','published_at' => '2021-01-19 02:54:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '541','title' => 'Divorce and Conjugal Property Ownership for Filipinos','slug' => 'divorce-and-conjugal-property-ownership-for-filipinos','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Divorce is the most common option for married individuals who want to separate or break their marital bond. Next to Vatican City, only one country does not recognize divorce, it is the Philippines. And while this is the absence of divorce in the country is somewhat workable for some Filipinos, it is burden for others.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Real estate lawyer, Atty. Joyce Villanueva says that "The most common issue on divorce in the Philippines is one involving mixed marriages." Either a Filipino married an alien (foreigner) or one of the Filipino couple became an alien and the other remains a Filipino citizen.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Now let us consider the marriage scenario of a Filipino <strong><em>Wife (W) </em></strong>to an alien  <strong><em>Husband (H)</em></strong>. <strong>W</strong> met <strong>H</strong>, an American citizen, while he was visiting the Philippines. They fell in love and decided to marry and move to United States of America. The marriage started off well but after a few years it gotten sour and <strong>H </strong>decided and filed for a divorce in the US. After the divorce was finalized, <strong>W</strong> left and went home to the Philippines to be with her family while <strong>H</strong> remained in the US.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A couple of years later,<strong> H</strong> found out that <strong>W</strong> has become successful in her business in the Philippines and was also dating a Filipino at that time.<br><br><strong>H </strong>decided to go to the Philippines knowing that the country does not recognize divorce to file a  case against <strong>W</strong>, alleging that the property<strong> W</strong> owned is considered conjugal property.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Under Article 116 of the Family Code, all Property acquired during marriage is presumed to be conjugal property in the absence of Prenuptial Agreement. The properties and its earnings is jointly owned by the both spouses as per Article 124, Family Code.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>"So even when <strong>H </strong>has no participation in the reaping of the disputed properties, if the disputed properties are conjugal in nature, H sill gets half of everything.", Atty. Villanueva explains.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Related Post:</strong> <em><a href="http://localhost:3001/property-ownership-before-during-and-after-marriage/">Property Ownership | Before, During and After Marriage</a></em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>How will the court decide on an issue involving a couple where one\'s country recognizes divorce and the other does not?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In the case of Van Dorn vs. Romillo [139 SCRA 139, No. L-68470 (October 8,1985)], the Supreme Court ruled that "aliens may obtain divorces abroad, which may be recognized in the Philippines, provided they are valid according to the national law.<br><br>Atty. Villanueva share that, "if the divorce obtained is valid under the laws of the United Stated, the said divorce is recognized in the Philippines"</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This means that<strong> H</strong> is no longer the husband of <strong>W </strong>with the validity of the divorce granted by his own country\'s court. And that the Philippine laws acknowledged the divorce obtained by <strong>H</strong> and on the eyes of both United States and the Philippines, <strong>H</strong> is no longer married to <strong>W</strong>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Conjugal property is referred to properties acquired during the validity of the marriage. Since the disputed properties between <strong>H</strong> &amp; <strong>W</strong> were acquired after the end of marriage, <strong>H</strong> has no right and legal capacity to demand a share of the property or its earnings.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Related Post: </strong><a href="http://localhost:3001/pre-nuptial-agreement-why-is-it-important/"><em>Pre-nuptial Agreement | Why is it important?</em></a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/01/Divorce-and-Conjugal-Property-Ownership-for-Filipinos.png','views' => '90','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2021-01-20 01:07:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '542','title' => 'How to Renew PRC License Online Without CPD units','slug' => 'how-to-renew-prc-license-online-without-cpd-units','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>Can I renew my expired PRC license without CPD units online?&nbsp;</em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The answer is <strong>YES</strong>.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Registered professionals can still renew their PRC ID without full compliance of the Continuing Professional Development (CPD) requirement <strong>until December 31, 2021</strong>. The better news is, the renewal of Professional Identification Cards (PIC) is now accepted online!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>How To Renew License Without CPD Units Online:</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Step #1</strong> Go to the official website of <a href="https://online.prc.gov.ph/">PRC – LERIS</a>&nbsp; to start the renewal application process.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Step #2</strong> Login to your LERIS account. If you don’t have any, register for one. To register, you only need to have:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Email address</li><li>Mobile Number</li><li>Personal information; employment and education</li><li>2×2 photo (in JPG format with white background and applicant wearing a formal collared top)</li><li>Valid ID</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Step #3</strong> Once logged in, you can choose among these options. To proceed with the online renewal process, choose <strong>“Renewal of License.</strong>”</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} -->
<ol><li>Exam Application- Online application of various licensure examinations with requirements to be submitted upon processing/issuance of Notice of Admission.</li><li>Exam Application (SPLBE)- Online application of various licensure examinations with requirements to be submitted upon processing/issuance of Notice of Admission. (For SPLBE applicants)</li><li>Initial Registration- Online Registration of new passers/successful examinees for the issuance of their licenses.</li><li>Initial Registration (SPLBE)- Online Registration of new passers/successful examinees for the issuance of their licenses. (For SPLBE passers)</li><li><strong>Renewal of License</strong> - Online renewal of Professional Identification Cards of Registered Professionals.</li><li>Verification- Online verification of rating of successful examinees and verification of license of registered professional.</li></ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here’s a sample screenshot:&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/l8tR7-CAWh8naOs3DDME1cQFeROSdWWUT27gcFW1wseEqmocBboK2dJ4JQC_NByK8X_g06kNmK59LL3DNOapNFMUcqtOA5Yrey4abfT-WryLa1pNzeCgqAOm3iFl99afEVCXtP23" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Professions allowed to renew online:</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Aeronautical Engineer</li><li>Agricultural and Biosystems Engineer</li><li>Agriculturist</li><li>Architect</li><li>Certified Mine Foreman</li><li>Certified Plant Mechanic</li><li>Certified Public Accountant</li><li>Certified Quarry Foreman</li><li>Chemical Engineer</li><li>Chemical Technician</li><li>Chemist</li><li>Civil Engineer</li><li>Criminologist</li><li>Customs Broker</li><li>Dental Hygienist</li><li>Dental Technologist</li><li>Dentist</li><li>Electronics Engineer</li><li>Electronics Technician</li><li>Environmental Planner</li><li>Fisheries Technologist</li><li>Foreign Medical Professional</li><li>Forester</li><li>Geodetic Engineer</li><li>Geologic Aide</li><li>Geologist</li><li>Guidance Counselor</li><li>Interior Designer</li><li>Landscape Architect</li><li>Librarian</li><li>Master Plumber</li><li>Mechanical Engineer</li><li>Medical Laboratory Technician</li><li>Medical Technologist (MedTech)</li><li>Metallurgical Engineer</li><li>Metallurgical Plant Foreman</li><li>Midwife and Midwife (RA 2382)</li><li>Mining Engineer</li><li>Naval Architect and Marine Engineer</li><li>Nurse</li><li>Nutritionist Dietitian</li><li>Occupational Therapist and Occupational Therapist Technician</li><li>Ocular Pharmacologist</li><li>Optometrist</li><li>Pharmacist</li><li>Physical Therapist</li><li>Physician (Medical Doctor)</li><li>Professional Electrical Engineer</li><li>Professional Electronics Engineer</li><li>Professional Mechanical Engineer</li><li>Professional Teacher</li><li>Psychologist</li><li>Psychometrician</li><li>Radiologic Technologist</li><li>Real Estate Appraiser</li><li>Real Estate Broker</li><li>Real Estate Consultant</li><li>Registered Electrical Engineer</li><li>Registered Master Electrician</li><li>Respiratory Therapist</li><li>Sanitary Engineer</li><li>Social Worker</li><li>Veterinarian</li><li>X-Ray Technologist</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:file {"href":"blob:https://filipinohomes.com/73b011bb-3831-44bc-89fe-468a39bad278"} -->
<div class="wp-block-file"><a href="https://filipinohomes.com/73b011bb-3831-44bc-89fe-468a39bad278"><strong>DOWNLOAD</strong>: LERIS Online Step-by-step Procedure</a><a href="https://filipinohomes.com/73b011bb-3831-44bc-89fe-468a39bad278" class="wp-block-file__button" download>Download</a></div>
<!-- /wp:file -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>Where to Claim PRC ID</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>After renewing your license online, your new PRC ID card can be claimed from your chosen PRC branch or satellite office. There’s also a delivery option for NCR applicants. Make sure to choose a time and date of delivery/pick-up.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Important Notice: </strong>CPD is a requirement in the renewal of the Professional Identification Cards (PICs) of all registered and licensed professionals under the regulation of the PRC, as mandated by Republic Act (R.A) No. 10912 or the Continuing Professional Development Act of 2016.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>PRC made this extension noting that the country is now under the State of Public Health Emergency and State of Calamity due to the spread of Coronavirus Disease 2019 (COVID-19).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

