  array('id' => '543','title' => '[Feature] Rent.ph Offers Online Program to Become a Certified Rent Manager','slug' => 'feature-rent-ph-offers-online-program-to-become-a-certified-rent-manager','content' => '<!-- wp:image {"id":6795,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/img5-1024x379.jpg" alt="Rent Manager Program by Rent.PH" class="wp-image-6795"/><figcaption> Rent Manager Program by Rent.PH</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong><a href="http://rent.ph">Rent.ph</a></strong>, a nationwide listing for rental properties and property-related services for renters, rent and property managers, agents, and real estate owners, now offers a free online course to become a rent manager in the country. The course consists of a two-part webinar and an online examination. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6807,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/132080255_10221955416328689_2360532317058635844_n-1.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-6807"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The first run of the program has produced 700 graduates from all over the Philippines The first session held on December 21, 2020, was on "Rental Opportunities Amidst COVID-19" with RNB Property Management founder, <strong>Raynald Bamba</strong>. Chairman of the Building Owners and Managers Association of the Philippines, <strong>Eduardo Manahan</strong>, was invited for the second session on "Property Rental Management" conducted on January 7, 2021. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":6806,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/photo_2021-01-15_13-58-16-1.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-6806"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The graduates who have completed the two-part webinar of the Rent Manager course will automatically become <em>Rent Manager Specialist</em> when they successfully pass the online examination prepared by&nbsp;Rent.ph. These specialists will become<em> Certified Rent Manager</em>s once they manage to complete rental agreements effectively and efficiently.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The second batch for the Rent Manager course is expected to start in February 2021. Join the roster of rent managers, and sign up at <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://www.rentmanager.ph/" target="_blank">http://www.rentmanager.ph/</a> to keep updated.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>About the Rent Manager Program</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"left","id":6797,"width":144,"height":26,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="alignleft size-large is-resized"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/image-1.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6797" width="144" height="26"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The <strong>Rent Manager Program</strong> is a peek into the world of Property Management. The course will specifically dive into Property Management and the various aspects of running a Rental Property as a Rent Manager. It teaches students to oversee real estate properties on behalf of owners with the primary goal to maintain the property\'s value and make sure it generates income.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>To learn more about the Rent Manager Program and how you can sign up for free, check out their website here&nbsp;<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://www.rentmanager.ph/" target="_blank">http://www.rentmanager.ph/</a><br><br></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/01/filipino-homes-blog-post-cover-16.png','views' => '42','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2021-01-22 01:30:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '544','title' => 'Unlawful Detainer | When a Lessee is Unable to Pay Rent','slug' => 'unlawful-detainer-when-a-lessee-is-unable-to-pay-rent','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A property offered for lease is generally seen as income generating property. The property owner has invested on buying or building that property to have it rented. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>So what happens when a lessee or renter is unable to pay rent?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The term <strong>UNLAWFUL DETAINER</strong> refers to the conduct of a lessee who is in possession of an apartment or leased property and refuses to leave the premises upon the expiration or termination of the lease.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>Take in the case of Ms. Lessee who rented an apartment from Mr. Lessor. Ms. Lessee is a single woman who lives alone in the apartment she rented and always pays on time. Mt. Lessor is a single man who happens to take interest in Ms. Lessee and one day took the courage to asked her out. After a few months of dating Ms. Lessee &amp; Mr. Lessor are now exclusively dating. While in the relationship, Ms. Lessee stop paying rent on the apartment and Mr. Lessor tolerated this.</em><br><br><em>After a few more months into dating, the relationship led to a break-up. Both were heartbroken and did not consider getting back together. Now that they are back to lessor-lessee relationship, Mr. Lessor started to charge Ms. Lessee for rent.</em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>Ms. Lessee started paying for her rent after the break-up but her depression from it also started her into controllable shopping sprees. She eventually concurred huge credit card bills and was not able to pay rent for four consecutive months as she struggled with her finances.</em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>Mr. Lessor now demands Ms. Lessee to pay her rent and to vacate the apartment she is renting from him. But Ms. Lessee never paid rent despite the demand letter from Mr. Lessor.</em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>What is the legal action can a lessor make against a lessee who is unable to pay rent?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When there is failure to pay rent, the Lessee has already committed a violation against the Lease Contract between her and the Lessor. It is because of this violation that causes the action against the Lessee as well as the right to consider the (lease) contract terminated.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Always make a clear communication with your Lessee or Lessor for situations where the Lessee is unable to pay rent. That way the Lessee is aware of the consequences where one is unable to pay the rent.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/01/Unlawful-Detainer-When-a-Lessee-is-Unable-to-Pay-Rent.png','views' => '43','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2021-01-23 08:18:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '545','title' => 'How to become a Rent Manager','slug' => 'how-to-become-a-rent-manager','content' => '<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>What is a Rent Manager?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Rent Manager </strong>is a registered trademark under the Intellectual Property Office (IPO) of the Philippines complied and filed by Rent.ph. A certified Rent Manager is a professional real estate practitioner who has successfully completed the Rent Manager Program.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong><em>READ: </em></strong><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/feature-rent-ph-offers-online-program-to-become-a-certified-rent-manager/" target="_blank">Rent.ph Offers Online Program to Become a Certified Rent Manager</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://cdn.pixabay.com/photo/2020/05/31/10/22/give-5242150_960_720.jpg" alt="Give, Key, Receive, Hand, Keys, Real Estate, Rent, Sale"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>How to become a Rent Manager</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong><a href="http://rent.ph/">Rent.ph</a></strong> has started a free online course to become a Rent Manager in the country. The course consists of a two-part webinar and an online examination. The graduates who have completed the two-part webinar of the Rent Manager course will automatically become <em>Rent Manager Specialist</em> when they successfully pass the online examination prepared by&nbsp;Rent.ph. These specialists will become<em> Certified Rent Manager</em>s once they manage to complete rental agreements effectively and efficiently.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Two-Part Webinar </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Interested practitioners will need to attend a 2-part webinar about property management. Each session is about 1.5 hours long.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>What you\'ll learn</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} -->
<ol><li>Understand the rental process from showing the property to a potential tenant to moving in.</li><li>Understand the importance of preventative maintenance and handling ongoing maintenance requests.</li><li>Establish a foundation of policies and procedures to help manage property operations, tenants, and maintenance.</li><li>Understand the concept of housing laws and how they affect the way you manage a property.</li><li>Understand the importance of excellent service in a Property Management career and the business or operations of a property.</li></ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="http://www.rentmanager.ph/img/img3.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Accreditation</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>An online examination will be given to those who have attended the 2-part webinar. Passers will be given a digital Certificate of Accreditation and will become a Rent Manager Specialist.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Specialists will need complete rental agreements effectively and efficiently to become Certified Rent Managers. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The first batch of <em>Rent Manager Specialists</em> has completed the course on January 7, 2021. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The second batch is expected to open in February 2021. Join the roster of rent managers, and sign up at <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://www.rentmanager.ph/" target="_blank">http://www.rentmanager.ph/</a> to keep updated.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>About the Rent Manager Program</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"left","id":6797,"width":144,"height":26,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="alignleft size-large is-resized"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/image-1.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6797" width="144" height="26"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The <strong>Rent Manager Program</strong> is a peek into the world of Property Management. The course will specifically dive into Property Management and the various aspects of running a Rental Property as a Rent Manager. It teaches students to oversee real estate properties on behalf of owners with the primary goal to maintain the property\'s value and make sure it generates income.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>To learn more about the Rent Manager Program and how you can sign up for free, check out their website here&nbsp;<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://www.rentmanager.ph/" target="_blank">http://www.rentmanager.ph/</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

