<!-- /wp:core-embed/youtube -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/02/ANC-Market-Edge-with-FH-Founder-Anthony-Leuterio.jpg','views' => '58','category_id' => '10','published_at' => '2021-02-12 03:43:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '563','title' => 'Developers, POGOs required to register with AMLC','slug' => 'developers-pogos-required-to-register-with-amlc','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Real estate developers, brokers, Philippine offshore gaming operators (POGOs), and OGO-service providers (OGO-SPs) are required to register with the electronic reporting system of the Anti-Money Laundering Council (AMLC) by mid-March.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This as real estate developers (REDs), real estate brokers (REBs), offshore gaming operators (OGOs), and OGO-service providers (OGO-SPs) are now covered persons <a href="http://www.amlc.gov.ph/publications/16-news-and-announcements/257-advisory-for-real-estate-developers-real-estate-brokers-offshore-gaming-operators-ogo-and-ogo-service-providers">under Republic Act (RA) No. 11521</a>, which strengthened the Anti-Money Laundering Act of 2001.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And as covered persons, they are now required to report all covered and suspicious transactions to the AMLC&nbsp;within the period prescribed and for the threshold amount fixed by the law.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>“If real estate developers and brokers do not submit certificates of [their] registration [with the AMLC], banks and other covered persons may refuse to open a bank account or to continue business relationships with them. The intention of this requirement is to avoid abuse of the Philippine financial system,” AMLC Executive Director Mel Georgie B. Racela said in a text message. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Registration with the AMLC\'s system is online and free</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Registration with the AMLC\'s system is can be done online and free of charge. AMLC said that real estate developers, real estate brokers, as well as POGOs and their service providers (OGO-SPs), need to register by March 16, 2021.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It is said that <em>failure to register would mean failure to electronically file covered and suspicious transaction reports with the AMLC, which is a money laundering offense per Section 4 of the AMLA.</em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Mr. Racela noted this is a criminal offense under the amended AMLA, which cites <em>“extreme circumstances where there is clear intention not to report.”</em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Those who fail to register may also request an extension with the AMLC’s Compliance and Supervision Group, citing specific reasons, Mr. Racela said.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Employees of real estate developers and brokers do not need to register individually so long as their employers register with the AMLC.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>“As of date, none has registered, but the AMLC has been receiving a lot of inquiries regarding the registration as well as requests for training and seminars from various real estate brokers’ associations,” Mr. Racela said.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Based on AMLC rules, failure to register with the electronic reporting system within the prescribed period is considered as a serious violation. Penalties will depend on a covered entity’s asset size: those with assets worth P10 million and below may pay P10,000 to a maximum of P500,000, while those with assets worth P50 billion and above may pay a maximum of P5 million.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Under RA 11521, entities regulated by the Philippine Amusement and Gaming Corp. including POGOs and their service providers are required to report a single casino cash transaction equivalent to P5 million.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Meanwhile, President Rodrigo R. Duterte signed <a href="https://www.officialgazette.gov.ph/2021/01/29/republic-act-no-11521/">RA No. 11521</a> on January 29, 2021, into law in order to address gaps in its “dirty money” regulations ahead of the Feb. 1 deadline set by the Financial Action Task Force (FATF).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em><strong>READ</strong>: <a href="http://localhost:3001/duterte-expands-amla-to-include-real-estate-developers-and-brokers/">Duterte expands AMLA to include real estate developers and brokers</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>This news article was originally published by <a href="https://www.bworldonline.com/developers-told-to-register-with-amlc/">Business World</a>.</em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Relevant links:</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><em><a href="https://portal.amlc.gov.ph/amlc/">AMLC Website Portal</a></em></li><li><em><a href="http://www.amlc.gov.ph/2015-12-09-07-34-10/amlc-registration">Registration Procedure</a></em></li><li><em><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://www.amlc.gov.ph/images/PDFs/AMLC%20Registration%20and%20Reporting%20Guidelines.pdf" target="_blank">AMLC Registration and Reporting Guidelines</a></em></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/02/Developers-POGOs-required-to-register-with-AMLC.jpg','views' => '40','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2021-02-16 04:05:15','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '564','title' => 'Who Inherits the Property of a Filipino with an Acquired Foreign Citizenship?','slug' => 'who-inherits-the-property-of-a-filipino-with-an-acquired-foreign-citizenship','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>What happens to the rights of a Filipino who acquired foreign citizenship? Will he or she lose his or her rights as a Filipino? How will it affect their rights in land ownership and property acquisition in the Philippines?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A<strong> Former Filipino</strong> is a Filipino who, after several years of working and  living in a foreign country, decides to denounce his/her Filipino citizenship to acquire the foreign citizenship. <strong>Atty. Rex JMA Fernandez </strong>shares the who will have the right to inherit a former Filipino\'s properties in the Philippine.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>If a former Filipino dies, who will inherit his/her properties in the Philippines?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A lot of people have a misunderstanding that when a Filipino acquires foreign citizenship, he or she loses any rights a filipino citizen has. "That is not true," says Atty. Fernandez. He added "Filipinos retain his/her rights of succession. This has many implications, including the rights to succeed from the spouse despite being divorced but without nullity of marriage."&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>Take in the case of now divorced Filipinos, <strong>Spouse A &amp; B</strong>, in the United States of America. Thy have who decided to live abroad for several years and has also acquired US citizenship. Their marriage was rocky and was not going well. So they had decided to end their marriage and got divorced in the US. They have yet to nullify their marriage in the Philippines when Spouse A passed away due to an illness. She left a few properties back in her home country, Philippines, that is still under her name. This led to her siblings and estranged husband are arguing on who has the right to properties in the Philippines which are still under her name.&nbsp;</p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Atty. Fernandez explains, "The spouse is an heir of the spouse. If a spouse in the Philippines dies the surviving spouse whether in the Phillipines or outside or even divorced but not annulled can succeed to the dead spouse properties."</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>READ:</strong> <a href="http://localhost:3001/can-a-former-filipino-with-acquired-foreign-citizenship-buy-a-property-in-the-philippines/"><em>Can a Former Filipino with acquired foreign citizenship buy a property in the Philippines?</em></a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This means that the properties left my Spouse A in her death, by law, should go to the husband even though he is a US citizen and they have divorced in the US prior to her death. This is because the law respects the marriage between them that was not annulled or nullified before her demise. In the Philippine courts, Spouse A &amp; B is still married at the time of Spouse A\'s untimely demise.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This means if a Filipino acquires a foreign citizenship and divorce his/her spouse, the remaining spouse will have the rights to any properties left if the marriage has yet to be annulled or nullified at the time of death.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/02/FILIPINOHOMES-BLOGS-XYZA-YAPE3.jpg','views' => '59','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2021-02-17 01:25:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '565','title' => 'Can a Former Filipino with acquired foreign citizenship buy a property in the Philippines?','slug' => 'can-a-former-filipino-with-acquired-foreign-citizenship-buy-a-property-in-the-philippines','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A good number of Filipinos work and live abroad. A good percentage of them find that living in the foreign country is good for their family and eventually consider acquiring citizenship in that country. But what if that person is still interest in purchasing property n the Philippines. Does the former Filipino has the right to purchase a property of has he/she forfeited his/her right to buy property in the Philippines?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A Former Filipino is someone who has denounce his or her Filipino citizenship over a foreign one. This is a bold move and one with implications for the person if he/she takes interest in the Philippine real estate.. <strong>Atty. Rex JMA Fernandez </strong>shares the rights to purchase a property for a former Filipino in the Philippines real estate. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Can a Former Filipino with acquired foreign citizenship purchase a property in the Philippines?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It is a common misunderstanding that once a person has denounce his citizenship for a foreign one, he or she has also lost his or her rights to purchase a property in the country. Atty. Fernandez says that "Filipinos retain his/her rights of succession. This has many implications."</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>Let us say for example that<strong> Lady A</strong> has worked in the United States of America right after she graduated from university for more than 10 years now. She has taken interest in applying for citizenship in the US. But she has plans to purchase several properties in the Philippines as a fallback and an investment. Now, she is having second thoughts about whether to denounce her Filipino citizenship over the foreign one or apply for a dual citizenship.</p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>READ:</strong> <a href="http://localhost:3001/who-inherits-the-property-of-a-filipino-with-an-acquired-foreign-citizenship/"><em>Who Inherits the Property of a Filipino with an Acquired Foreign Citizenship?</em></a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As a former Filipino, you can still buy parcels of land and other real estate properties. The <strong>Foreign Investment Incentives Act of 1991</strong> allows former Filipinos to buy parcels of land but limited to a maximum area. A Former Filipino can purchase parcels of land in urban or rural areas with the maximum of 5,000 square meters or 3 hectares.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Atty. Fernandez also adds, "But the law is clear that what you buy the first time is what you can only buy. If you buy an urban land, you can only buy an urban land and rural if rural the fist time. The former Filipino can an override this limitations if he or she repatriates him/herself through dual citizenship or revoking the acquired foreign citizenship." </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This means that if Lady A denounces her Filipino citizenship and acquires a US citizenship, she is still allowed, by rights, to purchase, a land property in the Philippines but it will come with limitations. If she has dual citizenship by acquiring a foreign citizenship but retaining her Filipino citizenship, she will able to exercise her rights without limitations when purchasing a property in her home country.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/02/FILIPINOHOMES-BLOGS-XYZA-YAPE1.jpg','views' => '83','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2021-02-18 06:08:12','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '566','title' => 'How to bid or buy a PAG-IBIG Acquired or Foreclosed Property this Pandemic','slug' => 'how-to-bid-or-buy-a-pag-ibig-foreclosed-property','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With the Philippine real estate boom, there are a lot of options for property investments. Prices are high nowadays and some homebuyers consider getting foreclosed properties for better deals and purchase a property for a lesser price.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Foreclosed Properties are acquired properties being sold by the lending institution or bank to recover the defaulted loan taken out by its previous owner.&nbsp; You will find foreclosed properties available for sale in Banks and on the Pagibig HMDF website. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The <a href="https://pagibigfundservices.com">PAG-IBIG Home Development Mutual Fund (HDMF) </a>is a Philippine government-owned and controlled corporation that provides affordable house financing for Filipinos. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>How do you bid for Pag-IBIG Foreclosed Properties this Pandemic?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7017,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/D404BF2B-586E-4417-8382-1092D1C330F0-1024x556.jpeg" alt="PAG-IBIG FORCLOSED " class="wp-image-7017"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>Check out the list of Foreclosed Properties</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Pag-IBIG releases the list of available foreclosed properties for bidding on their website. Visit the Pag-IBIG Fund website and click on Properties for Sale.&nbsp; You will find announcements and updates about acquired properties. Check the listings from the location where you want to bid.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>1] Properties Under Negotiated Sale<br>2] Properties Under Public Auctions (No Discount)<br>3] Public Auctions (With Discount)</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>Visit &amp; check the property</strong> personally</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Once you identified the property to bid for, visit the site personally. Visit and locate the property first before making a bid. That way, you will see the actual condition of the property you want to acquire. The listing from the website will tell you whether the property is occupied or not. If it is occupied, you may not be able to see the interiors of the property or go near it though. Also, remember if you win the bidding, you buy the property as-is. Pag-IBIG does not disclose any damage, history, or renovation needs.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:</strong> <a href="http://localhost:3001/foreclosed-property-why-people-are-buying-these-cheaper-properties/"><em>Foreclosed Property – Why people are buying these cheaper properties</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>Submit Offer to Purchase</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7018,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/EB99BA6A-FCD4-42C0-B45D-E038D341C2C0-1024x527.jpeg" alt="PAG-IBIG FORCLOSED " class="wp-image-7018"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Pag-ibig bidding is a closed type of bidding. Meaning, you cannot bid for more just to outbid the winner. You will only know how much your competitors bid for the property during the bidding session (<em>or during the announcement of winners already</em>) and you cannot edit the amount you placed.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The list from Pagibig will give you the minimum bid amount. You can choose to bid for the same price listed or go slightly higher. Complete the OFFER TO BID  form and Acknowledgement. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>READ:</strong> <a href="http://localhost:3001/pag-ibig-why-is-my-property-tagged-as-foreclosed/"><em>PAG-IBIG | Why is my property tagged as foreclosed?</em></a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Buyer must accomplish and submit an <strong>Offer to Purchase</strong> indicating the preferred mode of payment in a sealed envelope. <strong>You will need to submit the amount of your bid in cash or check on the day of the bidding. If you lose, you can get it back the day after.</strong> You will find all the information you need for the Offer Purchase, dropbox &amp; the schedule of the bidding session on the <a href="http://www.pagibig.gov.ph">Pag-IBIG website.</a> Drop the sealed envelope in a dropbox according to the schedule. Cut-off time for submission of offer/s is at 5:00 p.m. After the cut-off, no more offers will be accepted from unregistered buyers after the cut-off time and date. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>After selecting a property from the list and submitted Offer to Purchase (OTP) to Pag-IBIG Fund in a sealed envelope, you will then wait for the announcement of bid winners.  The determination of winning bidders shall be monitored by a representative from&nbsp;Commission on Audit (COA). Attendance of the bidder/s in the venue is not required. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The bidder who offers the highest bid shall be declared as the winner. The result of the sealed public auction shall be released and posted on the Pag-IBIG Fund\'s official website at <a href="http://www.pagibigfund.gov.ph">www.pagibigfund.gov.ph</a>.   </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Any notification sent by Pag-IBIG Fund through email or SMS shall be sufficient compliance to the notification requirements and presumed to be deemed received by the buyer. In this regard, the Bidder shall ensure that the contact number and email address indicated on the Offer to Bid are active. The bidder shall inform Pag- IBIG Fund immediately of any changes on his/ her contact number.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The winning bidder is required to pay his/ her BID BOND equivalent to five percent (5%) of the BID OFFER and shall be paid within 3 working days after the publication of the winning bidders. It shall be in Philippine Currency and maybe in the form&nbsp;of cash or manager’s check payable to Pag-IBIG Fund. It shall likewise serve as the down payment of the winning bidder. Bidders must check the results from the website.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For the remaining 90% of the price, You have the option to pay it in;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} -->
<ol><li>Spot cash</li><li>Short term Loan: Monthly installment of the entire amount for 12 months plus interest</li><li>Long Term Loan: Payable up to 30 yrs monthly amortization (with conditions)</li></ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ: </strong><a href="http://localhost:3001/5-simple-guidelines-purchasing-foreclosed-house/"><em>5 Simple Guidelines In Purchasing A Foreclosed House</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is the new guidelines of buying foreclosed properties through Pagibig HDMF this pandemic. Guidelines may change from time to time. Please visit their official website for a more updated guidelines in buying foreclosed properties or acquired properties for sale. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/02/FILIPINOHOMES-BLOGS-XYZA-YAPE.jpg','views' => '166','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2021-02-19 06:04:44','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '567','title' => 'How to apply for a housing loan in the Philippines if you are a foreigner','slug' => 'how-to-apply-for-a-housing-loan-in-the-philippines-if-you-are-a-foreigner','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In recent years, there has been a growing interest of foreigners to own real estate property in the country. &nbsp;However, Philippine law is strict when it comes to foreigners acquiring properties in the country.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>What types of real estate properties can a foreigner own in the Philippines?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>While purchasing a property in the Philippines is possible for a foreigner, there are limitations as to what property and how much a non-Filipino can buy.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>By law, non-Filipinos cannot own land in the Philippines.&nbsp;&nbsp;They may buy condominium units, but this is still subject to a&nbsp;40-percent restriction for foreigners.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:</strong>  <a href="http://localhost:3001/how-can-a-foreigner-own-a-property-in-the-philippines/" data-type="post" data-id="6931" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">How can a foreigner own a property in the Philippines?</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6955,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/philippines-5469389_1280-576x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-6955"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>What types of mortgages are available?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With an economy that’s growing and a property market that’s hot among foreign investors, banks have become a bit more relaxed, and home loans are now made available to foreigners.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There are local and global banks in the country offering a wide variety of mortgage products. Here are some banks you can look at. We recommend you contact each bank individually, for an individual assessment and up-to-date information.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.bdo.com.ph/mobile/personal/loans/home-loan" target="_blank">BDO</a></li><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.citibank.com.ph/gcb/loans/improve_your_home.htm" target="_blank">Citibank</a> </li><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.maybank.com.ph/en/personal/loans/maxihome-loan/home-acquisition.page?" target="_blank">Maybank</a></li><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://metrobank.com.ph/homeloan/FAQs/default.aspx" target="_blank">Metrobank</a></li><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.hsbc.com.ph/mortgages/" target="_blank">HSBC</a></li><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.bpihousingloans.com/pages?page=frequently-asked-questions" target="_blank">BPI Bank</a></li><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.rcbc.com/home-loans" target="_blank">RCBC Bank</a></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When choosing a bank for a home loan, weigh your options based on interest rates, payment terms, and processing period.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>What are the legal requirements needed?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The list of documents needed will depend on the bank you use. You will most likely be asked for the following:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Alien Certificate of Registration (ACR)</li><li>Copies of your personal identification documents (passport), your visa type, and validity</li><li>Proof of legal residence in the Philippines</li><li>Documents to support your application and proof of income (certificate of employment, bank certificate, etc)</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You might also need to have your paperwork translated by a sworn translator in order for the bank to accept it.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>What are the fees to be paid for?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You’re likely to have fees to pay such as administrative fees and legal costs when you arrange a mortgage. The exact costs will vary.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can also expect to pay the following fees when purchasing a property in the country:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Documentary stamps tax: 1.5% of purchase costs in most cases</li><li>Transfer tax: 0.5% to 0.75% of the house price, depending on the municipality you’re buying in</li><li>Notary fees: depends on the deal arranged, average of about 1% to 1.5%</li><li>Possible loan arrangement fees</li><li>Registration fee: based on the property price and location</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/02/filipino-homes-blog-post-cover-25.png','views' => '243','category_id' => '19','published_at' => '2021-02-26 10:26:23','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '568','title' => 'Building Smarter and Future-Proof Homes is the New Normal','slug' => 'building-smarter-and-future-proof-homes-is-the-new-normal','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The year 2020 was a challenging time for the property sector, but there had been signs of recovery from the later part of the year. The Philippine Central Bank expects a strong recovery this year with a 7.8 percent growth [<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.asiapropertyhq.com/philippines-real-estate-market" target="_blank">Asia Property HQ</a>]. A report from <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www2.colliers.com/en-ph/research/philippine-property-outlook-2021" target="_blank">Colliers Philippines</a>&nbsp;also indicates that the property market is expected to bounce back. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Property experts remain optimistic of the opportunities ahead, as investors and homebuyers with more purchasing power start to regain their confidence in the market [<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.lamudi.com.ph/realestate-trends/?" target="_blank">source</a>],</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7038,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/16200657610_98344dfc66_b.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7038"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The lifestyle changes brought about by the pandemic emphasized the need for digital connectivity in property developments. There is an increased demand for "smart homes" in the country. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Today\'s buyers look for power, water, and internet connectivity. A strong and reliable connectivity in the area is one of key factors that make customers decide to purchase a property.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7041,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/grovemade-RvPDe41lYBA-unsplash-1024x683.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7041"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As many companies will most likely continue to implement work-from-home schemes moving forward, homebuyers are looking for property development projects that are adaptable to the work-from-home setup.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>READ:</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/2021-ph-real-estate-trends-homebuyers-are-looking-out-for/" target="_blank">2021 PH Real Estate Trends Homebuyers are Looking Out For</a></li><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/do-you-work-from-home-buy-your-next-home-with-your-office-in-mind/" target="_blank">Do you work from home? Buy your next home with your office in mind</a></li><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/sustainable-architecture-the-new-normal/" target="_blank">Sustainable Architecture: The New Normal</a></li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/webinar-filipino-homes-plus-to-introduce-homes-that-are-designed-for-new-normal-living/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Filipino Homes Plus to introduce homes that are designed for new normal living</a></li><li><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/ph-property-sector-remains-optimistic-amid-covid-19-threat/" target="_blank">PH Property Sector Remains Optimistic Amid COVID-19 Threat</a></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/02/filipino-homes-blog-post-cover-24.png','views' => '71','category_id' => '16','published_at' => '2021-02-27 07:17:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '569','title' => 'Qualities That Make a Good Real Estate Agent','slug' => 'qualities-that-make-a-good-real-estate-agent','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you’re looking to buy or sell a property, you will need a good real estate agent or a <em>realtor </em>in that journey. Forgoing a partnership with a real estate agent not only saves you a lot of time and effort but also allows you to gain significant insights that can help you navigate your <a href="http://localhost:3001/real-estate-buying-process-developer/">homebuying process</a>.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>However, not all realtors are one and the same. A real estate agent might seem like a very straightforward job, but in reality, it can be as diverse as each realtor represents. They all have different experience levels and expertise.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So what makes a good real estate agent? Let’s take a look at the top qualities you should be looking for that makes a real estate superstar.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em>Related post: </em><a href="http://localhost:3001/tips-to-help-you-find-a-superstar-real-estate-agent/"><em>Tips to help you find a superstar real estate agent</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>Communicates regularly with client</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Communication is key! One of the main indicators that make a good real estate agent is being proactive and how well they’re able to communicate.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We know that the real estate market is time-sensitive, so you need an agent who communicates well and constantly keeps you in the loop about your current buying or selling situation. This helps keep you confident about the progress of the deal. If an agent is unresponsive and stays too long without getting in touch, you better get off and look for better ones.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>Highly knowledge of the local area</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We always say this. In real estate, <em>knowledge is power. </em>A good agent must have all-encompassing market knowledge (in theory and in practice) which requires deep understanding of the location you are in.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Before proceeding to any transaction, make sure that you critically ask your prospective agents a handful of questions about the local area. Ask about the amenities, its community, the <a href="http://localhost:3001/checklist-on-choosing-a-good-neighborhood/">neighborhood</a>, etc. Their responses will tell you how well they know the area and how honest they are in giving answers and recommendations. And we believe that this is something you cannot fake. If you’re keen on finding one, we have a <a href="http://filipinohomes.com/agents">list of approved Filipino Homes agents</a> near you to choose from.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><em>READ: Check out <a href="http://localhost:3001/what-to-know-about-a-community-before-buying-a-home/">What to Know About a Community Before Buying a Home</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>Good listener</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A good agent is one that listens. The ones who understand your wants and needs. If you think your real estate agent blabs so much and is not taking in your requests, then better weigh things out.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Note that an ideal agent should have a tendency to listen and ask probing questions before diving into conclusions. Good agents don’t make assumptions. They summarize and seek clarity especially when things are a bit confusing. Active listening in both parties builds strong relationships and reduces risk of miscommunication.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>Has a sharp eye on detail&nbsp;</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>While a warm heart will help you with networking, you’ll also need a sharp eye for details.&nbsp;And we believe this is a must-have for every real estate agent.&nbsp; A good agent is someone who has a keen eye for details especially on papers. He or she must be aware of those “little stuff.” Because these little things are what makes the big picture possible.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>Puts client as top priority</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This advice is heavily disguised for a reason. If there’s one thing that sums up the top quality you should look for an agent is their intentions.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You should look for agents whose motivations come from their clients -- what’s best for them, not theirs. After all, you’re paying them right? The best real estate agent should be able to give factual information, offer their honest opinion, help you make informed decisions, and someone who doesn\'t over compromise. Make sure to choose someone who is willing to go the extra mile to find the best solutions for you.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>BONUS TIP: Should be Tech-savvy</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is not new in real estate. But with the <a href="https://doh.gov.ph/2019-nCoV">COVID-19 pandemic</a>, this left us no choice but to shift going digital and be visible ONLINE. Being able to navigate the internet isn\'t a just cool skill to have, but it’s a must. This quality increases your productivity and efficiency since you are able to achieve more in less time.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong><em>Related blog</em></strong><em>: </em><a href="http://localhost:3001/advice-on-picking-a-real-estate-agent/"><em>Advice on Picking a Real Estate Agent</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/03/What-are-the-Qualities-of-a-Real-Estate-Superstar_.png','views' => '47','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2021-03-04 07:18:30','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '570','title' => 'How to Use the BIR Mobile TIN Verifier App','slug' => 'how-to-use-the-bir-mobile-tin-verifier-app','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR)&nbsp;has launched its <strong>Mobile Taxpayer Identification Number (TIN) Verifier Application</strong>, a service channel for taxpayers to send online TIN validation and TIN inquiry using their mobile phones with real-time responses from the concerned BIR office. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://www.facebook.com/plugins/post.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Fbirgovph%2Fposts%2F1755963811235426&amp;width=750&amp;show_text=false&amp;appId=180470228681693&amp;height=412" width="750" height="412" style="border:none;overflow:hidden" scrolling="no" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen="true" allow="autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture; web-share"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Revenue Memorandum Circular (RMC) No. 13-2021 was issued on January 27, 2021, to inform all internal revenue officers and employees of the availability of the TIN Verifier app and instructed them to encourage taxpayers to download the app and disseminate information about this new BIR-developed digital tool.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:</strong> <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.bir.gov.ph/images/bir_files/internal_communications_2/RMCs/2021%20RMCs/RMC%20No.%2013-2021.pdf" target="_blank">RMC No. 13-2021</a> </p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7069,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/154466853_10159269451854581_3144958657345749188_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7069"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>How to Use the BIR Mobile TIN Verifier App</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>1. Download the app</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The app is available for download on <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.bir.birrr6manila&amp;hl=en_US&amp;gl=US" target="_blank">Google Play Store (for Android)</a>. As of the time of writing,  the app is not yet on the App Store (for iOS).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Look for the BIR TIN Verifier Mobile Application in Google Play and hit install.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7078,"width":288,"height":512,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large is-resized"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/1_Google-Play-Store-576x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7078" width="288" height="512"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>2. Review the Mobile App Disclaimer and click Proceed</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Mobile App Disclaimer pops when you open the app.  This privacy notice tells you what personal information it collects, the limitations on use and disclosure of your personal information, how your data is being secured, the web browser cookies of the website, links to other websites, and your rights as a Data Subject. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[7079,7080]} -->
<figure class="wp-block-gallery columns-2 is-cropped"><ul class="blocks-gallery-grid"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/2_TIN-Verifier-Mobile-Application-2-576x1024.jpg" alt="" data-id="7079" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/2_TIN-Verifier-Mobile-Application-2.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=7079" class="wp-image-7079"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/Screenshot_20210305-140516_TIN-Verifier-Mobile-Application-576x1024.jpg" alt="" data-id="7080" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/Screenshot_20210305-140516_TIN-Verifier-Mobile-Application.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=7080" class="wp-image-7080"/></figure></li></ul></figure>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>At the end of the Disclaimer and Privacy Notice, you’ll be required to click on the “I have read and understood the Privacy Policy,” which will allow you to proceed to the application proper.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>3. Click the TIN Verifier button</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7082,"width":288,"height":512,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large is-resized"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/3_Google-Play-Store-576x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7082" width="288" height="512"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You will be directed to the home screen of the app, which displays the BIR logo and a large TIN Verifier button. Click the TIN Verifier button.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>4. Read the TIN Verifier Disclaimer and click Proceed</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Another disclaimer pops up, advising that the app covers Individual Taxpayers only at this time and is available only during office hours, Monday to Friday, from 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7083,"width":288,"height":512,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large is-resized"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/2_TIN-Verifier-Mobile-Application-576x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7083" width="288" height="512"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>5. Click on TIN Validation or TIN Inquiry</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7084,"width":288,"height":512,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large is-resized"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/Screenshot_20210305-140441_Google-Play-Store-576x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7084" width="288" height="512"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>After clicking the Proceed button, you\'ll see two buttons: TIN Validation or TIN Inquiry. Clicking on either of these will take you to a page that asks for more information.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[7086,7087]} -->
<figure class="wp-block-gallery columns-2 is-cropped"><ul class="blocks-gallery-grid"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/Screenshot_20210305-140447_Google-Play-Store-1-576x1024.jpg" alt="" data-id="7086" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=7086" class="wp-image-7086"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/unnamed-576x1024.jpg" alt="" data-id="7087" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/unnamed.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=7087" class="wp-image-7087"/></figure></li></ul></figure>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>TIN Inquiry button will take you to a page that asks for your name, birth date, address, civil status, spouse name, and a selfie with a valid Government ID. The same details are required for TIN Validation requests plus your TIN. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Provide the needed information and wait for your TIN to be validated. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>BIR launched the mobile app last January as part of the bureau’s digital transformation program.&nbsp;The development of the mobile application is one of the Bureau’s efforts in its digital transformation by giving our taxpayers a convenient way and alternative in availing of the TIN validation service instead of going physically and queueing in the BIR district office.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><br><br></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/03/Filipino-Homes-blog.png','views' => '286','category_id' => '13','published_at' => '2021-03-17 01:09:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '571','title' => '[Webinar] TGFI to Host a Free Real Estate Online Conference This Weekend','slug' => 'webinar-tgfi-to-host-a-free-real-estate-online-conference-this-weekend','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>The Global Filipino Investors Inc. (TGFI)</strong> is set to bring real estate and financial experts to the <a href="http://www.tgfiph.com/reoc" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Real Estate Online Conference</a> on <strong>March 20-21, 2021</strong> via Facebook Live. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With the theme&nbsp;<em><strong>Building and Investing in your First Home</strong></em>, REOC 2021 focuses on housing as one of the most crucial subjects in financial literacy and education.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://www.facebook.com/plugins/post.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2FTGFInvestors%2Fphotos%2Fa.588472297832363%2F4072749896071235%2F&amp;width=600&amp;show_text=true&amp;appId=180470228681693&amp;height=317" width="600" height="317" style="border:none;overflow:hidden" scrolling="no" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen="true" allow="autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture; web-share"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The online conference aims to provide information on the financial aspects and other practical and important considerations in building and investing in real estate. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes Founder and CEO <strong>Anthony Leuterio</strong> is among the panel of experts who will share his insights on residential real estate investment on the first day of the conference. Other notable speakers include <strong>Fermin Sta. Teresa</strong> (Pag-IBIG Fund), <strong>Pete Felix </strong>(Phinma Properties), <strong>Dr. Ruth Ang and Nica Masilang </strong>(Centro Mavens), and <strong>Pammy Vital </strong>(Ovialand). <strong>Arlene Reyes</strong> (Pag-IBIG Fund) and <strong>Rose Tsai</strong> (SHDA) will also join the panel discussion on financing options in housing. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://i0.wp.com/www.tgfiph.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/UPDATED-PROGRAM-SCHEDULE-19.png?fit=1373%2C1715&amp;ssl=1" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The second day of the conference will open with a discussion on future-proofing the real estate market with <strong>Romolo Nati </strong>(Italpinas). TGFI Chairman and CEO<strong> JJ Atencio</strong> will be joining <strong>Atty. Rachel Uy-San Juan </strong>(Uy-San Juan &amp; Associates Law) and <strong>Atty. Joyce Villanueva </strong>(Real Estate Broker) for the panel discussion on “What you need to know about buying your first home.” Atty. Uy-San Juan will also share the steps on effective house contract management and property taxes. To share their knowledge on interior design and construction, contractor <strong>Dino Aldeguer</strong> (Suretex Philippines), architect <strong>Dax Augustus </strong>(Delta Designs Construct) and interior designer and vlogger <strong>Roxanne Roxas</strong> will take part in the discussion. Other speakers include <strong>Andy Manalac</strong> (Havitas Development Corporation), <strong>Mary Gaw So </strong>(The Real Estate Hub), and <strong>Jay Castillo</strong> (Foreclosure Philippines). </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Join the free two-day collaborative event and learn from real estate leaders and industry experts. Register now for free via&nbsp;<em><strong><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://www.tgfiph.com/reoc/" target="_blank">www.tgfiph.com/reoc</a></strong></em>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4} -->
<h4>About The Global Filipino Investors</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"left"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="alignleft"><img src="https://i0.wp.com/www.tgfiph.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/website-2-38.png?resize=83%2C130&amp;ssl=1" alt=""/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Global Filipino Investors (TGFI) is a community geared to promote financial literacy to improve the financial well-being of every Filipino. Founded by a diverse and passionate group of Pinoy investors and entrepreneurs in the different parts of the world, TGFI is in a quest to break the endless cycle of Filipinos mismanaging their wealth or entering the wrong investments due to the misgivings of a lack of proper financial education program in the country a consequence that often leads to broken dreams and broken families.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/03/Filipino-Homes-blog-3.png','views' => '61','category_id' => '15','published_at' => '2021-03-18 05:16:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '572','title' => 'Rent Manager Program Produced Over 900 Rent Manager Specialists','slug' => 'rent-manager-program-produced-over-900-rent-manager-specialists','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The initial run of the Rent Manager Program, the first-ever free online course to become a rent manager in the country, has produced over 900 graduates. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The course is offered by <strong><a href="http://rent.ph/">Rent.ph</a></strong>, a nationwide listing for rental properties and property-related services for renters, rent and property managers, agents, and real estate owners. It consists of a two-part webinar and an online examination. Passers were given a digital Certificate of Accreditation and become a Rent Manager Specialist.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7097,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/144931724_855018808615770_9105239088281709184_n.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7097"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The first batch of&nbsp;<em>Rent Manager Specialists</em>&nbsp;has completed the course on January 7, 2021, with 4 batches of virtual graduation conducted:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Batch 1 with 400 graduates on February 2, 2021</li><li>Batch 2 with 251 graduates on February 9, 2021</li><li>Batch 3 with 239 graduates on February 22, 2021</li><li>Batch 4 with 72 graduates on March 8, 2021</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The specialists will need to complete rental agreements effectively and efficiently to become <strong>Certified Rent Managers</strong>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>About the Rent Manager Program </h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The <strong>Rent Manager Program</strong> is a peek into the world of Property Management. The course specifically dives into Property Management and the various aspects of running a Rental Property as a Rent Manager. It teaches students to oversee real estate properties on behalf of owners with the primary goal to maintain the property\'s value and make sure it generates income. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>What you\'ll learn: </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} -->
<ol><li>Understand the rental process from showing the property to a potential tenant to moving in. </li><li>Understand the importance of preventative maintenance and handling ongoing maintenance requests. </li><li>Establish a foundation of policies and procedures to help manage property operations, tenants, and maintenance. </li><li>Understand the concept of housing laws and how they affect the way you manage a property. </li><li>Understand the importance of excellent service in a Property Management career and the business or operations of a property. </li></ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>To learn more about the Rent Manager Program and how you can sign up for free, check out their website at&nbsp;<a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://www.rentmanager.ph/" target="_blank">http://www.rentmanager.ph/</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:</strong>  <a href="http://localhost:3001/how-to-become-a-rent-manager/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">How to become a Rent Manager</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For Rent Manager Program inquiries, you may reach <strong>Anthony Leuterio</strong> at 09778150888 or contact our Rent.ph Product Manager, <strong>Robert Laurente</strong> at 09565383022.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/03/Filipino-Homes-blog-1.png','views' => '43','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2021-03-24 02:40:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '573','title' => 'When Do You Need SPA or Special Power of Attorney?','slug' => 'when-do-you-need-spa-or-special-power-of-attorney','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Selling a home is a meticulous task. But it does not have to be tough even if you\'re not around to supervise it and to see into the legalities of the paperworks of the sale.&nbsp;The Philippine law, with certain conditions, allows sale of property even if you are in a different city or country from the property you want to sell.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>Take in the case of <strong>Ms. Property Owner</strong>, she is looking into selling her property in the province with plans to migrate to Canada. However, she does not have enough time for the sale to take place since she is leaving in two weeks. What should <strong>Ms. Property Owner</strong> do to dispose of the property even though she is out of the country already?</em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>What is <strong>Special Power of Attorne</strong>y?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A <strong>Special Power of Attorney </strong>or SPA is giving legal authority to an agent to&nbsp; represent and act in your behalf within the boundaries of the law. The law provides that a special power of attorney is necessary to enable an agent to enter into any contract by which the ownership of an immovable is transmitted or acquired either gratuitously or for a valuable consideration.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Articles 1874, 1877 and 1878 of the Civil Code addresses this situation:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Article 1874. </strong>When a sale of a piece of land or any interest therein is through an agent, the authority of the latter shall be in writing; otherwise, the sale shall be void.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Article 1877.</strong>&nbsp;An agency couched in general terms comprises only acts of administration, even if the principal should state that he withholds no power or that the agent may execute such acts as he may consider appropriate, or even though the agency should authorize a general and unlimited management.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Article 1878. </strong>Special powers of attorney (SPA) are necessary when the sale of a piece of land or any interest thereon is through an agent, the authority of the latter shall be in writing; otherwise, the sale shall be void.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Thus, the authority of an agent to execute a contract for the sale of real estate must be conferred in writing and must give him specific authority, either to conduct the general business of the principal or to execute a binding contract containing terms and conditions which are in the contract he did execute.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Article 1879 also states that a <strong>special power to sell does not include the power to mortgage</strong>; and a <strong>special power to mortgage does not include the power to sell</strong>. This gives the property owner an assurance that the agent can only act within the scope of his authority.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Thus <em>Ms. Property Owner </em>should seek someone to act on her behalf. Executing a special power of attorney will give the agent the authority to sell the property. Otherwise, the sale will be void. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/03/When-Do-You-Need-SPA-or-Special-Power-of-Attorney.png','views' => '70','category_id' => '9','published_at' => '2021-03-25 01:10:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '574','title' => 'Top 3 Key Changes in PH Real Estate Sector Amid the Pandemic','slug' => 'top-3-key-changes-in-ph-real-estate-sector-amid-the-pandemic','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes Founder and CEO Anthony Leuterio says the COVID-19 pandemic has boosted the demand for quarantine-friendly homes.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>Read: </strong><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.sunstar.com.ph/article/1890532/Cebu/Business/Aff" target="_blank">Affordable, ECQ-friendly housing projects to drive residential sales</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Real estate experts forecast an increase in residential property sales amidst the health and economic crises as many Filipinos look for stable, decent-quality, and affordable properties.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>Read:  </strong><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.cushmanwakefield.com/en/philippines/insights/philippine-property-market-news-march-2021" target="_blank">Philippine Property Market News - March</a><a href="https://www.cushmanwakefield.com/en/philippines/insights/philippine-property-market-news-march-2021" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"> </a><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.cushmanwakefield.com/en/philippines/insights/philippine-property-market-news-march-2021" target="_blank">2021</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The lockdowns implemented had resulted in changing needs and lifestyles, emphasizing the increasing demand for <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/building-smarter-and-future-proof-homes-is-the-new-normal/" target="_blank">smarter, future-proof homes</a>, featuring <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/sustainable-architecture-the-new-normal/" target="_blank">sustainable architecture</a>. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leuterio reports 10- to 20-percent new inquiries from people considering to transfer to another house where they can set up their home office.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7131,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/153132416_758068654825721_4367905750643155692_n-1024x832.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7131"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>New Normal Home Design Concepts</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With the changing needs of homeowners, Leuterio said they are now preparing new home designs to meet the new demand under the \'new normal\' living concept. This will be executed by <a href="https://www.facebook.com/filipinohomesplusofficial/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Filipino Homes Plus</a>, the construction management firm under the Filipino Homes company that specializes in custom-made houses.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>Read</strong>: <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/webinar-filipino-homes-plus-to-introduce-homes-that-are-designed-for-new-normal-living/" target="_blank">Filipino Homes Plus to introduce homes that are designed for new normal living</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>“We are coming up with designs that are now acceptable as \'new normal\',” said Leuterio, adding that they will consider the work-from-home concept in the crafting of the new home designs. The quarantine-friendly new normal homes will also take into consideration spaces for a built-in small gym, a small garden, among others.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Location matters</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Industry experts also expect a rise in residential developments in the countryside. As more businesses have invested in remote working setup, the future of work points to a blended workforce with companies adopting more flexible working arrangements, resulting to more workers coming back to their hometowns outside the metro. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Developers are expanding in other key cities in Visayas and Mindanao. <em>Cebu Landmasters Inc. </em>is going all out in its expansion in VisMin, including Dumaguete, Ormoc, and Davao City. <em>Johndorf Ventures </em>has started construction of Plumera, their ongoing OFW-targeted condo project in Mactan. <em>Priland Development Corp.</em> likewise announced a joint venture house and lot project in Davao City.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7132,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/nicolas-solerieu-CsFgzNtBq-8-unsplash-1024x683.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7132"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Tech-Driven Marketing</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>According to Leuterio, marketing to home buyers these days will be tech-driven, including virtual tours and online property roadshows.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>“Technology innovation and sustainability will be key drivers for value in real estate. We need to embrace digitization as we have really seen a big change in the real estate sector from various parties like developers and the market side. We need to understand how Covid-19 changed the buying habits of our target market,” Leuterio said.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>Read: </strong> <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/filipino-homes-ceo-anthony-leuterio-shares-about-marketing-in-the-new-normal-on-shda-kapihan/" target="_blank">Filipino Homes CEO Anthony Leuterio shares about “Marketing in the New Normal” on SHDA Kapihan</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/04/Filipino-Homes-blog-6.png','views' => '40','category_id' => '15','published_at' => '2021-04-09 03:56:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '575','title' => 'PRC Postpones April 2021 Real Estate Brokers Licensure Examination to July 2021','slug' => 'prc-postpones-april-2021-real-estate-brokers-licensure-examination-to-july-2021','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Professional Regulation Commission (PRC) postpones the April 2021 Real Estate Brokers Licensure Examination. Pursuant to Resolution No.&nbsp; 1338, (s.2021), PRC announced that the April 18, 2021 Real Estate Brokers Licensure Examination has been rescheduled to <strong>July 21, 2021</strong>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:  </strong>For the full text of Resolution, please click this link<a href="https://www.prc.gov.ph/sites/default/files/Reso2021-1338.pdf">: Resolution No.&nbsp; 1338, (s.2021)</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7136,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/REAL-ESTATE-BROKERS-POSTPONEMENT-1-724x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-7136"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"align":"left"} -->
<p class="has-text-align-left">For further queries and concerns, please email Licensure Office at&nbsp;<a href="mailto:licensure.division@prc.gov.ph">licensure.division@prc.gov.ph</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;and&nbsp;<a href="mailto:licensure.office@prc.gov.ph">licensure.office@prc.gov.ph</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/04/Filipino-Homes-blog-7.png','views' => '39','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2021-04-14 01:54:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '576','title' => 'Lag Internet? Try These Hacks to Improve Home Internet Connectivity','slug' => 'lag-internet-try-these-hacks-to-improve-home-internet-connectivity','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Internet connectivity has always been a challenge in the Philippines. A recent study conducted by SurfShark (VPN provider) <a href="https://surfshark.com/dql2020-slides.pdf"><em>Digital Quality of Life Index 2020</em></a>, affirms that the Philippines, which is highlighted twice in the 32-page report, ranks 66 out of 85 countries in terms of digital well-being -- which means the Philippines still falls behind much of the world.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>No wonder why so many people say our internet is, “<em>So slow, yet so expensive</em>.”&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Although it’s something beyond our control, there are actually hacks you can do to improve WiFi signal strength and speed up connectivity at home. We’ve gathered several recommendations from different sources online that <em>might </em>help boost your internet speed at home. Read on!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/3xrfAvg9mjqoKE51ydloDxod2Vc8FsWiapqcYRH7K-js5-HxaHDqgnBBo0ckJy2Nh7sRvVvMFfzew39pGIVSIKSYO9QALiI_2BFlQ6AIgKH-i420r4ktm6qGK14pUK1RjGHSqC-_" alt="internet connectivity"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Adjust the location of your router&nbsp;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is the simplest and least costly way to improve weak WiFi signals in your home or apartment. Keep in mind that a WiFi signal travels in all directions so placing it at a location that is central or almost equi-distant to all corners of your house will lead to much far better signal strength.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Since a WiFi router produces radio waves that travel in the space for Internet connection, the best location to position your router is in a high place of your house. Why? Simply because radio waves travel downwards in a lateral position. It would be best to adjust the location of your home WiFi router to a high place where it can maximize its effectiveness.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Update your security settings</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Too many users slow down your internet connection because it takes up internet bandwidth. If you’re experiencing a severe lagging, it is advisable to update your security settings. The safest way to go is to use WPA/WPA2 (passwords) in the security settings of your router, so hackers cannot break into your network.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Good thing is, you can always set your wireless network to be undiscoverable when a device is looking for an available Wi-Fi network. Setting this up makes your network secure to prevent unauthorized access.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Remove Interference (i.e home appliances)</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>One of the reasons why internet connection weakens is because some appliances or physical obstacles like walls in the house interfere with the signal of your WiFi router. This happens since WiFi transmits over a 2.4 GHz radio frequency which is the same with our common household appliances. Examples are power calves, microwave ovens, wireless video cameras, cordless landline phones and CCTV. Placing them away from your router might minimize the interference of your home WiFi.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>Read</strong>: <a href="http://localhost:3001/kitchen-organization-5-ways-to-create-open-pantry-space-in-your-home/" data-type="post" data-id="6143">[Kitchen Organization] 5 Ways to Create Open Pantry Space in your Home</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Use WiFi Extender</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you live in a huge house or mansion, and a dedicated router doesn’t do the trick, you might want to invest in WiFi extenders/repeaters that can boost your router’s signal to reach farther areas of your home. This is one of the most efficient ways especially if you have a really large area to cover or have dead zones in the house.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href="https://www.yugatech.com/wifi/12-tips-to-boost-your-wifi-signal-at-home/">Yugatech.Com</a><strong> </strong>explains, <em>WiFi extenders essentially create an extension network that allows you to login and get you a better signal quality while farther away from the router</em>. So by using additional WiFi routers as repeaters, you can extend the coverage of your WiFi signal even if you’re away from the main router. Since physical blockade like walls degrade the strength of your WiFi, it’s highly recommended to put the repeater closed to the router to get good signal.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Invest in a good router</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Maybe the problem lies within your router. How old is your router? If you’ve used the same router for years, this might be the time to ditch that out and invest in new ones. This is because internet providers make improvements every year and that old router of yours might not cope with the more modern WiFi standard.&nbsp; On average, combo modems issued by internet providers can only accommodate up to 10 devices at a time and you may experience signal drops here and there if you go beyond that.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So that’s it! How about you? Do you know other hacks that help improve home WiFi signals? Let us know in the comment section.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>Read: <a href="http://localhost:3001/5-tips-for-real-estate-agents-on-how-to-stay-productive-during-community-quarantine/" data-type="post" data-id="5319">5 Tips for Real Estate Agents on How to Stay Productive during Community Quarantine</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/04/Hacks-to-Improve-Home-Internet-Connectivity.png','views' => '61','category_id' => '13','published_at' => '2021-04-21 01:43:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '577','title' => 'Cebu Landmasters Flagship Sales Office formally opens','slug' => 'cebu-landmasters-flagship-sales-office-formally-opens','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>THE New Cebu Landmasters Flagship Sales Office was blessed and formally opened today, April 19, 2021, at the ground floor of Park Centrale, Cebu IT Park.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>SEE PHOTOS BELOW:</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/2lfxmNyYiIj598Jl5Elu8JJ--D7J1MaHm2OWJlGSp5H9fB48j3NW4XKUrKNfWKSgH-r3f2XkJ9Wxz1wbi-2hs2NBSkReFxm16Zq3ZBQDdOtBvTaacbletqxuk4M5DXE1QX6Frb5G" alt="cebu landmasters flagship"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/zMwKMSbBD2YnPXd177zQ0dWC0yFGh-ssOsHz9S_VXDWAH6L4ULn24tPyGQYXiJoSB1dSMi0X1n9o3koHy3TEmBJGY8pjB_JHr6705Z_ylLokrpnActG-9w27DqC7ENxmbHg2UnLX" alt="cebu landmasters flagship"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7154,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/Cebu-landmasters-opening-0.jpg" alt="cebu landmasters flagship" class="wp-image-7154"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/3fI9IXoDLqcAEgHZxRtm1NNzqu31EspCIjt65zws1cQEYexOEIBb_ghd_Z3-A2L5Ea8Nykkl1qnaQXQwgT8SHHnOjjfvhcpa6uTKTFXQS5E36AAASZKZvyvS6OFAqhO7k_Pxj9XR" alt="cebu landmasters flagship"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Cebu Landmasters Flagship Sales Office is open Monday-Friday from 9:00 am to 5:30 pm.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Redevelopment of <em>Patria de Cebu</em></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>On the same day, Cebu Landmasters Inc. (CLI) also announced its partnership with the Archdiocese of Cebu and French hotel giant Accor (France-based hospitality chain), as the National Historical Commission of the Philippines (NHCP) had given go-signal in the redevelopment of <strong>Patria de Cebu</strong>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7159,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/image-edited.png" alt="" class="wp-image-7159"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Named after the historic Catholic recreation center that heavily influenced young professionals in the ‘50s, Patria de Cebu’s redevelopment will offer 4,320 sqm of food, dining, and entertainment spaces and 4,400 sqm of offices.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This new mixed-use development will offer 21,000 square meters (sqm) of gross floor area and house the 182-room international hotel at the heart of Cebu City’s heritage trail.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Patria de Cebu redevelopment project was timed to celebrate the 500th year of Christianity in the Philippines.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>About Cebu Landmasters, INC. (CLI)</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong><a href="https://www.cebulandmasters.com/">Cebu Landmasters, Inc. (CLI)</a></strong> is a leading real estate development company in Cebu engaged in the development of residential, office, hotel, mixed-use and township projects all over Visayas and Mindanao. CLI was established in 2003 in the Queen City of the south founded by a true-blooded Cebuano entrepreneur.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Read more news &amp; updates about CLI:</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><em><a href="http://localhost:3001/cebu-landmasters-14-reservation-sales-growth/" data-type="post" data-id="6575">Cebu Landmasters: 14% reservation sales growth</a></em></li><li><em><a href="http://localhost:3001/leuterio-realty-bags-top-realty-award-from-cebu-landmasters-inc/">Leuterio Realty Bags Top Realty Award from Cebu Landmasters Inc.</a></em></li><li><em><a href="https://www.cebulandmasters.com/news/cebu-landmasters-earmarks-p12b-for-2021-capex/">Cebu Landmasters earmarks P12B for 2021 capex</a></em></li><li><em><a href="http://localhost:3001/davao-welcomes-cebu-landmasters-inc/" data-type="post" data-id="1386">Davao Welcomes Cebu Landmasters Inc.</a></em></li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/cebu-landmasters-expands-presence-in-northern-mindanao-with-two-new-residential-projects/" data-type="post" data-id="4323"><em>Cebu Landmasters expands presence in Northern Mindanao with two new residential projects</em></a></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/04/CLI-Sales-Office.png','views' => '50','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2021-04-26 06:38:45','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '578','title' => 'Filipino Homes CEO Anthony Leuterio speaks at UAPGA\'s Techtonics: Design and Build Hackathon','slug' => 'filipino-homes-ceo-anthony-leuterio-speaks-at-uapgas-techtonics-design-and-build-hackathon','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Filipino Homes founder and CEO Anthony Leuterio</strong> speaks during the virtual pre-event for "Techtonics: Design and Build Hackathon" hosted by the United Architects of the Philippines Graduate Auxiliary (UAPGA) - Cebu Chapter.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe src="https://www.facebook.com/plugins/video.php?height=314&href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Fuapgacebu%2Fvideos%2F467692814446380%2F&show_text=false&width=560" width="560" height="314" style="border:none;overflow:hidden" scrolling="no" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen="true" allow="autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture; web-share" allowFullScreen="true"></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7174,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/176398379_10219718723381329_6854742778841296375_n-1024x576.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7174"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>During the event, Leuterio shared about disruptive innovation to inspire all contestants for the virtual competition. He challenged the participants to develop something that will create a big impact in the architectural and real estate world.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leuterio is also set to join the roster of technology and architecture, engineering, and construction industry experts as a judge at the culmination of the hackathon event. He also said that Filipino Homes will be happy to incubate the creative project ideas that will shape the future of architecture and real estate.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p> </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>About Techtonics: Design and Build Hackathon</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The architecture, engineering, and construction (AEC) industry is known for its massive contribution to the built environment, where it creates spaces for the activities of every being. As an industry that heavily relies on engagement, interaction, and perception, a pandemic that forces us to stay at home and maintain distance poses a greater challenge in conducting its services.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Derived from the term tectonics in architecture, and the involvement of technology, this hackathon provides a platform for creative and fun innovation through fast-paced brainstorming and collaboration among people from different backgrounds. Hackers will be challenged to come up with a quick solution for the most pressing issues in the (AEC) industry, and present it to respected professionals. The idea with the biggest impact will be acknowledged and rewarded.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The hackathon will take place on April 30-May 2, 2021.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/04/Filipino-Homes-blog-8.png','views' => '47','category_id' => '14','published_at' => '2021-04-28 05:02:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '579','title' => 'OFWs, local markets keen about investing in Cebu properties this 2021','slug' => 'ofws-local-markets-keen-about-investing-in-cebu-properties-this-2021','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>CEBU, Philippines</strong> - More Overseas Filipino Workers (OFWs) and active local markets are seen to lead the robust property investing in 2021, according to Filipino Homes founder Anthony Leuterio.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Sharing his outlook for 2021, Mr. Anthony Leuterio said contrary to previous impression that OFWs are keeping their money while others are losing jobs, the demand for affordable condo properties such as properties priced at P2 million and below have expanded even during the height of the pandemic last year.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Furthermore, he said Cebu\'s property market is also gaining strong interest and has remained one of the best investment vehicles among buyers coming from other provinces.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Mr. Leuterio regarded these active condominium buyers from Dumaguete and Bohol, as well as others are <em>“mostly investors.”</em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>However, amid the rebound of buyers’ interest, Cebu is facing a shortage of affordable condominium inventories, Leuterio stressed.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>‘Mismatch in terms of supply versus real demand’</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>He believes that Cebu\'s property market is now facing a mismatch in terms of supply versus real demand.[<a href="https://www.philstar.com/the-freeman/cebu-business/2021/01/23/2072458/ofws-local-market-take-lead-buying-properties">1</a>]</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Thereby, he is urging developers to provide affordable properties and to continue to serve the requirements of Cebu’s end-user market that meet the buyers’ price.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If this demand cannot be met, “this could also raise the country’s residential backlog, which now stood at around Php 6 Million,” he reiterated.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Leuterio urges developers to ‘identify the backlog segment’</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is why Mr. Anthony Leuterio is <a href="http://localhost:3001/leuterio-realty-brokerage-what-property-developers-must-do-to-stay-productive-amidst-covid-19-pandemic/">urging property developers in the country</a> to “identify the backlog segment”. He said that about 80 percent to 90 percent of the country’s housing backlog is in the Php 2 Million and below level.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>From the hyper real estate developments in Cebu in 2018 to 2019, most developers stopped building in 2020 due to fear of the uncertainties. [<a href="https://www.jll.com.ph/en/trends-and-insights/research/philippine-property-market-overview-1h20">2</a>]&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leuterio said surprisingly, buyers’ appetite continued to rise even during the pandemic due to stable income of health workers abroad and realization of local buyers that property investment is one of the soundest investments during uncertainties.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>He hopes that developers will see this as a “good problem” to further fuel the promising outlook for Cebu property in times of COVID-19 pandemic.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>References:&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Dagooc, E. (2021). OFWs local market take lead in buying properties. <em>Philstar.</em></li><li>JLL (2020).<em> </em>Philippine Property Market Overview (1H20)</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/01/leuterio_2021-01-23_00-55-47.jpg','views' => '45','category_id' => '15','published_at' => '2021-04-28 07:45:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '580','title' => 'What You Need To Know about the Philippine Identification System (PhilSys)','slug' => 'what-you-need-to-know-about-the-philippine-identification-system-philsys','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>Good news! </em>Applicants for the country\'s National ID System may be able to register online<strong> </strong>starting <strong>April 30, Friday</strong>, National Economic and Development Authority (NEDA) Secretary Karl Chua said on Tuesday.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Chua said NEDA will launch its online system which will collect demographic data of those who will apply for the national ID, which has been defined as a valid proof of identity and is expected to simplify public and private transactions, enrollment in schools and opening of bank accounts.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>But before anything else, let’s explore what you need to know about Philippine Identification System or the <em>PhilSys</em>.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>What is the Philippine Identification System?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/z-EZPEqAQi3NgukOeuxCWNikZv0z_ikerkTlOYKSdqFe1_dZlI-2vqOltGODgWbkfrAeQczuAO29E8iicIoRxlYe268adIINkvJIZ6e8VSdNgW55OolMZrHO71SGB_YbnfbTHTfs" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Philippine Identification System (PhilSys) is the government’s central identification platform that aims to establish a single national ID for all Filipinos and resident aliens. It was established under the Philippine Identification System Act or <a href="https://psa.gov.ph/philsys/ra11055">Republic Act 11055</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Signed into law by President Rodrigo Roa Duterte in August 2018, its purpose is to establish a foundational digital ID System for easier accessibility and application of eligibility to social welfare programs and benefits from the government as well as enable the country to move away from inefficient and expensive physical documents, processes and credentials to the use of digital equivalents.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Components of PhilSys</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Philippine Identification System has three components to maximize data security and effectiveness. These are:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><strong>PhilSys Number (PSN)</strong> – which is the registrant’s randomly generated and permanent identification number. The PSN contains highly sensitive data and should remain confidential. It will be the standard number for the individual across all agencies of the government.</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><strong>Phil ID </strong>– a non-transferable card that shall preferably be issued to all citizens or resident aliens registered under the PhilSys subject to the guidelines to be issued by the PSA.</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><strong>PhilSys Registry </strong>– This contains the PSN, registered records, and information of all persons registered in the PhilSys. The PSA, as a repository and custodian of all data, shall create and maintain this registry.</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>PhilID</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As mentioned, the Philippine Identification Card (PhilID) is a nontransferable identification that can be used to transact with the government and private sector. The PhilID for Filipinos has no expiration date, whereas the PhilID issued to resident aliens is only valid for one (1) year.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The PhilID is free of charge for the initial issuance for Filipinos. However, the fee shall only apply for the replacement of the PhilID due to damage or loss. Plus, holders of Certificate of Indigency are exempted from the said fee as long as they present their certificate.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Features of PhilSys ID</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://s.yimg.com/ny/api/res/1.2/Oi.BXtPENu4WvrSQJKL4tg--/YXBwaWQ9aGlnaGxhbmRlcjt3PTk2MDtoPTY0Ny4wNDtjZj13ZWJw/https://media.zenfs.com/en-US/moneymax.ph/dd68e77ab3d917718f9e807ca935f48f" alt="PhilSys ID Features"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Who are eligible to apply?</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>All Filipino citizens are automatically eligible to register in PhilSys and get a national ID, including the following:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Overseas Filipino Workers and dual citizens living abroad</li><li>Foreign nationals living in the Philippines for over six months</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>How does it work?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With PhilSys, the person should declare his or her name according to his or her birth certificate, photograph, gender, blood type, and signature. The ID will come with its unique serial number, which will be called the Philsys Number (PSN). The reference number will be issued by the Philippines Statistics Authority (PSA).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The PhilSys, however, will NOT replace any existing functional IDs that serve other purposes. For example, a passport is a travel document and a driving license is proof that someone can drive. Functional IDs such as these will remain the responsibility of the issuing government agencies.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Social welfare and benefits granted by the government</li><li>Passports, driver’s license</li><li>Tax-related transactions</li><li>Admission in schools/government hospitals</li><li>Opening of bank accounts</li><li>Registration and voting purposes</li><li>Transactions for employment purposes</li><li>Cardholder’s criminal records and clearances</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>What information will be stored here?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This tamper-proof ID will be housing a smart chip that contains unique information associated with a person like his biometrics, iris scan, facial image reception code, and many other distinguishing features.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Other government-issued identification numbers such as the following will also be associated with the person’s designated CRN:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>SSS</li><li>Pag-IBIG</li><li>PhilHealth</li><li>Passport number</li><li>Voter’s registration</li><li>Tax Identification Number (TIN)</li><li>Driver’s license number</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>PhilSys Online Registration&nbsp;</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>NEDA chief has announced the launch of the online registration for PhilSys on April 30. Through the online portal, applicants for the national ID system may now be able to process Step 1 of the registration. <em>Check out the steps below</em>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Step 1 </strong>– Collection of demographic data and appointment-setting for Step 2</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Information to be collected and stored under the PhilSys shall be limited to the following:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Name</li><li>Sex</li><li>Birthdate</li><li>Birthplace</li><li>Blood type</li><li>Address</li><li>Filipino or Resident Alien</li><li>Marital status, mobile number, email address (optional)</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>After registering online, applicants will still have to personally go to their chosen registration centers to capture biometric information and validate supporting documents.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Step 2 </strong>– Validation of supporting documents and capture of biometric information</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Biometric information includes the following:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Fingerprints</li><li>Iris scan</li><li>Front-facing photograph</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Step 3</strong> – Issuance of the PhilSys Number (PSN) and the PhilID (physical card).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The PSA mentioned that the PSN and PhilID would then be delivered to the applicant via PHLPost.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/5uQx_LObnSZF8a4oMDOViqRXX-woqHf05gHBNT6yaYccWUBNfusCeJY6nWtT6MZWs7pAoqTE3rPHFYWbbVwPF5tCdl_WadBkWlb_Rq-QW5u5XmlaQY8AaX5Mpv_RpnbmirzlhAbA" alt="Philsys online registration"/><figcaption>Photo credits: PSA PhilSys</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>PhilID requirements</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>PhilSys applicants are advised to present an original copy of at least one (1) of the following:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><strong>Primary Documents:</strong><ul><li>PSA-issued Certificate of Live Birth and one (1) government-issued identification document which bears the full name, front-facing photograph, and signature or thumb mark.</li><li>DFA-issued Philippine Passport or e-passport</li><li>GSIS or SSS-issued Unified Multi-purpose Identification Card (UMID)</li><li>Land Transportation Office (LTO)-issued Student’s License Permit or Non-Professional/Professional Driver’s License</li></ul></li><li><strong>Secondary Documents:</strong><ul><li>PSA-issued Certificate of Live Birth/NSO-issued Certificate of Live Birth with Birth Reference Number (BreN)</li><li>LCRO-issued Certificate of Live Birth</li><li>PSA-issued Report of Birth</li><li>PSA-issued Certificate of Foundling</li><li>Integrated Bar of the Philippines (IBP) Identification Card</li><li>Professional Regulatory Commission (PRC) ID</li><li>Seaman’s Book</li><li>Overseas Workers Welfare Administration (OWWA) ID</li><li>Senior Citizen’s ID</li><li>SSS ID</li><li>Pantawid Pamilyang Pilipino Program (4Ps) ID</li><li>License to Own or Possess Firearms (LTOPF) ID</li><li>NBI Clearance</li><li>Police Clearance/ID</li><li>Solo Parent’s ID</li><li>PWD ID</li><li>Voter’s ID</li><li>Postal ID</li><li>Taxpayer Identification Number (TIN) ID</li><li>Philhealth ID</li><li>Philippine Retirement Authority (PRA)-issued Special Resident Retiree’s Visa (SRRV)</li><li>National ID from other countries</li><li>Residence ID from other countries</li></ul></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The PSA also noted that the following identification documents should be accepted as secondary supporting documents provided that they have a front-facing photograph, signature/thumbmark, full name, permanent address, date of birth.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Employee ID</li><li>School ID</li><li>Barangay Clearance/Certificate</li><li>Barangay ID</li><li>City/Municipal ID</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>PhilSys Data Privacy and Security</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>According to PSA, the<a href="https://psa.gov.ph/philsys/data-privacy-notice"> government agency ensures the privacy, security, and integrity of registered persons’ data</a>, of which sufficient safeguards shall be in place to ensure information security, cybersecurity, data protection, and privacy in compliance with the Data Privacy Act.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Furthermore, the PSA has been working closely with the National Privacy Commission (NPC), the DICT, and the National Security Council regarding the architecture and processes of the PhilSys and identifying and mitigating privacy cybersecurity risks.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>For More Info</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you have clarifications or concerns, you may directly reach PSA through email at <a href="https://www.yugatech.com/news/psa-philsys-step-2-registration-to-start-on-gradual-and-small-scale-basis/info@philsys.gov.ph">info@philsys.gov.ph</a>, or send a private message to its <a href="https://www.facebook.com/PSAPhilSysOfficial">official Facebook page</a>, or call the PhilSys hotline 1388.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Sources: <a href="https://psa.gov.ph/philsys">Philippine Statistics Authority- PhilSys</a>, <a href="https://psa.gov.ph/content/philippine-identification-system-philsys-project-information-memorandum-systems-integrator#:~:text=Project%20Overview,the%20Republic%20of%20the%20Philippines.">PSA</a>, <a href="http://legacy.senate.gov.ph/republic_acts/ra%2011055.pdf">Senate.gov.ph</a>, <a href="https://newsinfo.inquirer.net/1425076/philsys-online-registration-to-start-april-30">news inquirer</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>Related post:</strong> <a href="http://localhost:3001/where-to-apply-or-request-for-birth-certificates-cenomar-and-or-marriage-certificates-online/" data-type="post" data-id="6768">Where to apply or request for Birth Certificates, CENOMAR, and/or Marriage Certificates Online?</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/04/philsys-online-registration.png','views' => '59','category_id' => '13','published_at' => '2021-04-29 13:03:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '581','title' => 'Homebuyer Tips: 5 Facebook Groups for Financial Literacy','slug' => 'homebuyer-tips-5-facebook-groups-for-financial-literacy','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Your financial literacy journey is much easier and enjoyable when you surround yourself with like-minded people with similar goals. The key to success is surrounding yourself with&nbsp;smart people who can help when we need advice on how to handle our financial concerns. Luckily, there are many Facebook groups devoted to personal finance. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here are 5 of the best FB groups for Filipino young adults to connect with like-minded people and learn everything you need to know about financial literacy, including saving, insurance, budgeting, and investing.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/theglobalfilipinoinvestors" target="_blank">The Global Filipino Investors TGFI</a></strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/theglobalfilipinoinvestors" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src="https://scontent.fmnl8-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.6435-9/139494302_4008223632523862_955105372227696777_n.jpg?_nc_cat=106&amp;ccb=1-3&amp;_nc_sid=825194&amp;_nc_eui2=AeGihiPDc5cOCiC7rJSD-LWQLJbWwSoO4YssltbBKg7hi8BZ2dkOVST3QRy9MPldLx8&amp;_nc_ohc=oi-gqrV1Om0AX_MRU6Z&amp;_nc_ht=scontent.fmnl8-2.fna&amp;oh=38602d7791f164f4c8057417a17d4542&amp;oe=60C38B1D" alt=""/></a></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is a community by <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.facebook.com/TGFInvestors" target="_blank">The Global Filipino Investors (TGFI) page</a>, which promotes financial literacy to improve the financial well-being of every Filipino. It is founded by a diverse and passionate group of Pinoy investors and entrepreneurs in different parts of the world. TGFI aims to break the endless cycle of Filipinos mismanaging their wealth or entering the wrong investments due to the misgivings of a lack of proper financial education program in the country. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/brightmillennials/" target="_blank">Bright Millennials</a></strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/brightmillennials/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src="https://scontent.fmnl8-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.6435-9/p960x960/91315860_10158264762442630_5860889329622056960_n.jpg?_nc_cat=102&amp;ccb=1-3&amp;_nc_sid=825194&amp;_nc_eui2=AeFGdfsqVSggYjSc7lhaztmkTp8OZDAe2r9Onw5kMB7av2sKRGFKueFewyEukPEes08&amp;_nc_ohc=iLN0HC3jwcIAX9bwshW&amp;_nc_ht=scontent.fmnl8-2.fna&amp;tp=6&amp;oh=656121f80c1faab83e090b1229f02b0e&amp;oe=60C58DEB" alt=""/></a></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Bright Millennials is a community founded by <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.facebook.com/thebrightmillennial" target="_blank">The Bright Millennial</a>. It\'s a group where young professionals can freely discuss matters about personal finance, investments, and insurance.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/Ready2AdultPh/" target="_blank">Ready2Adult Ph</a></strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/Ready2AdultPh/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src="https://scontent.fmnl8-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.6435-9/125879864_10218815183951241_9066872104576736034_n.jpg?_nc_cat=110&amp;ccb=1-3&amp;_nc_sid=825194&amp;_nc_eui2=AeFYqqlyNjjSAdXkoXjzLZVi3vEQaa-9jgTe8RBpr72OBCPW3IY-RLWpuwnh-isDmmo&amp;_nc_ohc=i_-e0X6CEIEAX8AJMq_&amp;_nc_ht=scontent.fmnl8-2.fna&amp;oh=2d782a903f75f213b4aa431838cb76f8&amp;oe=60C473F7" alt=""/></a></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is a community of young adults, discussing about personal finance, entrepreneurship, and adulting how-tos. This group challenges you to step outside your comfort zone to achieve your goals and also help each other out in the challenges you might face along the way. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong><a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/finlitph" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Financial Literacy</a></strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/finlitph" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src="https://scontent.fmnl8-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.6435-9/p960x960/130703152_10221764621937327_274667869254720697_n.jpg?_nc_cat=104&amp;ccb=1-3&amp;_nc_sid=825194&amp;_nc_eui2=AeEiL5KOt8gu49Or2dtA9UWRAuirzPdv1p0C6KvM92_WnU38o2MsvcPPLium1x000s0&amp;_nc_ohc=wWq5U6Qqml8AX8Jyfoc&amp;_nc_ht=scontent.fmnl8-2.fna&amp;tp=6&amp;oh=051f915d19eb4f466aa99afed0482d00&amp;oe=60C307EE" alt=""/></a></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This Facebook group is meant for spreading financial literacy where anyone can talk freely about savings, budgeting, insurance, and investments.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong><a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/2181291708569233/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">No NonSense Personal Finance</a></strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://scontent.fmnl8-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.6435-9/48365735_10156939111677630_6885403548440330240_n.jpg?_nc_cat=100&amp;ccb=1-3&amp;_nc_sid=825194&amp;_nc_eui2=AeHyHFzEubftQUoco4uZHWH7n0TUJ3cv0NafRNQndy_Q1jJ8FYx1ih8GU8R6ST1SPTw&amp;_nc_ohc=Ehtre1rmNYMAX9P9lCP&amp;_nc_ht=scontent.fmnl8-2.fna&amp;oh=ba6925c003f91d3bdbe53728e0cc02b2&amp;oe=60C33AFF" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is the official Facebook group of Mr. No Nonsense Personal Finance, <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.facebook.com/RandellT" target="_blank">Randell Tiongson, RFP</a>. This online community is for insightful sharing and discussions about Financial Education. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This community is open to anyone who wants to share their ideas on how to save, invest, start a business, and other financial concerns. You may also post your financial queries here, and Mr. Randell Tiongson may answer them personally or other members may be able to share their thoughts on the topic.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/05/Filipino-Homes-blog-.png','views' => '48','category_id' => '15','published_at' => '2021-05-15 04:49:58','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '582','title' => 'Filipino Homes partner, Cebu Landmasters posts strong Q1 2021 numbers','slug' => 'filipino-homes-partner-cebu-landmasters-posts-strong-q1-2021-numbers','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leading developer in VisMin Cebu Landmasters Inc. delivered robust growth in the first quarter of 2021 posting a 25% year-on-year increase in net income attributable to parent of P714 million.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Meanwhile consolidated net income grew year-on-year by 12% to P725.2 million on the back of consolidated revenues of P2.35 billion, which is 11% more than year-ago figures.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7225,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/CASA-MIRA-SOUTH-1-1024x682.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7225"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The industry outlier attributed its exceptional Q1 2021 performance to sustained construction activities and the strong sales take-up of its residential projects in key cities of Visayas and Mindanao.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Moreover, the firm’s growth momentum is expected to speed up in the second half of the year as CLI’s joint ventures mature for revenue recognition, according to CLI chief operating officer Franco Soberano. In addition, CLI is set to produce fresh inventory in the next three quarters from its 2021 projects remaining in the pipeline. The <a href="http://www.cebulandmasters.com" data-type="URL" data-id="www.cebulandmasters.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">listed company</a> is set to roll out P14 billion worth of projects this year.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>CLI has so far launched three projects from January to March worth P4.9 billion which boosted reservation sales to P3.3 billion or 17% more year-on-year. Sales from the mid-market Garden Series accounted for 66% of the total while the balance of 33% was attributable to economic housing brand Casa Mira.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7227,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/CASA-MIRA-SOUTH-2-1024x682.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7227"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Soberano reported that once lockdown measures were eased towards the end of 2020, CLI quickly responded by stepping up activity to 95% in most of its construction sites. He clarified that mobility issues are no longer pronounced in the <a href="http://localhost:3001/cebu-landmasters-flagship-sales-office-formally-opens/" data-type="post" data-id="7149" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Visayas and Mindanao</a> where COVID infections have remained relatively manageable. Cebu City, the largest metropolis in the South, for instance, was experiencing low infection rates in the past weeks, which its medical facilities could easily address.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>“We are pleased that our teams in each of the cities we serve have stepped up to fill the pressing need for residential units that deliver quality, safety and security. This need was especially highlighted by the pandemic,” he observed. Even prior to COVID 19, VisMin’s housing backlog had been consistently underserved. Today, there is a backlog of 800,000 units a year with the industry supplying only 200,000.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7226,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/Latitude-Corporate-Center-1-576x1024.jpeg" alt="" class="wp-image-7226"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Soberano is optimistic that with the rollout of the vaccines, the business activity would step up once again paving the way for full economic recovery. “While there is still considerable work to be done to finally lay this pandemic to rest, we see light at the end of the tunnel and are preparing for improved economic activity. In fact, CLI has set for itself a growth target of 15 to 20% this year.”</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>CLI focused its capital expenditures in the first three months of 2021 mostly on project development. Land acquisitions have been scheduled for the rest of the year. CLI also recently paid out a cash dividend of P.25 per share to shareholders on record as of April 16, 2021, last May 10, 2021, in recognition of the firm’s stellar performance in 2020. The company’s 123% stock dividend declaration is also on track to get SEC approval within the month. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Leading developer in VisMin Cebu Landmasters Inc. delivered robust growth in the first quarter of 2021 posting a 25% year-on-year increase in net income attributable to parent of P714 million.','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/05/FILIPINOHOMES-BLOGS-XYZA-YAPE.jpg','views' => '43','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2021-05-17 04:08:45','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '583','title' => 'Credit Score - Do we have it in the Philippines?','slug' => 'credit-score-do-we-have-it-in-the-philippines','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When planning to buy a house or take out a loan for a home, business or a car, we will always hear the term, "Credit Score".&nbsp; Acquiring a credit or having additional funds lent is use to help in financial footing, in acquiring a property that requires money the individual does not have in the bank but is able to pay off in a timeframe.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>What is a Credit Score?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Credit Score is the number used to determine someone\'s capability to manage debt. It is a numerical expression based performed by banks or lending institutions on an analysis of a person\'s credit files. It will represent the creditworthiness of an individual if banks or lenders will allow the person to place a loan. This will help the lenders decide to accept, deny or extend credit.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Do we use Credit Score in the Philippines?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Unlike other countries, the Philippines currently does not have a unified system of credit reporting. Even though there is no standard system of credit reporting, the Credit Information Corporation in the Philippines is in charge of credit scoring. And banks uses available credit reports provided to check if an individual is eligible for a loan. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ: </strong><a href="http://localhost:3001/are-you-ready-for-a-home/"><em>Are You Ready For A Home?</em></a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>How does it work?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There are different credit scoring method that lenders use. Basically the credit scoring system will come up with a number between 300-850 with 850 being the highest possible score. The credit scores is influenced by:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Payment history - 30%</li><li>Amounts owed - 30%</li><li>Length of credit history - 15%</li><li>New credit - 10%</li><li>Credit mix - 10%</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Why is credit score important?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A credit score will impact a person\'s financial transactions and plans. These included mortgages, auto loans, credit cards and even private loans. This is also the basis for lenders to accept  loan application based on the person\'s ability to pay. They use it in risk-based pricing in terms of the loan amount and interest rate offered to borrowers based on their probability of repayment. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ: </strong><em><a href="http://localhost:3001/are-you-financially-ready-to-buy-a-house/">Are You Financially Ready to Buy A House?</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you are planning to apply for a loan, it is best that you build your credit score as early as you can. This includes paying your bills on time, paying off any existing loans you have and using your credit card smartly to not go into debt.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/05/Credit-Score-Do-we-have-it-in-the-Philippines-.png','views' => '40','category_id' => '19','published_at' => '2021-05-21 01:57:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '584','title' => 'CLI’s second horizontal project in CDO 75% sold out in a month','slug' => 'clis-second-horizontal-project-in-cdo-75-sold-out-in-a-month','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leading developer in VisMin Cebu Landmasters’ Velmiro Heights CDO with 518 house-and-lot units is 75% sold out one month after market introduction. The project is expected to earn P1.78 billion in sales revenue.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The high sales velocity of the listed company’s latest horizontal project in Cagayan de Oro City shows a strong mid-market residential arena in the Visayas and Mindanao region.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7245,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/188752605_342868387359375_4927027211345778920_n-1024x576.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7245"/><figcaption>Velmiro Heights CDO, CLI’s second horizontal development with 518 house-and-lot units in Cagayan de Oro City, is 75% sold out after a month of market introduction. The photo above is an architect’s perspective of the Dara model, a one-story single detached unit. </figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The P983 million development is the second horizontal project of CLI in Cagayan de Oro carrying the same residential brand.&nbsp;Velmiro’s house-and-lot units have floor areas ranging from 48 sqm to 140 sqm and have experienced high sales velocity in its five VisMin locations. CLI has thus far launched 1,800 Velmiro units priced from P2.3M to P7M.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>“COVID 19 heightened the need for homes offering safety and security not only among wage earners but also among mid-market executives and entrepreneurs in key cities in the South,” according to CLI chief operating officer Franco Soberano. Studies have identified an annual housing backlog of 800,000 units in VisMin with the entire industry able to supply only 200,000 units a year.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In the first quarter of 2021, CLI’s reservation sales increased by 17% year-on-year to P3.3 billion owing mostly to sales from its mid-market Garden Series developments including Velmiro. CLI’s growth momentum is highly likely to speed up even more as the year progresses with more projects getting launched and sold out and as constructions continue.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Buyers of the 12.2-hectare Velmiro Heights CDO have been attracted to the project’s generous open spaces, its accessibility to major destinations and unmatched views. The hilltop residential enclave offers 180-degree views of Macajalar Bay and the Bukidnon mountain range.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Cebu Landmasters also offers a range of house models to suit a spectrum of needs. Targeted for starting families are the Cita townhouse unit; the Dara one-story single attached unit; and Zuri, the two-story single detached. The house models are named after virtues and range from 48.3 sqm to 53 sqm.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7246,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/186953839_492836128804682_4313158630877704647_n-1024x576.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7246"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Meanwhile, growing families may choose from the Asha two-storey single attached unit and the Geila two-storey single detached unit. These models range from 60 sqm. to 140 sqm.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The units have been designed to offer clean, contemporary architecture and an uncluttered frontage. The simple lines recall that of a modern cabin and highlight the roomy interiors. An open floor plan and expansive windows to maximize natural lighting further enhance the space. The high sales velocities of its projects affirm that CLI is meeting the needs and preferences of its markets. “We are proud to be a homegrown VisMin brand and will keep drawing from our roots in the region to serve our clients,” said Soberano.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Leading developer in VisMin Cebu Landmasters’ Velmiro Heights CDO with 518 house-and-lot units is 75% sold out one month after market introduction. The project is expected to earn P1.78 billion in sales revenue. #filipinohomes ','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/05/FILIPINOHOMES-velmiro-heights-cdo-BLOGS-XYZA-YAPE.jpg','views' => '53','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2021-05-21 09:29:11','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '585','title' => '5 Tips to Finding the Best Location for First-Time Homebuyers','slug' => '5-tips-to-finding-the-best-location-for-first-time-homebuyers','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Buying your first house is often one of the most important decisions we make in our lives, but getting ready to buy your first house can be a little intimidating.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you are ready to start your journey to homeownership, here are some tips Filipino Homes Founder and CEO <strong>Anthony Leuterio</strong> shared during the <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/webinar-tgfi-to-host-a-free-real-estate-online-conference-this-weekend/" data-type="post" data-id="7104" target="_blank">2021 Real Estate Conference </a>hosted by The Global Filipino Investors.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7204,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/image-1.png" alt="" class="wp-image-7204"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Understanding your purpose for buying a home:</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Before buying a home, you should know your purpose. There are three types of buyers:&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><strong>Investors</strong> - those who buy a property and rent it out</li><li><strong>Flippers</strong>  - homebuyers who purchase a property and sell it out after some time for a significantly higher cost</li><li><strong>End-users</strong> - those who buy a property and use it long-term</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leuterio shared 5 tips for first-time homebuyers to find the best location for your :</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>1. Find a good real estate agent</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>According to Leuterio, finding a good real estate agent is the most important step to ensure that the house you will purchase fits your needs and preferences.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>He advises that first-time homebuyers should:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Check the agent\'s background if he/she belongs to a trusted real estate company</li><li>Evaluate their knowledge and experience in the local real estate market</li><li>Examine the agent\'s track record</li><li>Find out if they offer excellent customer service</li><li>Make sure they have knowledge in rentals in case you decide to rent out the property</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>2.&nbsp;Find a location that would be convenient for daily commutes</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A good investment property should be in an ideal location. This means a buyer should check:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Availability of amenities within the neighborhood, such as malls, grocery stores, gyms, etc.</li><li>Access to transportation</li><li>Time of commute to work or school</li><li>Proximity to school and hospital</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leuterio advised property investors to check the business establishments surrounding the area, emphasizing that these are the things that will contribute to the appreciation of your property value, especially when they want to sell or rent it out.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>3. Check the background of developers</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leuterio suggested a list of questions to answer when assessing a developer’s background and track record:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Do they have previously completed projects?</li><li>Do they have working phone numbers that are publicly available?</li><li>What are their company recognitions or awards?</li><li>Do they have a physical office?</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>4. Choose quarantine-friendly home</strong> designs</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As people continue to navigate the "new normal" lifestyle, the demand for smarter, future-proof is increasing. A good quarantine-friendly home design has space for a home office, gym equipment, outdoor space, and a quality air system.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:  </strong></p><p><a href="http://localhost:3001/top-3-key-changes-in-ph-real-estate-sector-amid-the-pandemic/" data-type="post" data-id="7127"></a><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/webinar-filipino-homes-plus-to-introduce-homes-that-are-designed-for-new-normal-living/" target="_blank">Filipino Homes Plus to introduce homes that are designed for new normal living</a></p><p><a href="http://localhost:3001/building-smarter-and-future-proof-homes-is-the-new-normal/" data-type="post" data-id="7034">Building Smarter and Future-Proof Homes is the New Normal</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong>5. Check the terms of payments</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It is crucial to pre-qualify yourself as a buyer. Make sure that you are financially ready to buy the property that they want.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:  </strong><a href="http://localhost:3001/are-you-financially-ready-to-buy-a-house/" data-type="post" data-id="4918">Are You Financially Ready to Buy A House?</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It won’t make sense if you find the "perfect property" for your needs if you can’t afford to keep up with the terms of payments. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:  </strong><a href="http://localhost:3001/what-are-the-hidden-charges-when-buying-a-property/" data-type="post" data-id="6144">What are the “Hidden Charges” when buying a property?</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here\'s the link to Day 1 of the <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://vimeo.com/524742124/2672377387?fbclid=IwAR3ggY5KcIz0qqPDWMsDVb9oML76hxCe61w4RtFE6zc3a7mqFYFshygo7OY" target="_blank">Real Estate Online Conference 2021</a>: </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<iframe title="vimeo-player" src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/524742124" width="640" height="360" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen=""></iframe>
<!-- /wp:html -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/05/Copy-of-Filipino-Homes-blog-1.png','views' => '40','category_id' => '15','published_at' => '2021-05-22 01:54:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '586','title' => 'Is it okay not to pay your credit card debts?','slug' => 'is-it-okay-not-to-pay-your-credit-card-debts','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A credit card is a convenient financial product to use for everyday expenses like groceries, gas, shopping and even dining out. It can also be very handful for large purchases like a new television, travel expenses or new furnitures for the home. You do not have to bring cash with you and there are also some benefits to using a credit card.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>However, mismanagement and failed payments to your credit card can damage to your credit score.  And repeated missed payments has a significant impact — your credit score is your entry ticket for most of adult life.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Benefits of having a credit card</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Using a credit card gives you the opportunity to build credit, earn rewards that you can use to purchase, cash-back or miles points. It is also a good protection against fraud and gives you an increased purchasing power. One of the top reasons why people get a credit card is to increase their Credit Score. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Using the credit card responsibly by making purchases with it and paying on time will show in the person\'s Credit Score. A Credit Score allows any bank or lenders a view of the person\'s ability to pay should a loan is placed or applied for.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>What happens if you don\'t pay your credit card debt</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Like most financial products, credit cards are very useful when used responsibly. It can, however, turn for the worst if the credit card owner fails to make payments for purchases used with the card. Let us say that you only paid the minimum amount required for you monthly credit card bill. The remaining balance that was not paid will be carried over to the following month with applied interest fee. Every month you have a remaining balance left or late payments made and was forwarded to the next billing will incur interest and late payment fees. This will increase you credit card debt over time. That is why it is best to purchase items you know you will have the funds to pay for.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: <em><a href="http://localhost:3001/credit-score-do-we-have-it-in-the-philippines/">Credit Score - Do we have it in the Philippines?</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>How will credit card debt affect me</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Failure to pay existing credit card debt will affect your credit scores affecting any financial transactions you will be able to perform in the future. Because credit card holders uses the credit card to build their credit scores, it can give negative impact on the credit score if managed poorly. If you are not able to pay off the minimum balance in 90 days, the credit score will take a hit. This is tell the bank or any lending institutions that you are unable to manage your repayments well and may affect if your loan gets approved or not.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So if you are planning to buy or renovate you home, buy a car or apply for personal loan in the future, you have to think twice about swiping your credit card with unnecessary spending that could lead you to debt.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Will I go to jail if I can\'t pay my credit card debt?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>According to the Bill of Rights, Article III, Section 20, of the 1987 Charter states that "No person shall be imprisoned for debt." Non-payment of credit card debt will not land you in jail according to the Philippine law but it will be regarded as a civil case because of it and not a criminal offense. However, if proven that there is fraudulent transactions made with the credit card, this can be subjected to criminal prosecution with corresponding jail time.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>How to manage a credit card debt</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Call your bank or the credit card company and ask that your credit card be closed or set to inactive. This is one way to stop you from using it and racking up the bill that you are already unable to pay. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can then avail a credit card amnesty program that allows you with unpaid balances to settle their debt at a lower interest rate and a longer repayment term.  This can help you get back on track with your finances and improve your credit standing.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>How to use the credit card responsibly</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Credit card allows you to spend money that you may not yet have in your wallet, this gives you an increased purchasing power. It is essential for the person to consider how they plan to pay the payments of the expenses made. A good rule of the thumb is to only use the credit on necessary items and to not use it for impulse purchases. Only use it for affordable items that you can pay of when the bill comes.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/05/Is-it-okay-not-to-pay-credit-card-debts.png','views' => '47','category_id' => '19','published_at' => '2021-05-23 01:54:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '587','title' => 'How to Avail of the Credit Card Amnesty Program in the Philippines','slug' => 'how-to-avail-of-the-credit-card-amnesty-program-in-the-philippines','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>While the use of a credit card allows a person to purchase items in credit, at the end of each month a bill will arrive stating the financial obligation the credit card owner needs to pay. There are a lot of good reasons and factors why one person should use a credit card like being able to purchase in advance before monthly income comes in, and to be able to work on a good credit score and history. However, a misuse of a credit card can also spell badly for its owner. Are you worried about your existing credit card debt and not sure how to handle and managed it?&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>What is Credit Card Amnesty Program in the Philippines?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The credit card amnesty program in the Philippines helps credit card owners with existing credit card debt settle their unpaid balances. This program offers lower interest rates and longer repayment term to help the credit card owner back on his track and to improve credit standing.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas, Banco de Oro, and Credit Card Association of the Philippines (CCAP) member-banks have a debt restructuring program called the Interbank Debt Relief Program (IDRP) to help credit cardholders settle their unpaid credit card sccounts. This is a repayment plan that consolidates and restructures your credit card debts It is manageable way to pay off all your credit card debts. Most importantly, it will not negatively affect your credit history.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>How do you qualify for the amnesty program?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Credit card holder must be Filipino with at least one credit card from two of the participating banks. You must have at least PHP 10,000 outstanding balance per credit card and at least PHP 100,000 total credit card obligations for all credit cards. And your age plus the repayment term of the restructured credit card accounts should not exceed 65 years. A co-maker or guarantor is also required if the applicant exceeds the 65 combined age limit, has no income source, or earns an insufficient income to cover the monthly amortization.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>How to Apply for Credit Card Amnesty</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Call your issuing bank to apply for credit card debt restructuring under the IDRP. If you have multiple credit cards from different banks, the credit card provider with the highest combined outstanding balance will be the lead bank in processing your credit card amnesty application. A representative from the lead bank will call you regarding the arrangements and application process.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>What does credit card amnesty program offers?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The credit card amnesty program offers low-interest rates ranging from 0% to 1.5 with long repayment terms ranging from 12 to 16 months (extended up to 10 years for extreme cases of credit card debt). Same interest rates and repayment terms applied to all unpaid credit card accounts.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Banks That Provide Credit Card Amnesty in the Philippines</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} -->
<ol><li>Asia United Bank (AUB)</li><li>Bank of Commerce</li><li>Bank of the Philippine Islands (BPI)</li><li>BDO Unibank, Inc. (BDO)</li><li>China Banking Corporation</li><li>EastWest Banking Corporation</li><li>Equicom Savings Bank</li><li>Hongkong and Shanghai Banking Corporation Ltd. (HSBC)</li><li>Citibank, N.A. Philippine Branch</li><li>Maybank Philippines, Inc.</li><li>Metrobank Card Corporation</li><li>Philippine National Bank (PNB)</li><li>Rizal Commercial Banking Corporation (RCBC)</li><li>Standard Chartered Bank</li><li>UnionBank of the Philippines</li></ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>How to apply for credit card amnesty or IDRP and document needed:</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Contact your credit card issuing bank regarding the amnesty program. If you have several credit cards, the credit card provider with the highest combined outstanding balance will be the lead bank to process your credit card amnesty application. Below are the requirements that you may need for the application</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} -->
<ol><li>Accomplished application form</li><li>Valid government ID of the applicant and co-maker (if required)</li><li>Statement of income and expenses</li><li>Proof of income<br>a. For employed applicants: Payslips for the last three months or income tax return (ITR)<br>b. For self-employed applicants: Latest ITR or audited financial statement</li><li>Proof of other sources of income</li><li>IDRP Payment Agreement Contract signed by the applicant and co-maker (if applicable)</li><li>Debtor’s consent form, promissory note, or post-dated checks</li></ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Can I apply for a new credit card after fully paying my credit card debt?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Yes. Once you have fully settled your financial obligation, you can apply for a new credit card. However, the application is still subject for approval based on your financial status and capability. The CCAP recommends to wait at six to twelve months from completing replaying and applying for a new credit card.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>SOURCES:</strong><br>https://www.moneymax.ph<br>https://www.ecomparemo.com</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/06/How-to-Avail-of-the-Credit-Card-Amnesty-Program-in-the-Philippines-2.png','views' => '379','category_id' => '35','published_at' => '2021-05-24 06:02:05','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '588','title' => 'CLI to rise above industry trends in 2021 with 25 projects in the pipeline','slug' => 'cli-to-rise-above-industry-trends-in-2021-with-25-projects-in-the-pipeline','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leading developer in VisMin Cebu Landmasters Inc. (CLI) aims to buck industry trends once again in 2021 with 25 projects in the pipeline–15 of which target the economic and mid-market residential segments in the region and are collectively valued at Php 19 Billion, according to Jose Soberano III, CLI chairman, president and CEO at the firm’s annual stockholders meeting in Cebu City. The company has set aside P12 billion for its capital expenditures for the year.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7257,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/190376453_506363843846105_7385506283211138985_n-1024x576.jpg" alt="Cebu Landmasters introduced phase 3 of the close to 12-hectare Casa Mira Linao in Talisay City, Cebu." class="wp-image-7257"/><figcaption>In photo: Architect’s perspective of Casa Mira Homes Dumaguete, which was successfully launched last year among nine other projects despite the pandemic.</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>CLI is setting its sights on a 15%-20% increase in revenues from the P8.3 billion in consolidated revenues it registered in 2020, closely matching 2019’s P8.5 billion. Parent NIAT in 2020 was at P1.85 billion. “Our 2021 projects will expand our VisMin footprint to cities like Ormoc, Bohol, Bacolod, Dumaguete, Iloilo and other key cities in the region while further strengthening our market share in Cebu and Cagayan de Oro where we have established a strong presence,” according to Soberano.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>At the same time, the firm is confident it will complete ongoing residential and other projects totaling 33 including mixed-use developments, hotels and townships. A significant number of these will mature for greater revenue recognition before the year ends.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As of Q1 2021, CLI posted a 25% year-on-year increase in net income attributable to CLI shareholders from P572 million to P714 million. Consolidated net income likewise grew 12%. This was due to strong sales take-up of its residential projects and unhampered construction activity bolstered by CLI’s financial assistance totaling P12.5 million to its 5,000 third-party construction workers in 2020.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As CLI prepares to further strengthen its capital base, the Company applied to increase its authorized capital stock to P10 billion, and subsequently will issue a 123% stock dividend. Last May 21, the company received SEC’s approval for the increase in authorized capital which will be the source of the stock dividends. And yesterday (May 26), the SEC has approved the issuance of such shares to pay the stock dividends. The record date will be on June 18 and payment date will be no later than July 14, 2021.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7259,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/192102924_1951417235020884_4922128080331990566_n-1024x576.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7259"/><figcaption>Cebu Landmasters introduced phase 3 of the close to 12-hectare Casa Mira Linao in Talisay City, Cebu. </figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Even at the height of COVID 19, CLI maintained its position that VisMin – where COVID cases have been relatively low – would easily bounce back economically from the pandemic. It avoided layoffs, maintained its workforce and even increased its headcount to over 600 employees by the end of the year, said Soberano.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Soberano observed: “2020 was a very challenging year. But we at CLI chose to look at opportunities and focus on the brighter side when we could.” He cited the firm’s heavy investment early on during the pandemic in establishing a strong digital presence that would allow clients here and abroad to select units all the way to making reservation payments. Its online platforms and flexible payment terms were largely responsible for the company’s record reservation sales of P14.25 billion in 2020.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Project planning likewise continued even during lockdown periods with CLI personnel in the key cities of VisMin following up on the close to 30 permits and other requirements needed to launch a project. Thus, CLI was able to launch three of the 25 projects in Q1 2021 with more in the pipeline.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>“We have deep roots in VisMin. We are homegrown and make the most of this unique advantage and expertise,” said Soberano.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Meanwhile, opportunities continue to abound in VisMin where the housing backlog has been estimated at 800,000 units a year. Industry studies estimate that only 200,000 units are produced annually.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>“We truly look forward to a better year. We hope to see even stronger buyer confidence as the vaccines continue to rollout,” he said.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/05/Copy-of-Copy-of-Filipino-Homes-blog.png','views' => '40','category_id' => '16','published_at' => '2021-05-27 08:00:14','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '589','title' => 'Leuterio, PRBRES Virtual Enhancement Training Program','slug' => 'leuterio-prbres-virtual-enhancement-training-program','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Professional Regulatory Board of Real Estate Service (PRBRES) held a Virtual Enhancement Training Program last February 1-5, 2021 as a Continuing Professional Development (CPD) and skills enhancement training. Real estate professionals joined the training program to be updated with the right practices and <a href="http://localhost:3001/what-are-the-certificates-and-licenses-needed-to-be-a-real-estate-salesperson-in-the-philippines/" data-type="post" data-id="6839">RESA compliance</a> for property selling.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Anthony Leuterio, the founder of Filipino Homes, the largest comprehensive real estate solutions portal in the Philippines, received a certificate from Board Members of the Professional Regulatory Board of Real Estate Service for sharing his expertise as a speaker and lecturer at the PRBRES Virtual Enhancement Training Program. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>"The renewal of my accreditation as a Speaker/Lecturer means a lot to me as Filipino Homes continuously train new agents in the proper real estate profession practice and RESA compliance." Leuterio says.</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":7265,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/Professional-Regulatory-Board-of-Real-Estate-Service-PEBRES-Virtual-Enhancement-Training-Program.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7265"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes provides one-stop-shop services for professional real estate buyers and sellers. It is powered by its growing property agents, Filipino Homes provides a full range of services including property management, in tandem with affiliate Rent.ph; foreclosure listings; and real estate insurance and consultancy services. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Not only does it provides much-needed market information, extensive property listings, statistics, and experts\' industry assessments but also known to uphold professionalism and compliance to law to protect every Filipino homeowner.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You may also like to read;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/filipino-homes-ceo-anthony-leuterio-speaks-at-uapgas-techtonics-design-and-build-hackathon/" data-type="post" data-id="7171">Filipino Homes CEO Anthony Leuterio speaks at UAPGA’s Techtonics: Design and Build Hackathon</a></li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/4362-2/" data-type="post" data-id="4362">Cebuano Broker, Stepped up his Digital Business Strategy with MIT Sloan School of Management</a></li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/filipino-homes-launches-digital-buy-and-sell-app/" data-type="post" data-id="4378">Filipino Homes launches digital buy-and-sell app</a></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Professional Regulatory Board of Real Estate Service (PRBRES) held a Virtual Enhancement Training Program last February 1-5, 2021 as a Continuing Professional Development (CPD) and skills enhancement training. Real estate professionals joined the training program to be updated with the right practices and RESA compliance for property selling. >>>[Click the link to Read more]','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/05/187838639_5572135959524841_5250932149627481383_n.png','views' => '59','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2021-05-29 06:33:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '590','title' => 'Can Unpaid Credit Card Prohibit Me from Getting a Home Loan?','slug' => 'can-unpaid-credit-card-prohibit-me-from-getting-a-home-loan','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When planning to buy a house for your family or a property for investment, one should look into his financial status to make sure he can afford the purchase. Financial status is one of the major factors that allows you to purchase a property. Most lender like banks look into the person\'s capability to pay off debt before they approved any home loan application.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>But what if you have an existing unpaid credit card, will that show during financial capacity evaluation and affect your home loan application?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>What do lenders look into a home loan application?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Are you planning to buy a property soon and wondering if an outstanding credit card debt will affect your home loan application? One of the main factors that lender will look into is your financial capacity. This includes your income, credit history and your debt service ratio. Your income will tell the lender how much you\'re earning and they can compute your debt service ratio from it. Debt service ratios is the portion of your monthly take-home pay that will go to your monthly amortization. This will let them know that you have enough money to cover for you monthly needs and expenses will be able to pay for you monthly amortization is approved. Lenders also looks into credit history which is a record of how a person managed his or her credit in the past. These includes total debt load, number of credit lines and timeliness of payment.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: <em><a href="http://localhost:3001/financially-prepared-buy-first-home/">How to be Financially Prepared to Buy Your First Home</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Will the lenders see unpaid credit card history from another bank?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Yes. Lenders like banks and non-banking financial institutions provide information to the credit bureaus or offices to make a the information into one credit report. This credit report can be looked up by any of the lending institutions. This financial background check allows them to see any undisclosed information like unpaid credit cards.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: <em><a href="http://localhost:3001/credit-score-do-we-have-it-in-the-philippines/">Credit Score – Do we have it in the Philippines?</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Why is credit card payment history important when applying for a home loan?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Credit card transactions is one of the easiest to build a credit score and credit history. But when not managed well, it can also pull you down when applying for a loan. Lenders look into history of credit card payment to decide whether or not they will approve a loan application or not. This will tell them the ability and timeliness of the person to pay his debt. So when you have an outstanding unpaid credit card payment, this will show up when they are evaluating your credit history and will tell them the risk involved of not being paid back the money they will lend you to buy your home.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: <em><a href="http://localhost:3001/is-it-okay-not-to-pay-your-credit-card-debts/">Is it okay not to pay your credit card debts?</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Can I still apply for a home loan even though I have an existing unpaid credit card?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The best thing to do is to go over your credit history and check for any existing unpaid credit card or any outstanding debt you have. Settle any existing debt first before applying for another loan. The reason while you need to settle a debt first is because any existing debt is considered in your debt service ratio. If the ratio shows that you have more debt than funds for your basic necessity, it will tell the lender that you do not have extra money to pay off the amortization if they approve your home loan application. When you pay off your debt, it is best to work on your savings to show your lenders that you have fixed your financial difficulties and is now ready to take on the responsibility of pay for a home loan to get your dream house.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ: <em><a href="http://localhost:3001/tips-to-get-you-in-good-financial-shape-to-buy-your-dream-home/">Tips to Get You in Good Financial Shape to Buy Your Dream Home</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/06/Can-Unpaid-Credit-Card-Prohibit-Me-from-Getting-a-Home-Loan-.png','views' => '41','category_id' => '35','published_at' => '2021-05-31 02:44:01','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '591','title' => 'Things you need to know about CLOA Title','slug' => 'things-you-need-to-know-about-cloa-title','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>CLOA or Certificate of Land Ownership Awards is the distribution and giving ownership of agricultural land to farmers. The Philippine government has won a co-financing program from the World Bank for individual titling of lands to farmer beneficiaries.  These are certificates of land ownership (CLOA) under land reform into individual titles for the agrarian reform beneficiary (ARB) after a loan agreement signed on 14 July 2020 worth $370 million.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>"<em>We have been competently distributing lands to our farmers because that is the main mandate of the department: Address the social injustice of our land acquisition and distribution, considering that many of the lands here in our country are actually owned by a very few people… landed people,</em>” DAR Secretary Brother John R. Castriciones said.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>What is CLOA Title?&nbsp;</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>CLOA or Certificate of Land Ownership Awards is a document evidencing ownership of the land granted or awarded to the beneficiary by the Department of Agrarian Reform (DAR). The DAR has intensified CLOA distribution in the country to support the government’s thrust to emancipate farmers from the bondage of soil. CLOA contains the conditions and restrictions provided for in the Comprehensive Agrarian Reform Law (CARL) and other applicable law.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Can CLOA land be sold?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>While the land ownership is given to the individual, there are limitations to the selling or transferring of ownership to it. These CLOA lands cannot be alienated or sold to any other person. There is a 10-year restriction period  that the beneficiaries cannot dispose of these lands. The land can not be sold or given its titled under CLOA. Selling them to any developer or any private citizen without the permission of DAR considered illegal.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>When can CLOA Land be sold or transferred?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Under the law, a CLOA beneficiary is prohibited to sell, transfer or convey the right to use the land he or she acquired. Lands acquired by beneficiaries may only sold, transferred or conveyed to their children, the government, the Land Bank of the Philippines (LandBank), or other qualified beneficiaries after 10 years. Under the land reform law, farmer-beneficiaries can only sell the land after 10 years and only after the original owner has been compensated. The DAR has to issue a CLOA (Certificate of Land Ownership Award) or EP (Emancipation Patent) before a person can claim ownership of agricultural land.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Can a land title be cancelled in the Philippines?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As a rule, after the issuance of the certificate of title covering a parcel of land, the title can no longer be altered, modified or cancelled except in a direct proceeding in accordance with law (Sec. 48, Presidential Decree [P.D.] No. 1529).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Can CLOA land be mortgaged?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>President Duterte has directed LandBank to accept CLOA as collateral. The LandBank of the Philippines has to accept certificates of land ownership award (CLOA) as collateral for mortgage so that farmers could borrow money.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>SOURCE:</strong><br>https://www.dar.gov.ph<br>www.manilatimes.net<br></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/06/Things-you-need-to-know-about-CLOA-Title-2.png','views' => '384','category_id' => '15','published_at' => '2021-06-11 05:51:28','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '592','title' => 'Tips for Negotiating Your Household Costs','slug' => 'tips-for-negotiating-your-household-costs','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When it comes to expenses on amenities and utilities for your home, you might feel like spending is unavoidable, but there are a ton of ways to save cash and put money back into your pocket. Simple<a href="https://mint.intuit.com/blog/early-career/negotiation-tactics/"> negotiation tactics</a> and strategies can help you <a href="http://localhost:3001/5-money-saving-tips-for-gen-z/">save money</a> when it comes to home expenses, so use these tips to try negotiating your way to better savings.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>How can I negotiate?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Negotiating is a very important skill, especially when you need to speak up about your financial affairs. Although negotiating with a friend, colleague, or even a stranger might seem intimidating, it can lead to beneficial changes in your life. Whether you are negotiating your cable bill or your new <a href="https://mint.intuit.com/salary/">salary</a>, you can improve your financial situation and be equipped for future bargaining situations with a few of these techniques.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><strong>The Foot-In-The-Door Technique: </strong>To increase the chances of someone complying with a large request, you can start by making a small one. For example, if you are looking to buy a secondhand lamp for $20, you might negotiate the price down to $15. You could then follow up by asking if you could purchase two lamps for $30. This allows you to leverage the small, initial discount to get an even better discount.</li><li><strong>Door-In-The-Face Tactic:</strong> This technique uses the opposite approach to the Foot-In-The-Door tactic. Initially, you make an unreasonable request to get turned down. After your first request is shot down, you follow up with a smaller request. This will make the person you are negotiating with feel obligated to agree to a more reasonable ask.</li><li><strong>Take It or Leave it Method: </strong>This tactic is a hard bargaining method. You may list a price for an item you are interested in and instead of negotiating the price, you respond by explaining that the price you offered is the only price you are willing to pay or you will walk away. This puts pressure on the seller or vendor to make a quick decision.&nbsp;</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Try negotiating your rent</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Whether you are looking to settle down in an apartment or your landlord is raising the price, you may not have known that you can negotiate your rent. Here are a few possible strategies that may work for you.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Politely ask your landlord if the rent price is open to discussion</li><li>Express your track history as a good tenant</li><li>Inquire about a possible lease extension</li><li>Compare their rent ask with market prices and negotiate based on data</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Lower your utility bills</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We all know how expensive utilities can be because they add up over time. If you’re paying for cable, lawn services, cell phone bills, electricity, trash pickup, and many other costs, these tactics could be super helpful to cut down on your monthly bills.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Assume that your regular costs can be negotiable by researching discounts</li><li>Avoid contracts that may impose costly fees</li><li>Shop around and compare utility prices for different vendors</li><li>Call to inquire about quotes and ask a company to match a lower rate you found somewhere else</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Negotiating is a great way to cut down on your expenses and funnel your money back into your bank account. For more great negotiation inspiration, check out the infographic below from <a href="https://mint.intuit.com/">Mint</a> for conversation starters and additional tips.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<center><a href="https://mint.intuit.com/blog/early-career/negotiation-tactics/"><img src="https://blog.mint.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/negotiation-tactics-save-money-earn-more.png?resize=1000,7799" alt="negotiation-tips-and-tactics" width="540x" border="0"></a></center>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/07/Screen-Shot-2021-07-02-at-6.48.23-PM.png','views' => '50','category_id' => '9','published_at' => '2021-07-02 10:52:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '593','title' => 'Duterte signs law extending estate tax amnesty','slug' => 'duterte-signs-law-extending-estate-tax-amnesty','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://cnnphilippines.com/.imaging/mte/demo-cnn-new/750x450/dam/cnn/2020/12/8/Duterte-Covid-19-Address-120820_2_CNNPH.jpg/jcr:content/Duterte-Covid-19-Address-120820_2_CNNPH.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>President Rodrigo Duterte has signed a law extending the availment period of estate tax amnesty for two years, or until June 14, 2023. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Republic Act No. (RA) 11569, signed by Duterte on June 30, 2021, amended RA 11213. The Tax Amnesty Act previously set June 14, 2021, as the due date for the filing of estate tax returns.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ: </strong><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.officialgazette.gov.ph/2021/06/30/republic-act-no-11569/" target="_blank">Republic Act No. 11569</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7330,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Republic-Act-No.-RA-11569-1.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7330"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7331,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Republic-Act-No.-RA-11569-2.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7331"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>“The executor or administrator of the estate, or if there is no executor or administrator appointed, the legal heirs, transferees or beneficiaries, who wish to avail of the Estate Tax Amnesty shall, within June 15, 2021, until June 14, 2023, file with the Revenue District Office of the Bureau of Internal Revenue, which has jurisdiction over the last residence of the decedent, a sworn Estate Tax Amnesty Return, in such forms as may be prescribed in the Implementing Rules and Regulations,” the new law stated.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>RA 11569 directs the Secretary of the Department of Finance, in coordination with the Commissioner of the Bureau of Internal Revenue, to issue the necessary rules and regulations for the effective implementation of this Act “within 60 days from its effectivity.”</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Lawmakers who pushed for the two-year extension said COVID-19 restrictions have made it difficult for taxpayers to settle their estate tax dues even with the amnesty.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/07/Filipino-Homes-blog-10.png','views' => '44','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2021-07-03 01:33:44','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '594','title' => 'Asia Pacific Commercial Property Markets Slowly Rebounding Post Covid','slug' => 'asia-pacific-commercial-property-markets-slowly-rebounding-post-covid','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>CBRE\'s latest <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.cbre.com/research-and-reports/Asia-Pacific-MarketView-Q1-2021" target="_blank">MarketView and Investment Trends research </a>report a steady increase in commercial property leasing and capital markets activity in Asia Pacific in Q1 2021. The commencement of COVID-19 vaccination programs and an improving economic outlook have contributed to this economic rebound.  However, recovery remains uneven across the region, with the momentum in each country largely correlated with the degree of success in containing COVID-19. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7324,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/david-milmont-3WX60TlLIdw-unsplash-1024x683.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7324"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Office Sector Highlights</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In the office sector, the report highlights higher tenant inquiries and more frequent site inspections, translated to stronger office leasing demand in Q1 2021.&nbsp;Regional Grade A rents decelerated from 1.2% q-o-q in&nbsp; Q4 2020 to 0.7% q-o-q, bringing the y-o-y fall to 5.0%.<br></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Retail Sector Highlights</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In the retail sector, Asia Pacific retail rents fell by 0.4% y-o-y in Q1 2021, a slower rate of decline than the 2.1% y-o-y drop recorded in the previous quarter. <br><br>Retailers in most markets were more active in looking for new leasing opportunities, particularly in prime locations, backed by a steady improvement in retail sales and consumer confidence. <br></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Industrial Sector Highlights</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Industrial sentiment continued to pick up in Q1 2021, with global manufacturing Purchasing Manufacturers Indices (PMI) reaching 55 in March, a ten-year high. Warehousing demand remained upbeat, with Asia net absorption totaling 15.6 million sq. ft., the highest first-quarter total in recent years. Asia Pacific logistics rents rose by 0.7% q-o-q, the strongest rate of growth since the onset of the pandemic.<br></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Asia Investment Trends</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Asia Pacific commercial real estate investment volume totaled US$26 billion in Q1 2021, an increase of 12% y-o-y. Investment sentiment continued to strengthen over the quarter, with most markets observing an increase in inquiry levels.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ full report here: </strong><a href="https://www.cbre.com/research-and-reports/Asia-Pacific-MarketView-Q1-2021" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Asia Pacific MarketView Q1 2021</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/07/Filipino-Homes-blog-CBRE-market.png','views' => '45','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2021-07-05 02:57:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '595','title' => 'Cebu Landmasters achieves record high Php 8.5 billion H1 reservation sales, 14% increase','slug' => 'cebu-landmasters-achieves-record-high-php-8-5-billion-h1-reservation-sales-14-increase','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leading developer in VisMin Cebu Landmasters, Inc. (CLI) announced a record Php 8.5 billion in reservation sales in H1 2021, a robust 14% increase from Php 7.4 billion year-on-year boosted by sustained housing demand in its geographic scope.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>CLI launched six projects during the first six months across different segments in Cebu, Iloilo and Ormoc. In Q2 2021 alone, the listed company recorded Php 5.2 billion sales, exceeding the Php 4.6 billion reported in the same period last year.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>CLI maintained its foothold in Cebu, which accounted for 29% of sales; and heightened its presence in Iloilo, which contributed 27%, and Cagayan de Oro, accounting for 20%. The rest were the result of sustaining sales from Davao, Bacolod, Dumaguete, Bohol and from a new expansion area in Ormoc.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7341,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Cebu-Landmasters-achieves-record-high-Php-8.5-billion-H1-reservation-sales-14-increase-01-1024x576.png" alt="" class="wp-image-7341"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In terms of market segments, CLI’s mid-market and economic housing units accounted for 38% and 41% respectively while its high-end developments pulled in 21%. These figures are in line with a study by Leechiu Property Consultants indicating that the VisMin housing backlog would post an annual average demand of 475,000 up to 2022 and that close to half or 200,000 would be generated by the mid- and economic segments.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>These findings were further affirmed by the high take-up of CLI’s recently launched projects: Velmiro Heights CDO now 83% sold out; and Mandtra Residences in Cebu, 82% sold out.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The company has begun offering higher-end units in anticipation of a post pandemic boom in VisMin which appears ready to host a recovery. Its efforts have been rewarded especially in Iloilo City where its premium Terranza Residences has sold out 81% of inventory in just three months beginning April.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Overall, CLI’S upgraded digital capabilities have proven invaluable in its sales efforts. A buyer can now inquire about a unit in any of its projects in 15 VisMin cities, get real-time responses, check construction progress, join virtual events and do many more activities online over a number of channels and platforms. A new flagship sales office recently opened in CLI’s Cebu headquarters, a “<em>perfect venue for us to serve our partner brokers and agents and the increasing demand for our products</em>” according to CLI vice-president for Sales Rose Yulo.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>All these developments have kept CLI on track as of mid-year to meet its targeted 15-20% growth for 2021. CLI chief executive officer Jose Soberano III said: “<em>Our robust sales performance indicates CLI’s income streams in the near future. We have been working hard for this kind of growth trajectory</em>.”</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Its economic momentum will further be sustained with fresh inventory to be launched in the next six months. The firm will tap its existing landbank for these projects. Meanwhile, land purchases in key growth areas to secure a new pipeline of revenue streams are on the drawing board and are expected to be closed in the coming months.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>“<em>The pandemic has given rise to a new generation of property owners and we are very pleased that the recent announcement of BIR maintaining the Php3,199,200 VAT threshold has proved that housing is still one of the country’s priorities. This keeps homes affordable for more potential homeowners in the mid-market and economic segments</em>,” added Soberano.“<em>Our vision is to see many more families securing their future in our communities</em>.”</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/07/Cebu-Landmasters-achieves-record-high-Php-8.5-billion-H1-reservation-sales-14-increase-02.png','views' => '45','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2021-07-05 08:03:47','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '596','title' => 'Why You Should Invest on UptownCommunities?','slug' => 'why-you-should-invest-on-uptown-communities','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Buying a home but not sure where to buy one? There are a lot of factors to consider when purchasing your forever home. One of the important consideration before architecture, facilities or interiors is the location of the home. One of the trends in homebuying is purchasing a home is finding a property in elevated communities. With the Philippine weather and the threat of flooding as well as the lure of open spaces and clear skies elevated communities offers, no wonder families are grabbing these properties quickly.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you are still not sure whether to buy a home in these locations, here is why you should invest on uptown communities:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7348,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/VIDERE-Subdivision-Uptown-Living-Cagayan-De-Oro-City.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7348"/><figcaption>VIDERE Subdivision Uptown Living at Cagayan De Oro City</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>No flooding in the community</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Philippines has a bad cases of flooding year in and year out. Filipinos are not actually surprised when they hear news of flooding during the country\'s rainy season. With at least 20 typhoons passing by the Philippines every year, Filipinos are no stranger to flooding. However, flooding can be very emotional draining and financially costly for families living in low-lying areas. The constant threat of flooding from heavy rain can trigger worries and anxiety. The most difficult part is having to save home items when the flood waters enter the homes.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Living in elevated and high grounds community gives the family a safer home without the fear of flooding. It gives you the peace of mind you need during the rainy season the Philippines go through every year.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:</strong><em> <a href="http://localhost:3001/5-tips-to-finding-the-best-location-for-first-time-homebuyers/">5 Tips to Finding the Best Location for First-Time Homebuyers</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7350,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Townhouse-at-Navona-Lumbia-Cagayan-De-Oro-City.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7350"/><figcaption>Townhouse at Navona Lumbia at Cagayan De Oro City</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Cool breeze and lower temperatures</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>One of the perks when living in high communities is the peaceful and serene atmosphere. Not only is the community peaceful but you will be granted some fresh air and cool breeze even during the hot humid summer days. And in the cooler season of the year, you can enjoy a lower temperature. This in turn will help you save on electricity, skipping blasted air-conditioning because you does have to.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:</strong><em> <a href="http://localhost:3001/10-tips-to-buy-real-estate-without-breaking-your-budget/">10 Tips to Buy Real Estate Without Breaking Your Budget</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7349,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/The-Grove-at-Pueblo-Golf-Course-Uptown-Living-Cagayan-De-Oro-City-.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7349"/><figcaption>The Grove at Pueblo Golf Course at Cagayan De Oro City</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Excellent real estate investment returns</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Uptown communities have larger land areas for development hence why you will see excellent community facilities. These are some of the factors why families are moving to higher grounds communities - looking for wide and nature-filled areas for their children to grow up in. Without the treat of flooding and having more spacious community areas, uptown communities is looking to have excellent real estate investment returns for its property owners.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ: </strong><em><a href="http://localhost:3001/what-to-know-about-a-community-before-buying-a-home/">What to Know About a Community Before Buying a Home</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you\'re looking for properties for sale check out the comprehensive list of properties for sale at <em><a href="https://filipinohomes.com/properties.php?sparam=forsale">Filipino Homes Property For Sale listing</a></em>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/07/Why-You-Should-Invest-on-Higher-Ground-Communities-2.png','views' => '52','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2021-07-06 02:59:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '597','title' => '5 Reasons Why You Need a Home Office','slug' => '5-reasons-why-you-need-a-home-office','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The COVID-19 pandemic is changing life as we know it. The community quarantine restrictions imposed since last year have forced employees to move into a work-from-home setup. While a home office used to be considered as a luxury home feature in the past, the shift in the way we work requires us to adjust to new ways of working, including having a dedicated quiet space to allow us to work effectively and productively. Here are 5 reasons why you need to set up a home office:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7313,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/work-desk.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7313"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>1. Home office encourages productivity.</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As we are forced into shifting to remote work, we need to have a proper office setup to encourage us to work effectively and maintain productivity. This means having appropriate desk space, enough power outlets, and office storage to allow us to do our work properly. This also means having a suitable private space for online meetings with colleagues and clients. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>2. Your dedicated work area helps with d<strong>iscipline and motivation.</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Self-discipline and focus are often tested for employees who choose to work from home. It may sound ideal to be able to work inside the comforts of your own home, but the distractions from children, work, neighbors, friends, and family can be disruptive and get in the way of completing tasks. An environment designed with your productivity in mind can help you with your discipline and motivation to keep on track. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1605565348518-bef3e7d6fed8?ixid=MnwxMjA3fDB8MHxwaG90by1wYWdlfHx8fGVufDB8fHx8&amp;ixlib=rb-1.2.1&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;w=755&amp;q=80" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>3. You can design your home office into an area that adapts to your needs and personality.</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Especially when you are paid based on your output, you need a work area that makes your job easier for you. With your home office, you have the freedom to design your dedicated workspace according to your personal taste and work process. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For example, you may add a coffee corner and snack station if you need constant access to food while working.  You may also consider assigning a personal nook for your breaks. There are also office desks and chairs equipped with a treadmill and pedals so you can work out while working.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>4. Your home office allows better work-life balance</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>At this time when we spend our time working at home and spending free time there as well, creating a physical distinction between professional workspace and domestic family space is important. Your home office should be a dedicated space for work during the day, but make sure to be  able to close the door once you’re done and spend time with your family at the end of the shift. This is vital in maintaining a healthy work-life balance. A home office can help create physical boundaries within the home, where your office is off-limits to children and pets.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>5. A home office can increase the value of your home</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The global pandemic has increased the demand for quarantine-friendly homes. This means that if you take advantage of unused space, convert one room into an office, or add one to your home, you increase its resale value should you ever decide to sell up or rent it our later on. Many potential homebuyers will be looking for homes that offer the functionality of a dedicated home office or study space. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:  </strong><a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/top-3-key-changes-in-ph-real-estate-sector-amid-the-pandemic/" data-type="post" data-id="7127" target="_blank">Top 3 Key Changes in PH Real Estate Sector Amid the Pandemic</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/06/Filipino-Homes-blog-9.png','views' => '70','category_id' => '31','published_at' => '2021-07-07 03:37:51','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '598','title' => 'Is it safe to buy a property with CLOA Title?','slug' => 'is-it-safe-to-buy-a-property-with-cloa-title','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Looking for a property to invest or a land where you can build your future home one can be taxing. There are are lot of factors to look into including and importantly the legality of the property that you are eyeing. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Is someone selling you a property or have you gained interest in a property that has CLOA title and you\'re not sure whether or not it is safe to buy a property with CLOA Title? Here are some of the important information about CLOA land to help you decide whether or not it is worth all the effort to acquire it.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7358,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Is-it-safe-to-buy-a-property-with-CLOA-Title-3-1024x576.png" alt="" class="wp-image-7358"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>What is CLOA Title?&nbsp;</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Certificate of Land Ownership Awards or CLOA is a document that states ownership of the land granted or awarded to the beneficiary by the Department of Agrarian Reform (DAR). This means that the current owner of the CLOA land had acquired the property from DAR. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Can the owner sell the CLOA Land awarded to him?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The CLOA land is legally under the name of the owner or the beneficiary but it has some conditions and restrictions under the Comprehensive Agrarian Reform Law (CARL) and other applicable law. Included in the limitations is the selling or transferring of ownership of the CLOA Land to other people. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Unfortunately, CLOA lands cannot be alienated or sold to any other person. There is an existing 10-year restriction period from the time the land was award to the beneficiary stating that the beneficiary cannot dispose of these lands whether bu selling it or transferred. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Selling them to any developer or any private citizen without the permission of DAR considered illegal.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>When can I buy a land with CLOA Title?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Since the CLOA land beneficiary is prohibited to sell, transfer or convey the right to use the land, it can only be sold, transferred or conveyed to their children, the government, the Land Bank of the Philippines (LandBank), or other qualified beneficiaries after 10 years. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Only after 10 years that the CLOA land title restrictions has lapsed can you safely and legally purchase the land.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Under the land reform law, farmer-beneficiaries can only sell the land after 10 years and/or only after the original owner has been compensated.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:</strong> <em><a href="http://localhost:3001/things-you-need-to-know-about-cloa-title/">Things you need to know about CLOA Title</a></em></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Should you invest in a CLOA titled land?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The straight answer to this is unless the CLAO titled is over 10 years old or the current owner or beneficiary had fully compensated the original owner of the land is when it is safe to buy the property. Make sure to do your due diligence and look up the legality of the property you are buying - regardless if it is CLOA titled or otherwise.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/07/Is-it-safe-to-buy-a-property-with-CLOA-Title-2.png','views' => '796','category_id' => '15','published_at' => '2021-07-08 01:22:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '599','title' => 'Homebuyer Tips | When is the best time to buy a property?','slug' => 'homebuyer-tips-when-is-the-best-time-to-buy-a-property','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When buying a house timing is not crucial but it is a big factor. When investing in a property, homebuyers attempt to predict the property values if these are on the rise or fall while also checking out the mortgage rates that may follow.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>But when is the best time to buy a property?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Buy only after you\'ve visited the site</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Many homebuyers check out images and videos online on the property listings. And while that is an ideal way to go at it especially when you are unable to visit the site, it is still best to see the location for yourself.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You need to visit the area where the building or community will be put up so you can check out the neighbouring community and other business establishments nearby. You will also see first hand the traffic leading to the property, schools that are available for your kids, and even check if the property gets flooded in the rainy season or gets pretty hot during the summer days.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7371,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Buy-a-home-or-property-01-1024x576.png" alt="" class="wp-image-7371"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Buy during pre-selling stage of the build</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Pre-selling homes are much cheaper than getting a ready to occupy property. Pre-selling price is an introductory rate to attract homebuyers to invest and buy a property in that development. You can save as much as 30-40% than buying a finished or built one. Developer would also throw in 5-15% discounts and/or offer flexible payment schemes during this stage to lure in more buyers. Not only are you getting a new home but you are getting it cheaper and by the time your home gets turn over, it\'s market value will have increased.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7372,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Buy-a-home-or-property-02-1024x576.png" alt="" class="wp-image-7372"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Buy when the market is low</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Real estate value is very tricky to predict when it rise or falls. Properties get easily snatched and developed, so when you think you want to wait for a few more years before buying the property that you like, it might have already gone up. When areas and communities get developed, the market value surrounding it will also increase. And since there is the constant need for infrastructure and community development, there is low chances for property values to actually decrease.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>But the best time that the market is low is buying a property now or in the present before it increases.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7373,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Buy-a-home-or-property-03-1024x576.png" alt="" class="wp-image-7373"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Buy when you can afford it</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>However given with all the factors to consider on when to best buy a home the most definite answer is when you can afford to. Before you get into the homebuying process, you should check your finances and see if you can afford the payments. Buying a home is a big financial move, you need to pay reservation fee, downpayment or equity, move-in and utility service fee and monthly mortgage, etc. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So when you have the money and budget for it, there is no stopping you from buying that dream home.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/07/When-is-the-best-time-to-buy-a-property-.png','views' => '90','category_id' => '13','published_at' => '2021-07-12 02:55:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '600','title' => 'Filipino Homes launched FH CRM Plus for brokers and agents','slug' => 'fh-crm-plus','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes, the leading real estate service solutions provider in the country, has launched FH CRM Plus, a FREE world-class customer relationship management tool for its agents and brokers. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://scontent.fmnl13-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.6435-9/230960187_10220323418578331_3974668318609743539_n.jpg?_nc_cat=102&amp;ccb=1-5&amp;_nc_sid=730e14&amp;_nc_ohc=ijL0UoliSAcAX-37Ndc&amp;tn=By_9R0LsGFcaUw8n&amp;_nc_ht=scontent.fmnl13-2.fna&amp;oh=5242a3e0790250b766f15d5f20e53bc1&amp;oe=61433AD6" alt="May be an image of text that says \'FILIPINO HOMES. COM RENT| CREATING A NEW INTEGRATED REAL ESTATE PLATFORM IN THE PHILIPPINES FH CRM PLUS DESIGNED TO HAND-HOLD PROPERTY BROKERS AND AGENTS TO THRIVE IN THE NEW NORMAL ITS FEATURES INCLUDE Built-in reminder features. Contact management. This feature allows organize contacts, contains client details inquirie groups better cater them. Customizable agent daily remember meetings, deadlines and other important dates. own workflow. User-friendly. Ûotware easy-to-use, reliable seamless functionality that allows agent to focus his most mportant task. Available Tailored-fit to cater your system for project selling, brokerage and rental 24/7\'"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This app is designed to help real estate practitioners <a href="http://localhost:3001/5-things-real-estate-agents-can-do-now-to-adjust-to-the-new-normal/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">thrive in the new normal</a>.  The tool will aid agents and brokers attain greater efficiency and better client organization through integrated profiles and combining real estate marketing and sales tasks that help strengthen customer connections. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7392,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/image-1024x576.png" alt="Filipino Homes CRM Plus for agents and brokers" class="wp-image-7392"/><figcaption>Filipino Homes CRM Plus </figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Its features include contact management, built-in reminder features, a user-friendly interface, customizable design, and available online 24/7.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Filipino Homes CRM Plus allows users to:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Create a label for the tasks and client profiles (ex. Brokerage Sales, Rentals, etc.) </li><li>Move items anytime by dragging to where the action is </li><li>Create fields like phone numbers, email addresses, etc for contact management</li><li>Customize the app layout to your style, and more!</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes brokers and agents may access the software via the Dashboard. Agents may also contact their team leader with any questions about the app. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Filipino Homes has launched FH CRM Plus, a FREE world-class customer relationship management tool for its agents and brokers. ','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/08/Filipino-Homes-blog-11.png','views' => '67','category_id' => '16','published_at' => '2021-08-19 13:55:28','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '601','title' => 'Xavier Ateneo, Cebu Landmasters seal agreement on the ‘Campus of the Future’ and University Township in CDO','slug' => 'xavier-ateneo-cebu-landmasters-seal-agreement-on-the-campus-of-the-future-and-university-township-in-cdo','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Cebu Landmasters Inc. (CLI), the leading VisMin developer, has signed a Memorandum of Agreement (MOA) on August 20, 2021, to purchase 14.3 hectares of Xavier University – Ateneo de Cagayan\'s Manresa Property in uptown Cagayan de Oro City. The proceeds will be utilized to build the new 21-hectare XU Masterson Campus dubbed as “Campus of the Future”, which will be three times larger in area than the current campus. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image -->
<figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="https://scontent.fcgy1-1.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.6435-9/234151870_4308522159228068_3584628620133237358_n.jpg?_nc_cat=1&amp;ccb=1-5&amp;_nc_sid=730e14&amp;_nc_ohc=P82HtjTKhogAX_h2ho3&amp;_nc_ht=scontent.fcgy1-1.fna&amp;oh=6adb6ef752c6445abc79ac538fea1026&amp;oe=6145516F" alt="May be an image of 4 people and people standing"/><figcaption>(L-R): Engr. Lennie K. Ong (Xavier University Ateneo de Cagayan Treasurer), Fr. Mars P. Tan, SJ (Xavier University Ateneo de Cagayan President), Jose R. Soberano III (Cebu Landmasters Chairman &amp; CEO), Jose Franco B. Soberano (Cebu Landmasters Executive Vice President and Chief Operating Officer)</figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:gallery {"ids":[7407,7408]} -->
<figure class="wp-block-gallery columns-2 is-cropped"><ul class="blocks-gallery-grid"><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/239635721_1309494702839749_3356422129378669971_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="7407" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/239635721_1309494702839749_3356422129378669971_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=7407" class="wp-image-7407"/></figure></li><li class="blocks-gallery-item"><figure><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/239062042_532671298019685_1526683497142284457_n.jpg" alt="" data-id="7408" data-full-url="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/239062042_532671298019685_1526683497142284457_n.jpg" data-link="https://filipinohomes.com/blog/?attachment_id=7408" class="wp-image-7408"/></figure></li></ul></figure>
<!-- /wp:gallery -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Vatican has approved the provisions in the agreement written by Xavier University and endorsed by Jesuit leadership in the Philippines and Rome after a two-year review process. This came after a series of meetings with XU employees, students, alumni, parents, CDO officials, clergy, and other members of the CDO community in 2019.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:video {"id":7406} -->
<figure class="wp-block-video"><video controls src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/10000000_258683495879188_2552014642683684872_n.mp4"></video></figure>
<!-- /wp:video -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The primary planning components include the main plaza, interconnecting courtyards, campus-wide wifi connection, bike lanes, sports facilities, an amphitheater, and a University Forum that includes a museum, theatre, and gallery.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7409,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/234495391_4308522975894653_4011338950477660272_n-1024x576.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7409"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Masterson Campus has state-of-the-art school buildings and administrative facilities to support XU\'s colleges and schools\' academic programs. It will be adaptive to changes in academic fields, curricula for 21st-century learning, and technological advancements. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This “Campus of the Future” aims for a more socially relevant and inclusive learning institution focused on strengthening Xavier University’s colleges and schools. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7410,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/234495391_4308522975894653_4011338950477660272_n-1-1024x576.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7410"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><br>The XU Masterson Campus masterplan will blend seamlessly with the adjacent Manresa Town, which will be developed by Cebu Landmasters, a 14.3-hectare mixed-use university town with generous open spaces that will provide XU students with convenient and safe residential options, easy access to commercial establishments, and future-ready offices. The University Town idea offers substantial synergies that benefit both XU and the uptown CDO neighborhood.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7411,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/234205324_4308522699228014_7773178966075600925_n-1024x576.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7411"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The project will be built in phases, with campus development scheduled to begin in the second quarter of 2022.<br></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>More details here: <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.cebulandmasters.com/news/xavier-ateneo-cebu-landmasters-seal-agreement-on-the-campus-of-the-future-and-university-township-in-cdo/" target="_blank">CLI PR/Disclosure</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/08/Filipino-Homes-blog-12.png','views' => '48','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2021-08-21 11:20:55','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '602','title' => 'Filipino Homes Facebook page is now verified!','slug' => 'filipino-homes-facebook-page-is-now-verified','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The <a href="https://www.facebook.com/filipinohomes/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Filipino Homes</a> Facebook Page now bears the Blue Check, showing that it is already a Verified account representing a reputable brand name and a company of public interest. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7419,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><a href="https://www.facebook.com/filipinohomes" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/verified-FB-page-1024x536.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7419"/></a></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":1} -->
<h1><strong>What does this mean?</strong></h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The blue checkmark or verified badge  <img alt="" src="https://static.xx.fbcdn.net/assets/?revision=1494502497564782&amp;name=fb-verifiedbadge-desktop&amp;density=1">  that appears next to a Facebook Page name means that Facebook has confirmed that the Page is the authentic presence of the brand it represents. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7418,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><a href="https://www.facebook.com/filipinohomes" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/image-1024x491.png" alt="" class="wp-image-7418"/></a></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The verified badge is a tool to help people find brands\' real Pages. A Page with a verified badge means that it represents what it says it does. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The badge is a testament to Filipino Homes\' commitment to continue to be the largest comprehensive real estate solutions portal in the Philippines, providing one-stop-shop services for real estate buyers and sellers. This one-of-its-kind facility connects people to all related products and services in the real estate business.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It provides much-needed market information, extensive property listings, statistics, experts\' industry assessments, events, and activities to assist clients to make sound decisions.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you haven\'t yet, like and follow our verified Facebook page at <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://www.facebook.com/filipinohomes/" target="_blank">Filipino Homes</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/09/verified-FB-page.jpg','views' => '48','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2021-09-08 08:54:18','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '603','title' => 'Apartment Hunting Tips for Renters','slug' => 'apartment-hunting-tips-for-renters','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Apartment hunting can be very daunting for some potential renters. Often the variety of options available to these renters is a source of overwhelming frustration for the renters. With so many appealing options it can be difficult to choose just one. However, there are some tips that can help to ease the process of apartment hunting. The process of finding the perfect apartment can be broken down into three simple steps. The first step is to set a budget. Next, the renter should research their available options and then comparison shop to determine which option is the best.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Set a Budget First</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":2342,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/pool-money-with-family-and-friends-real-estate-investment-filipinohomes.jpg" alt="pool money with family and friends real estate investment filipinohomes" class="wp-image-2342"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For many renters, the most important consideration is how much they are willing to spend on an apartment per month. For this reason, it should come as no surprise that the first step in the apartment hunting process should include establishing a budget. Renters should consider their monthly income and subtract out all of their monthly expenses from this amount. Monthly expenses should include all bills which are paid regularly as well as money spent on food, entertainment, and miscellaneous items each month. The renter may also wish to subtract out an additional amount to allow for some savings each month as well as emergencies. The total left after these subtractions is the amount the renter is able to spend on an apartment per month. Once this amount is established the renter will have a better understanding of the type of apartment they are able to afford.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Research Available Properties</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7440,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Fullscreen-capture-19102021-10513-AM.bmp-1024x503.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7440"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Once a budget has been established, the renter should begin researching the properties which fall within his budget range. It is likely to consider properties that are slightly above the range as well as properties that are slightly below the range. Doing this will allow the renter to see if there is an opportunity to either make improvements on the amount of monthly spending to allow for the renting of more expensive property. The renter can also determine whether or not they feel there is the opportunity to negotiate a lower rental rate on a particular property.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When initially researching properties, the renter does not necessarily have to visit each property. Most of the pricing information can be obtained from resources such as Internet websites, newspapers, and rental magazines. Since pricing is the primary concern at this point, the initial research will enable the renter to eliminate properties that are too far out of their price range.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Comparison Shop</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":7441,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/gathering-options.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7441"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Once the renter has narrowed down his list of possible apartment complexes to a more manageable number it is time to start visiting these properties. It is during this step that the renter will really get a feel for the quality of the apartment as well as the amount and quality of amenities offered by the complex. This is very important because this information can be used to decide between properties that are otherwise very similar.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The comparison shopping process is also worthwhile because it gives the renter some bargaining power in negotiating more favorable rent rates. Renters who have visited a number of apartments likely have a good idea of the going rate in a particular area for a particular size apartment. These renters can use this information to potentially convince some leasing agents to lower their prices at least a little bit. There will not likely be huge drops in price from these negotiations but it will likely be enough to be considered worthwhile.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you are not comfortable enough to do the hassle of having to scout rental properties that are within your budget, you can choose to work with a Rent Manager.<a href="http://www.rentmanager.ph" data-type="URL" data-id="www.rentmanager.ph"> </a><a href="http://www.rent.ph" data-type="URL" data-id="www.rent.ph">Rent Manager</a><a href="http://www.rentmanager.ph" data-type="URL" data-id="www.rentmanager.ph">s</a> are trained professionals that can help you with your renting needs. Search for the available Certified Rent Manager in your area here. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Apartment hunting can be very daunting for some potential renters. Often the variety of options available to these renters is a source of overwhelming frustration for the renters. With so many appealing options it can be difficult to choose just one. However,>>> READ MORE ','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/10/REAL-ESTATE-SUPERSTARS.jpg','views' => '54','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2021-10-19 00:08:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '604','title' => 'Benefits of Renting','slug' => 'benefits-of-renting','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>While there are some renters who view renting an apartment/condominium or a house as a failure, there are others who see the benefits there are to be gained from renting a property as opposed to purchasing a property. Some of the benefits of renting include the ability to save money while renting for the purpose of purchasing a home, few maintenance requirements, and the inclusion of amenities that the renter would not likely be able to afford if they were to purchase a home instead of renting. Although there are some negative aspects to renting an apartment, this article will focus exclusively on the benefits of renting a property.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>The Ability to Save Money</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":6054,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Filipino-Homes-Philippines-1.png" alt="" class="wp-image-6054"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Being able to save up a great deal of money for the purpose of making a down payment on a dream home is just one of the many great advantages of renting a property. Many homeowners were able to realize their dream of homeownership only after living in a rental property for a certain amount of time. Although renting is often criticized as throwing money away because it does not result in equity, the ability to save money while renting is unparalleled</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Rent for an apartment is usually considerably less expensive than the monthly mortgage on a home. The home is also typically much bigger than the rental property but in cases where the renter is renting for the sole purpose of saving money, the value of renting cannot be denied. Depending on how long the renter stays in the apartment, they may save hundreds or even thousands of pesos during the course of the rental agreement.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>No Maintenance Properties</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":4671,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/plumber-228010_1280-1024x680.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-4671"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Another advantage to renting a property is it is typically little or no maintenance required by the renter. This is especially true in an apartment situation. The renter may be responsible for small items such as changing light bulbs but more extensive repairs such as leaks in plumbing or clogs in drains are typically handled by the maintenance staff of the rental property.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Additionally, common areas such as grassy areas or gardens are maintained by the maintenance staff. The exception is usually when the renter rents a home as opposed to the apartment. In these cases, the renter may still not be responsible for small repairs but might be obligated to take care of items such as maintaining the grass.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Worthwhile Amenities</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://www.brickunderground.com/sites/default/files/styles/blog_primary_image/public/blog/images/180622OverratedAmenitiesComp.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Another advantage to apartment living is often the amenities offered to the residence. Such amenities might include the usage of the pool, an exercise room, meeting spaces, and a function room. In most cases, these amenities are offered free of charge to resident and their guests. Many renters who might be able to purchase a home would not likely be able to purchase a home with amenities such as a pool, fully equipped exercise room, and a  function room or party hall.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>These items are often considered luxurious and are not available in the majority of homes that are on the market at any particular time. In fact, searching for homes that specifically have these features may severely limit the number of search results and may result in no search results at all when these features are searched in conjunction with a typical price range. However, those who rent can enjoy access to these amenities. They may pay more in rent than those in a comparable apartment complex without these amenities but they are also still likely saving a considerable amount of money each month as long as they are budgeting wisely and have chosen a rental property within their price range.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>How about you? Would you rather rent or buy a home? Whether you are looking for a property to rent or a property to buy, contact your Filipino Homes Agents and Rent Managers to help you with your property needs. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'While there are some renters who view renting an apartment/condominium or a house as a failure, there are others who see the benefits there are to be gained from renting a property as opposed to purchasing a property. Some of the benefits of renting include ... >>>READ MORE','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/10/REAL-ESTATE-SUPERSTARS-1.jpg','views' => '66','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2021-10-20 15:48:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '605','title' => 'What to watch for in Bank Financing','slug' => 'what-to-watch-for-in-bank-financing','content' => '<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://youinc.com/cached_images/stories/full/how-to-get-bank-financing-1920x800.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Philippines is experiencing a transformation in real estate financing. In the past decades, banks were highly conservative concerning real estate lending. Today, real estate is one of their favorites.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Two vital factors affect real estate finance; </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:columns {"verticalAlignment":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-columns are-vertically-aligned-center"><!-- wp:column {"verticalAlignment":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-column is-vertically-aligned-center"><!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} -->
<ol><li>Interest Rate</li><li>Term of the Loans</li></ol>
<!-- /wp:list --></div>
<!-- /wp:column -->

<!-- wp:column {"verticalAlignment":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-column is-vertically-aligned-center"><!-- wp:image {"id":7451,"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/1-164-1024x683.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7451"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image --></div>
<!-- /wp:column --></div>
<!-- /wp:columns -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Interest rates have plunged from highs of 18-24% several decades ago to lows of 5-8% today. Loan periods have also become more lengthy, and some banks today offer up to 20 years. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>These low-interest rates are now desirable for consumers the borrowers. Since our economy today is experiencing much money in banks, finance institutions tend to be more relaxed and approve the majority of loans, most especially for real estate loans. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As the consumer, here are things to watch for in Bank Financing;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>1. <strong>Look for the lowest interest rates available.</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://media.istockphoto.com/photos/wooden-blocks-with-percentage-sign-and-down-arrow-financial-recession-picture-id1227064262?k=20&amp;m=1227064262&amp;s=612x612&amp;w=0&amp;h=_U83PRBCGd4x4E0KKCrbG3PmaMYqCoBblpY76BTtiYA=" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Lowest does not just mean nominal rates. Some banks offer a rate that may seem very low but are good for only one year and re-priceable annually. Thus, it is good to inquire about a bank\'s re-pricing practice. Are the new rates based on an average or just the bank\'s whim? </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>2. Look for a longer-term</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://www.canarahsbclife.com/content/dam/choice/blog-inner/images/benefits-of-limited-premium-payment-term-insurance-plans.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The only purpose of obtaining credit is to make the monthly payment affordable. Otherwise, if you have the cash to spare, something not used for any other more profitable purpose, then no need to borrow on real estate to make the monthly payment affordable; the interest rate should not just be low. However, the loan term should be as long as possible. Nevertheless, the borrower can always accelerate the payment if he becomes more liquid in the future. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><strong>3. Understand the loan provisions</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://www.investopedia.com/thmb/9JU7CSxXBVk3VymAW5l6l6XG_fw=/2121x1414/filters:fill(auto,1)/GettyImages-103405221-8696f029989f4b7bb3270a18ac983aaa.jpg" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It is also essential to read, scrutinize the fine print of the mortgage contract. Find out if there are high closing costs and other hidden charges, such as insurance, appraisal, etc. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Check for the following;</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Prohibited provisions such as "pactum Commissorium" (auto-sale) or "Practicum de non-alienado" (prohibiting sale)</li><li>Conditions that will mean as "default."</li><li>Foreclosure and redemption provisions and costs</li><li>Liquidation provisions, pre-termination charges</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Please take note of these things, as it will be your guide on handling your payments for the loan in the future. Do not be pressured to sign the contract directly without reading these fine prints. If you have questions about what you read, you can verify it with the loan coordinator or officer, and they will gladly explain the conditions to you. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Related articles:</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/homebuyer-tips-when-is-the-best-time-to-buy-a-property/" data-type="post" data-id="7366">Homebuyer Tips | When is the best time to buy a property?</a></li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/credit-score-do-we-have-it-in-the-philippines/" data-type="post" data-id="7231">Credit Score – Do we have it in the Philippines?</a></li><li><a href="http://localhost:3001/how-to-apply-for-a-housing-loan-in-the-philippines-if-you-are-a-foreigner/" data-type="post" data-id="6963">How to apply for a housing loan in the Philippines if you are a foreigner</a></li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->','excerpt' => 'These low-interest rates are now desirable for consumers the borrowers. Since our economy today is experiencing much money in banks, finance institutions tend to be more relaxed and approve the majority of loans, most especially for real estate loans. As the consumer, here are things to watch for in Bank Financing;>>> READ MORE','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/10/filipinohomes-xyzayape.jpg','views' => '51','category_id' => '16','published_at' => '2021-10-25 22:06:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '606','title' => 'PH is not in a Real estate bubble: economists said','slug' => 'ph-is-not-in-a-real-estate-bubble-economists-said','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Despite a rise in construction permits issuance and a drop in the residential real estate price index (RREPI), one economist has dismissed a real estate bubble.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>ING Bank Manila senior economist Nicholas Mapa used statistics from the Philippine Statistics Authority (PSA) to show that building activity increased in the second quarter of 2021 compared to the previous year.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>"This reflects pent-up permits as construction activity was finally allowed to resume in some parts, albeit on a staggered and limited basis," he said in a report released Tuesday, citing the impact of the government\'s movement restrictions imposed last year in response to the rise in coronavirus disease 2019 (Covid-19) infections.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In the second quarter of this year, the PSA announced that the overall number of constructions increased by 114.1 percent year over year.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For one thing, residential development increased by 102.8 percent, owing mostly to those outside the National Capital Region (NCR).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Cavite, Laguna, Batangas, Rizal, and Quezon (Calabarzon) had the most real estate constructions, accounting for 9,773 or 25.5 percent of the total during the time.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>According to Mapa, the increase in residential unit building in Region 4-A "mirrors recent events" reported in the RREPI report by the Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>He claimed the RREPI was remained negative, citing the central bank data, "since the broader market was weighed down by the sharp reduction in condominium prices and prices in the NCR in general."</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>According to Mapa, the same analysis also reveals that housing costs outside of the NCR and for single-family detached homes have increased, as seen by the permits data.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>"This tendency shows that the Philippines is likewise experiencing the worldwide phenomenon of Filipinos seeking more space migrating from urban centers to locations outside the metropolis." It\'s no surprise that, after being confined to the city for more than a year, there is now a natural and healthy demand for land and residences outside of the city."</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The RREPI calculates the average change in prices of various dwelling unit types based on bank-issued real estate loans.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It is used to assess the situation of the domestic real estate and credit markets.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>"As the Philippines intends to experience some type of deurbanization," Mapa added, the tendency of growing residential-related projects in the provinces is likely to enhance developments outside of the national capital.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Despite the increased granting of construction permits, he claims that "signs of a real estate bubble have yet to emerge in a perceptible form."</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>"The BSP\'s RREPI remains negative, and the epidemic appears to have deflated previously inflated condominium values." In the meanwhile, rental inflation has slowed and now stands at 1.1 percent in August," he noted.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Residential real estate prices of different types of new dwelling units fell 4.2 percent year over year and 1.6 percent quarter over quarter in the first quarter of 2021, according to the RREPI, due to decreasing demand due to the pandemic. (Source: <a href="https://www.pna.gov.ph/articles/1153538" data-type="URL" data-id="https://www.pna.gov.ph/articles/1153538">Philippine News Agency</a>)</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'Despite a rise in construction permits issuance and a drop in the residential real estate price index (RREPI), one economist has dismissed a real estate bubble.','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2021/10/REAL-ESTATE-SUPERSTARS-2.jpg','views' => '45','category_id' => '16','published_at' => '2021-10-27 07:00:03','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '607','title' => 'OSHDP Affordable Housing Summit 2021: The Home EveryJuan Deserves','slug' => 'oshdp-affordable-housing-summit-2021-the-home-everyjuan-deserves','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
