<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2022/02/Filipino-Homes-CPD-programs-are-now-PRC-PRBRES-accredited.png','views' => '73','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2022-02-15 05:36:29','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '623','title' => 'Feng Shui in Real Estate Sales','slug' => 'feng-shui-in-real-estate-sales','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Literally translated "Feng" means wind and "Shui" mean water. Deeply rooted in connection to nature, Feng Shui is the 4000-year-old Chinese are of placement and philosophy that supports living in awareness and harmony with our surroundings.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As the awareness of Feng Shui increases, more real estate agents are being asked to show buyers homes with "good" Feng Shui. If a real estate agent has knowledge of this ancient and highly respected design philosophy will assist him/her to:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>Increase the value, marketability, and emotional appeal of a home.</li><li>Build confidence with Feng Shui savvy buyers and sellers.</li><li>Provide solutions to remedy a home\'s Feng Shui energy challenges.</li><li>Build referrals by selling "Feng Shui friendly" homes that support the well-being of your clients and their sphere of influence.</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This section will explain the 5 Feng Shui tips for your reference.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://www.holisticfamilypracticeva.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/feng-shui.jpg" alt="" /></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong><u>Tip 1: Main Entrance</u></strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The main door is like the mouth of the house. It is the gateway between the world and the privacy of the home and air currents literally enter and exit at this point.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>The positioning of the main door can determine the fortune or misfortune of the occupants. Therefore you must keep the entrance clear of any clutter to allow the energies to flow freely.</li><li>Make sure there is nothing in direct alignment with the door such as a tree or telegraph pole. To remedy this place a Bagua mirror over the door so it is reflecting the Sha Qi.</li><li>Avoid facing a dark, pokey room, an interior staircase, mirror, stove, sink, fireplace, the door of a toilet, laundry, bathroom, or bedroom. To remedy this keep the doors closed or place a screen between the doors.</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong><u>Tip 2: Bedrooms</u></strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Bedrooms should be sacred spaces where an adult or child can retreat and regenerate. Most people spent roughly one-third of their lives in their bedroom, so maintaining balance and serenity in this area is essential.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong><u>Tip 3: Kitchen</u></strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In any case, it\'s better if you don\'t see the kitchen immediately upon entering the house, as this can portend digestive, nutritional, and eating problems. Having the kitchen at the entry point can also mean that guests will come over and eat and then leave immediately, and such a placement can also encourage the inhabitants to eat all the time.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong><u>Tip 4: Windows</u></strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A house should have sufficient windows. Windows are very important to allow sufficient light or pleasant views into the room.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong><u>Tip 5: Dining &amp; Living Room</u></strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Whenever possible the dining room should be separate from the living room. It is a social area for family members, thus it better to have it as big as possible.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><strong><u>Summary</u></strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So with the above tips, as a<a href="http://localhost:3001/6-reasons-why-you-should-buy-real-estate-in-december/"> real estate agent </a>when meeting with a Feng Shui savvy buyer, you can use the above tips to talk with them, the chances to close the deal are high because the buyer sees you as knowledgeable in Feng Shui and the property you propose to them must be good in Feng Shui. And this is a very good topic when comes to price negotiation with the sellers, agents with Feng Shui knowledge might be able to negotiate a better selling price for their buyers and close the sale. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For your listings, you may also want to hire an<a href="https://www.facebook.com/propertyprosperityph/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"> expert</a> to give an honest opinion about the property and teach you how to increase the positive energy of the property. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => 'As the awareness of Feng Shui increases, more real estate agents are being asked to show buyers homes with "good" Feng Shui. Knowledge of this ancient and highly respected design philosophy is essential in Real Estate Sales.
','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2022/05/real-estate-philippines-xyza-yape-xyzaspeaks-realtor-blogger-1.jpg','views' => '62','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2022-05-30 05:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '624','title' => 'How to Save for a House in 2022: 5 Ways to Keep Your Money Saving Goals','slug' => 'how-to-save-for-a-house-in-2022-5-ways-to-keep-your-money-saving-goals','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Are you one of the few who really started saving this 2022? <em>We are way halfway through the year and</em> you may be thinking about how you can spend less and save more to finally buy a house. And while setting the intention is a great first step, the most important part is actually following through with it beyond July. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here are some easy ways to keep you on a money-saving spree.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7576,"sizeSlug":"large","linkDestination":"none"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Copy-of-Filipino-Homes-blog-5-1024x576.png" alt="" class="wp-image-7576"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>1. Have a SMART <a href="http://localhost:3001/5-major-reasons-why-you-should-buy-a-home-instead-of-rent/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Goal</a>.</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you\'re saving for a specific goal, you\'re a lot more likely to modify your spending patterns. If you\'re saving up for your dream home, you\'re more likely to stick to a plan if you are anchored to a clear vision of what you want. Take time to map out your plan of action, starting with your SMART goal. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>S-&nbsp;Specific </strong> <em>What do you really want? </em>Be very detailed about what you want in a house. Is there a specific location you want to live in? Do you need to be close to your place of work? Do you need grocery stores and malls within walking distance? Do you want some outdoor space for your pets? How many bedrooms? Do you need a large kitchen space? Consider your lifestyle and your finances. Identify your non-negotiables vs. your nice-to-haves.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>M-&nbsp;Measurable</strong>. <em>Understand your financial capability.</em> One of the most powerful tools for success is measurement. As they say, you can\'t improve what you can\'t measure. Start by tracking your income and expenses, existing debts, and savings for a downpayment. From there, you can set measurement milestones.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><br><strong>A-</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Achievable. </strong><em>What can you afford and by when?</em> Think through all the details. Does it really make sense to purchase a home this year? If not, you might need to consider pushing your timeline a little further as you work on the nitty-gritty of your homeownership goal.<br></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>R-&nbsp;Relevant. </strong><em>Where does "buying a house" fit in your life goals? </em>Take into consideration your short-term plan and long-term vision. Are you building a home for starting or expanding your family? Will you be living in the house you would purchase or would it be a rental property? <strong><br></strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>T-&nbsp;Time-Based</strong>. <em>When can you start the buying process?</em> <em> </em>It might be helpful to define deadlines for each step of your home-buying journey. Set a deadline for each milestone. Instead of just stating, "I will buy a house this year," it will be much better if you get a little more specific:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul><li>I will narrow down my search area to 3 areas by March.</li><li>I will find a real estate professional by May.</li><li>I will establish my home budget by September.</li><li>I will start house hunting by October. </li><li>I will pay the downpayment by December 2022. </li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>2. Track Non-Essential Spending</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Regardless of how large your target savings for your house fund is, you must first figure out where your money is going before calculating how much you can save. Start by reviewing your spending for the previous month on the first day of the next month, categorizing <em>essentials and non-essentials</em>. Non-essentials are "wants," where you can have some wiggle room — shopping, movies, restaurant trips, and maybe spa trips —while essentials (needs) are largely set prices (house rent, car payments, food, etc.).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Be honest and look into what you could go without and make a commitment to putting that money aside. Can you, for example, forego going out to eat twice a week in favor of cooking at home? Or maybe unsubscribe to your cable and just keep Netflix? </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In terms of how much you should save each month, a good starting point is 10% to 20% of your monthly salary. You might also follow the 50-30-20 rule, which recommends allocating 50% of your take-home pay to needs, 30% to wants, and 20% to savings.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>3. Get Rid of High-Interest Debt</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There is no one-size-fits-all way to tackle high-interest debt, which is often associated with credit card bills. Assuming you have some money set aside in an emergency fund, the first thing you should do is pay off high-interest debt before focusing on long-term savings objectives. If, on the other hand, you don\'t have an emergency fund, start there before getting rid of your high-interest debt.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The advantages of paying off high-interest debt are twofold: the sooner you pay it off, the less money you\'ll pay in interest. Plus, once you\'ve paid off the debt, you\'ll be able to put the money you were paying each month into savings. The best thing is that you won\'t notice a difference because you\'re already used to setting aside that amount.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>4. Automate Your Savings</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Schedule a monthly transfer from your payroll account to a connected savings account. This method eliminates the need to remember to make a deposit and decreases the likelihood of you squandering the money before it is saved. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>5. Don’t Spend “Found Money”</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When you have "extra money," like monetary gifts and bonuses, it\'s advisable to put this money toward your savings goals rather than spending it. After all, you won\'t miss it since it wasn\'t in the budget in the first place. This also applies to raises. Instead of overspending, save the difference (but feel free to treat yourself to a little congratulatory present!).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Bonus Tip: </h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Saving money isn’t always easy! If you know a friend, family member, or co-worker who is also trying to save, teaming up with them may help you stay on track. Having an accountability buddy can help you stay motivated and stick to your savings plan. You\'ll be able to discuss your progress, vent about setbacks, and lean on for support.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2022/01/Copy-of-Filipino-Homes-blog-6.png','views' => '48','category_id' => '15','published_at' => '2022-07-25 11:07:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '625','title' => 'Homebuyer Tips: 5 Facebook Groups for Home Design Inspiration','slug' => 'homebuyer-tips-5-facebook-groups-for-home-design-inspiration','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Designing and decorating your own home is a fun and exciting experience, but it can be a little overwhelming. Whatever project you\'re working on in your house, you know you want it to stand out, but you\'re not sure how to do it.   We\'re here to help by pointing you to Facebook groups that can give you home design inspiration. Here are 5 of the best FB groups to get you started on your interior design project.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/615328352487784" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Home Buddies</a></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7612,"sizeSlug":"large","linkDestination":"custom"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/615328352487784" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/image-1024x517.png" alt="" class="wp-image-7612"/></a></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong><a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/615328352487784" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Home Buddies</a></strong> is perhaps one of the most popular Facebook groups of home enthusiasts in the Philippines. This group was created "to be a safe space for home enthusiasts to share inspiration, tips, experiences, finds, and everything in between." With 3 million members as of writing, you will surely find some ideas that will work for you (and your budget!). </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/216747326258976/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Tiny House and Small Space Living</a></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7613,"sizeSlug":"large","linkDestination":"custom"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/216747326258976/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/image-1-1024x522.png" alt="" class="wp-image-7613"/></a></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you prefer a less crowded group and are more interested in tiny house living, the group <strong><a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/216747326258976/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Tiny House and Small Space Living </a></strong>is for you. &nbsp;If you\'re embracing a minimalist lifestyle, you may get some design ideas from members who are living in tiny and container houses. There are lots of recommendations for decors and furniture that are multi-functional and space-saving. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/762218901039953" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Home Design PH ( Native &amp; Modern House)</a></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7614,"sizeSlug":"large","linkDestination":"custom"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/762218901039953" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/image-2-1024x550.png" alt="" class="wp-image-7614"/></a></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For homeowners who are interested in modern bahay-kubo concepts, the <a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/762218901039953" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><strong>Home Design PH (Native &amp; Modern House) </strong></a>Facebook group may be a good fit. The admin and members share low-cost home design ideas that are perfect as farmhouses in a rural area. The posts will also give you an idea of the approximate cost of building your own modern bahay-kubo.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/738251360100136/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Minimalist &amp; Nordic Home Decor PH</a></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7615,"sizeSlug":"large","linkDestination":"custom"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/738251360100136/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/image-3-1024x512.png" alt="" class="wp-image-7615"/></a></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you\'re looking for <a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/738251360100136/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><strong>minimalist and Nordic home decor</strong></a> ideas, this Facebook group is for you. There are sellers, suppliers, and retailers in this space. You\'ll surely get some budol-worthy finds.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2><a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/804373510271924/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Living In A Tiny House Philippines</a></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7624,"sizeSlug":"large","linkDestination":"custom"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/804373510271924/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/image-4-1024x520.png" alt="" class="wp-image-7624"/></a></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A relatively small (and quiet) group on tiny living is the<a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/804373510271924/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"> <strong>Living In A Tiny House Philippines</strong></a> Facebook group. Though it has only around 4,000 members, you will never fall short of inspiration. Members share their experience with tiny living as well as curate design ideas you can re-create in your own home. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2022/02/Homebuyer-Tips-5-Facebook-Groups-for-Home-Design-Inspiration.png','views' => '93','category_id' => '29','published_at' => '2022-07-29 10:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '626','title' => 'ACRES Philippines established to protect licensed real estate agents','slug' => 'acres-philippines-established-to-protect-licensed-real-estate-agents','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Accredited Real Estate Salespersons in the Philippines (ACRES Philippines) has been established to widen their opportunities in anticipation of a significant boom in the real estate market in a post-pandemic era.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The organization was founded in 2020 and registered with the Securities and Exchange Commission on February 15, 2021. It envisions to represent salespeople in the real estate industry and has a mission to enable and empower licensed practitioners to become highly ethical and knowledgeable professionals in their real estate practice.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7644,"sizeSlug":"large","linkDestination":"none"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/Anthony-Leuterio-president-of-A-Better-Real-Estate-Philippines-ABREP-796x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7644" /><figcaption><strong>Anthony Leuterio,</strong> <em>president of&nbsp;A Better Real Estate Philippines (ABREP)</em></figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>ACRES Philippines also strives to raise the standards and level the playing field in real estate selling while also supporting&nbsp;the&nbsp;growth&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;real&nbsp;estate&nbsp;business&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;face&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;challenges&nbsp;and&nbsp;uncertainties&nbsp;of&nbsp;the present times.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Anthony Leuterio</strong>, the president of A Better Real Estate Philippines (ABREP), the mother organization of ACRES, says that the founding of this new organization is crucial because salespeople are on the frontlines and are therefore the lifeblood and biggest contributor to real estate development sales. They also make up the largest group of real estate service professionals.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leuterio&nbsp;also added&nbsp;that&nbsp;the&nbsp;establishment&nbsp;of&nbsp;ACRES&nbsp;was&nbsp;a&nbsp;first&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;industry as most&nbsp;of&nbsp;real estate-related groups in the nation catered mostly to brokers and other real estate service providers outside of the sales and marketing sector.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>“It is high time that our real estate salesforce need to be represented and for both industry practitioners (salesperson and brokers) to work together and be united in helping the industry reap better results at post-pandemic,” he said, pointing out that real estate also experienced a rocky performance since the pandemic happened in 2020, taking a toll on several aspects of the economy, which had the unfortunate effect of dampening the outlook for the sector even now.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The establishment of ACRES will also help in developing better laws and policies in the country to hasten the development of the sector. It will operate as a catalyst to modify real estate regulations that are now thought to be out of date and unnecessary, and it will represent industry professionals in advocating for a better, more inclusive agenda that will maximize potential for the business.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The group will also act as a watchdog against the sale of anomalous properties, shady developers, and anyone who falsely advertise projects, or any questionable land ownership.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>According to Leuterio, the establishment of this body will aid in policing the sector against the growth of unauthorized practitioners or colorum salespeople.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Each city in the nation will elect officers for ACRES. Salespeople now have a group to turn to if they come into issues with real estate after being organized.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leuterio stated that they intend for the new group to have between 20,000 and 50,000 salespeople as members, but they must first register with the Professional Regulation Commission (PRC).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2022/07/ACRES-Philippines-established-to-protect-licensed-real-estate-agents.png','views' => '52','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2022-07-29 10:56:13','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '627','title' => 'Freelancers:  How to Get Your Finances Ready to Buy a House','slug' => 'freelancers-how-to-get-your-finances-ready-to-buy-a-house','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When buying a property, you wouldn\'t want to cancel your purchase because you\'re unable to keep up with the amortizations. The disadvantage of not being able to continue with your monthly payments is that you will never receive a full refund on all of your payments. You may be entitled to refunds, but these may range from 50% up to 90% of the total payments you have made, depending on your situation. To make matters worse, you\'ll have to wait for a period of maybe a few months to a year, and in some cases even longer, to receive your refund. As you can see, it\'s a tedious and stressful process. Imagine losing that much money!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>READ:</strong>  <a href="http://localhost:3001/maceda-law-need-know/">Maceda Law | What You Need To Know</a> </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Especially as freelancers with irregular cash inflows, careful planning and decision-making are important so that you avoid experiencing the inconvenience and losses of canceling your property purchase. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7606,"width":768,"height":432,"style":{"color":[]}} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image is-resized"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/Copy-of-Filipino-Homes-blog-9-1024x576.png" alt="Freelancers: How to Get Your Finances Ready to Buy a House" class="wp-image-7606" width="768" height="432"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Before you decide...</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Before&nbsp;you&nbsp;decide&nbsp;to&nbsp;buy&nbsp;a&nbsp;house,&nbsp;know&nbsp;whether&nbsp;or&nbsp;not&nbsp;you&nbsp;are&nbsp;financially ready&nbsp;to&nbsp;purchase&nbsp;your&nbsp;ideal&nbsp;home. But&nbsp;how&nbsp;can&nbsp;you&nbsp;determine&nbsp;if&nbsp;you\'re&nbsp;ready&nbsp;or not? You should look beyond your bank account and the property\'s listing price. Here are some things to think about before meeting with real estate agents and fantasizing about your new homeowner lifestyle.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>1. Build your financial foundation.</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Before buying a house, whether it\'s for you to live in or as an investment, make sure you have enough savings to meet any financial emergencies or future bills. If you want to be financially secure, you should have a savings or emergency fund before placing a downpayment on a property.  Ideally, an emergency fund should be enough to cover your expenses for 3-6 months. As freelancers, it is wise to have <strong>at least 6 months\' expenses in cash or near-cash assets.</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>2.  Keep your consumer debt under control.</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Before buying a home, consider your debt-to-income ratio, which is the percentage of your gross monthly income that goes toward debt payments. Ideally, your monthly debt payments should not exceed 40% of your gross monthly income. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Homeownership is still a debt in a different form. Unless you pay cash, buying a property in the Philippines is almost always tied to either bank or PAG-IBIG financing. If you\'re currently paying off a large credit card debt or an auto loan, taking on a new financial duty may be challenging.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>3.  Have a stable job or source of income</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you buy a house or a condo, you will have to pay monthly amortizations. You\'ll also need a steady source of income to pay the monthly amortizations.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>One of the things that banks and lenders look for is financial stability. This is why they want proof of work and income before obtaining a mortgage. As a freelancer, you would need to show proof that you have a stable source of income. Be prepared to show proof of source of income such as Certificate of Employment or Certificate of Engagement from your clients. If you use Upwork, you may get a Certificate of Earnings. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you want to purchase a property in the Philippines, you need to have worked for at least a year or run a business for at least two years.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>4.  Know how much you can spend on a new home in your budget.</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Before looking at properties you would want to purchase, look at your budget to see how much you can afford. Many lenders suggest that your home costs should be no more than 28% of your total monthly income. So, if your monthly gross income is P50,000, your monthly mortgage payments for your new home should not exceed P14,000. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Consider if you have any additional expensive expenses, such as your children\'s college tuition or a car loan. Use the figure you came up with as a starting point for determining how much house you can realistically afford.  Make sure that you can still live comfortably, even with the mortgage.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>5.  Save up extra money for the downpayment or renovation.</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you\'re purchasing a condo, set aside at least 5% of the purchase price as a downpayment. For example, a studio apartment costs roughly PHP 1.5 million, so plan on putting down around PHP 75,000 as a downpayment, which can be made all at once or over several months.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Homes for sale that are eligible for PAG-IBIG financing, on the other hand, do not require a downpayment. There may, however, be some processing costs. Also, keep in mind that some of the housing units for sale may have been abandoned for a long time or may not have been repaired or remodeled. To make it livable or ready for occupation, you may require at least PHP 100,000.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Also, take note that the cost of owning a house does not end with the mortgage payment. Moving fees, furniture, parking spots, association dues if you live in a condo or planned community, house repairs, and other expenses must be included in your budget. Keep in mind that you\'re in this for the long haul, so your finances should reflect that.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ</strong>:   <a href="http://localhost:3001/financially-prepared-buy-first-home/">How to be Financially Prepared to Buy Your First Home</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2022/02/Copy-of-Filipino-Homes-blog-8.png','views' => '47','category_id' => '15','published_at' => '2022-08-01 01:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '628','title' => 'Basic Real Estate Terms You Need to Know','slug' => 'basic-real-estate-terms-you-need-to-know','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For first-time homebuyers, purchasing a property can be a little bit challenging or overwhelming. Before you begin the buying process, you should have a basic awareness of important real estate principles. This will not only save you money in the long run, but it will also offer you peace of mind. Here are some <strong>basic real estate terms you need to know.</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Ready For Occupancy (RFO) </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The property/unit you are purchasing is already livable. Thus, the buyer needs to pay spot cash downpayment (usually 10% - 20% of the total contract price) so he/she can move in, considering the bank loan has been approved and ready for a take-out loan.<br></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ:  <a href="http://localhost:3001/ready-for-occupancy-condo-unit/">Advantages of Buying a Ready-for-Occupancy (RFO) Condo Unit</a> </p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Preselling </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The property is not yet built, or the construction has just been started. Thus, the buyer only needs to pay the monthly equity (downpayment which is divided into a number of months, mostly equivalent to the turnover date of the property). Preselling is much cheaper than RFO.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ:  <a href="http://localhost:3001/pre-selling-properties/">Should you Invest in Pre-selling Properties in the Philippines?</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3><br>Assumed property, equity period </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This means that the owner is still paying the monthly equity. The new buyer needs to pay spot cash called <em>assumed price</em> to the owner, then the new owner will continue paying the remaining equity as well as the loanable amount either through a bank or PAG-IBIG financing.<br></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Assumed property, bank loan period </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This means that the owner has paid the downpayment in full, and has started paying the monthly amortization. The new buyer needs to pay spot cash called <em>assumed price</em> to the owner, which is usually the sum of all payments the owner made + possible ROI.&nbsp;The new owner will then continue paying the remaining loanable amount either through a bank or PAG-IBIG financing.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Equity&nbsp; </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is the amount that represents the difference between the selling price and loanable amount.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Transfer charges</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is the amount the buyer will need to pay for the processing of&nbsp;the condo or lot title before the turnover of his/her unit.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Condominium Certificate of Title &nbsp;</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is the title that provides evidence of ownership of a condominium. Verification and registration of title certificates is done through the local Land Registration Authority.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Transfer Certificate of Title&nbsp;</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is the title that provides evidence of ownership of a property. Verification and registration of title certificates is done through the local Land Registration Authority.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>READ:  <a href="http://localhost:3001/basic-real-estate-terms-definitions/">Basic Real Estate Terms and Definitions For Home Buyers</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2022/02/Basic-Real-Estate-Terms-You-Need-to-Know.png','views' => '118','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2022-08-07 23:00:00','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '629','title' => '7 Important Tips for Your Retirement Home Search','slug' => '7-tips-for-your-retirement-home-search','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As you approach retirement, you\'ll probably want to look for a new home. You could choose to leave a place where you\'ve worked for a long time, relocate closer to relatives, or just invest in a house that will better suit your needs as you ease into retirement.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In this post, we\'ll share our top 7 tips to make your retirement home search easier.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7560,"sizeSlug":"large","linkDestination":"none"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Copy-of-Filipino-Homes-blog-1-1024x576.png" alt="7 Tips for Your Retirement Home Search | Filipino Homes" class="wp-image-7560" /></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>Tips for Finding a Retirement Property</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>1.  Identify your goals.&nbsp;</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It\'s helpful to know exactly what you\'re looking for before you start looking. Are you seeking for a place to live that is closer to your family? Is it important to be within a short distance to particular stores? Are you looking for your dream retirement home, and if so, what features will make it so?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>2. Know whether to buy or rent.&nbsp;</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The idea that homebuying is fundamentally better than renting is deeply ingrained in our culture. However, renting may be a more cost-effective choice for you, and you should consider it. It may also be beneficial to have a landlord who is responsible for regular upkeep and repairs.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p>Read: <a href="http://localhost:3001/benefits-of-renting/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Benefits of Renting</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>3.  <strong>Focus on long-term living</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Most retirees aren\'t going to move every few years. Moving becomes more difficult and less necessary as you get older, so take your time and concentrate on locating a house where you can envision yourself spending the rest of your life. That means spending more time examining each property and considering your needs years, if not decades, in the future.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>4.  Check nearby amenities</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Speaking of long-term living, consider also the availability of amenities within the neighborhood, such as malls, grocery stores, parks, etc. Make sure to check the property\'s proximity to a quality hospital. Especially if you prefer to move in the province, make sure to check if the nearby healthcare facilities have specialists or available machines or facilities. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>5. Look for a gated community. </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There\'s so much value in having guards or admins to check on the residents. You can also walk around the village safely. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>6. Consider accessibility to public transport. </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Nowadays, it can be a challenge to get stay-in help (driver or maid), so it would be good to consider their commute as well.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3>7. Work with a realtor</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Unless you\'re an expert real estate buyer or seller, you\'ll want to work with a licensed real estate agent. These professionals can assist you in understanding your goals, narrowing the list of homes that fit your needs, and helping you get the best value for your hard-earned money. The process will be simpler, faster, and clearer for you. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2022/01/Copy-of-Filipino-Homes-blog.png','views' => '61','category_id' => '15','published_at' => '2022-08-15 00:00:49','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '630','title' => 'Top 3 Real Estate Investment Tips for Freelancers','slug' => 'top-3-real-estate-investment-tips-for-freelancers','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The<strong> real estate market</strong> is one of the most popular investments for a lot of people. But is it possible for freelancers with variable cash flows to invest in real estate? It can be if you take these 3 tips into consideration:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7568,"sizeSlug":"large","linkDestination":"none"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Copy-of-Filipino-Homes-blog-3-1024x576.png" alt="Top 3 Real Estate Investment Tips for Freelancers | Filipino Homes" class="wp-image-7568" /></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>1. Have your finances in order.</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Before investing, you have to make sure you have a solid financial foundation.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With a freelancer\'s irregular income, money management can be tough. You may be aware of your outflow of money through expenses, but not the inflows. That\'s why freelancers need a well-devised plan. Here are some points to help you develop a sound financial plan:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Create other sources of income:</strong>&nbsp;With your freelance income being irregular, having a steady cash inflow becomes important. The second stream of income will provide stability to your life.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Get rid of debt: </strong>Prioritize eliminating your debt. Track your spending, and set up a budget. Develop a plan to pay off your debt, and you will save on interest in the long run.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Build your emergency fund: </strong>As freelancers with irregular income, you might need to double your emergency fund. Your emergency fund should cover expenses for a year. It should be available at the bank in the form of cash or near-cash. Apart from ordinary home costs, this will be useful in the event of an emergency. The fund will also assist you in keeping track of your spending and will help you avoid costly credit card and personal loan debt.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Insurance: </strong>Make sure you have both health and life insurance for yourself. This will help you in covering the hospital bills or in case of emergencies. The life insurance coverage should be 10 times that of your annual income. Health insurance also becomes important because you do not have an employer who provides for it.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>BONUS TIP:  </strong><a href="http://lovettejam.com/financial-planning-session/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Contact a financial advisor to help you with your financial planning.</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>2. Consider what type of investor you are </h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When you start to invest in any market, it is important that you determine your risk appetite —&nbsp;or how much investment risk you can handle. You need to consider these 3 questions:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>How much investment risk can I take?</strong>  If you want to achieve a certain amount of financial growth, you need to have financial and emotional tolerance for risk. If you are uncomfortable with market fluctuations, you might want to think about investing in vehicles that have lesser risk.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>What is my investment goal? </strong>Looking into the bigger picture can help you decide which investment vehicles to put your money into.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>What is my investment timeframe?</strong> If you are expecting returns in the short term, your risk appetite would be low, since your priority is capital preservation. On the other hand, if you’re planning to go the long-term route, then your&nbsp;risk appetite&nbsp;would need to be moderate to high, since you would be staying invested for quite a bit of time, you can afford to take a little bit of calculated risk.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Answering the 3 questions above can help you determine if you are a conservative, moderate, or aggressive investor.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>BONUS TIP:  </strong>Do not invest in an area that\'s too risky for your level of comfort or financial capacity.</p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>3.  Consider your cash flow situation and how it relates to investing in real estate</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you have a low income, don\'t invest in large-scale properties with multiple units because it will be difficult for your cash flow to keep up with the payments on such properties, as well as meet other responsibilities. There are opportunities available at a lower cost, such as pre-selling condominium units. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you don’t have the time and resources to be hands-on, you can take real estate investing to the stock market through Real Estate Investment Trusts&nbsp;(REIT). REITs are great ways to invest in real estate without being actively involved.&nbsp;A REIT is essentially a company that invests in income-producing properties like shopping malls, office spaces, hospitals, or condominiums. REIT shares are traded on stock exchanges, meaning investors can instantly invest in a diverse portfolio of properties by simply placing an order.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2022/01/Copy-of-Filipino-Homes-blog-2.png','views' => '64','category_id' => '15','published_at' => '2022-08-22 10:06:17','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '631','title' => 'Home Buyer\'s Checklist:  Things You Need Before Buying Your First Home','slug' => 'home-buyers-checklist-things-you-need-before-buying-your-first-home','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Buying your first home isn\'t just about finding a beautiful place that suits your needs. You have to do your homework before you start looking at houses, houses, and more houses. Here\'s a list of things that most first-time home buyers typically overlook.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">FINANCING</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":8109,"width":"840px","height":"auto","aspectRatio":"1","sizeSlug":"large","linkDestination":"none"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large is-resized"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/tierra-mallorca-rgJ1J8SDEAY-unsplash-1024x769.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-8109" style="aspect-ratio:1;width:840px;height:auto"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Know your budget.</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It\'s important to have a realistic idea of how much you can afford to spend on a home. In addition to the purchase price, there are also other associated costs such as home insurance, property taxes, electricity and water installation, homeowner association fees, and repair/maintenance costs. Make sure to factor all of these when determining your budget.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>READ:  </strong><a href="http://localhost:3001/financially-prepared-buy-first-home/" data-type="post" data-id="1453" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">How to be Financially Prepared to Buy Your First Home</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Shop around for the right home loan. </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Not all home loans are created equal. Shop around and compare interest rates and terms before setting on a loan.  </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Get pre-approved for a home loan.</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Before you start seriously shopping for a home, it\'s important to get pre-approval for a home loan. This will give you an idea of how much money the bank is willing to lend you, and what your monthly mortgage payments will be. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">PHYSICAL ASPECTS</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7341,"sizeSlug":"large","linkDestination":"none"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Cebu-Landmasters-achieves-record-high-Php-8.5-billion-H1-reservation-sales-14-increase-01-1024x576.png" alt="" class="wp-image-7341"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Find the right home in the right neighborhood.</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Once you know how much you can afford to spend, it\'s time to start shopping for your dream home. Consider your needs and wants, and make sure to find a home in a neighborhood that you feel comfortable with.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Check out access to public transportation, or if there are any slaughterhouse, piggery or poultry nearby. Find out if there is an adequate water supply or if there are any frequent power interruptions in the area.  You might also want to check if the internet connection and the data signal is strong, especially if you consider <a href="http://localhost:3001/do-you-work-from-home-buy-your-next-home-with-your-office-in-mind/" data-type="post" data-id="4519">working from home</a>. Ask around whether it could potentially be a flood-prone area and if there\'s a regular garbage collection schedule. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Decide on the right home type for you. </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Decide whether you need a condo or a house and lot. Majority of Filipinos want a house and lot, and for good reason. Unlike condominiums and flats, where your options for remodeling are more constrained, it allows you the opportunity to make home changes. Additionally, it allows you more privacy. However, if you\'d prefer living within the central business district, a condominium unit might be a better option for you.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>READ:  </strong><a href="http://localhost:3001/condo-vs-house-not-sure-whether-to-buy-a-condominium-or-a-house/" data-type="post" data-id="6385">Condo vs House: Not sure whether to buy a condominium or a house?</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">REAL ESTATE BROKER</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here in the Philippines, it is not a common practice to hire <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="http://localhost:3001/what-are-the-different-real-estate-professionals/" data-type="post" data-id="1375" target="_blank">real estate brokers</a>. Most homebuyers just take on the burden of calculating expenses, haggling over the price, and completing documentation. Even though this can be successful, hiring a real estate broker can make the process easier for you.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You may get assistance from a licensed real estate professional since they can walk you through the procedure and clarify important information like property values and related taxes. Additionally, he or she can handle the paperwork related to the title transfer.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Hire a real estate broker if you feel you don\'t have the time to deal with the details of the transaction or if you want to be sure of the actions you do.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>READ:  </strong><a href="http://localhost:3001/real-estate-advise-from-realtors-to-first-time-home-buyers/" data-type="post" data-id="1156">Real Estate Advise from Realtors to First Time Home Buyers</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">HOME INSPECTION</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Get a home inspection. </h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Once&nbsp;you\'ve&nbsp;narrowed&nbsp;down&nbsp;your&nbsp;list&nbsp;of&nbsp;potential homes, it\'s important to get a professional home inspection to check for any hidden problems or defects. Take time to do ocular inspections of the house models, the subdivision and its amenities.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>READ:  </strong><a href="http://localhost:3001/answers-to-every-first-time-homebuyers-questions/" data-type="post" data-id="2807" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Answers To Every First-time Homebuyers Questions</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => NULL,'views' => '99','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2022-11-12 06:29:54','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '632','title' => '10 Indoor Gardening Ideas for Small Spaces','slug' => '10-indoor-gardening-ideas-for-small-spaces','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>What better way to enjoy nature than inside your home? If you live in a condo or an apartment, then you probably have limited space. However, with some creative indoor gardening ideas, overcoming this problem becomes easier. Here are some ideas:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>1.  Minimalist vibes</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":7665,"sizeSlug":"full","linkDestination":"none"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/da2397fe11c31722cf4555e605b720fe.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7665" /><figcaption><a href="https://www.pinterest.com.au/pin/578008933439872293/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">[src]</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you\'re going for a minimalist feel in your home, you might not want a lot of plants covering your flooring and other surfaces if your home is meant to have a minimalist feel. Instead, try adding a single piece of greenery; when placed in the ideal location, it may bring a touch of elegance without overdoing it to any space.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>2. Home Office Garden</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":7666,"sizeSlug":"large","linkDestination":"none"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/195e097d937429876b099aaa6d068f80-576x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7666" /><figcaption><a href="https://www.pinterest.com.au/pin/943574559403827003/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">[src]</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Whether it\'s a stylish workplace or a spacious study, there\'s always potential for improvement in our WFH spaces. It\'s always a great idea to introduce greeneries. This also helps alleviate your stress.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>3.  Hanging Herb Garden</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":7667,"sizeSlug":"full","linkDestination":"none"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/c39f9b1a6d7cf69e04579fd9951b8aa7.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7667" /><figcaption><a href="https://www.pinterest.com.au/pin/425590233550538574/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">[src]</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is a great idea if you love cooking. You have access to a fresh herb garden, and you\'ll be inspired to cook delicious meals. You don\'t even have to give up any counter space with a hanging arrangement like this to develop a modest herb collection. Even better, you\'ll get to save cash.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>4. Small Terrarium Garden</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":7668,"sizeSlug":"full","linkDestination":"none"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/d58d686db90af60d53d0af3a71131e57.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7668" /><figcaption><a href="https://www.pinterest.com.au/pin/68398488081826988/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">[src]</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>An indoor garden doesn\'t have to be extravagant or take up a lot of room. It only takes a few glass display cases and a few of your favorite succulents or air plants to create a miniature plant ecosystem.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>5. Mini Succulent Garden</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":7669,"sizeSlug":"full","linkDestination":"none"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/c1f3cb9c9729336609bd69d595d2c664.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7669" /><figcaption><a href="https://www.pinterest.com.au/pin/249246161029435453/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">[src]</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You have space for an indoor garden if you have a little unoccupied spot. Here\'s a little succulent collection that fits into a tiny house but still offers a boost of greenery.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>6. Floating Shelf Garden</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":7670,"sizeSlug":"full","linkDestination":"none"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/8e5834a60b4559c9b3b156a6a8f9e864.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7670" /><figcaption><a href="https://www.pinterest.com.au/pin/275001120988567006/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">[src]</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You may exhibit plants from floor to ceiling using floating shelves. Plants may be arranged according to how much light they prefer or even rotated as necessary to keep them healthy.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>7. Bathroom Indoor Garden</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":7671,"sizeSlug":"full","linkDestination":"none"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/f385a7ccd69643648b66c7129b3d6fba.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7671" /><figcaption><a href="https://www.pinterest.com.au/pin/275001120988567006/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">[src]</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Are you sure you have absolutely no space for an indoor garden? Whether you place a couple on a shelf, hang one from the ceiling, or hang one from the shower head, your bathroom may be a beautiful place for plants (or all the above).</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>8. Propagation Wall</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":7672,"sizeSlug":"large","linkDestination":"none"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/b8564b458bda6652d5f7d3c810bbc2b6-545x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7672" /><figcaption><a href="https://www.pinterest.com.au/pin/352547477094638972/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">[src]</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you\'ve begun collecting cuttings of your favorite plants because you\'re in full plant parent mode, put them in a stylish wall display until they need to be potted.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>9. Planter Divider</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":7673,"sizeSlug":"large","linkDestination":"none"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/fa3ee0abd2352db77da6abd6f48d707351c89087-1-683x1024.webp" alt="" class="wp-image-7673" /><figcaption><a href="https://www.apartmenttherapy.com/studio-apartment-space-planning-ideas-253753?epik=dj0yJnU9cGRTclAxSW91Sm1Fdk1scHdsM1ZpdU1hd3liSDZnQlYmcD0wJm49MEliZEVHM2M4V3BELTVvcTQ3aWhndyZ0PUFBQUFBR052UVhV" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">[src]</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You may also design a room divider that doubles as a planter to provide your space with both seclusion and a small garden.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>10.  Clothing Rack as a Vertical Garden</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":7674,"sizeSlug":"full","linkDestination":"none"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/119107c6c8384a149005cdec8060ec47.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7674" /><figcaption><a href="https://www.pinterest.com.au/pin/1055599903591778/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">[src]</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you\'re not the DIY kind, a clothing rack with hanging plants would work just as well.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2022/11/Filipino-Homes-blog-2.png','views' => '77','category_id' => '27','published_at' => '2022-11-12 08:08:47','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '633','title' => 'Filipino Homes Founder and CEO is one of Kabayan 2022 Awardees, pledges his prize to the company\'s Christmas community outreach fund','slug' => 'filipino-homes-founder-and-ceo-is-one-of-kabayan-2022-awardees-pledges-his-prize-to-the-companys-christmas-community-outreach-fund','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Our very own founder and CEO <strong>Anthony Gerard Leuterio</strong> was recognized one of the 2022 Kabayan Entrepreneur Awardees during Go Negosyo’s 17th anniversary on December 3, 2022.  The event was attended by thousands of current and former OFWs who want to learn about financial management and best practices from OFWs who have become entrepreneurs, businessmen, and content creators.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7696,"sizeSlug":"full","linkDestination":"none"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/leuterio.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7696" /><figcaption>Photo courtesy of <a href="https://web.facebook.com/gonegosyoofficial/posts/pfbid027fLab918o4htySpuiR6AXCtgCNB2uWxbasnFuSKg8tJ2rats2UsjHurtmvtgY1ECl?__cft__[0]=AZVVwmdyODIbdRBHi9XUqK_TJ-xEI6yT2VAABeWjEZrBo5KhMjcHcrSbflFd9yHeuCeMDOc_Z926arJovP9HXY45NZdN_5LAdAdF2ZuACNd26oDksaBjUI9l5DOO4RZu7vXCNciM6ITG923ulRGmiXCNE_pf6TTom-BLJPZhvtLtyw&amp;__tn__=%2CO%2CP-R" data-type="URL" data-id="https://web.facebook.com/gonegosyoofficial/posts/pfbid027fLab918o4htySpuiR6AXCtgCNB2uWxbasnFuSKg8tJ2rats2UsjHurtmvtgY1ECl?__cft__[0]=AZVVwmdyODIbdRBHi9XUqK_TJ-xEI6yT2VAABeWjEZrBo5KhMjcHcrSbflFd9yHeuCeMDOc_Z926arJovP9HXY45NZdN_5LAdAdF2ZuACNd26oDksaBjUI9l5DOO4RZu7vXCNciM6ITG923ulRGmiXCNE_pf6TTom-BLJPZhvtLtyw&amp;__tn__=%2CO%2CP-R" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Go Negosyo</a></figcaption></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Filipino Homes\' Leuterio is joined by eight other awardees, namely Arvin Esperida of Bodega ni Tatay; Angelito Castro of Angel Castro Aqua Ventures; Elpidia Abel, Inspiring OFW awardee; Jeffrey Guansing, YouTube influencer and founder of Team Harabas; Malou Prado, owner of MPQ Travel &amp; Tourism; Mardel delos Santos of Ledam’s Collections Company; Mark Durotan of Diko’s Food Processing &amp; Diko’s Integrated Farm; and Marvin Intal of Intal Garments.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":7697,"sizeSlug":"full","linkDestination":"none"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/kabayan-2022.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7697" /></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Leuterio said it\'s an honor to be named as one of the Filipino entrepreneurs who have helped OFWs invest in real estate, contributing to the country\'s economic prosperity. Filipino Homes has been helping OFWs and their families realize their dreams of home ownership. It also provides opportunities to Filipinos to explore the limitless opportunities in the real estate industry. The company has been promoting property investing in the Philippines to OFWs and foreign buyers in Singapore, the United States, the Middle East, and many more.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>During the year-end summit held in Pasay City, First Lady Liza Araneta-Marcos announced that President Ferdinand "Bongbong" Marcos Jr. is giving ₱200,000 each to the nine recipients of the Kabayan 2022 Awards.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:  </strong><a href="https://www.cnnphilippines.com/news/2022/12/3/Marcos-Go-Negosyo-Kabayan-2022-Awards.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Marcos pledges ₱200,000 each to \'Kabayan 2022\' awardees</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:image {"align":"center","id":7698,"sizeSlug":"large","linkDestination":"none"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/leuterio-marcos-1024x768.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-7698" /></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And because the ₱200,000 cash prize came as a pleasant surprise, Leuterio, in a Facebook post, has pledged to contribute the cash bonus to the Christmas community outreach programs to be organized by <a href="https://web.facebook.com/filipinohomes?__cft__[0]=AZXm9hhcE2IOlgg0xPGGqT8zvqa_sYVbNxrS1U35tzWMfw9fpl4h_SFg0jN0AmhaulcVoS4lAFaU_5iplfFvEXUcDV9A3PeOP6fM8gJshxWplF5vS5XDE0MedyNHmz1wp1jlbxXLmtp4n9gSEssyepKnyqTW0Sxvq2L6gven7y8hjg&amp;__tn__=-]K-R">Filipino Homes</a> and <a href="https://web.facebook.com/acresph?__cft__[0]=AZXm9hhcE2IOlgg0xPGGqT8zvqa_sYVbNxrS1U35tzWMfw9fpl4h_SFg0jN0AmhaulcVoS4lAFaU_5iplfFvEXUcDV9A3PeOP6fM8gJshxWplF5vS5XDE0MedyNHmz1wp1jlbxXLmtp4n9gSEssyepKnyqTW0Sxvq2L6gven7y8hjg&amp;__tn__=-]K-R">ACRES Philippines</a>. </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2022/12/Filipino-Homes-blog-5.png','views' => '50','category_id' => '17','published_at' => '2022-12-09 07:48:53','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '634','title' => 'Achieving Financial Freedom At Any Age: Expert Tips for Jumpstarting Your Real Estate Investment Goals','slug' => 'achieving-financial-freedom-at-any-age-expert-tips-for-jumpstarting-your-real-estate-investment-goals','content' => '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Are you longing to achieve financial freedom? With the right mindset and guidance, it is possible to jumpstart your real estate investment goals at any age. In this blog, we’ll share some tips to help you make smart investments in property. We will also discuss how buying a property now – even if you’re young – can help ensure your financial success in the future. So keep reading for tips on jumpstarting your real estate investment goals today!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Achieving financial freedom at any age</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Achieving financial freedom is something that many of us aspire to. But it can be hard to know where to start, especially if you’re young. Investing in property now could be the key to unlocking your long-term financial success. In this blog, you\'ll learn how to make smart investments in property and create a path toward achieving financial freedom.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:image {"id":7704,"sizeSlug":"large","linkDestination":"none"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="http://localhost:3001/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/Filipino-Homes-blog-1080-%C3%97-608-px-1024x576.png" alt="" class="wp-image-7704" /></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Tips for jumpstarting your real estate investment goals</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Real estate investing can be a great way to jumpstart your financial future. Here are some tips for kickstarting your real estate investment goals:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>1. Do your research</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>First, make sure you do your research and understand the market trends in the area where you plan to invest. Knowing what properties are selling for will help ensure that you don’t overpay or buy a property that won’t appreciate in value.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>2. Seek out sources of financing</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It\'s a good idea to check your current financial status and then seek out reliable sources of financing so that you can secure an appropriate loan amount and terms for each purchase.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>3. Consult with licensed real estate professionals</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Lastly, consult with licensed <a href="http://localhost:3001/what-are-the-different-real-estate-professionals/" data-type="post" data-id="1375">real estate professionals</a> to help you with all documentation related to purchasing a property so as not to miss any key details during the process.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><p><strong>READ:  </strong><a href="http://localhost:3001/what-are-the-different-real-estate-professionals/" data-type="post" data-id="1375" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">What Are The Different Real Estate Professionals?</a></p></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Taking these steps now will help guarantee success down the line when it comes time to reap the rewards of your investments.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>How buying a property at a young age can help you achieve financial freedom</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Buying a property at a young age is an excellent way to jumpstart your financial future and achieve lasting financial freedom. With the right mindset, strategy, and guidance from experienced real estate investors, you can maximize returns on your investments while minimizing risks. Not only will buying a property now help you build equity in the long term, but it can also provide additional income through rental payments or Airbnb hosting. With all these benefits combined, purchasing a property at a young age could be the key to unlocking long-term financial success!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Conclusion: Jumpstarting your real estate investment goals today</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you’re looking to jumpstart your real estate investment goals, <strong>now is the time!</strong> Investing in property now can provide many benefits such as building equity over time and creating additional income streams through rental payments or Airbnb hosting. So don’t wait –<strong> start researching today and make smart investments in property that will help secure your future financial success!</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Overall, starting the journey to achieve financial freedom through real estate investments does not have to wait. Following the tips can assist young and old alike in jumpstarting their investments today. With patience and dedication, you can begin building a portfolio that will help support your future for years to come. Put simply, beginning early on achieving financial freedom through Real Estate will likely result in higher gains than waiting until much later in life, so start investing now!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => NULL,'views' => '49','category_id' => '12','published_at' => '2022-12-23 04:56:13','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
  array('id' => '635','title' => 'How to Maximize Space in Your Compact Dining Room','slug' => 'how-to-maximize-space-in-your-compact-dining-room','content' => '<!-- wp:image {"align":"center"} -->
<div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/1571463/pexels-photo-1571463.jpeg?auto=compress&amp;cs=tinysrgb&amp;dpr=1&amp;w=500" alt="Free Round Brown Wooden 5-piece Dining Set in Room Stock Photo"/></figure></div>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>According to a 2020 survey of Filipino households by the Statista Research Department, 35.2 percent of families live in residential units that are from 10 to 29 square meters in floor area. An additional 30.2 percent of Filipino households live in units with a floor area ranging from 30 to 49 square meters, while, at the opposite end of the spectrum, only 2.3 percent of the population live in units exceeding 200 square meters.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Considering how often dining rooms are used to entertain guests and to dine with the family, it’s important to maximize and optimize the space so that it can be both functional and elegant. But, how do you get started? This guide will provide you with a few helpful tips.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Start with the Dining Table&nbsp;</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Most interior designers explain that the dining table should be the focal point of a compact dining room. When selecting a dining table for a smaller home, try to look for one that easily incorporates into your kitchen and living area so that the design is consistent throughout your apartment, condo unit, or tiny house. Look into different compact dining sets, and also consider the placement of appliances and furniture around it. It makes sense to take into consideration how the other elements in your dining space will be positioned around the dining tables since this will likely be the biggest object that will have to be accommodated into this part of your home.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can also consider giving away your current dining furniture set to a friend if it’s too big or clunky for your space, or put up your dining chairs and <a href="https://www.lookingfour.com/categories/furnitures/kitchen-dining-furniture/dining-tables">dining table for sale</a> on an online marketplace or at a neighborhood weekend market. Then, you can buy a replacement set that is more compact and occupies less floor space.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Understand the Layout of Your Home</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Though it sounds quite obvious, some people may forget to consider how their home or apartment is designed. Look at your dining area and consider how it flows into other rooms. Does it extend to your living room or is it cut by a bedroom? Is there a wall in the middle of the kitchen or are there any other blockages that prevent you from placing certain appliances in specific areas? If you live in a studio-type apartment, consider how much space you are willing to allocate for your dining area.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>An expert tip would be to measure your dining room’s floor space and how much you’re willing to set aside for your dining table. This makes shopping for a new furniture set easier as you’ll know the dimensions of the ideal dining table for your home.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Consider Multifunctional Dining Sets</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When considering a dining set for a smaller area, try to look for sets that serve more than one function. Some dining tables, for example, double as storage units, which can be helpful in clearing your dining space of clutter. Other dining sets can be folded and hidden from view when not in use, which means you’ll have more room to move about when it’s not time to eat.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If your budget is limited, you can opt for banquette seating instead. Rather than buying an actual table, you can solve limited space issues and budget concerns by selecting a comfortable sofa or bench first, then spending less on a foldable table.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Work Around Your Budget and Style</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Just because you live in a smaller home, doesn’t mean that you must sacrifice style. There are many options available for you, including a breakfast nook dining set. These are sets that include bench-type seating along two walls, with a park table. Because these sets usually are placed by the corners of a room, they allow you to save space while also providing a comfortable environment to entertain people in.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If that’s not your style, then you can also consider a collapsible table. Gone are the days when these tables were made from clunky materials that also looked cheap and breakable. Many furniture suppliers today offer a wide range of products, including elegant collapsible tables that you can prop up whenever you need them. A good tip would be to measure how wide and tall your table will be once it is collapsed, as you would need to have the right storage space for your table as well.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Another recommendation would be to incorporate shelves into your dining area to make the most of your wall space. You can easily install shelves onto your wall (if you’re renting, make sure that you secure permission from your landlord first), and use these shelves as additional storage space or as a way to display your family photos. If you’re shopping online and can’t otherwise inspect the actual furniture you’re intending to buy, make sure that you correctly measure the area where you intend to place your shelves and compare these measurements with the stated dimensions of the shelves. Also look at the maximum weight each shelf can accommodate.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When you have a compact dining room, it may seem impossible for you to entertain or live life in style. But with the right tricks for maximizing your dining space, you can easily turn a small area into the heart of your home.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','excerpt' => '','featured_image' => 'blog_news/uploads/2023/03/pexels-photo-1571463.jpeg','views' => '51','category_id' => '31','published_at' => '2023-03-28 04:17:08','created_at' => '2026-01-07 02:04:21','updated_at' => '2026-01-07 02:13:54'),
